msgctxt "items"
msgid "Relic"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:418 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2036
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A powerful weapon said to have been delivered up from the Netherworld in response to the wish of a prolific mass murderer.  The weapon inflicts terrible wounds with its razor sharp edge and drips acid constantly.  Not only a terrible weapon, the sword bestows the cunning of a master thief for disarming traps and the luck of the devil in escaping the damage they do.  Hades draws its power from its wielder slowly and constantly.  (Special Powers:  +20 Poison Damage, +20 Luck, Thievery, and Negative Regeneration)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:419 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2037
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Ares"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:419 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2037
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A powerful war-mace, Ares burns with fires from the heart of the mountain it was made from.  The same magic that causes it to burn with a terrible fire bestows resistance to fire upon its wielder.  (Special Powers:  +30 Fire Damage, +25 Fire Resistance)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:420 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2038
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Poseidon"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:420 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2038
msgctxt "items"
msgid "This trident is probably what inspired the Regnan navy to adopt the trident as their favorite weapon of war.  Poseidon fills its wielder with a frightening battle rage, increasing the wielder's might, endurance and accuracy at the cost of personal safety.  So consuming is the wielder's desire to smite his enemies while using Poseidon that he neglects to dodge blows he might otherwise have avoided.  On the other hand, dead enemies (usually) don't fight back.  (Special Powers:  +20 Might, +20 Endurance, +20 Accuracy, -10 Armor Class, and -10 Speed)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:421 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2039
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Cronos"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:421 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2039
msgctxt "items"
msgid "More a magical curiosity than a truly useful weapon, Cronos increases the wielder's vitality fantastically, and decreases his luck by half as much.  (Special Powers:  +100 Hit Points and -50 Luck)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:422 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2040
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Hercules"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:422 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2040
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A huge sword meant for the unsubtle, Hercules fills its wielder with the strength of a hundred men.  In keeping with its 'big and stupid' theme, the sword reduces the intelligence of its wielder while held.  (Special Powers:  +50 Might, +20 Endurance, and -30 Intellect)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:423 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2041
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Artemis"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:423 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2041
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Graced with the might of thunder, Artemus fires bolts magically charged with electricity.  While powerful, the user of the bow should be careful--elemental magics seem drawn to the bow, and do more damage when they hit the wielder.  (Special Powers:  +20 Electricity damage, -10 to Resistances)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:424 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2042
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Apollo"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:424 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2042
msgctxt "items"
msgid "This unique armor graces its owner with luck, helping him to escape the brunt of most elemental attacks.  It draws its energy, however, from the constitution of its wearer, making the wearing of this armor a risky proposition.  (Special Powers:  +20 to Resistances, +20 Luck, and -30 Endurance)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:425 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2043
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Zeus"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:425 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2043
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Perhaps this suit of armor was meant only for the Gods.  Worn at times by barbarian chieftains, the armor will increase the physical vitality and magical energy the wearer has at his disposal, but at a terrible cost.  House plants have been known to score higher on intelligence tests than wearers of this armor.  One would think that accidental death would surely follow such a precipitous loss of thought, yet the luck the armor bestows seems to prevent disaster.  Often the wearer of the armor becomes so stupid he forgets to remove it.  (Special Powers:  +50 Hit Points, +50 Spell Points,  +50 Luck, and -50 Intellect)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:426 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2044
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Aegis"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:426 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2044
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Legend has it this shield was given as a gift from the Gods to a man wishing to fight the terrible medusas in their stronghold.  The shield is reflective and prevents the wielder from being frozen by the stoning gaze of the medusa.  It also carries an enchantment that helps protect against arrows, but the shield is very heavy and will slow the user down a bit.  (Special Powers:  Immune to Flesh to Stone effects, Shielding +20 Luck, and -20 Speed)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:427 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2045
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Odin"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:427 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2045
msgctxt "items"
msgid "This crown is a mighty relic that protects against elemental magic attacks of all kinds, but has a flaw that slows the wearer down tremendously.  (Special Powers:  +50 to Resistances and -40 Speed)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:428 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2046
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Atlas"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:428 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2046
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Legends say this cape was discarded by a God who became annoyed with the cape's magical slowing of his actions.  It confers an incomparable might to its wearer, at a large cost to speed.  (Special Powers:  +100 Might and -40 Speed)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:429 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2047
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Hermes"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:429 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2047
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A relic from before the Silence, these boots must conceal some hidden magic as they are very heavy, yet light once worn.  They act upon the nerves and muscles of their wearer, heightening his speed and reflexes to inhuman levels, but simultaneously causing inaccuracy and over-compensation.  The boots have been owned by many through the ages, all of whom have died from some speed related accident, like running up a hill at blazing speeds and then falling down the cliff at the top.  (Special Powers:  +100 Speed and -40 Accuracy)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:430 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2048
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Aphrodite"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:430 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2048
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Desired and sought after by the foolish for ages, this beautiful ring smoothes the skin, clears the voice, and dramatically improves the physical beauty of its wearer, as well as enhancing the personality.  The ring also carries a curse of ill luck, and the wearer usually dies of some tragic accident soon after finding the ring.  (Special Powers:  +100 Personality and -40 Luck)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:431 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2049
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Athena"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:431 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2049
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Also known as the Scholar's Ring, Athena vastly sharpens and improves the intellect of its wearer at the cost physical might.  Though the effect upon the physical body is nearly crippling, most sorcerers find the temptation to wear the ring too great to resist.  (Special Powers:  +100 Intellect and -40 Might)"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:432 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2050
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Hera"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:432 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:2050
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sometimes referred to as the Amulet of the Fool, this curious relic from before the Silence dramatically increases the personal vitality, magical energy, and luck of the wearer at the expense of personality.  While the armor is worn, the face goes slack, the eyes vacant, and the voice subsides to a monotone.  (Special Powers:  +50 Hit Points, +50 Spell Points, +50 Luck, and -50 Personality)"
msgstr ""

