msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:174
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:123
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1061
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1865
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must be a member of this guild to study here"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:175
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1866
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For your numerous crimes and evil deeds, you have been sentenced to one year in prison. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1867
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Followers of Baa and a band of cutpurses have been raiding Mist from the islands to the north.  They come to Mist through a teleporter on the northwest of the island.  I'll activate the teleporter so that you can get to their islands and get rid of them.  I'm sure they have all the things they've stolen on those islands, and you can get back from their teleporter.   "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:177
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1868
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You never found it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:178
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1869
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here is the %s you have misplaced.  You must be more careful in the future."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:179
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1870
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Slicker Silvertongue refused my order?  This must be treason!  Still, I've known him so long, and he's never disobeyed an order before…perhaps he is suffering from delusions.  Yes, that's it.  He's been spending so much time investigating that horrible Baa cult that it's affected his mind– I even found one of their cloaks in his room.  Perhaps you can find a cure for him.  They must surely know what they've done to him!  I would start at their headquarters east of Castle Kriegspire.  Here, take the cloak– perhaps you can find some use for it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:180
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1871
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, my!  It appears that Slicker Silvertongue really is a traitor!  Who ever would have guessed it?  You've done a good thing, bringing this letter to me.  Take it to High Council immediately so we can be rid of this wicked traitor for once and for all!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:181
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1872
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Please hurry in your quest to find Slicker Silvertongue's cure!  I am sure the poor man must be suffering horribly under their dreadful mind control spell!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:182
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1873
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to the Circus of the Sun!  We have a variety of games for your amusement.  You can take the prizes you win from the various games and trade them in here for either kegs of wine or golden pyramids.  You need at least 10 points to get a keg of wine, and 30 or more points will win you a golden pyramid.  In case you didn't know, each lodestone is worth 1 point, each harpy feather is worth 3 points, and each four leaf clover is worth 5 points.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:183
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1874
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Missing Text:  Circus Main Tent Trade for Prize"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:184
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1875
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm sorry, but you don't have 10 points yet.  Why don't you try a few more games?"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:185
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1876
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!  You win a keg of wine!  There are no limits on the prizes here, so keep playing!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:186
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1877
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!  You win a golden pyramid!  Good work– remember there are no limits on the prizes, so keep playing!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:187
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1878
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome!  To play my game, simply pay 50 gold and step right up to compete against me.  Depending on how well you do you can win either a lodestone, a harpy feather, or a four leaf clover.  If you do poorly, you win nothing.  You can trade in your lodestones, feathers, and clovers in the main tent."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:188
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1879
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Too bad!  You came pretty close.  For 50 gold, I'll give you another chance."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:189
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1880
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good job, I thought I had you there.  You win a lodestone!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:190
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1881
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent work, you win a harpy feather!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:191
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1882
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Incredible!  Are you sure you didn't cheat?  Well, a rule's a rule.  Here's your prize– a four leaf clover!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:192
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1883
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As part of the effort to rebuild the Temple here in Free Haven, I'm collecting temple gongs.  If you have any gongs, I'll pay you 2000 gold for each of them."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:193
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1884
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one's a little dirty, but I suppose it will do.  Here is the gold I promised you for it.  Thanks for your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1885
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm looking for bones to use in my rituals.  I prefer bones from humans or humanoids, but I suppose I can make do with whatever you find.  I'm willing to pay up to 1000 gold for bones that I can use."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:195
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1886
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm...  A leg bone of a human?  This will do nicely.  This bone is certainly worth 1000 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1887
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many people aren't able to visit the circus, so I'm collecting circus prizes to give away to those not able to visit it themselves.  I'll buy lodestones for 5 gold each if you want to part with them."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:197
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1888
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you!  You're too generous– this will make a lovely gift.  Here's the 5 gold I owe you."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1889
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My daughter wants to go to the circus, but we never have the time when the circus is near here.  I'd love to give her a bunch of the pretty harpy feathers for her.  I'll take any harpy feathers you have for 10 gold each."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:199
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1890
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks!  Don't tell my daughter about this, I want to surprise her.  Here's the 10 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:200
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1891
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard that you can get really nifty things from Abdul's Desert Resort if you pay with golden pyramids.  I'm hoping to go there one day, and I want to stock up on the pyramids now.  I'll take any golden pyramids you have for 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:201
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1892
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome, adventurers!  Did you have something for me?  I'm a very busy man, you know.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:202
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1893
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can help you become an expert in the use of the staff as a weapon.  All you need is an intermediate skill in the staff (Rank 4) and 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not to brag, but I'm the best staff fighter in the land.  I will teach any student who is already an expert with the staff and has a high degree of skill (Rank 8) for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:204
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1895
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My teaching can improve your sword technique.  You must already be of intermediate skill (Rank 4) to benefit from my advice.  I charge 2000 gold per student."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am amongst the finest swordsmen in the land.  I will teach students free of charge who possess a high degree of skill (Rank 8) and are cavaliers in the eyes of Lord Osric Temper, the greatest swordsman ever to live.  I won't waste my time with anyone else."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:206
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1897
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wanna learn a few tricks with the dagger?  You've come to the right place, my friend.  I'll teach you if you already know a thing or two with a dagger (Rank 4), and of course can pay my fee of 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The dagger is a quick and subtle weapon that needs more brains than brawn to use.  If you're already skilled enough (Rank 8) and quick enough (Speed 40), I can train you to master rank for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:208
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1899
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Using an axe is trickier than you think.  If you've already had some practice with the axe (Rank 4), I'll be happy to show you the finer points of splitting skulls.  My fee is 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, you want to train your axe skill the dwarven way?  My tutorage will show you how to dramatically increase the damage you inflict with an axe."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:210
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1901
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It takes practice to use a spear right.  You have to know how to keep your enemy from getting past the point, and what to do when he does.  If you have enough skill already (Rank 4), I can show you the right moves.  All I want is 2000 gold for my services."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A little practice with the spear keeps you from making deadly mistakes in battle, but a lot more practice will help you get the best results from your spear.  I will teach you the secrets of the masters if you've already had a little practice (Rank 8) and have achieved cavalier or honorary cavalier status.  My fee is 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:212
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1903
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Learning to use a bow quickly and accurately is a skill that can take a lifetime to master.  I can start you down that road if you've already had some basic training (Rank 4) and 2000 gold in your purse.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many years ago, I discovered a technique for firing twice as many arrows as the conventionally trained archer can in the same amount of time.  Since all battle mages receive their titles from Lord Stromgard and I know he's a good man, I can rest assured you'll measure up to my standards.  My teaching is free, but you must already be highly skilled (Rank 8) in the bow and, of course, a battle mage. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:214
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1905
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A lot of people think there isn't much finesse in using a mace or hammer, but they're wrong.  Beating something to death with a mace is a lot like playing the drums.  You have to target the hard, bony parts of your enemy so your weapon will bounce back quickly, cocking itself for another strike.  I can teach you this technique if you already have a little skill (Rank 4) for 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of the mace can strike enemies senseless with a single blow.  I've been practicing this technique for years and have it down to a science.  If you have the strength (Might 40) and the skill (Rank 8), I can teach you my technique for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:216
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1907
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No weapon today can match the power of the weapons from the Time of Wonders.  I'm not sure any of those ancient weapons exist anymore, but I can show you some tricks if you find one.  Really!  I'm not crazy!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:217
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1908
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Long ago I found an old weapon that fired sunlight and could kill almost anything I used it against.  I killed so many dragons, it got to be routine.  I could shoot them out of the sky like big, slow ducks.  One day, it just stopped working, and my career as a dragon slayer ended.  If you ever bring me one, I'll show you how to use it right for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:218
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1909
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Used correctly, a shield makes a big difference in a fight.  You have to defend yourself if you're going to have a chance of winning.  I can give you a some advanced training if you've already practiced a little (Rank 4) and have 2000 gold to spend."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's easy to use a shield, but hard to use it right.  I can drastically improve your defense if you give me the chance.  Since I only offer extremely advanced training, you have to be an expert student (Rank 10) before I can help you.  All I ask is 5000 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:220
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1911
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can teach expert skill in leather armor for a modest fee of 1000 gold if you already have a little skill (Rank 4)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My teaching will bring you up to master ranking in leather armor for 3000 gold.  My students must already be highly skilled (Rank 10) in the use of leather armor for my teaching to be worth anything to them."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:222
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1913
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Using chain armor is a skill that must be developed like any other.  It's not like wearing a heavy coat, that's for sure!  I can train a little expertise into you for 1000 gold, provided you already have some skill (Rank 4) with chain armor."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Chain armor is a weapon of war, there's no doubt of that, and I'm careful who I train in its use.  I'll only take crusaders recommended by King Roland or his regent, Wilbur Humphrey.  I have no fee, but I do require my students to be well practiced (Rank 10) before I'll train them."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:224
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1915
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An expert with plate armor can wear it with elegance and style.  I can instill this grace in my students if they already have a little skill (Rank 4) and 1000 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "One who is a master in the use of plate mail wears it as easily as he wears his own clothes.  Since plate mail is such a militarily important skill, I'll only teach it to people designated heroes by the king or his regent."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:226
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1917
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The secrets of the fire are deep indeed, and can only be taught to one well initiated in the art (Rank 4).  I can bring your skill to expert level for 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Long have I studied the mysteries of fire magic, and have finally come to master the skill.  I can teach the highly skilled (Rank 12) some of the things I've learned for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:228
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1919
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are ways to draw magical energy from the air to power your spells longer and more efficiently.  If you're practiced in the art of air magic (Rank 4), I can teach you for 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Air magic is the most subtle and quirky of the elemental magics you can study.  Because of the difficulty involved in learning this skill, I can only teach those who have achieved arch mage status.  My price is 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:230
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1921
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Water is the element of movement and change.  Without skill in water magic, it takes forever to get from one side of the kingdom to the other.  I can improve your skill to expert status if you've already had a little practice (Rank 4).  My fee is 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of water magic with the Lloyd's Beacon spell can travel about the kingdom as much as he pleases.  I teach the skill to the most advanced students (Rank 12) for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:232
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1923
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you want to become an expert in earth magic, you've come to the right place.  All you need is a modest level of skill (Rank 4) and 1000 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can teach experts in earth magic to become masters of earth magic.  You must be very highly skilled (Rank 12) before I can help you, and my fee is 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:234
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1925
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Spirit magic is the magic you need to bring life from death.  I can train you in this important skill if you've already had a little practice (Rank 4) and are willing to pay me 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The most advanced spells of spirit magic permit the practitioner to raise the dead back to life. The choice of bringing a soul back from its final resting place is a weighty one indeed, and I will only train those sanctioned by Lord Stone as High Priests in the mastery of spirit magic.  In the service of humanity I freely perform this service."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:236
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1927
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can fine tune your skill in mind magic, bringing you up to the level of expert in this vital skill.  You must have had a little practice (Rank 4) and be willing to pay a fee of 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will train any experts of mind magic sufficiently skilled (Rank 12) to master level for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:238
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1929
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Body magic is the magic of healing and strengthening spells.  I will train anyone who is interested up to expert level for 1000 gold.  All you need is a little prior practice (Rank 4) for me to help you."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The mysteries of the body can be yours all for the low, low price of 4000 gold.  Only highly skilled (rank 12) experts can benefit from my teachings."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can show you some of the secrets of light magic if you already have a little skill (Rank 4) to start with.  My fee is 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of light magic is amongst the most powerful spell casters in the world.  I can improve nearly any expert to master status, but I do not do this lightly.  I will only teach persons of the highest reputation.  Living saints."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah!  A student of darkness, no doubt!  If you want schooling in dark magic, I can help you if you've already practiced a little (Rank 4).  My fee is 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can bring experts of dark magic up to master, provided they meet my standards.  I only teach the genuinely dedicated– those so evil their reputations are as bad as they can get.  The truly notorious.  I make no exceptions, and charge no fee in the interests of spreading darkness throughout the world."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:244
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1935
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you've spent any time adventuring at all, you'll know how important it is to know what your equipment does and how much it's worth.  I can improve your expertise with this skill if you already have a little identify skill to start with (Rank 4).  My price is 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You may already have found that while being an expert in identifying your treasure is good, it's not good enough.  I change  that.  I will teach experts to become masters for 2500 gold.  All you need is sufficient skill (Rank 7) and smarts (Intellect 30)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:246
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1937
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will happily teach anyone with enough (Rank 4) merchant skill to become an expert merchant for 2000 gold.  It may seem expensive, but it's worth it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Rare is the expert merchant, but rarer still is the master.  I can finish your merchant's education for 4000 gold, provided you have the skill (Rank 7) and the charm (Personality 30)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:248
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1939
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Any blacksmith shop can repair your equipment, but what do you do when something breaks while you're on the road?  I can make you an expert at mending things that are broken.  All you need is a little repair skill (Rank 4) to start with, and the gold to pay me.  My fee is but 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I teach experts in repair skill to be masters in the repair skill.  You must have a high skill (Rank 7), fine agility (Accuracy 30) and 2500 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:250
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1941
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ja, you want to learn body building, right?  Then you listen to me.  I teach you right for 500 gold, if you have a little meat on your body (Rank 4) to start with."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If ever I've seen such pathetic weaklings as you, for the life of me I cannot remember!  Starving rats have more meat on their bones!  For a fee of 2500 gold, I'll beat you mercilessly until you become master body builders!  You must, however, already have spent time working out (Rank 7) and be tough enough to take my punishment (Endurance 30) before I'll have anything to do with you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:252
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1943
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The way to achieve strength in the material realm is to achieve strength in the spiritual realm.  I can show you the way.  For a fee of 500 gold, I will help you attain expert skill in meditation if you have already had a little practice (Rank 4)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who disturbs my meditation, as the pebble disturbs the stillness of the pond?  Ahh, seekers of the True Path.  If you have already traveled the path of meditation for some time (rank 7) and have the strength of character (Personality 30) necessary for my teaching, I can lead you to master status for 2500 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:254
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1945
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The watchful can sometimes see a trap just before it goes off.  The lucky and skillful can sometimes avoid damage altogether.  I can teach you to recognize and avoid these traps provided you've already practiced a little (Rank 4) and have 500 gold for my fee.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The lucky person with a well trained eye can often stay out of harm's way when a trap goes off unexpectedly.  If you've already had a lot of practice (Rank 7) and are lucky enough (Luck 30), I'll make you a master of the perception skill.  My fee is but 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:256
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1947
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Having trouble getting people to talk to you?  That's your reputation speaking!  A little skill in diplomacy will lessen the impact of your past misdeeds.  I can bring you up to expert diplomat if you've already practiced your diplomacy a little (Rank 4) and have 500 gold for my fee.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:257
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1948
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Even a murderer is entitled to his day in court, and a good diplomat can turn a premeditated ambush into a case of desperate self defense.  I specialize in training expert diplomats into master diplomats.  You must have had plenty of practice (Rank 7) and enough fame (200) for my teaching to be of help.  My fee is 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:258
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1949
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So much of the treasure of the land is in the hands of monsters and criminals, and they have been getting very clever with their traps.  You really need to know how to get past those traps and live to tell the tale.  I can help.  If you already have a little skill (Rank 4), I can train you to expert rank for just 500 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:259
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's one thing to kill a rich and powerful monster, but it's something else entirely to get past the traps it puts on its treasure chests.  My disarm training is the best in the kingdom.  If you're already an expert and have the skill (Rank 7) and the talent (accuracy 30), I can train you to master rank for 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:260
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1951
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must learn to learn well if you're to enjoy a long and fruitful life.  If you already understand what I'm talking about (Rank 4), I can take you a lot farther.  My teachings cost 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the teacher of teachers, the master of learning.  I can bring your understanding of the world around you to new heights.  I will only train those who have studied under my old students and have a thorough understanding of my precepts (Rank 7).  If you are smart enough (Intellect 30), I can bring you to master rank for 5000 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:262
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:126
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:126
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:741
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:126
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:741
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1064
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1953
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You don't have enough gold!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:263
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:129
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:129
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:129
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1067
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1954
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You don't meet the requirements, and cannot be taught until you do."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:264
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:133
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:133
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:133
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1071
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1955
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must know the skill before you can become an expert in it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:265
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1956
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must first be an expert in the skill before you can become a master."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:266
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:124
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:124
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:124
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1062
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1957
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not in your condition!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:267
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:130
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:130
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:130
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1068
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1958
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are already an expert in this skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:268
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:131
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:131
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:131
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1069
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1959
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are already a master in this skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:269
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1960
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The best staff teacher in the land, Jasper Rice, lives up near Silver Cove.  You'll want to talk to him if you wish to continue your training with the staff."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:270
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1961
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Guy Hampton in Blackshire taught me everything I know about the sword.  If you're looking to master the blade, he's the one to train under."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:271
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1962
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm only a novice when compared to someone like Jules Miles.  He lives near Castle Stone, and he can teach anyone how to improve their dagger skills."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:272
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1963
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Avinril Smythers mastered the axe before most of us were even born, but he doesn't train humans.  I'm sure if you could do something special for him, he might consider teaching a human how to really swing an axe.  He spends most of his time in the Haunt in the Mire of the Damned."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:273
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1964
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The best spearman in Enroth, Burton Rutherford, lives in Darkmoor.  I'm not sure why he picks such a remote place to call his home.  Maybe he doesn't like being bothered with students?"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:274
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1965
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As good as Lord Stromgard is with a bow, he won't accept students.  To master the bow, you need to talk to Desmond Weller in Kriegspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:275
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1966
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you want to master the mace, you need to speak to Errol Ostermann in Blackshire."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:276
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1967
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Very few people even know that these weapons exist.  The only other person I've ever seen using an ancient weapon is Rexella, but she was last living in Paradise Valley– I'm not sure she's even there anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:277
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1968
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No one can use a shield like Bronwyn Meck in Blackshire.  That's the person to talk to if you want to master the shield."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:278
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1969
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Arlen Sailor runs the best school in the art of wearing leather armor.  He normally holds his classes near Castle Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:279
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1970
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Darkmoor is the home of David Feather, the only person I know of that can teach you to master your skill in chain armor."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:280
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1971
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Forrest Suthers, one of the head Paladins in Enroth, teaches how to master plate near Castle Temper."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:281
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1972
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To master the fire skill you need to speak to Jezebel in Mist."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:282
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1973
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Caao Salem can show you even more tricks with air magic in Mist."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:283
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1974
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To gain mastery of the water skill you need to train under Harper Collins in Mist."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:284
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1975
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Revee Botania can train you to master the earth skill in Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:285
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1976
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Spirit can be mastered with the help of Bishop Inquisitorio.  He lives right behind Castle Ironfist, you can't miss him."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:286
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1977
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thane Roper can train you to master the mind skill in Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:287
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1978
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you're looking to master body magic, you need to talk to Gilbert Hammer in Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:288
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1979
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Light magic is a difficult skill to learn, and the Great Teacher, Ki Lo Nee, can only be found somewhere around Castle Alamos."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:289
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1980
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Su Lang Manchu was my teacher in dark magic.  He maintains a small house in a village in Paradise Valley."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:290
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1981
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hans Gifford can show you even more neat tricks in identifying items in Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:291
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1982
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The smoothest talking merchant I've ever seen is Will Ottoman in Silver Cove.  If you're looking to improve your merchant skill, he's the man to see."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:292
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1983
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you think I'm good at repairing things, Ryan Treacle is the best around.  I'm sure he can be convinced to assist you in mastering the skill.  He lives up near Castle Stone the last I heard."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:293
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1984
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jason Traveler will coach you in the finest points of body-building.  He works in Free Haven, if you can handle his rigorous training."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:294
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1985
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If mastering meditation is your goal, you'll need to see Norio Ariganaka in Mist."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:295
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1986
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Perception can be mastered with help from Macro Caligula in Darkmoor."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:296
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jacques Kohl is working with Lord Stromgard to develop the lord's eloquence and tact.  If he has time, perhaps he can assist you as well in mastering the art of diplomacy."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:297
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1988
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The greatest trap disarmer, Gabe Lester, is currently teaching his craft near Castle Stone.  He's the person to talk to if you want to learn all the best tricks."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:298
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1989
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "John Tuck can teach you to master the learning skill.  I believe he's still living in Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:299
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1990
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The King of the Dwarves, Snergle, usurped Rocklin for leadership of the dwarven clans.  Now Rocklin is in exile somewhere and Snergle is in charge.  Most dwarves don’t like Snergle and would like to see Rocklin back in power.  Unfortunately, Snergle has claimed both Rocklin’s caverns and the largest dwarven Iron Mine.  Snergle, fearing treachery near home, has removed me, the Dwarven Weaponmaster, from my position.  We need someone to get Snergle out of power by any means necessary.  I’d even consider training you humans how to use an axe like a true dwarf if you’ll help us."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:300
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1991
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I need proof that Snergle has been defeated.  I’m sorry, but I just can’t take your word for it.  Bring back some personal item of his, like his axe maybe."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:301
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1992
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, glorious day!  With Snergle’s passing, we can now search for Rocklin to put him back in power.  Eternal thanks to you for this, and dwarves everywhere owe you a debt of gratitude."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:302
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1993
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Mayor here in Mist is considering allowing the Fraternal Order of Silver to police the town in their battle against evil.  I know the Silver Helm Persecution Squads have murdered innocents in their misguided crusade against ‘evil,’ but there are no living witnesses to their atrocities.  I need you to storm their outpost to the south of here to find proof so that I can convince the mayor to ban them from Mist."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:303
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1994
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Keep searching– the lives of the mayor and myself could very well be in your hands.  We can’t take action against them without proof."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:304
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1995
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Just as I suspected!  I’m surprised the Mayor was number three on their enemies list.  I suppose he IS a tad incompetent, but he’s not a bad person.  Thanks again, please accept this gold and my gratitude as your reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:305
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1996
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I think I might just allow the Fraternal Order of Silver to police the areas around Mist.  Maybe they’d be able to hunt down all the evil people and leave this island a paradise."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:306
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1997
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can’t believe those Silver Helms wanted to kill me!  I’ve never done anything wrong in my life!  Well, nothing more wrong than any other mayor at least.  Thank you again for stopping them."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:307
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1998
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Could you do the Temple of Baa a favor?  It appears that my brethren left the old temple to the northwest of here in a little too much of a hurry, and a candelabra necessary for some of our rituals was left behind.  None of the Baa priests want to go back because they’re afraid of whatever curse has been placed on the temple.  If you were to bring back the candelabra to me, however, I could reward you in their place."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:308
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1999
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Did the curse frighten you away as well?  I can understand.  Baa is patient, however.  Should you work up the courage to find the candelabra, I’m still prepared to compensate you for it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:309
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2000
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  Baa be praised!  I see you were not frightened of the curse after all.  Here is your reward and thank you again for your assistance."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:310
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2001
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who would have thought that the evil I sought to fight all across Enroth would be found so close to my own home?  Gerrard Blackames was once my second in command.  Not long before he murdered me he began corresponding with the Temple of Baa, and they began to feed him targets for our Order.  I ended up being one of the targets, and Gerrard took control of the Order.  Now, the Silver Helms are as evil as the people they hunt.  I’m certain the Temple of Baa is responsible for the corruption of our Order.  At the same time, Gerrard’s brother, Marcus the Sorcerer, has been supplying the Silver Helms with high quality equipment.  The last I heard, Marcus was assisting someone in a forge on an island to the southeast."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:311
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2002
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My niece, Melody, has been kidnapped from her home in Mist and locked in a Silver Helm outpost near there.  She’s one of the few people who know that I’ve been murdered.  I’m sure Gerrard has her locked up for that reason, but I believe he wants to force her into marriage to eliminate any opposition to his leadership of the Fraternal Order of Silver."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:312
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2003
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for saving my niece.  Behind this wall is a secret area I’ve kept hidden from even Gerrard all these years.  You are welcome to take whatever you want; I’d prefer you have this than Gerrard."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:313
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2004
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gerrard has an ankh inscribed with his name given to him by the priests of Baa.  I’m not sure exactly what the ankh is used for, but he may use it to identify himself as a friend of Baa."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:314
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2005
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You want to defeat Snergle, do you?  Well, he knows how he stands among most dwarves.  He’s holed up in Rocklin’s old caverns surrounded by a horde of his loyal dwarves.  If anything were to happen in there, he’d just immediately lock himself in his private room and let his followers handle it.  You’ll need a key to get into his room; there’s no way you’ll bash down a high quality dwarven door.  I was a steward for Rocklin– I know that room well and I happen to still have a key to it hidden on me.  Fortunately for you, I’m in this cell because of Snergle, and there’s nothing I’d rather see than his reign put to a quick end.  Here’s the key– think of it as payment for letting me out of this cell."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:315
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2006
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for releasing me.  The only thing keeping the Silver Helms from killing me was the fact I’m a priest.  Frankly, I’m surprised they would show me any mercy at all.  Listen, I’ve heard some strange sounds coming from around here… I think there might be a hidden passage near here.  In any event, I should probably be leaving now; I don’t want to stay in this cell any longer."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:316
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2007
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dragoons that have been plaguing the roads around here recently stole a harp of mine from one of my caravans.  I’m not strong enough to get it back from them, but I’m willing to pay someone capable to do it for me.  Find the harp and return it, and I’ll reward you."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:317
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2008
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My harp is still lost, so the reward is still available for it.  I know the Dragoons base their operations to the south of here near the coast.  Please bring back my harp."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:318
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2009
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My gratitude!  My wife loves this harp; I’m so glad you were able to recover it!  Here, take this as a reward.  I’ve heard rumors that the Dragoons were working with the Shadow Guild.  If that’s the case, I’m sure the Mayor of New Sorpigal would love to see proof of it.  Thank you again for your assistance."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:319
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2010
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, this IS a musical instrument, but it’s not a harp.  Let me explain the difference:  You brought back a flute.  A flute is a pipe with holes in it.  A harp has strings.  Does that help?  I’m sure they still have the harp and I will reward you well for its return."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:320
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2011
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have a few theories about the undead that I would very much like to prove.  What I really need is the remains of an undead creature, preferably a powerful one.  Actually, what I really need is the remains of the FIRST lich, Ethric the Mad.  I am a scholar, however, and don’t have the means to gain such a specimen.  I do have some money saved up, and I’d be willing to pay you well for Ethric’s remains."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:321
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2012
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am well aware of the difficulty of the task, believe me.  Take your time but at the least, do the job properly. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:322
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2013
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work! Now I can conclude my research.  If I can learn how the Ritual of Endless Night works, perhaps I can find a way to reverse the process.  Here is the reward I promised you. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:323
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2014
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our town is periodically plagued by giant spiders.  I’m pretty sure that if the spider queen were killed, the rest of the spiders would go away.  Currently, I’m offering a reward to the person that can kill the spider queen."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:324
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2015
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No one has returned with proof that they’ve killed the spider queen, so the reward is still available."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:325
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2016
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What a gruesome trophy!  This heart proves you’ve defeated the wicked spider queen.  Hopefully now the spiders won’t plague New Sorpigal anymore.  Here is the reward I promised."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:326
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2017
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Cedric Druthers and his Celestial Order have taken over the Monolith, an ancient place sacred to druids.  Their dark rituals are corrupting the Monolith and they need to be stopped– whatever altar they use as the center of their ceremonies needs to be defaced.  Do this for us and we will compensate you for your time and services."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:327
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2018
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I’m glad to see you again, but the Celestial Order is still in the Monolith."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:328
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2019
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for your help!  Please allow me to compensate you for your efforts.  We can rest more safely knowing that Cedric and his renegade druids are no longer polluting that sacred area. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:329
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2020
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am a collector of rare and exotic creatures, and I make a living by selling some of these creatures as pets.  Currently, cobras are in great demand, and I don’t have many cobras left to sell.  Therefore, I’m willing to pay handsomely for any cobra eggs you might have.  Remember, if you find any cobra eggs, I’ll give you the best prices."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:330
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2021
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent specimen!  I should be able to hatch this in no time and help my flagging business.  Here is my payment for this wonderful egg.  I’ll buy any more cobra eggs you have as long as they are in demand."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:331
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:332
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:333
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2022
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2023
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2024
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Removed Bat Guano Message"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:334
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2025
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Near here is a temple dedicated to the Order of the Fist.  I once belonged to that order, but recently they uncovered a powerful evil crystal.  They hope to use the crystal as a bargaining chip to be accepted into the Temple of Baa.  I don’t want to see the crystal fall into Baa’s hands– it must be destroyed.  Please infiltrate the temple and destroy the crystal."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:335
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2026
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must hurry and destroy the crystal before Baa claims it.  I’m not sure how long it will take, so time is of the essence."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:336
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2027
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work!  I’m glad you made it in time.  I don’t like to think about what Baa would have done with that crystal.  You have done all of Enroth a great service."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:337
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2028
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My husband, Emmanuel, went to Star Island a few weeks ago with a few friends hoping to find some treasure.  I haven’t seen him since, and I’m worried about him.  I don’t dare go to the island; it’s rumored to be the home of medusas!  If you could find him and bring him home, I would be very grateful."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:338
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2029
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No luck?  He must be in grave danger if you did not find him.  If you do happen to find him, please bring him back here.  I’ll be waiting for him."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:339
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2030
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, thank you for bringing Emmanuel back to me!  Nothing in this world means as much to me as him!  Please take this as a reward.  I know it’s not much, but you deserve it for bringing him back to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:340
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:341
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2031
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2032
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for turning me back to normal. I’d love to stay and chat, but I really should be getting out of here."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:342
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2033
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Could you help me get out of here?  I need to get back to my wife in Blackshire."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:343
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2034
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An explorer friend of mine recently uncovered a powerful artifact, Mordred, in his travels.  He wanted to sell it to me, and shipped it here for me to decide if I wanted it.  Unfortunately, raiders attacked the caravan it was on and stole the artifact.  They were last seen headed to an area west of Castle Temper; I’m sure they must have some sort of base there.  If you bring back Mordred for me, I’ll give you a cut of what I’m paying my friend for it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:344
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2035
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again.  No one has found Mordred yet, so our deal is still good.  I’ll give you part of the selling price for the artifact if you return it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:345
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2036
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So this is the legendary Mordred, eh?  Interesting, I was expecting something much grander.  I don’t think I want it, actually.  Why don’t you keep it, and I’ll deal with my friend on the cost."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:346
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2037
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Members of the Shadow Guild have moved down south recently, and have been trying to exert their influence over merchants in the area.  I refused them access to our town, so they kidnapped Sharry Carnegie, an old healer loved by the townspeople, in an attempt to ‘convince’ me to let them operate here.  I can’t believe that their extortion has moved so far south, I thought I was safe from that down here.  Please rescue Sharry– I can offer you some money as a reward, and I’m sure the townsfolk would appreciate her return."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:347
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2038
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found Sharry yet?  No?  I’m sure she’s wherever the Shadow Guild is hiding out.  Find them and you’ll find her."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:348
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2039
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you so much for saving Sharry!  I can’t tell you how much this means to both New Sorpigal and myself.  You have our gratitude forever."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:349
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2040
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Interesting.  The Dragoons were hired by the Shadow Guild.  I’m certain Anthony Stone will want to hear about this.  I’ll present this letter when I see him next. Thank you for this.  I’m sure he will want to take action against the Shadow Guild now that we have some proof of their deeds."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:350
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2041
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for rescuing me from these horrible ruffians!  I’d like to go back home to New Sorpigal now."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:351
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2042
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh dear, can you help me?  My daughter Angela is missing!  I think she may have wandered into the abandoned temple near town, and if she did she could be in terrible danger– who knows what kind of horrible things are lurking in that cursed place!  Please find her and bring her back to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:352
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2043
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You didn’t find poor Angela?  Something horrible must have happened to her!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:353
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2044
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "She’s alive!  Thank you so much for finding Angela!  If I weren’t so happy to see her, she’d be in a lot of trouble.  Please take this as a reward for all you’ve done."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:354
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2045
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I think I'm lost…<sob>…I want to go home!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:355
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2046
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A good friend of mine, Sherell, went with a group of friends to the islands in Bootleg Bay to explore an old temple rumored to be there.  Her friends returned and said she was captured by cannibals on the island and taken to some ancient temple.  I’m sure she doesn’t have much time before they do something dreadful to her, please rescue her!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:356
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2047
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh dear!  You haven’t found her yet?  Surely she must have been sacrificed or eaten or something.  Please try to find her, or at least avenge her death."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:357
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2048
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wonderful!  She’s not dead after all!  Thank you for all your trouble.  I hope you will accept this token of my gratitude."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:358
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2049
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello!  Please, oh please, get me out of this temple.  I don’t want to die!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:359
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2050
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our town is under a terrible curse, though most people don’t believe it.  Under a full moon, we all change into werewolves.  Although none of us are truly evil, we don’t really know what sort of horrible things we do as werewolves.  We can’t approach our lord, Acton Spindler about the problem because he doesn’t realize that we are the werewolves.  Please find a way to turn us back to normal!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:360
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2051
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Is there no hope for us?  Please promise me you’ll keep searching for a way to reverse the curse and turn us back to normal people."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:361
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2052
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you!  We can now sleep at night without worrying about what kinds of foul acts we will commit as monsters!  It’s a tragedy that our lord was a werewolf himself; he’ll be sorely missed.  Please accept this for your help, and for believing in us."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:362
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2053
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Blackshire has been plagued by werewolves lately.  These caves must be where the werewolves are coming from!  However, I will need help destroying them.  You’re welcome to any of the treasure we find.  I’m only concerned with destroying them once and for all!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:363
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2054
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You see, I am a werewolf and soon you will be one too!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:364
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2055
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was a guest at Lord Spindler's manor when it was attacked by a band of werewolves that had tunneled in from the mountains.  I fought my way back down the tunnels they had created hoping to escape.  Eventually, they cornered me and I was killed at this very spot. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:365
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2056
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In my flight, I managed to hide the Pearl of Purity in these caverns.  The pearl will both protect you from the curse of the werewolves, and will also destroy the Altar of the Wolf if the pearl touches it.  That should free everyone afflicted by the curse these werewolves have caused.  The pearl is at the end of the cavern across from this one.  Please do me one favor, return the Pearl to Wilbur Humphrey.  He is the lord in charge of paladins and the pearl belongs with him."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:366
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:367
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2057
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2058
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The werewolf leader possesses the Pearl of Putrescence, the opposite of my Pearl of Purity.  With this pearl, he has been able to cause the curse.  I was never able to kill him in my retreat.  I will be able to rest in peace knowing that he has been defeated."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:368
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2059
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for defeating the werewolf leader.  I wish that I had been strong enough to stop this from happening.  Please accept my thanks for allowing my spirit to move on.  I will take the pearl away so that it may no longer cause any harm to the people of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:369
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2060
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What’s this?  You have the Pearl of Purity?  I thought Balthasar– oh, he’s dead is he?  I’ll keep it for now, then, as per his last wishes.  Thank you on behalf of both him and me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:370
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:353
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:134
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:134
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1258
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2061
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This month's bounty is on a %s.  Kill it and return before the end of the month to collect the %lu gold reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:371
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:354
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:135
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:135
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1259
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2062
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations on defeating the %s!  Here is the %lu gold reward.  Come back next month for a new bounty."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:372
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:355
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:136
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:136
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1260
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2063
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Someone has already claimed the bounty this month.  Come back next month for a new bounty."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:373
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2064
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not used."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:374
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2065
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You no goblin!  You leave!  We take castle to watch over humans!  You no more kill us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:375
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2066
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work removing the goblins from this keep.  We have the situation mostly under control now, though your help is always appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:376
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2067
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, my pupils!  I'm afraid there is nothing more I can teach you– your experiences must guide you from this point on.  I know nothing more than you do about the devils that destroyed Sweet Water, but I know who you need to ask.  The Oracle in Free Haven will know what to do to rid Enroth of the terrible devils.  Unfortunately, you will need the approval of the six High Council members, each of which represents one of the lords of Enroth.  You must do whatever necessary to speak to the Oracle in Free Haven and rid Enroth of the devils."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:377
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2068
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As you may know, the last members of the Necromancers' Guild in Enroth fled to Castle Darkmoor after their defeat in the Succession War.  Who knows what foul magics they're concocting while we wait around.  I'm certain that the book containing the Ritual of Endless Night, known as the Book of Liches, has been moved into that castle.  If the book were to be destroyed, it would deal a severe blow to whatever evil plans they have.  I've tried a few times to get to the book, but the castle is too well defended.  If you are able to destroy the book, come back to me and I'll reward you personally."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:378
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2069
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There's no rush in destroying the book.  If you manage it, come back and talk to me.  I'm not sure it's even possible to get to the book and destroy it– there are far too many evil creatures in that castle."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:379
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2070
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Incredible!  I didn't expect you'd be able to do it.  Now that the Book of Liches is gone, the Necromancers' Guild here in Enroth will slowly fade away.  This is all thanks to you!  Here, take this as a reward and accept my gratitude as well."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:380
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2071
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was once the court magician, long ago.  That all ended when Archibald… disrupted… things.  Archibald had acquired some skill as a sorcerer and had knowledge of spells beyond that taught to magicians today, and therefore didn’t require my services.  Since then, I’ve lived in this little shack, conducted my own research, and have grown old."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:381
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2072
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I’ve discovered a way to reverse the effects of time and make myself young again.  This requires a complex magical ritual, which I’ve worked out.  The problem is that I need to place magical statuettes on various pedestals. The tiger statuette goes on the pedestal near Sweet Water, the bear statuette in Kriegspire, the eagle statuette in Dragonsand, the wolf statuette in the Mire of the Damned, and the dragon statuette in Bootleg Bay.  The distances are too far for me to travel in my old age, and in the meantime I need to prepare the ritual itself.  There is no way I can do all of this on my own; I need your help.  The statuettes are in the chest outside my house.  Place them on the pedestals and return to me.  Even if the ritual is a failure, I'll pay you for your efforts."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:382
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2073
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was one of the mages studying at Kriegspire when the creatures there went completely out of control.  In my escape from the castle, I left a valuable item behind, a jeweled egg.  This egg is a family heirloom that goes back in my family as far as the Silence.  I have tried a few times to get it back, but the creatures there are too powerful for me.  I’d gladly trade a generous sum of money to get my egg back."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:383
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2074
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kriegspire is the castle inside the volcano.  We mages were forced to raise the earth around the castle to try and prevent the creatures from overrunning the surrounding towns.  Now they’re contained inside, and that’s where the egg is."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:384
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2075
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for returning this egg to me; it’s the most precious thing I have."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:385
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2076
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the Lord of Fire, an immortal earth spirit.  My power is drawn from below the earth.  The channels that I use have been blocked by doors warded with powerful magic in the north.  I need you to unward the doors so that I may awaken again.  Though the enchantments on them are powerful, amber will break the ward on the doors."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:386
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2077
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you get lost in the caverns, you may find assistance from my servants.  If you have a piece of amber, they will assume you are under my care and will teleport you back to me if you talk to them.  If you do not have any amber, they will drain with some of your life force as payment for teleporting you back up here.  Don’t worry, they rarely kill anyone."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:387
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2078
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The doors became warded when a strange creature came to reside here.  I am not familiar with this type of being, and I’ve seen many types in my long time here in Enroth.  I do not know why it chose this place as its home, or why there is only one, but I would like to see it destroyed for the trouble it has caused me. "
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:388
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2079
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As patient as I am, I would like to see the channels I use to sustain me opened again.  Please do not fail."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:389
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2080
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for your assistance.  I am grateful to you for returning my source of sustenance to me.  I need to recharge what little power I have left now that I am able to again."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:390
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2081
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you again for assisting me, but right now I'm quite busy preparing everything I need to complete the ritual."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:391
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2082
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, Sir John was murdered and the Silver Helms were bought off by the Temple of Baa?  That explains a great deal.  Good work on bringing this to me, but you’ll need to collect your reward from Anthony Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:392
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2083
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I should have known Baa was behind this, they seem to be behind everything.  Thank you for bringing this to me.  It answers the questions I had about the Fraternal Order of Silver."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:393
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2084
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So Baa was behind the corruption of the Silver Helms and the murder of Sir John Silver?  What a tragedy for Sir John, rest his soul.  <blink> Loretta told you to collect the reward from me?  Greedy witch.  Here, your services should not go unrewarded."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:394
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2085
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work!  Have you ever thought about assisting me full-time?  I could certainly use reliable help.  I've managed to collect a variety of trinkets over the years, so please help yourself to a few of these in payment for your services.  I need to clean up a few things here, but I think I'll head back to Castle Ironfist in a bit and see if there's an opening for a court magician."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:395
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2086
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks!  I can't wait to take this to Abdul's Desert Resort and see what I get!  Oh, here's the money I owe you."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:396
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2087
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My favorite wine is the stuff they give you for winning at the circus.  I'll pay 300 gold for any keg of wine from the circus that you can bring me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:397
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2088
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My favorite!  Thanks for the wine!  Here's 300 gold, it's well worth the price."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:398
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2089
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have an incredible teeth collection, but I'm always looking for more.  If you find a tooth I don't have in my collection, I'll pay you 500 gold for it."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:399
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2090
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't believe I have a tooth like this one yet, here's 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:400
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2091
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have been to the circus three times, and I can't win anything.  All I really want are the nifty four leaf clovers they use as prizes there.  I'll pay 25 gold for any four leaf clover you bring me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:401
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2092
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm so tired of the Shadow Guild, but I don't have any substantial proof of their activities.  I'd love to have something I could show to Anthony Stone proving the Shadow Guild is up to no good down here."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:402
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2093
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "One of the few remaining Paladin artifacts left is the Pearl of Purity.  Balthasar was in possession of the pearl the last I heard.  He was visiting Lord Spindler in Blackshire, but I haven't heard anything from him in months."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:403
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2094
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will only speak to the Chosen Ones; those that bring the symbol of fire."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:404
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2095
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Recently, the Fraternal Order of Silver has been disrupting my business and my caravans.  I'm not sure why Sir John feels it necessary, but I'd like this to stop.  If you could convince him to leave me alone, I'm sure I could give you a portion of the money you would be saving me."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:405
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2096
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Fraternal Order of Silver has begun more direct attacks on my legitimate, underworld associates.  I would appreciate it greatly if you could talk to Sir John and learn why he feels these actions are necessary."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:406
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2097
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hurray!  This is much easier and much less embarrasing than going to the circus and losing!  Here's 25 gold!"
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:407
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2098
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard it's possible to find large chunks of amber in a series of caves north of Castle Ironfist.  I never have the time to leave Free Haven, but I'd love to get my hands on some of that amber.  I'll pay 500 gold for any piece of amber."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:408
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2099
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This will do nicely!  Thank you for the amber, here is the 500 gold I promised you."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:409
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have almost prepared the entire ritual– all that is left is to place the statuettes."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:410
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work!  I have my youth again, thanks to you– have you ever thought about assisting me full-time?  I could certainly use reliable help.  I've managed to collect a variety of trinkets over the years, so please help yourself to a few of these in the chest outside as payment for your services.  I need to clean up a few things here, but I think I'll head back to Castle Ironfist and see if there's an opening for a court magician."
msgstr ""

