msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:25
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "As a long time member of the Merchant's Guild, and a former rug merchant myself, I know all the tricks of the trade like the back of my hand.  I can give you advice while bargaining with other Merchants to improve the prices you get.  My fee is but 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:26
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Who will warn you of danger if not me?  You're making a big mistake, boss!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:27
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Four point bonus to Alchemy skill for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:27
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "In my studies I've gathered quite a knowledge of reagents and catalysts.  I'm sure I could assist you in creating and mixing potions, if you'll only hire me.  400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:27
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Well!  After all I've done for you you're going to fire me?!  Just like that?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Eight point bonus to Alchemy skill for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I have dedicated my life to the study and mastery of alchemy.  I can increase the potency of the potions you mix.  I only charge 600 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:29
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:30
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You'll be sorry the next time a trap goes off because I wasn't around to save you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:31
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:32
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Sure has been fun following you around!  See ya!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:35
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:36
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're going to lose a lot of money without me, mark my words!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:37
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Prepare Meal"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:37
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Back to stale bread and water, eh?  <grumble> fine by me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Prepare Feast"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I have studied in the finest cooking schools in Erathia, and I am willing to prepare your meals for a paltry 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:39
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Well, I guess I can understand.  <sniff> you don't need me anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:40
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I thought we had a deal!  You're just going to cast me aside like trash! How could you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases protection from air, earth, fire, water, body, and mind by 20 constantly.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Dangerous Sorcerers abound throughout the land of Erathia.  Most use spells that do some sort of elemental damage, like fire or lightning.  Others use body or mind magic to assault their foes.  I know a spell that will help protect you from these, and I can keep it going all the time.  I'll cast it for you if you take me along.  All I want is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Not afraid of hostile magic anymore eh?  Ok, your choice.  Don't say I didn't warn you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:42
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Even if you can cast Wizard eye on your own, keeping me around would save you the spell energy.  Did you think of that?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Wind Walk"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power of flight over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Cross Water"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power to walk on water over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Gate to Town"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "There are spells that duplicate some of the natural magical features of Erathia.  One of those, Town Portal, I've learned to cast at master level.  I'll  cast it for you up to once per day if you hire me.  My price is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power to travel instantly for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Bless Party"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I checked with the gods, and they said they would be angry with you if you dismissed me.  Just thought I would let you know…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Play Tune"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You'll miss my inspiring battle tunes!  It makes a big difference during battle!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:48
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You don't find me useful?  Well, just remember that I save you time, and time is money!    "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:49
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Arrr.  Ye be firing this poor old sailor unjustly ye be.  Won't ye reconsider?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:51
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I predict you'll regret dismissing me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:52
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I cook your food and save you money, and this is the thanks I get?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:53
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Your party is considered to have the most beneficial arrangement of races in any social situation while %01 is in your party.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:53
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Wait!  Let's talk about this!  I know you don't really want to dismiss me.  We can work it out!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Disarm Traps and Stealing skills are increased by eight points for each character and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 costs you nothing!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Need traps disarmed?  Perhaps something retrieved without the owner's knowledge or consent?  I've been doing it ever since I was released from jail three years ago.  If you need help, I'll come with you for free!  I need the practice.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "What?  I didn't do nothin!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Hour of Power"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts Hour of Power once per day for a duration of six hours.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Few people outside of the Wizard's realm possess the knowledge to cast Hour of Power.  I can cast it once per day for your party if you'll hire me.  I only charge 2500 gold initially, and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up all the spells I cast on you for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Two point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can assist your spell casting by slightly boosting your spells of the Self for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "By firing me, you're not just losing a friend and spiritual advisor, but your link to the Gods!  I know you don't really mean it.  You won't dismiss me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Initiate"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Three point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "My prayers can magnify your Self spell skills for 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Four point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can greatly increase the effect of your Self spells for a small initial donation of of 2000 gold and then %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Monk"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the unarmed and dodging skills by two for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can help train your minds and bodies to perfect your unarmored, unarmed combat techniques.  I only require 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You, uh, haven't snatched the pebble from my hand yet, grasshopper.  Will you cut short your training so casually?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the identify item and identify monster skills by six for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I have considerable knowledge of the items and creatures of Erathia.  I'd be willing to help you out in your travels for 750 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You will miss my excellent advice and knowledge the minute I am gone, mark my words!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Hunter"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the identify monster skill by four for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I've hunted most every type of creature in Erathia, and I know a little something about all of them.  Though I'm retired from hunting, I'll share my knowledge with you for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Well, this old hunter knows not to beg.  Go on and dismiss me if you want."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:940
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Emerald Island is southeast of Erathia, and far away from pirates and other ruffians.  It would be ideal, if not for the constant swarms of dragonflies that infest the island.  Fortunately, the large number of armed and skilled people this contest has attracted should thin their numbers a bit.\n"
"\n"
"Lord Markham has supplemented the normally sparse village with a weapon, armor, and alchemist shop for your convenience during the contest.  A temple and basic magical guilds are also available.  I would suggest making sure that you are completely ready before you start off on the contest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:941
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to Emerald Island!  I'll be your docent for your stay on the island.  It is my duty to see that you understand the rules of both the island and the contest.  For the duration of your stay on Emerald Island please refrain from gross violations of civilized behavior."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:942
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I respect your decision.  I am, however, a patient man, and will offer you this chance until a winner in the contest is proclaimed."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:943
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The rules of the contest are simple:  The first person to return with the items is the winner.  All you need to do is collect a wealthy hat, a red potion, a longbow, a seashell, a musical instrument, and a floor tile from the Temple of the Moon and bring them to the judge to win."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:944
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Isn't this hunt exciting?  I really am grateful you came to my little event, and I hope you have fun, even if you don't win.  I think it's great that everyone is competing in a spirit of good sportsmanship and camaraderie."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:945
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you win, you'll be in charge of one of the most scenic areas in all Erathia!  Harmondale is just outside of the Tularean Forest, right on the edge of the Elf-Human border.  And I'm sure you'll love the castle.  It's a bit of a fixer-upper, but it's quite roomy and has excellent ventilation.  It breaks my heart to part with this property, but I feel that the time has come for me to give something back to the people."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:946
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!  You are the new Lords of Harmondale!  Isn't it thrilling?  You can't imagine how good it feels for me to give this property away to you!  All of the benefits and rewards, and of course, the responsibilities of governing the town of Harmondale are now yours.  (Lord Markham produces a deed and contract) Just sign here...And here... And if I could just get your initials here... Yes!  Well, that's that!  You're all set.  And once again, congratulations!!!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:947
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, the ship that will take you to your fiefdom awaits you in the harbor.  My entourage and I will be taking a different ship out.  Just board whenever you're ready."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:948
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Allow me to introduce myself.  My name is Mr. Malwick.  I represent a group of, shall we say, \"investors in the future\".  I have been observing you since you arrived on this island, and I believe your values and goals have much in common with ours.  I am empowered to grant you a fireball wand to help you win the Hunt today, in exchange for a favor in the future.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:949
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We have reason to believe that whoever is in charge of Harmondale in the next few months will have an unprecedented opportunity to shape the future.  That is why I am here today--to make sure the shape of the future is pleasing to my associates.  I'm sure you understand."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:950
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent.  Sometime in the future, I or a representative of my group will call on you to return the favor.  I hope you won't disappoint us.  Here is your fireball wand.  We should not be seen talking again, the others might get suspicious."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:951
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I love being out on this side of the island, the view of the ocean is much better than from town, don't you agree?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:952
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have some nice sea shells for sale, shells that you can only find on Emerald Island.  Can I sell one to you?  They're only a hundred gold pieces each."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:15
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:953
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here you go, I hope it reminds you of your trip to Emerald Island."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:954
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I really can't go any less than 100 gold; I need to make a living, too."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:955
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see you have a fine hat, there.  How about a deal:  You give me your hat, and we let you keep your lives?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:18
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:956
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the hat, friend!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:957
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You should have accepted my offer…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:958
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This Temple is a pretty nasty place.  You should probably watch your back around here-- you never know what might want to kill you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:959
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You should have listened to me; I warned you this was a nasty place.  Now get out of here before I decide to take something else from you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:960
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I take this to mean you don't wish to accept my proposal.  I believe our business is concluded."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:961
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The toughest band of contestants have apparently hid out in the Temple of the Moon.  I think they might be wanting to ambush any group that tries to go there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:962
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know how to make a blue potion, but not red ones…Just about any blue herb will do.  Just mix it with an empty bottle and voila!  Instant blue potion.  I guess that making a red potion is similar, but I'm not sure.  They say mixing potions improperly can have really bad effects."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:963
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sorry mates, this vessel's moored until a winner has been declared in the contest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:964
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good afternoon.  My duty is to verify that you have all the items necessary to win the contest.  You are required to bring a red potion, a longbow, a floor tile from the Temple of the Moon, a wealthy hat, seashell, and an instrument to me.  You can bring them in any order, just show them to me one at a time so that I may verify them."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:27
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:965
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see you have found a wealthy hat.  I shall mark this off your list accordingly, good work."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:966
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm, a fine lute this is.  Let me mark off the instrument from your list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:967
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Adventurers indeed!  I didn't expect anyone to bring back a tile so quickly.  This is certainly a tile from the Temple, however so I shall mark the tile off your list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:968
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This longbow certainly qualifies for the hunt.  Good work, I shall mark that off your list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:969
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A beautiful shell, much like the ones that Sally sells.  This certainly came from Emerald Island- I shall mark the shell off your list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:970
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What took you so long?  Almost every group has turned in a red potion by now.  This is the easiest item in the hunt to manage, but better late than never.  I will mark it off your list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:33
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:971
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, that's all six items.  You're the winner of the contest!  I suggest you talk to Lord Markham for the details on gaining your fiefdom, my work is done here."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:972
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm sorry, but nothing you have is necessary for the hunt.  I don't mean to belittle what you have, but I'm not looking for any of it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:973
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you contestants in Lord Markham's Scavenger Hunt?  How neat!  I'm here to provide entertainment to Lord Markham's entourage, the contestants, and to anyone else that would like to hear a song."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:974
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I own a few instruments, but I only brought my lute with me.  Its old and not quite as well kept as some of the others, but I didn't want one of my good instruments stolen by pirates or damaged from exposure to the humid, salty air."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:975
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You say you need an instrument for the Scavenger Hunt?  I suppose you could buy my lute, but I've had it for such a long time.  I guess I'd part with it for 500 gold.  Interested?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:976
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, promise to at least take care of it and not use it for firewood.  I suppose I'll have to make do without an instrument for the rest of this trip.  Maybe I should tell stories instead of sing until I get back home."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:977
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It would help if you had the 500 gold pieces.  Please don't try and cheat me out of my instrument."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:978
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello there!  I suppose you're part of the contest?  Good to hear.  We were wondering if you would want to trade a red potion, assuming you have one, for a hat.  We could help each other along a little."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:979
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wonderful!  Here's the hat and I'll take the potion.  Thanks so much, now we're almost finished with our list."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:980
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What's the matter?  You don't like to work with others?  Fine then, you'll get no help from us."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:981
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Is this some sort of trick?  You don't even have a red potion.  You don't think I'll just give you the hat, do you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:982
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good job, mates!  We'll be heading off for Harmondale right now.  Congratulations."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:983
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Keep in mind I have a 1000 gold reward for the group to bring back information on the contestants that have disappeared."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:984
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No news on the missing people yet?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:985
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There really is a dragon on the island?  I thought everyone was referring to the dragonflies everywhere.  I'll warn everyone to stay away from that cave so we don't lose anyone else."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:986
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm… I recall a few strangers poking around the entrance to the Dragon's Cave recently.  I didn't notice if they went inside, but I haven't seen them around since.  They must have realized how dangerous that place is and headed back to town."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:987
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The cave right behind my house is not the Abandoned Temple.  It belongs to Morcarack the Pitiless, the Dragon of Emerald Island.  He doesn't appreciate visitors, so I wouldn't advise going there.  The Abandoned Temple is buried in the hill south of my house.  You can get to it by entering the caves at the top of the hill."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:988
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wild Dragonflies have infested the northwestern side of Emerald Island recently, making it dangerous to store things in our shed out there.  Dragonflies aren't terribly powerful, but they are fast and can even occasionally shoot fire at you.  Don't take them too lightly!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:989
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dragon of Emerald Island lives in a cave in the northeast.  I wouldn't go there, though, he doesn't like visitors.  He spares our town so that we may pay him tribute, and in return he keeps pirates and undesirables out."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:990
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You're contestants in the Scavenger Hunt?  If so, I wouldn't wander off to the Dragon Cave, then.  Morcarack doesn't tolerate strangers very well.  I bet the missing people went there thinking his cave was the Abandoned Temple--they're probably long dead."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:991
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'd watch those other contestants-- some of them seem ruthless.  One particularly nasty group headed to the north side of the island, and I haven't seen them since.  I'm surprised at the attention this contest has received, apparently people are hoping to get on the good side of the contestants for future favors if they win."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have decided that you no longer desire my information about the places on Emerald Island.  If you later decide that you'd like to hear what I have to say, then select Tour On."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:993
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have decided to listen to my tour about the points of interest on Emerald Island.  If you decide that you no longer want me to point out areas of interest then select Tour Off."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:994
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though the law may decide who is guilty and who is not, I decide who is called Thief, and who is just a criminal.  Bring me that lovely vase I saw on the mantle in Lord Markham’s manor, and I shall call you Rogue."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:57
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:995
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Common criminals steal whatever catches their eye; Rogues steal what I tell them to steal.  I shall not grant titles to failures.  Return with Lord Markham’s Vase and I will promote all Thieves to Rogues, and all non-thieves to Honorary Rogues."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:58
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:996
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well done.  Stealing that vase took guts and skill.  I grant you the title of Rogue, and a small payment for your services. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:59
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:997
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have chosen the path of Darkness, and I will promote you no further.  Perhaps an Assassin would have something to teach you.  I hear there is one in Deyja."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:60
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:998
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are not quite ready to take the next step.  The time is fast approaching when you must decide whether to follow the path of light, or the path of darkness.  If you choose the Light, return to me to complete your training."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:61
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:999
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your next task is somewhat more difficult…more suited for Spies than Rogues.  I have been asked to ensure that Watchtower 6, the only tower to survive the recent wars against the Necromancers, be unable to defend itself the next time it is attacked.  Killing the guards inside won’t help—the Necromancers will just fill it again with more troops.  The tower is on the southern edge of the Necromancers’ land.  I want you to slip inside and move the counterweight in the gatehouse at the top of the tower to the gatehouse at the bottom of the tower.  It is a heavy weight that can be found in a slot against the wall with a rope tied to it.  When the time comes for an attack, the misplaced weights will be noticed too late, and the gate will not close.  If you can do this, you will have proven your status as a Spy."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:62
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1000
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Um…The weight needs to go in the box in the lower gatehouse—not here.  Go back to Watchtower 6 and put the weight in the right box!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:63
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1001
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm.  Removing the weight from the upper gatehouse was a start, but where is it now?!?  The plan won’t work unless you put the weight in the lower gatehouse!  Go back to Watchtower 6 and put the weight in the right box!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:64
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1002
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You haven’t done the job yet!  Remember, you must go to Watchtower 6 and move the weight from the box in the upper gatehouse to the lower gatehouse.  I will not promote you until that is done. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1003
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work!  Some day, your sabotage of that watchtower will save hundreds of lives.  For your services, I hereby promote the Rogues among you to the status of Spy, and the Honorary Rogues to Honorary Spies! Oh, and here’s some gold as payment. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:66
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1004
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, Johann be wanting the Faerie Pipes, eh?  I can't say I'm surprised--he wouldn't come here himself, the coward.  The Pipes will cost you, though… all your food.  Of course, I've got some delightful food down below, should thee be wanting to restock your packs."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:67
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1005
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Refreshing! (+50 Endurance temporary)"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1006
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So…you wish to become an Assassin.  Very well.  I can provide the Rogues among you the training necessary, but you must prove both your skill and your loyalty before I will invest time in you.  My superiors inform me that a certain Lady Eleanor Carmine’s life must end.  She used to work for us, but has taken up residence in the Celestial Court with our enemies, and is providing them with information damaging to our cause.  Silence her, and return with a trinket of hers to prove the job is done."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1007
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have chosen the path of Light, and therefore can never become an effective Assassin.  I cannot train you.  Perhaps you should continue a softer hearted training with the Spy."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:70
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1008
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can turn a simple Rogue into a fearsome killer, but only if he has the right kind of temperament for the job.  The time is coming when you must choose to walk in the light, or in the dark.  If you prefer the shadow, come to me and I will complete your training."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1009
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you were looking for someone to train you in advanced stealth techniques, I  would be your man.  But you still need someone to teach you basic techniques.  Return to me when you achieve Rogue or Honorary Rogue status.  Then, perhaps, I can further your education.  Seek the Master Thief in the sewers of Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:72
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1010
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Without proof, I cannot assume Lady Carmine is dead.  Bring me proof, and I will honor you with the title of Assassin."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:73
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1011
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, the job is done. [He examines the dagger slowly, then sighs.] She was very dear to me, but emotion is the enemy of reason.  I could not have done the job myself.  Thank you.  Truly now, you are Assassins.  The rogues among you, I will give special training to.  Here is a small payment to help cover the expenses you incurred on the job. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1012
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You don't have the tapestry yet, and the clock is ticking.  It would be prudent to keep to the task at hand rather than bothering me with your babble."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:75
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1013
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ha! So, thee wishes to take the test to be a crusader?  I cannot blame thee—the sense of pride one feels when one has accomplished a heroic deed is sublime!  The test is simple.  A dragon must be slain.  I know just the one—Wromthrax the Heartless!  He lives in a cave in Tatalia, and terrorizes the peasants who live near him when he’s home.  He should be in the cave this time of year.  Because this is probably thine first dragon, I will travel with thee to give thee pointers.  So, let us go forthwith, and spill this monster’s black blood!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1014
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hurrah!  The Dragon has fallen!  Truly thou art grand Crusaders in good standing, with a fine deed behind thee.  I would stay and sing songs of thy bravery with thee, but duty calls.  Surely we will meet again, Crusaders!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1015
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We must finish our quest before I can name thee Crusaders, friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1016
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am pleased to see thee chose the path of Light, Crusaders!  A wrong has been committed, friends, and who else but us can put it right?  A wicked villain has kidnapped a fair maiden by the name of Alice Hargreaves.  His name is William Setag, and he has imprisoned her in his tower.  You must ride forthwith to put this villain to the sword and rescue sweet Alice!  If you succeed, you will truly be Heroes of the Land!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:79
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1017
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will not have truck with thee further, scoundrel!  I see now thee hath chosen the path of Darkness.  Mayhaps thee should seek a villain like thyself for training."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1018
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, fellow Crusaders!  I know thee thirsts for another task with which to hone thy Crusading skills, but first thee must pass a far more serious test.  Thee must agree to follow the Path of Light before I can help thee further.  You will know when you have made this choice.  Return to me then."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:81
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1019
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thee’ve done it! I knew thee could do it!  I’m so proud of thee!  Alice has been freed of the clutches of the wicked William Setag, evil has been vanquished, and good upheld.  Where once there was wrong, now there is right! [Charles sighs and smiles broadly] Well.  My work here is done!  Thee have passed the tests and deserve thy reward.  Therefore do I solemnly declare thee Heroes! "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1020
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though thy deeds remain impressive indeed, crusaders, I cannot declare thee Heroes until you have rescued the girl!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:83
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1021
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tsk tsk.  You haven't finished your training as a Crusader; I cannot instruct you until you show proper dedication."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1022
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It should be impossible for you to see this right now.  If you are reading this, tell Bryan that the event and/or logic of this quest is messed up because you should either be good attempting the Hero quest, or evil attempting the Villain quest and you are apparently neither."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:85
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1023
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Help!  William has captured me and imprisoned me in this tower.  Please get me out of here as quickly as possible, I don't want to die."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1024
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you so much for helping me away from William's clutches."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:87
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1025
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excuse me, but who might you be?  Hey!  Get your hands off of me!  Help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:88
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1026
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where do you think you're taking me?  I have a rich family-- you'll be in a lot of trouble if you don't let me go!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:89
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1027
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Let's get down to business, shall we?  I know you are well aware of my standing as the blackest Villain in Erathia.  It requires effort and drive to prove to be this evil-- I hope you have the mettle for it.  I would love nothing more than to keep you in my training for years and teach you the finest parts of being a Villain.  Unfortunately, I am under pressure to speed up your tutelage.  To this end, I have a direct way to learn the arts of Villainhood.  There is a woman, Alice Hargreaves, who is of noble blood and pure character.  Capture this woman from her residence in Castle Gryphonheart. Return here and imprison her in my tower.  Complete this, and I shall promote all Crusaders in your group to Villains, and the rest of your group to Honorary Villains."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1028
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'd certainly love nothing more than to corrupt your obviously pious soul, but I'm afraid you wouldn't have the stomach to follow through with my teachings.  You have chosen the Path of Light, you will garner no assistance from me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1029
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Before you make this decision, you have a more pressing, immediate decision you will be forced to make.  If you choose the darker road, you may return to me and complete your training in the Paladins' arts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1030
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Capital!  You have shown dedication, daring, and the power of raw force.  Certainly the imprisonment of such a fair and noble creature in this wicked place earns you the right to be called a Villain-- or Honorary Villain.  Go now upon the world and make all fear your name."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1031
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where's Alice?  I'm not asking for much, just a simple kidnapping.  Is it really that difficult?  I suggest you speed up your efforts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:94
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1032
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, it is normal for novice Monks to ask for the path of enlightenment.  I shall tell you of the path, though the journey is yours to make.  In the Barrow Downs is a series of tombs-- one of which was constructed on a site of great natural power.  You will know the right barrow because it is different from the rest.  Reach this barrow and meditate by the water, and your promotion to Initiate will be complete."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1033
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Bartholomew Hume contacts you mentally] Congratulations, young ones.  My final lesson given to you as Monks is this:  enlightenment is gained by the journey, not the destination.  In this case, the destination was critical to prove that you were capable of the journey.  I shall now promote all Monks to Initiates and everyone else to Honorary Initiates-- congratulations."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:96
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1034
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not finished your journey.  Return to me only when you have completed your task."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1035
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see you wish to continue your journey.  Excellent!  Have no fear, for you are prepared for your next step.  You must extinguish the remnants of an evil order- the Order of Baa.  Defeat their High Priest and return to me and I shall complete your training and promote you to Master."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:98
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1036
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am sorry, but I am permitted to train you no longer.  You will need to find a new Master to learn from."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:99
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1037
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A fork approaches in your path.  I will only train you after you've chosen to walk the lighter path."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1038
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I cannot improve upon training you do not already have.  You must be promoted to Crusader before I can train you in the ways of villainy."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:103
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1041
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Air is the element the sorcerers join the profession to learn!  We have all the best spells--including the glorious Fly spell.  Don't miss out on this fantastic opportunity to join the Air guild!  Just 50 gold!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:104
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1042
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Membership in the Guild of Earth will give you access to our excellent library of earth spells.  This membership is good for all Earth Guilds on the continent of Erathia.  The cost to join is but 50 gold pieces."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:105
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1043
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why be subtle when you can learn Fire magic?  Joining our guild costs but 50 gold for a lifetime membership."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:106
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1044
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Membership in the Guild of Water gives you the right to buy our spells of change and movement.  It's my job to recruit new members and collect membership dues from them.  The price is 50 gold, and that includes membership in all of our guild halls."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:107
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1045
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the guild recruiter for the Guild of Body.  A lot of people think that our spells just heal the body, but some can damage the bodies of your opponents too.  The cost is 50 gold pieces."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:108
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1046
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "50 gold pieces buys you membership in the Guild of the Mind.  Why fight a monster yourself when you can get its friends to fight it for you?  Kills two birds with one stone, if you ask me.  Well, what do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:109
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1047
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many believe the most powerful magic to be Light magic, or Dark magic, or something destructive, like Fire.  We at the Spirit guild would like to point out that no magic besides Light magic can raise the dead, and even then it takes a Grandmaster in the element.  If you want power over life and death, choose Spirit magic.  The cost to join is but 50 gold pieces."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:110
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1048
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Light magic represents the most powerful magic a person can wield without cost to his soul.  We feel confident our price of 1000 gold pieces for guild membership is fair.  You won't regret your decision to pursue Light magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:111
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1049
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "At last you have an opportunity to learn Dark magic by joining the Guild of the Dark.  Don't squander it!  Dark magic is the strongest magic.  The cost is only 1000 gold pieces.  You know it's worth it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:127
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:127
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:127
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1065
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must first be an expert in this skill before you can become a master!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:128
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:128
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:128
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1066
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must first be a master in this skill before you can become a grandmaster!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:132
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:132
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:132
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1070
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are already a grandmaster in this skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:135
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1073
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work.  No longer shall the Order of Baa stain the lands of Erathia.  Now, allow me to promote all Initiates to Masters, and all Honorary Initiates to Honorary Masters.  Keep in mind that this is but a stop along the path of enlightenment.  Your journey only ends with your eventual death-- never close your mind."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:136
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1074
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Temple of Baa still stands, their High Priest still lives.  Until this is completed, you are not ready for the title of Master.  Go now and do not fail."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:137
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1075
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An agent of mine has sent me a message I need deciphered.  The cipher relies on knowing which word of which a certain book to match it against.  If you wish to become a Ninja, this is what you must do: Infiltrate the School of Wizardry and find out what the third word of the famed Scroll of Waves is.  Use it to decipher the message, then do what the message tells you to do.  It is the key to enter the Tomb of the Master.  You'll find the tomb in Southern Erathia.  [Stephan hands you a scrap of paper] Here is the encoded message."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:138
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1076
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ambition is good, but I only train experienced students.  Come back when you've achieved Initiate status, and perhaps I'll teach you…IF you have the right outlook.  If you're looking for someone who is willing to help you become an Initiate, perhaps you should start with that wimp Bartholomew Hume.  I'm sure he'd be willing to give you an elementary education."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:139
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1077
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Stephan Sand sneers] YOU want ME to teach you something?  You sniveling do-gooders make my knife arm twitch!  Get out of my sight before I REALLY teach you about fighting!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:140
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1078
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though you have achieved initiate status, I am uncertain that you can stomach some of my more extreme teachings.  Return to me when you have formally rejected all philosophies that turn people into weaklings and cowards."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:141
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1079
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you have the key, but you haven't followed the directions in the message.  Remember, the tomb is in Southern Erathia.  Complete your task, and return to me to report success.  If you can't complete your mission, don't bother returning to me.  Failure is pathetic."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:142
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1080
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Sand sighs] Once again, the cipher key is the third word of the first paragraph of the Scroll of Waves.  You can find it somewhere in the School of Wizardry.  I don't care how you get in there--kill anyone who gets in your way, or sneak in.  Whatever you want.  The only thing that matters is success.  Everything else is an excuse for personal weakness."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:143
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1081
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well done.  No one can argue with success except apologists for the weak and the cowardly.  I hereby promote all Initiates to Ninjas, and all non-Initiates to Honorary Ninjas.  Oh yeah, go ahead and keep that little trinket you stole from the tomb.  This was just a training exercise, after all."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:144
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1082
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A few generations ago, an enchanted bow was created by alchemists in the Tularean Forest to seal another peace treaty between the elves and the humans.  While en route to Erathia, the bow was taken from the couriers by the Titans in Avlee.  They have no use for the thing, so it's probably in their stronghold still.  Strike a blow for our profession, and get that bow back.  It is absolutely the finest thing of its kind ever made.  Oh, and while you're there, feel free to cut some of those bullies down to size--They stole it out of cruelty, not need!  If you are successful, I will promote all Warrior Mages to Master Archers, or honorary Master Archers, as the case may be."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:145
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1083
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, you've achieved the rank of Warrior Mage, and wish to advance to Master Archer!  A worthy goal, but I only promote those who's heart and courage match their skill.  Come back to me when you have firmly committed to the Light.  Then I will help you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:146
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1084
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have chosen the path of Darkness.  I will never help you improve, for fear you will use your skills to advance your selfish goals!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:147
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1085
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the person to see if you want to become Master Archers, but you have come too soon!  You must have the proper background to become a Master, and that means first becoming a warrior mage.  Return when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:148
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1086
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You found the bow!  Let me take some measurements and adjust it to your specific style of archery. Once I have finished you should keep it, and use it in defense the of the land and the people.  I am happy to promote all Warrior Mages to Master Archers, and all Honorary Warrior Mages to Honorary Master Archers."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:149
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1087
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No luck getting the bow?  Well, take your time, and plan your assault against the Titans carefully.  Against such powerful opponents, there is no shame in striking and retreating.  Do what you must to defeat these monsters."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:150
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1088
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Wheeze] So you think you can become Warrior Mages, do you?  It isn't easy.  You must be equally proficient in magical skills and physical skills.  There is a test of this.  Visit the Red Dwarf Mines.  Inside you will find two kinds of beasts--one that can be harmed only with magic, and one that can be harmed only with steel.  In the back of the lower section of the mines you will find a machine created by the Dwarves that powers the lift-- the only access between the upper and lower sections of the mines.  To keep the creatures trapped in the lower section, you will have to replace the belt in the machine with this one, a worn belt that will only last about an hour before breaking.  This should give you enough time to get to the lift and get out before you are trapped down there.  Seal away these creatures and return to me-- only then will I call you Warrior Mages."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:151
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1089
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Very Good.  You have passed the test.  Now the creatures are sealed away and won't be able to prey on the dwarves any longer, and you have proven your ability in both sorcery and steel.  I am proud to declare all Archers amongst you Warrior Mages, and everyone else Honorary Warrior Mages.  Congratulations!  Now get out.  I already weary of your company."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:152
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1090
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You haven't sabotaged the machine yet.  You must finish this before I'll promote you to Warrior Mage."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:153
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1091
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Getting ambitious, are we?  Think you can earn the title of sniper?  Perhaps you can.  Here is what you must do:  In the stronghold of the Titans is a very special bow that was meant as a peace offering from the elves to the humans to quell a conflict long since forgotten.  [Master Snick shakes his head] Gads! This peace stuff makes me nauseous!  In any case, fetch the bow for the good of our profession, and I'll promote you to Sniper.  [Heh] you better act like snipers if you expect to defeat the Titans.  A toe to toe...or should I say head to knee fight won't go well for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:154
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1092
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Want to be a Sniper, eh? Maybe.  But I doubt you have the heart for it.  It needs to shrivel like a raisin and get hard as a stone to be able to do what you must.  Prove to me you are following the Path of Darkness, and then I will teach you further."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:155
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1093
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Following the Path of Light, are we?  How can you be a Sniper if you cry everytime you shoot someone in the back?  Maybe you should ask that lily-livered Lawrence Mark to help you.  I know that I will not."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:156
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1094
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have the bow?!  Excellent!  It's been centuries since someone was brave enough to take on the Titans and try to get that bow back!  Let me take some measurements and adjust it to your specific style of archery.  I am proud to be the one to first call all Warrior Mages amongst you Snipers, and to say that all Honorary Warrior Mages are Honorary Snipers!  I must admit I didn't think you had it in you to succeed.  I am happy that I was wrong."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:157
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1095
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "More failure? [Master Snick yawns]  How surprising.  I'll make it simple--no bow, no title."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:158
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1096
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you want to be champions, do you?  Ha!  How can you be a champion if you don't win any tournaments?  You know, I can't really promote you to Champion status--you have to do it yourself, just like everything else.  Go and win five championship tournaments in the Arena at Knight level, and come back to me.  I'll call you Champions then, if you want."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:159
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1097
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can see you very much want to be called Champions, but I'm not so sure I should help you.  Prove to me that you follow the Path of Light, and then we'll talk about promotion."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:160
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1098
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Call you Champions?  Never!  The only reason I'm not hacking you evil doers to bits is that you came here peacefully.  Leave now, before I change my mind and rid the world of another problem."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:161
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1099
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the person to talk to if you want to be called Champions.  First, though, you must practice.  Return to me when you've become Cavaliers.  Then, if you have the right outlook, I will tell you what you must do to become Champions."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:162
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations for you recent tourney victories, my friends!  I gladly name the Cavaliers among you Champions, and the Honorary Cavaliers I name Honorary Champions!  Always fight for the Light, Champions!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:163
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not yet won 5 championship tournaments in the Arena.  Return to me when you have won five, and I will promote you.  Remember, these battles MUST be at the Knight difficulty level."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:164
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The hallmark of the Cavalier is courage.  I can promote you to Cavalier status, but before I'll do that, you'll have to prove to me your bravery in battle.  Since most people are yellow bellied cowards at heart, I doubt you'll succeed.  But if you want to try, here is what you must do: Destroy all the undead in the haunted mansion in the Barrow Downs."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:165
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1103
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you're back!  And from the look on your faces I see you have finished the job.  Well done!  I hereby officially promote all Knights amongst you to Cavaliers, and everyone else to honorary Cavaliers.  Carry your title with pride!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:166
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1104
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Did one little haunted house send you packing in fear?  I've seen chocolate eclairs with more backbone than you!  Get you gone, and don't come back 'til you've stiffened your spine!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:167
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1105
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you think you can become Black Knights, do you?  Very well.  You know, I've heard many people say that criminals are cowards.  That just isn't true.  It takes a lot of courage to risk your life in a robbery, or in battle.  You've already proven you are courageous, and now it's time to put that courage and your skills to use.  I want you to rob the Elvish Treasury.  It's one of the biggest hoards of treasure in the land, and it is very well guarded.  Do the deed and abscond with the wealth.  Return to me when you've finished.  Then I will promote you to Black Knights."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:168
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1106
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's true that I am the one you go to when you're looking to be promoted to Black Knight status.  But how can you become a Black Knight when you haven't even decided whether or not you're evil?  Return to me when you have fully committed to Darkness.  Only then will I resume your training."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:169
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1107
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bah!  You do-gooders are worthless!  It is impossible for me to teach anything more to you!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:170
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1108
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All RIGHT!  That robbery was brilliant!  I am very proud of you.  Keep the loot--it's your reward for a job well done.  I can safely say the Cavaliers among you have become Black Knights today, and I'll throw in an Honorary Black Knight title for the rest of you.  You've done well, my students!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:171
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1109
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Robbery not complete?  No.  Don't come to me and report failure.  Don't come and tell me you lost your nerve.  Get out there and rob that treasury!  Failure is not an option!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:172
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1110
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, it looks like you might be able to do the job I have in mind.  The fundamental task a Ranger Lord faces is caring for the land.  Recently, poachers removed a magical gemstone called the \"heart of the forest\" from the Tularean Forest.  The forest has become restless, and attacks travelers who come too close.  The forest blames all 'Walkers' for the theft, and won't calm down until the stone is returned.  Find the stone and return it to the oldest tree in the Forest.  Come back to me when you've done this."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:173
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1111
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would like to be your teacher--I really would, but I'm not sure you're cut out to be a Ranger Lord.  Soon you must make a decision of the heart.  If you choose the Path of Light, return to me.  I would be honored to be your teacher."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:174
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Lysander shakes his head, smiling gently] Too soon, eager ones.  I train only the most advanced students.  Seek me out again when you reach Hunter status."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:175
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1113
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Lysander frowns] You've chosen the path of darkness.  I refuse to teach such as you--you would only use my lessons to further your selfish goals.  May Heaven have mercy on your souls."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you can't figure out where to start, you should try finding the oldest tree in the forest.  It should be somewhere outside of Pierpont in Avlee.  The oldest tree has the power of speech, and may know something helpful.  It will be happy to tell you whatever you want to hear, plus a whole lot more.  You'll see."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:177
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1115
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, you've spoken with the tree, and now know as much as I do about the theft.  If you manage to find the stone, take it directly to the tree and then come see me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:178
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1116
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've done a good thing, returning the Heart.  The forest is quieter now, and no longer attacks travelers.  You've probably saved many lives.  For service to the Land and the Light, I hereby promote all Hunters among you to Ranger Lords, and all honorary Hunters to honorary Ranger Lords!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:179
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Think you can improve?  I have a test for you.  A hunter needs to understand the woods, and a hunter needs to be as skilled with magic as with a blade.  The best teachers for that are the faeries.  There's a faerie mound in Northern Avlee.  Figure out how to get in, and the Faeries will grant magic to the genuine rangers among you, meaning that they will be promoted to Hunter status.  The rest of you will be honorary hunters. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:180
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Foxed by the Faeries? [Ebednezer snickers, then begins to laugh uproariously at his own wit] Foxed?  Faeries?  Hahahah!  Get it?  Foxed… you know…ah ahahah.  Maybe not.  Well, I've already told you how to become Hunters.  Get inside the Faerie Mound in Avlee.  Now, stop bothering me!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:181
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1119
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Better a bounty hunter than a plain old hunter, huh?  Well, this test is even simpler than the Faerie Mound idea, and you won't have to think so hard.  Ever notice how the town halls are always looking for someone to kill a monster for them?  All you have to do is collect 10,000 in bounties from town halls.  When you've done that, come back to me, and I'll promote you to Bounty Hunters.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:182
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1120
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'll be blunt.  I don't think I like you.  You'll have to prove to me you're worth something.  Soon, you will have to choose if you'll follow the Path of Dark or the Path of Light.  If you choose Light, don't even bother speaking to me again.  Got it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:183
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1121
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gahhh!  I can smell the stink of self righteousness on you!  Get away from me!  G'won, get!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:184
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1122
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, how did if feel?  All that killing?  Mmmmm.  Heh.  You qualify, my friends.  You definitely qualify.  All Hunters amongst you are now Bounty Hunters, and all Honorary hunters and Honorary Bounty Hunters!  Good job."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:185
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1123
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not yet, not good enough!  You need to collect more bounties, and more importantly, kill more creatures.  There's some good clean fun in that.  Killing, don't you know."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:186
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1124
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Come to my door looking for magic?  Thee've always had it, if thee knew where to look.  Some I tell this to, and they still can't see it, though it be plain as the nose on their face.  Those amongst thee that are simple Rangers are now Hunters, and those who aren't are but Honorary Hunters.  Clever the ones who can knock on my door!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:187
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1125
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The thieves reached deep inside me to take my Heart.  The grapevines say they are hiding in the Mercenary Guild in Tatalia.  We would squeeze them, but they aren't close enough to reach.  Walkers are needed to catch walkers.  Catch the thieves for us.  Ok?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:188
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1126
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ahhh!  [The tree sighs happily]  You have the heart!  The forest sings with joy!  Tonight we will recite the song of the ancestors.  Will you stay and recite with us?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:189
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1127
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, the forest is still very angry.  The grapevines say the thieves have not left their hiding place.  You will catch the thieves for us, won't you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:190
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1128
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Priests.  You have come to me seeking that I be your guide on the Path of Light.  But be warned, to learn its ways, you must learn the ways of your own soul.  I would suggest that we meditate on this for awhile, but you look like you're in a hurry.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n"
"\n"
"The Church of the Sun was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Light.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Sun.  Using the map that Daedalus Falk sent you to find in order to become priests, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Sun by purifying the altar in the Church of the Moon.  This will so weaken the Moon cult that the Church of the Sun will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:191
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1129
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you wish to follow the Path of Light, first you must formally choose it.  Soon you will be asked to make the choice, and the way will be clear.  Until then, I cannot be your guide."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:192
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1130
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you wish to become Priests of the Light, you must first become Priests.  I don't have time to train priests, but my bitter rival, Daedalus Falk, does.  Do not worry, he will promote you fairly, even if you do not wish to follow the terrible path of darkness that he represents."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:193
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1131
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've come to the wrong person if you want to be promoted beyond priest.  I am well aware of your choice to follow the Path of the Dark, and I will have nothing to do with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1132
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your bravery has advanced our faith tremendously, Priests.  It's with a glad heart that I can hereby promote all Priests to Priests of the Light, and all honorary Priests to Honorary Priests of the Light.  Thank you so much for your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:195
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1133
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must visit Evenmorn island and purify the Altar of Darkness in the Church of the Moon.  Only then can I promote you to Priests of the Light."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1134
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Falk gives you a grandfatherly smile] You have, perhaps, an ambition to be priests?  I can help you, if you'll help me.  There is an island south of Bracada where stands an old temple that I need to find again.  I think the pirates west of Erathia must know where the island is.  The Erathian navy is rather feeble, and hasn't been able to root them out of their hiding places amongst the Tidewater Caverns.  Perhaps the pirates have a map.  If you can bring me that map, I would promote you to Priest status immediately."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:197
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1135
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Map!  You found it!  [Falk looks at the map, and points at the island] There it is.  The island has been shrouded in mist since the Churches of the Sun and Moon began fighting over a century ago.  Keep the map--I have the coordinates now, and will have no trouble finding the place when I need to.  I am proud to declare the Clerics amongst you to be Priests, and the rest to be honorary Priests.  Thank you so much for your good work!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1136
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If there is a map that says where that island is, the map would be in the Tidewater Caverns of western Erathia.  When you bring me that map, then I will be happy to promote you all to Priests."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:199
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1137
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Priests.  [Falk gazes coldly at you] Well it is that you have come to see the wisdom of the Path of the Dark.  Never regret your decision, and never look back.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n"
"\n"
"The Church of the Moon was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Darkness.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Moon.  Using the map that I sent you to find, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Moon by defiling the altar in the Church of the Sun.  This will so weaken the Sun cult that the Church of the Moon will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:200
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1138
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you wish to follow the Path of Darkness, first you must formally choose it.  Soon you will be asked to make the choice, and the way will be clear.  Until then, I cannot be your guide."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:201
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How dare you insult me with your presence?  You have chosen the Path of the Light, and have forever renounced me as your teacher.  Go now, and wallow in your weakness somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:202
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:202
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your bravery has advanced our faith tremendously, Priests.  It's with pleasure that I can hereby promote all Priests to Priests of the Dark, and all honorary Priests to Honorary Priests of the Dark.  Thank you so much for your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:203
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1139
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must visit Evenmorn island and defile the Altar of Light in the Church of the Sun.  Only then can I promote you to Priests of the Dark."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:204
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1140
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I am indeed the one to speak to if you wish to become Wizards.  Every student of mine must complete a project before I name them Wizards.  This year's project is to build a golem.  There are spare parts scattered about the lands from here to Avlee.  You'll need all four limbs plus the torso and the head.  Pay special attention to where you get the head--one of my students made a mistake while making a head last summer and gave the defective head away as a joke.  \n"
"\n"
"When you have all the parts, come talk to me.  I'll promote you to Wizards then, and I'll animate your Golem.  Well, on your way, and have fun!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:205
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1141
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[You proudly display your assembled golem to Master Grey, and he nods approvingly] Well done.  Head looks alright, but you can never be sure…Well, good work!  Clearly, you qualify for Wizard status.  All Sorcerers amongst you are now Wizards, and all non Sorcerers are now honorary Wizards!  [Master Grey spends awhile casting the spell that animates your golem] He's all yours!  Take him back to your castle and put him where you want.  He'll attack intruders relentlessly.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:206
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have to have all the parts together and properly assembled for me to animate it, students!  I can't animate incomplete golems."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:207
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1142
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Welcome back, students.  The golem lesson was just an exercise, but to advance to Archmage, you really have to do something for the profession.  Copies of the fabled Divine Intervention spell are very rare, and unfortunately the School doesn't have one.  There's been a history of bad luck regarding the spell.\n"
"\n"
"It has been around for time immemorial, but the spell has never found its way into our hands.  Always just out of reach, we often send guild members to find it, but every one has failed.  Sometimes they have it in their hands, but lose it on the way back, other times, the book seems to vanish, only to resurface 20 years later in some old dungeon, or on a deserted island.  Right now, we think it's in the Breeding Zone in the Pit.  Find the spell, and return with it.  Break the curse!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:208
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1143
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Archmage training is reserved only for people dedicated to the Path of Light.  Prove to me you have chosen the right way, and I will be proud to be your teacher."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:209
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1144
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've chosen Darkness, my students.  I will teach you no more."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:210
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1145
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The book!  The book!  [Master Grey clutches his ears and spins around in joy] You did it!  Oh, what a wonderful day!  I am so proud of you!  You're all Archmages!  Of course, if you weren't Wizards to begin with, it's only an honorary title, but who cares?  You found the book!  [The Master sets the book down on a table next to a blank book.  Both open simultaneously, and quill arises from the desk to begin copying the text in the new book] You may keep the copy, and you should start seeing more copies in the Light guilds of Bracada and Celeste."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:211
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1146
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I expect trouble finding the book, which is why I'm sending you to find it.  I know you can succeed in this mission.  Keep trying!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:212
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1147
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fear not death?  I can perform the Ritual on any Wizard.  You need a Soul Jar.  Years ago the Wizards stole a shipment of Jars en route from Nighon to Deyja.  The jars are very hard to destroy, so they hid them, thinking we would never be able to find them.\n"
"\n"
"Fortunately for us, dead men do indeed tell tales.  Better, in fact, than living ones--dead men never forget, never refuse to talk, and never lie.  So, we found the one who buried the Jars, and made him die.  He was very cooperative after his death, and said he hid them somewhere in the Walls of Mist for the Wizards in Celeste. \n"
"\n"
"Retrieve these jars and I will perform the Ritual on all Wizards amongst you.  The rest may become Honorary Liches, for what that's worth, in thanks for finding the extra Jars for us."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:213
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1148
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you haven't even become Wizards yet, you aren't ready to become Liches.  Trouble me not 'til you're qualified."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:214
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1149
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Only followers of the Dark Path can become Liches.  You have not yet chosen the path.  Return when you choose Darkness."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:215
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1150
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Having chosen the path of Light, you are not suited to become Liches.  The Ritual would reject you, and you would die a real death.  If that is what you want, you certainly don't need my help…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:216
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1151
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jars.  Yessss.  You have helped us greatly.  Now for the Ritual.  [The Lich draws a knife, and approaches you]  This won't hurt a bit!  [The ritual actually hurts quite a bit, and takes several hours to complete.  When it is over, the Lich speaks again]  So, now it is done.  Those among you who were Wizards are now most certainly Liches.  Those who were not, have my gratitude for returning the jars, and I will call you \"Honorary Liches\".  Remember, Liches must keep their Soul Jars with them at all times while they travel.  You cannot be separated from your Jar for long, or you will die a real death."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:217
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1152
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have no spare Jars with which to perform the Ritual.  It is impossible for me to promote you until you return with the Jars.  Remember, each one of you must have a Jar to be Promoted."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:218
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Advancement as a Druid is simple.  You must visit the three ancient temples to nature we erected centuries ago and pray at their centers.  They are in Tatalia, Evenmorn Isle, and Avlee, and look like circles of stone with an altar of water in their centers.  Where exactly I will not say, but exploring the land about them is part of the process.  When you have visited all three Circles, return to me to detail your experience."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:219
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Visit the Circles, then return to me.  That is the process.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:220
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1155
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've found a circle!  Very good, but you must find all three before you will be ready for promotion.  Remember, circles three, then return to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:221
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have only to look into your eyes to see where you've been.  You have seen the circles, and they have left their imprint upon you.  Telling you that all Druids amongst you are now Great Druids is but a formality.  Telling the rest of you that you're now honorary Druids is showing you respect for the respect you have shown me and my faith.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:222
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1157
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"To be named an Arch Druid, you must serve the land.  I know of a service you could perform.  In the land above Stone City, where the Dwarves bury their dead, is the barrow of King Zokarr IV.  He died fighting in defense of Stone City during the invasion of Erathia by Nighon.  His remains were never recovered and still lie in those tunnels.    \n"
"\n"
"Retrieve his bones and place them in his coffin in his barrow.  When you have done this, the King will rest, and so will the land.  Return to me when you've performed this service, and I will perform the Ceremony of Ascension and name you Arch Druids."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:223
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1158
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am dedicated to the service of the Light.  I will not promote you further until you are as dedicated as I.  Come back to me when you choose the Light."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:224
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Servants of Darkness, I am sorry I promoted you earlier.  I am ashamed I didn't notice the darkness in your souls until it was too late.  Leave me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:225
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1160
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"[Master Green seems beside himself with joy at your accomplishment] I felt the King's soul return to the land of the dead when you returned his bones.  The land breathed a sigh of relief--did you feel it?  \n"
"\n"
"The Ceremony of Ascension is complete.  I'm happy to promote all Great Druids amongst you to Arch Druids, and all honorary Great Druids to Honorary Arch Druids.  This is a very happy day!  Your service will be remembered!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:226
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1161
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Service is not easy, but it needs to be done.  Remember, you must bring the bones of King Zokarr IV from where they lie in the tunnels between Stone City and Nighon to Zokarr's coffin in a secret dwarven barrow.  Only then can I perform the Ceremony of Ascension and promote you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:227
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1162
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Becoming a Warlock for some is a simple process, and for others it is nearly impossible.  You need to find a familiar suited to your personality.  The familiar will help to focus your magical abilities and sharpen your concentration.  Sometimes a single familiar can be shared, other times not.  The magical effects will not be noticed by anyone but a Great Druid--someone who is already attuned to nature.  Now, let me see what kind of familiar you will need...[Tor picks up an elaborately carved gem and peers at you through it.  He frowns.]  Hmm.  Well, the good news is that you all need the same familiar, and when you find it, you will be very powerful.  The bad news is that you need to find a dragon familiar.  \n"
"\n"
"You must find a dragon egg.  Bring them back here and I will hatch it, and cast the familiar spell.  The baby dragon will imprint to you all, and you to it.  You may be able to find an egg in a dragon cave in the Land of the Giants.  'Ware the mother, though."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:228
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would love to get you started on the way to becoming Warlocks, but nothing I can do for you will be of any use until you become Great Druids.  Return when you have achieved that level of understanding."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:229
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though I like to think of the Warlocks as being followers of the Path of Twilight, or Dawn, we are technically followers of the Path of Darkness.  You must be dedicated followers of Darkness before I can help you.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:230
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmmmm.  [Tor looks at you carefully]  Nope.  Can't teach you.  You chose the Path of Light.  I can smell it on you.  I can sympathize with your choice, but I know that none of our spells or rituals can promote you once you have started down that path.  Sorry."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:231
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1166
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Tor looks at you in astonishment] You really found a dragon egg!  It's been more than a century since any Warlock has both needed and found a dragon familiar!  This will go down in the history books, that's for sure!  My spell book!  I need my book!  Ah, here it is.  [Tor chants a spell from the book, then taps the egg three times.  The egg hatches, and a baby dragon crawls out of the shell]  There you are!  Awww, isn't he cute?  Congratulations!  No longer are you simple Great Druids, but Warlocks!  Of course, that's just an honorary title if you weren't a natural Great Druid to begin with, but nonetheless, something to be proud of.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:232
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You need to bring me a dragon's egg so you I can hatch your familiar.  There is no way around this.  Try looking in the Land of the Giants for a dragon cave-- perhaps there you can find an egg."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:233
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the torso for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:234
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1169
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the left leg for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:235
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the right leg for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:236
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the left arm for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:237
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the right arm for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:238
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1173
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the head for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:239
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You prepare the head (with a dent in it) for assembly with the rest of the parts."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:240
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1175
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have no parts to assemble yet."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:241
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have all the parts together!  Now you just have to return to Master Grey for the animation process."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:242
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1177
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You remove the normal head and replace it with the dented head."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:243
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You remove the dented head and replace it with the normal head."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:244
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1179
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You should not be reading this message.  This means that you somehow have triggered this event without holding the normal or Abbey normal Golem heads which, based on the preconditions for this event, is absolutely impossible.  Please tell Bryan that he lost his bet and owes Keith 5 bucks because this event doesn't work properly."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:245
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank heavens you've cleaned them out!  Now we need to find a way to clean up the castle and rebuild the damaged sections.  The only people I can think of who would have the inclination and the ability to do this are the Dwarves in Stone City, located in the Barrow Downs to the south.  The entrance to Stone City lies in the center of the Barrow Downs on one of the largest hills.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:246
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1181
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I fear that talking will fail with these goblins, my lords.  May I suggest violence?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:247
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"So…The new lords of Harmondale I have before me.  Not impressed.  Doubt other kings think much of you either.  Hrmph.  Probably get yourselves killed soon.  But maybe there's more than meets the eye here.  Yes.  Maybe you can do something for me, and I for you.  Medusas have taken my mines in eastern Bracada.  Turned a few of my people to stone.  Dangerous monsters, don't want to lose more lives on a rescue.  Ok to lose yours though.  \n"
"\n"
"Take this elixir and pour it on the statues.  Wake them up.  Then I will fix up your castle.  Give you respect.  Go now, and beware the griffins in Bracada.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:248
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Welcome back, Lords of Harmondale!  Now, I will help you.  My engineer will work for you.  Fix up your castle.  You have my thanks.  You are welcome here forever.\n"
"\n"
"Hmmph.  One more thing.  Your work has interested the other courts.  They will send ambassadors to you now--check your throne room.  Watch your back, my friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:249
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Back again, eh?  Your part of the bargain isn't finished.  No help 'til you're done.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:250
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1185
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your Queen wishes to speak with you as soon as possible.  Since the War, she has taken up residence at Gryphonheart Castle in Steadwick.  This is strictly business--whenever new lords assume their office she meets with them to make sure there are no misunderstandings.  Queen Catherine is particularly interested in you, and has told me she wishes to employ your services."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:251
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've received word that you met with the Queen.  I hope it went well."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:252
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1187
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The queen is very pleased with you!  The rescue operation went well, and Loren can no longer be held as a bargaining chip for that wicked King Parson!  When the current Harmondale conflict is over, I'm sure the Queen will reward you for your aid."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:253
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1188
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Queen tells me your loyalty is very strong.  You did the right thing when you informed the Queen of the treachery King Parson was plotting.  And I'll tell you this:  Your loyalty is not only strong, but it is well placed.  Harmondale is the rightful province of Erathia, despite Elvish claims to the contrary.  Your work for us helps to ensure that Harmondale will forever be in the hands of Humans."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:254
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Lady Ellen gasps in delight] You have Gryphonheart's Trumpet!  This is wonderful!  When it disappeared from the strongbox, we thought it had been stolen by the enemy!  Thank you for bringing it back to us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:255
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gryphonheart's Trumpet was no doubt stolen by the Elven raiding party.  You were too late to save it.  [Lady Ellen sighs] Well, this is bad, but I suppose we've suffered much worse disasters."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:256
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've learned from Queen Catherine that you betrayed us with the old false prisoner trick.  [Lady Ellen curtsies respectfully] Your skills in the art of deception are formidable.  I will be sure not to be tricked so easily by your sincere manner again."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:257
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though Avlee is not currently in charge of Harmondale, my King, Eldrich Parson of Avlee, lays claim to this territory as our rightful domain.  The reasons are complicated, but boil down to the simple fact that Erathia stole our land in the Timber Wars many years ago, and we will not give up until we have it back.  My King wishes to speak with you.  Please travel to Pierpont in the Tularean Forest and meet with him.  We will make it worth your while."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:258
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Messengers have informed me of your visit with my King.  I hope you can see now why we are the rightful rulers of Harmondale.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:259
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1194
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard of your daring infiltration of Fort Riverstride, and I am impressed!  Our strategists are analyzing the plans now, and they say the information will be very useful in any assault they mount against the Fort.  You have Avlee's gratitude!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:260
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Word from Court is that you rejected a request from Erathia to break that spy Loren Steel out of prison.  Not only that, you helped us plant a false prisoner who has been feeding them misinformation ever since he got there.  Avlee is in your debt!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:261
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1196
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have Gryphonheart's Trumpet!  Excellent!  We lost track of it during the raid, and were afraid that one of the Erathians got away with it.  Thank you very much for your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:262
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It seems our raid on the Erathians has failed, and they or someone else got away with the Trumpet.  [Ambassador Alain shakes his head sadly] Maybe next time things will go our way."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:263
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1198
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've received a warning from my superiors regarding your delivery of falsified plans from Erathia.  The King is not amused. And there was some concern that you had more treachery in store for us.  [Alain smiles, true to his profession] All's fair in love and war, so it's all water under the bridge, eh?  Yes, all is forgotten.  [The ambassador chuckles heartily].  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:264
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"[Queen Catherine inclines her head regally] You are the lot that won Lord Markham's silly contest, I see.  I must admit I had little faith until the Dwarf King recognized you as the rightful rulers of Harmondale.  You must have done something to win his respect, or he would have nothing to do with you.  I'm still not sure what he saw in you, but perhaps there really is something of substance here.  We shall see.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe you can do something for me that would make me think I should let you keep your new titles.  Recently, a valuable...agent of mine was arrested in the Tularean Forest for merely doing his job.  They're keeping him in a cave somewhere outside of Pierpont.  His name is Loren Steel, and they are threatening to execute him if certain unacceptable conditions are not met in 28 days.  Return with him before then and you will win respect, gold, and gratitude."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:265
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1200
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Catherine stands and smiles] Good job!  You've really solved a terrible dilemma for me.  [Catherine turns to Loren and shakes his hand] Loren.  It's good to meet you at last.  Since everyone knows who you are now, you're not much good to me as a spy, but I would like to offer you a job in the Royal Diplomatic Corps.  Please give it some thought.  As for our heroes, you have my thanks.  My purser will credit your bank account with 5000 gold pieces for your services.   "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:266
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Loren's life is on the line.  I cannot give into the Elvish demands, or many more lives will be lost.  Please hurry.  I'm sure Avlee will execute him on schedule."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:267
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1202
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Catherine stands and smiles] Good job!  You've really solved a terrible dilemma for me.  [Catherine turns to the false Loren and shakes his hand] Loren.  It's good to meet you at last.  Since everyone knows who you are now, you're not much good to me as a spy, but I would like to offer you a job in the Royal Diplomatic Corps.  Please give it some thought.  As for our heroes, you have my thanks.   "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:268
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The Queen's eyes narrow] What's this?  You're admitting to treachery?  How noble.  Guards!  Off with their heads!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:269
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1204
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "King Parson asked you to steal the floor plan to Fort Riverstride?  Hmmm.  [Catherine turns to one of her advisors] Have some false plans of Fort Riverstride drawn up.  Make it painful.  [She turns back to you] If it's plans he wants, it's plans he'll get.  Give these plans to the King.  I'm sure he'll be grateful.  Make sure you don't let him know they're fake.  [After awhile the advisor returns with the plans and gives them to you]  You'll need to get the plans back to him on time, of course.  I'm sure he plans to attack us soon."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:270
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "He took the plans?  Excellent!  I'll have the Riverstride commander roll out the red carpet for them.  As for you, I've instructed my purser to deposit 5,000 gold pieces in your account."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:271
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:271
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have to get the plans to him before he attacks Riverstride.  If you don't, they won't lead his forces into all the traps we've prepared for them.  So hurry up and deliver those plans!  I'm counting on you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:272
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:272
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You told the king the plans were fake?!?  [The Queen puts her hand on her head, jaw agape] I have never seen such incompetence in all my life!  Astounding!  Get out of my sight!  Just go!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:273
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:273
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The Queen raises her eyebrows with interest as you tell her how you infiltrated her fort, stole secret plans, and killed many of her guards while in the service of a foreign king] I wish I could truthfully say this is the most shocking treason I have ever witnessed, but unfortunately, it's not.  Nonetheless...Guards!  Off with their heads!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:274
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:274
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, time ran out for poor Loren.  He was executed for espionage by Avlee on schedule.  Don't bother with the rescue.  He's gone."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:275
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:275
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "King Parson is beyond the date when he could have used those false papers.  Don't bother taking them to him--it doesn't matter anymore.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:276
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:276
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Welcome.  I understand you've been appointed Lords of Harmondale by that idiot Markham.  You know, I WILL restore Avlee's rule over Harmondale--the only question is whether you are with me, or against me.  If you're with me, I will ensure that you retain your post.  Against me, and I will have done with you once my armies occupy your lands.  \n"
"\n"
"[King Parson smiles affably] So, of course you're with me!  You just need to prove it.  Like a famous leader once said:  Trust, but verify!  Words to live by.  What I want right now is the plans to Fort Riverstride.  It's a huge fort that stands between your lands and Erathia proper.  You can't miss the thing.  Sneak in there and get me those plans.  If you can do this, I will be in your debt.  Not only that, there's a substantial gold reward as well.  If the plans are to be any use to me at all, though, I need them delivered to me within a month."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:277
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:277
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The King smiles broadly as you hand him the plans]  Thank you!  These will be VERY useful.  My factor will deposit 5,000 gold pieces in your bank account for services rendered.  When we finally win this round against Erathia, I will not forget you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:278
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:278
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I really do need those plans soon.  If you take too long, I'll have to prepare my attack without the plans."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:279
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:279
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The King smiles broadly as you hand him the false plans.  Sucker! ]  Thank you!  These will be VERY useful.  When we finally win this round against Erathia, I will not forget you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:280
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:280
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What do you mean, these plans are false?  So you admit to plotting against me?  [The King throws up his hands in disgust] Guards!  Take these traitors to the courtyard and execute them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:281
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:281
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The wily queen moves against me, eh?  [The King frowns in thought, then brightens] I have an idea!  I know someone who looks just like that spy she wants you to rescue.  Bring my man with you and deliver him to the Queen.  She's never met him, and won't know the difference.  His 'inside information' will encourage her to make mistakes.  [The King takes a moment to summon the imposter]  Be careful not to tip your hand.  It wouldn't do for her to discover our little plan.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:282
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:282
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The imposter has infiltrated her military and diplomatic advisors' ranks, and will cause plenty of damage before he's discovered, I'm sure.  Thank you for your help! My factor will deposit 5000 gold into your account at the bank."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:283
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:283
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's important to get the imposter to the Queen before Mr. Steel's scheduled execution.  After all, you can't rescue Mr. Steel if everyone knows I've executed him.  And she'll become suspicious if I stay the execution.  I've never stayed one before."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:284
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:284
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You told Queen Catherine about the imposter?!? I can't believe my ears!  Why did you do it?  Why?  [The King stands and points at the door] Get out!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:285
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:285
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The king is silent while you detail your crimes against Avlee, then smiles and spreads his hands once you've finished] Well!  I suppose that story speaks for itself, doesn't it?  Guards!  Take these traitors to the courtyard and execute them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:286
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:286
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The time where I could have used those plans is over.  Thanks for any efforts you may have put into finding them, but I no longer need the plans."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:287
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:287
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The execution date for Loren Steel has passed.  Don't bother bringing the imposter to the Queen--she'll be too suspicious for our ruse to succeed.  He'll be leaving you now."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:288
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:288
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My loyal subjects!  You were the ones who took the Trumpet!  Good work.  We thought it lost forever.  Once again, my purser will deposit gold in your account.  5,000 gold, to be exact."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:289
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:289
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the Trumpet!  You captured it!  We weren't sure how things turned out when news of the human raid reached us.  Thank you again, my friends.  My factor will deposit 5,000 gold in your account for your services."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:290
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:290
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If there is one piece of advice I could give you, it would be to fix your castle.  I don't know how you're going to find the gold and workers to do it, as only wealthy nobles and kings can afford such large scale projects.  I suppose it's the old chicken and egg question...you must appear noble to gain wealth and respect, but you must have wealth and respect in order to appear noble.  \n"
"\n"
"In any event, if you expect to be lords of Harmondale for more than a few months, you need to find a way to prove you're not just lucky peasants.  You must prove that you're fit to rule."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:291
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:291
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Once again, the Human kingdom of Erathia and the Elvish kingdom of Harmondale are fighting.  As the local Judge, it has fallen to me to patch up their differences and bring the two sides to the negotiating table.  The two sides are so evenly matched that either could prevail.  [The judge leans closer to you, lowering his voice] And I'll tell you something else--I don't much care anymore who wins.  They are like children fighting over a toy.  Neither really wants Harmondale--they just want to deny it to the other.  \n"
"\n"
"So, you're on your own.  Whatever actions you take now in support of one side or another could really make a difference.  Just remember that they couldn't possibly care less what happens to you or who rules in Harmondale.  Protect yourselves and your people first.  We didn't have this conversation."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:292
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:292
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You were wise to return the Trumpet to me.  Now I can use it to help shore up the weak side in this conflict and promote peace.  Thank you.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:293
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:293
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A wise decision.  You won't regret this--believe me.  I knew you were going to make this decision, and my bags are already packed and ready to go.  All you need to do now is get me to my new home, and I'll take care of the rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:294
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:294
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your first order of business is to talk to Lord Ironfist and complete his 'mission.'  Once your ability and loyalty are proven, you will be allowed to help in more…interesting… ways."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:295
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:295
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Each of the advisors to Lord Ironfist has a task for you, complete each one.  Talk to Kastore, Dark Shade, and Maaximus for more information.  The completion of these tasks is vital for our future."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:296
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:296
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tolberti has a mission of great importance.  Everything we've staked so far rests on its completion.  Prepare well for his task or you will certainly fail."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:297
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:297
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Xenofex and the rest of the Kreegan must be put down; go to their 'hive' in the Land of the Giants and put a stop to Xenofex and his minions once and for all."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:298
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:298
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You will need to visit the craft that brought Kastore and his men to Erathia to continue.  Go west of Avlee, and make sure to be properly outfitted."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:299
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:299
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bring the Oscillation Overthruster back to Kastore with all possible speed!  Every moment you dally allows a chance for failure!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:300
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:300
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great!  You've done the right thing!  Though the path of light can be hard to walk at times, the ultimate rewards are well worth it.  I'm already prepared for the trip.  All you need to do now is get me to my new home, and I'll take care of the rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:301
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "First, you need to speak to Gavin Magnus in Celeste and complete his training.  After you have proven your ability and loyalty you will learn more about your role in the future of Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:302
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Each of Gavin's advisors has a task for you.  Talk to Resurectra, Sir Caneghem, and Crag Hack for more information.  Do not fail in these missions- in them rests the balance of the future."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:303
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Robert the Wise has a regrettable, but necessary, mission for you to complete.  For any of our plans to continue, this mission must succeed.  Prepare most carefully for the task, or you invite certain failure."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:304
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Kreegan, the Devils, and their leader Xenofex must be destroyed completely for the plan to have any long-term benefit.  You will find their 'hive' in the Land of the Giants."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:305
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To the west of Avlee lies the craft that Resurectra and her associates used to come to Erathia.  Visit the ship and retrieve the Oscillation Overthruster to insure our victory.  Make sure to be properly outfitted for the journey."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:306
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bring the Oscillation Overthruster back to Resurectra immediately!  Every moment wastes valuable time!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:307
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Test involves entering the 'front door' of the Walls of Mist, and exiting through the 'back door'.  I use the word 'door' loosely--you'll see when you get there.  You will not need your weapons.  You will fail the test if you kill any creature in the Walls of Mist.  If you can complete this task, you will be given membership in the Guild of Light. Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:308
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You passed the Test!  That's quite an achievement--few succeed as quickly as you did.  My advisors are now eager to speak to  you; they can be found in the four houses on the eastern side of Celeste.  Once again, congratulations!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:309
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Remember, you must enter through the front door of the Walls of Mist, and exit through the back door.  You must not kill any creatures in the Walls of Mist.  When you have done this, return to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:310
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We need your help retrieving half of a key to a very important place from our enemies, the Necromancers.  Like us, they have enshrined their half of the key in their highest temple--The Temple of the Dark.  I'm under no illusions this will be easy.  Take your time and act when you're prepared.  Also, bring our half of the key to us, as well.  It is enshrined in the Temple of the Light.  Since you're our ally, no one should trouble you when you go there to fetch the key.  By the same token, please don't harm any of them, either."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:311
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No key halves yet, I see.  Well, take your time.  It must be done eventually, and sooner is better than later, but later is better than being chained to an altar and sacrificed by the High Priest of the Dark in one of their bloody rituals.  Just bring back both halves of the key from the temples of Dark and Light, and try not to get yourselves killed doing it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:312
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I'm glad you found our half of the key, but you still need their half.  Hold onto it until you get the other half.  When you have both halves, return to me.  I will make them whole."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:313
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1218
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work on retrieving their half of the key, but you still need ours.  It is located in the Temple of the Light here in Celeste."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:314
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I knew you could do it!  Never doubted you for a second!  [You hand her the key halves, and she joins them by running a finger along the crack between them.  It mends before your eyes, good as new] Finally!  One piece of the plan is in place.  Your assistance has been invaluable.  We are already in your debt, and I expect we'll be even deeper in debt before our plan comes to fruition.  So have faith in us awhile longer--the future we're planning will astound you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:315
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our plans rapidly approach their conclusion, but there is a hitch.  The Kreegan--also known as the Devils, or the Demons, must be destroyed before we finish our plans.  They represent a terrible threat, and though they do little but lick their wounds today, will one day regain their strength and devastate the world.  If anything we do is to have lasting effect, we must first destroy these monsters for once and for all.\n"
"\n"
"You are strong, but not strong enough to defeat the devils on your own.  They are vulnerable to the brand of magic most commonly wielded by the Necromancers, and less so by our own Wizards.  It is imperative that you infiltrate the Devil's base and kill their leader Xenofex.  That should end their threat to this world for some time.  The Warlocks have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land the Devils claim as their own.  Perhaps you can use that."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:316
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "YOU ARE HEROES!!!  Your work against the devils was masterful!  And the rescue of King Roland was as delightful as it was unexpected.  History will never forget your names for doing what you just did!  I, for one, am very proud to know you.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:317
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I guess there's no hurry getting this job done, but we don't want the Necromancers to grow bored waiting for us to do our part and destroy the blocker.  So, please, as soon as you feel ready you must attack the Devils.  Remember that the Warlocks have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the land of the Devils.  You should be able to use that to get yourselves there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:318
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our allies in Tatalia have been complaining for some time of a mysterious presence.  There have been numerous deaths and disappearances for the last few months, and they've asked us if we knew anything about it.  I think I do.  I suspect a vampire is preying on Tatalia.  I don't have time to pursue the question myself, but to keep our allies happy, I'm asking you to please look into it.  It's possible the monster's presence has deeper implications than just bad luck for Tatalia."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:319
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1224
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Just as I suspected!  Good work.  With the death of the Vampire, Tatalia can sleep a bit easier now.  Queen Catherine is grateful as well, and has been making moves to further strengthen the ties between Bracada and Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:320
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Keep looking for that Vampire.  I'm sure that's our problem, and he must be somewhere in or near Tatalia.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:321
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The plan involves stealing the soul jars the Necromancers rely on to prolong their miserable lives.  They have them hidden somewhere in their Guild Castle, and are probably not prepared for the kind of small scale assault you people are so good at.  A quick strike--in and out--should do the trick.  Don't hang around the castle too long, or reinforcements will arrive, and try to get it right the first time, or they will permanently double their patrols.  Once you have the soul jars, bring them back here so we can dispose of them properly."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:322
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Sir Caneghem looks at the jars curiously, as though observing a poisonous snake behind glass] So these are soul jars.  I expected something more…impressive, I suppose.  Good job!  [he takes the case of jars] I will make sure these jars are never seen again."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:323
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Be well prepared when you go for the jars.  Their security won't be so lax if you have to retreat and return.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:324
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our counterparts, the former advisors to Archibald, each carry a token called a command cube on their person that we absolutely must acquire to complete the Goal.  There is no way any of them will part with their cube willingly, which means that we must get it some other way.  You will have to take it from one of them, and we think the easiest would be Tolberti.  Unlike the rest of them, he disdains proper security and has taken up residence in one of the apartments in the Pit.  I need you to infiltrate the pit again and get the cube from him.  Be careful--he is well armed and much tougher than he appears.  When you have the Cube, return to me.  We have but a short distance to the Goal, and all will be revealed very soon."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:325
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1230
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Robert takes the cube] Once again, you succeed!  The Goal is so close!  I know you have many questions, and I'm sure Resurectra will answer them all, after you do just one more mission for her.  You will find her with Gavin Magnus in the throne room of Castle Lambent."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:326
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Keep trying to find his apartment.  Tolberti has never really believed anything bad could happen to him, and so far he's been right.  We need to prove him wrong.  Take the cube any way you can.  If you can do it without violence, fine.  If you must kill him, well, that's O.K. too.  Just get the cube."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:327
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We need your help retrieving half of a key to a very important place from our enemies, the Wizards.  Like us, they have enshrined their half of the key in their highest temple--The Temple of the Light.  It'll be a snap.  Most so called good people spend more time defending and healing themselves than delivering damage.  How can you win if you don't fight?  Anyway, take your time and act when you're prepared.  \n"
"\n"
"Also, bring our half of the key to us, as well.  It is enshrined in the Temple of the Darkness.  Since you're our ally, no one should trouble you when you go there to fetch the key.  But if you feel like you need the practice, go ahead a take a whack at some of them.  They're not very important, and most of them can regenerate from even the most severe injuries.  Try it--it's alot of fun!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:328
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No key halves yet?  Bah!  I hope you're more competent than you seem right now!  How hard can this be?  All you have to do is burst in the front door and start shooting.  When there's no one left, you can clean their place out at your leisure.  Just hurry up and bring us both key halves."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:329
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I'm glad you found our half of the key, but you still need their half.  Hold onto it until you get the other half.  When you have both halves, get back over here and I'll fix them."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:330
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Finally!  I was beginning to wonder if you might have got yourselves killed already.  Well, no matter.  You forgot to get the key from the Temple of the Dark, so be on your way.  When you have it, return to me so I can make the two halves whole again."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:331
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  [Kastore takes the two halves of the key and bangs them together.  With a bright white flash, they join together seamlessly]  The first part of the Plan is complete.  I knew we, uh, Archibald made the right decision in trusting you!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:332
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Soon our plans will bear fruit, but there are a few details that must be handled before we are ready.  The Kreegan, also known as the Devils, share this world with us.  The only reason we're sharing is because they are weak right now.  If they ever get strong, they will try to kill every person in the world.\n"
"\n"
"Anyway, it's no fun to rule a world full of dead people, so we have to kill the Devils before they kill us.  Our plan is for you to infiltrate the Devils lair and destroy their leader, Xenofex.  The warlocks of Nighon have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land of the Devils.  You can probably use that tunnel to get there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:333
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "THAT WAS AWESOME!  You did it!  And now the single greatest threat to our plans is gone!  We will be Kings of the World!  [Kastore throws his head back and laughs wildly] AHAHAHAHAHA!!!!! Ah ha ha. Yes.  Well, good job.  I'll even forgive you for letting that King Roland character go free--we could have used him as a bargaining chip, you know.  [he shrugs] you probably didn't have a choice, I suppose.  In any event, this is a happy day!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:334
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Could you please hurry up with this raid against the Devils?  Archibald has promised forces, but they won't be available forever.  What's worse, the devils breed faster than rabbits.  The longer you wait, the more you'll have to fight."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:335
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Archibald has asked us to find a source of soul jars for his necromancers.  These are the jars that are needed to complete the Ritual that gives them eternal life, and we're almost out.  There are far more candidates for Lichdom than we have jars, so some of our necromancers are facing the grim possibility of real death.  The makers of the jars are the Warlocks.  Go to them and convince them to give us the jars.  If they won't hand them over, take the jars by force-- I'm done negotiating prices with them."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:336
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Maximus takes the case of jars with obvious delight] Nice work.  I won't even ask what you had to do to get them.  Success speaks for itself.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:337
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You don't have to be nice about getting the jars from them--just get the jars any way you can.  We can renegotiate peace with them if we must, just like we renegotiate the price for each purchase of soul jars."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:338
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lord Archibald has another request--the creatures that have inhabited Clanker's laboratory must be evicted--and the teleport shield brought down.  The laboratory is on an island east of Pierpont in the Tularean Forest.  Be careful--the monsters in that lab were created by Clanker himself, and some of them are much more powerful than their more common fellows elsewhere in the world.  Take whatever you like from the place.  Lord Archibald is only interested in the real estate and the laboratory equipment.  Once the shield is down, Lord Archibald will be able to begin moving necromancers and equipment inside via Lloyd's Beacon. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:339
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1244
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's good to see we can count on you.  So few of our allies are as reliable and capable as yourselves.  Thank you very much for your aid."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:340
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This is a simple task--get a move on!  Once again, the laboratory on an island east of Pierpont in the Tularean Forest.  Get the shield lowered, and your part of the job is done."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:341
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Just as Archibald has us, King Magnus of Bracada has his advisors.  And, just like us, each of them wears a small token called a command cube.  We need one of their cubes, and they're not going to just hand one over to us.  We must take one of their cubes, and we have decided it should be Robert the Wise who suffers.  One of our spies in their castle has damaged the lock to his room.  They have been lax about replacing it, so you should have no trouble going through the door.  I don't care if you kill him or not--just get the cube and return to me at once."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:342
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Tolberti takes the cube] This brings us very close to completing our Plan.  I know Kastore hasn't told you exactly what the Plan is, but you'll like it, I'm sure!  I am not allowed to say much, but I can tell you your position will be much higher than simply Lords of Harmondale, you can count on that!  You will find Kastore in his place on the throne of Castle Gloaming."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:343
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What's wrong?  Don't tell me you're losing your nerve?  He's tough, but not immortal.  You can take him!  I wouldn't have sent you on this mission if I didn't think you could handle it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:344
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, the test.  It's simple.  Near the center of the city is a place we call the Breeding Zone.  There's a lot of foul monsters in the pit, and they regenerate constantly.  It makes for a good source of slaves, spare parts, and target practice.  All of our necromancers are tested there when they want to rise above the level of initiate.  I'm sure you'll pass the test.  Just jump in the pit and find a way out.  Kill anything you want down there.  Show no mercy.  When you escape, crawl out of the pit and come see me again.  If you complete this, I will give you membership in the Guild of Dark. *If* you complete this..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:345
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You show promise, my friends.  A fine performance.  I think it will be sufficient proof of your skill for my advisors.  They are quite eager to assign tasks to you now; they can be found in the four houses in the western side of the Pit.  And don't worry.  Rewards will follow, of course."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:346
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am beginning to suspect my allies were right about you.  Can't you pass this simple test?  Are you too afraid, or too feeble to succeed?  Perhaps we need new allies?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:347
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The time has come to achieve our Goal.  The reason we have sent you on all these missions is simple:  we have been busy gathering the parts needed to open a gate to the Ancients--the ones who colonized this world ages ago.  Unfortunately, our former compatriots also seek those parts for their own dark dreams.  They wish to rebuild the Heavenly Forge from the times before the Silence, and use it to duplicate the weapons we brought with us to your world.  We have been competing with them for these parts, but at last we have what we need.  \n"
"\n"
"Except for one thing.  We have been unable to find the Oscillation Overthruster on your world.  All would be lost, but there is one such device aboard the Lincoln--the vehicle that brought us to your world.  It is in the sea west of Avlee and secured against entry, even from ourselves.  Now you must wear our environment suits, enter the ship, and return with the Overthruster; you will find these suits in the chest outside this throne room.  For the suit to function properly you must not be wearing any equipment.  As for us, we must stand watch at the gate, and battle our former comrades.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:348
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have returned!  At last!  We have the Overthruster.  Now, come with us as we open the way to the Ancients!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:349
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1254
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't forget you'll need the wetsuits to get to the Lincoln.  These suits are in the chest outside this throne room and the Lincoln is in the sea west of Avlee.  Return here with the Overthruster as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:350
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our finest hour is upon us.  While you have been taking care of all those important tasks, my compatriots and I have been struggling with our former friends for the parts we need to rebuild the Heavenly Forge of legend.  By former friends, I mean the four chief advisors to King Magnus of the Wizards.  They have a plan to build a gate to the Ancients.  They could have stood with us, but threw it all away on some vague hope of a 'better future'.  But you!  You have stood with us all this time.\n"
"\n"
"Only one task remains--we need the Oscillation Overthruster from our old vehicle, the Lincoln.  We have been unable to find one on your world.  The ship is in the sea west of Avlee and secured against entry, even from ourselves.  Now you must wear our environment suits, enter the ship, and return with the Overthruster.  Our old environments suits have been prepared for you in the chest outside this throne room.  For the suit to function properly you must not be wearing any equipment.We will stand watch over the Forge, and defend it against our enemies.  Bring us the Overthruster, my friends, and together, we shall rule the world!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:351
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1256
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "YOU'VE DONE IT!!!  You have the Overthruster!  Quickly, come with me to the laboratory!  The forge is ready…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:352
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1257
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't forget you'll need the environmental suits to get to the Lincoln.  These suits are in the chest outside the throne room, and the Lincoln is in the sea west of Avlee.  What else do you need to know?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:356
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You need to have your own deck of cards to play. We will supply the opponent.  Victory conditions vary per inn. Build your tower, destroy your opponent's tower, or collect enough resources before your opponent does. \n"
"\n"
"Large yellow numbers in column are the generators. This is how many new units of a particular resource you will receive on your next turn. Small black numbers in column are the resources. This is how many units you have available to spend on your current turn.\n"
"\n"
"Cards: Each have their own cost to play, indicated in a small circle in the lower right corner of the card. The cost will be deducted from your resources according to the color of the card.  Left click on a card plays the card. Right click on a card to discard without playing.\n"
"\n"
"Red represents your Quarry Generator which produces your Brick resources, blue represents your Magic Generator which produces Gem resources, green represents your Zoo generator which produces Beast resources. \n"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:357
