#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:602
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1506
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So YOU'RE the ones that won Lord Markham's contest!  How do you like your winnings so far?  Had enough winning?  If I were you, I'd give him a piece of my mind!  His mansion is in Tatalia, near the wharf."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:603
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1507
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Watch your wallet while you're here, my friends--Steadwick abounds in thieves.  As a matter of fact, we are the world capital of thieves!  It's common knowledge that Bill Lasker, the Master Thief, lives in the sewers beneath Steadwick."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:604
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1508
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Back when I was in the army, I was assigned to scout out the watchtowers in Deyja.  <chuckling> It's no good trying to go through the front door, so I usually looked around for another way in.  Those Necromancers are so cowardly, they always have an escape route.  And a way out is also a way in..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:605
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1509
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bill Lasker may be a criminal, but he has worked for the Crown from time to time.  Special missions, official denials of involvement, spying…that sort of stuff.  Quite a few unusual events can be tied to Bill, but none to the Crown.  Seriously, don't you think the Queen's men could find and arrest one man, even if he was hiding in the sewer?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:606
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1510
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You want to know about that traitor, Carmine?  Well, she used to work for the diplomatic corps, until she went soft and signed up with the goody two-shoes wizards.  Now she walks the streets of Celeste freely, without a care in the world for the people she left behind.  Something bad will happen to her soon, mark my words!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:607
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1511
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looking for \"work\"?  You can find the Master Assassin somewhere in the Pit.  He'll have something for you.  There's always someone or something that needs killing, that's for certain."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:608
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1512
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Until recently, our local dragon Wromthrax the Heartless has confined his depredations to the hills in the south--eating goats, farm animals, and stray dogs.  But he has developed a taste for elvish blood, and now hunts us as well.  If you should care to confront him, his cave is in the north, west of the Mercenary Guild in the mountains.  He isn't always there.  Be careful--he is mighty."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:609
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1513
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What, you wanna be a crusader too?  This town is filling up with them, I swear!  Well, there's a crazy man living in the back of a building near the center of town.  People keep trying to sign up with him, and he keeps rejecting them.  Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:610
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1514
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Just a minute, let me check.  Mirror, mirror, on the wall… <the witch peers into her mirror for a few minutes, then sighs> It's still Alice Hargreaves.  She lives in Castle Gryphonheart.  She's quite a noble beauty, that girl is!  Takes me back to my youth, this one does."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:611
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1515
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One of our finest, most upstanding citizens is William Setag, considered by some to be the most black hearted villain alive.  As a matter of fact, he's one of our best agents.  Wizards and their ilk complain because they've been on the receiving end of his schemes too many times-- but he's about the best there is in his profession.  \n"
"\n"
"If you're looking for employment, go see him.  His tower is on the north shore of Deyja at a rather inaccessible point.  He doesn't like visitors, but he should be glad to see more students turn up at his door."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:612
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1516
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you're looking for a teacher to begin serious monk training, speak with Bartholomew Hume--you can find him in the village south of the town of Harmondale."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:613
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1517
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I hear there are markings on the walls of the barrows that can be used to find your way around the tombs.  It'll keep you from getting lost, but it won't save you from the undead that defend those graves."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:614
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1518
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A few years back, a weird cult called the Temple of Baa moved into the area.  At first they seemed popular, what with their free offers of healing, but it soon became clear they were devoted to darkness.  No one goes up there very much, now, and it seems that whatever evil gods were backing them have withdrawn their support.  But they're up there still, lurking in the shadows.  Creepy."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:615
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1519
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lots of sheep have gone missing since the Baa cult moved in--and I mean lots.  No doubt they were taken to the Baa temple for sacrifice.  I'm going to go broke if someone doesn't do something about those cultists!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:616
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1520
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ssspies abound in places like this, my friendsss.  If you wish your letters and communiqués to remain sssecret, you should use a cipher when you write.  There is a book in the Castle library that will explain everything, my friendsss."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:617
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1521
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Eight years ago, we sent a team of scholars to what is now the Red Dwarf Mine to study the strange creatures that would occasionally show up there.  \n"
"\n"
"The first thing we noticed was that Ooze ectoplasm makes an excellent potion catalyst.  The second was that ooze just can't be physically damaged--they split apart or squish, then run back together. If you want to kill one, you'll have to do it with magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:618
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1522
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There is a breed of Medusa infesting the Red Dwarf Mines that is immune to magic.  These monsters are a real terror!  I can only thank the Gods that these creatures haven't escaped the mine.  What would we do then, beat them to death with our staves?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:619
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1523
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you head south past the Wyvern Plains, don't go knocking at the door of that huge fortress you'll see standing in the middle of the water.  It's the Titan's Stronghold, and they don't much like visitors."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:620
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1524
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Arena fighting is available to anyone who wants to practice against any kind of opponent.  You can get to the arena by visiting a stable on any Sunday and asking them to take you there.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:621
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1525
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Arena Champships are held on each Sunday.  They are open to all--but be careful!  Your opponents are chosen by the Arena management, not you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:622
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1526
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Every graveyard or ancestral burial place seems to have a haunted house nearby--and ours is no exception.  There is a mansion near one of the plateaus on the surface in the northwest.  It is most certainly haunted."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:623
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1527
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fear the touch of the Ghost as you fear the loss of your life.  It inflicts terrible spiritual wounds and drains your youth before your eyes!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:624
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1528
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A few wars ago, my great grandfather worked on an escape tunnel from the Elvish castle to the Tularean Caves.  I don't think it's ever been used--no attack on the castle has ever brought it down--but it sure is an interesting piece of history, don't you think?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:625
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1529
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "They say that elves are faeries, but in truth we are only distantly related.  The true faeries don't live in civilization, and they're just like the stories say--playful, cruel, magical, and dangerous.  But if you really want to meet them, you could visit them in their Hall under the Hill, as they call it.  It is just outside of the village, to the North and West.  It will be challenging to get to the front door... "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:626
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1530
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A while ago, I saw some men come to the Tularean Forest at night with axes and torches, following some sort of map.  When they left, they were laughing and happy.  It looked like they were carrying a big green rock.  My brother says they were a band of mercenaries from Tatalia.  Anyway, the next day was when the forest went mad.  It's too dangerous to go there now."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:627
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1531
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Tularean Forest is so old that it has developed a mind…sort of.  The forest is vaguely aware of who walks through it, but only one part of the forest can communicate with people.  That's the oldest tree.  If you want to have a very long and slow conversation, it will be happy to oblige.  Look for it on an island to the south east of the forest.  It's larger than the rest of the trees.  You can't miss it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:628
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1532
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Anyone needing to earn some spare cash can visit a town hall in any major city to pick up a bounty hunting assignment.  City councils are always fearful of the latest man eating monster or bandit or mad wizard, and set bounties on the creature that is bothering them most this month.  There's no rhyme or reason to their choices, so don't try to figure it out.  They often pay quite well."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:629
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1533
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you ever get tired of amateur bounty hunts, and want to advance your career, speak with Ebednezer Sower in Avlee.  He only teaches followers of the shadow path, though."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:630
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1534
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pirates been operating out of the tidewater caverns for twenty years.  They're not Regnans, and they aren't part of Bill Lasker's men, but they're still pretty mean.  You want to get in there, just get yourself out to the islands to the west."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:631
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1535
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Evenmorn Island isn't lost, so much as hard to get to.  It is surrounded by treacherous reefs, sandbars, whirlpools, and sharks.  If it's dangerous, the Island is surrounded by it.  There are only one or two safe ways in, and the map for those ways was stolen by pirates during the chaos of the recent wars.  They probably still have the map in their caves.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:632
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1536
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The boat captains would be happy to take any paying fare to Evenmorn island, but they don't have proper maps.  There's no way anyone is going to risk their ship in the reefs around the Island unless they have the map!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:633
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1537
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I don't have any golem parts--I never took that class--but there are students all over Bracada who have spare golem parts lying around.  They aren't worth anything unless you have them all, so they'll probably just give them to you for free."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:634
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1538
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You see all those golems walking around Bracada?  Every single one of them was made by the School.  Not bad for students, eh?  They don't have much to say, but they're tough guardians and can tell when a follower of Darkness is near.  You should see them go into action when one of those Necromancers or Warlocks wanders into our lands.  Zowwwwwieeee!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:635
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1539
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our astrologers have determined that the missing Divine Intervention text lies somewhere deep under the ground.  Under Deyja, to be precise.  They fear that the current incarnation of the text has fallen into the Breeding Pit--the Necromancer's version of our Proving Grounds.  Oh, what must we have done to offend the Gods so?  We will never retrieve the text from that forsaken place!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:636
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1540
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The spell of Divine Intervention, the highest of the school of Light magic, has been missing for centuries.  It is a curse, we believe, for our lack of devotion and faith to the Light.  We struggle, and some go forth to find the spell, from time to time, but none have been successful.  Each time they find it, fate cruelly snatches it from our hands.  Our Grandmasters have been bereft of this final, great spell for as long as anyone alive can remember."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:637
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1541
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The only people in the world who make soul jars are the Warlocks of Nighon.  It is a secret of their profession--which is strange, since they have absolutely no use for them.  Still, we are forced to bargain for the jars in order to advance our craft.  Of course, we have wrested the jars from them, from time to time...but then they raise their prices in revenge.  It must be our fate to suffer so."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:638
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1542
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Every Necromancer aspires to be a Lich one day.  All you need is a Soul Jar, knowledge of the Ritual, and the magical skill to survive the journey to the Land of the Dead and return.  The body withers while the soul lives on in a glorious state free from hunger, disease, and injury.  Only shallow and superficial people would mind what the Ritual does to one's appearance.  True practitioners hardly notice."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:639
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1543
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Three circles of stones were built by the Druids long ago.  Since hearing of their locations ruins ascension attempts for would be Great Druids, I can only give you a general clue--All are in the open, unhidden and bare, and all are distant from settlements.  To tell you more would spoil your Ascension."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:640
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1544
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Originally, there were four Circles of Stone, one for each Cardinal direction and season, but the Eastern Circle was destroyed somewhere in Nighon during the wars between the Churches of the Sun and the Moon."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:641
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1545
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The graveyard does indeed hold the bones of the ancient King, but the hallowed land will curse any who disturb it.  I don't envy you this task.  Each grave you open will unleash its curse, and possibly some other trap.  Best be sure you're opening the correct grave when you begin to dig."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:642
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1546
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though the barrows were built to deter thieves, a way was needed to navigate them during burials and ceremonies.  Near each of the gates you'll find a plaque.  These plaques are cryptic, but they will keep you from losing your way, as long as you use them.  No thief yet has realized their significance, so once they enter the barrows, they never leave."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:643
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1547
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We built a tunnel leading from our Thunderfist Mountain to the Land of the Giants during the War.  It was there we discovered the Kreegan, and more titans and dragons then you can imagine.  I suppose one who's familiar is to be a dragon could find eggs in one of the dragon caves of that terrible land.  'Ware the mother..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:644
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1548
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard legends that there is a dragon in the Land of the Titans greater than any that have come before.  Lesser dragons and titans do battle on the slopes of the mountain in which its cave resides.  This dragon is so huge, and so mighty that the other dragons feed it for fear it will one day leave its cave and devour them all in its fury.  The dragons believe it is a god.  If that is so, imagine its treasure..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:645
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1549
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Glad you found the way in the back door.  You probably avoided a really nasty ambush that way.  I hope my advice was useful!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:646
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1550
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So…what goes around comes around, eh?  Good job with that Carmine traitor!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:647
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1551
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The dragon is fallen--and at your hands!  You are a hero!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:648
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1552
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Baa cult is gone?  Well that IS good news!  Everyone is in your debt, whether they know it or not.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:649
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1553
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Glad to hear the Baa cult has gone missing, instead of my sheep!  Good job!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:650
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1554
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm impressed--very few actually make it inside the fairy mound, or get very far."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:651
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1555
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The forest is much safer now, thanks you to!  The oldest tree is very happy with you, and has included you in its history recitals."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:652
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1556
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, so the map is found?  What will you do with your newfound treasure?  Share it, I hope!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:653
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1557
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you have the map, I guess you'll be going there soon.  Be careful--they say the island is cursed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:654
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1558
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you don't mind the swamp and fog, Evenmorn Island is a great place to live.  Of course, the Curse doesn't help--ghosts and skeletons roam the island freely--but other than that, the neighbors keep to themselves.  The Churches of the Sun and the Moon don't even fight each other very much anymore.  <Heh!> probably means they're running out of adherents..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:655
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1559
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Divine intervention has been found and copied?  A miracle!  I never expected to see it in my lifetime!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:656
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1560
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All the grandmasters are very pleased with you.  You have done our profession a great service!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:657
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1561
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Since you've discovered the circles on your own they have worked their magic on you.  I hope you will refrain from telling others of their whereabouts, as I have done for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:658
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1562
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "During the wars between the Temples of the Sun and Moon, three statuettes were stolen from the shrines in the Bracada Desert, Tatalia, and Avlee.  I represent a group of Druids that want these shrines back to their original form-- it is critical for their worship.  To this end, I am offering a substantial reward for anyone that will find the statuettes and place them on the shrines."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:659
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1563
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All three statuettes are not placed.  I cannot reward partial success.  Return when you have placed all three."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:660
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1564
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great work!  The Druids are so pleased, they threw in a little extra for your fine performance.  Take this… you most certainly deserve it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:661
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1565
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As you may have already guessed, I'm a collector of fine art.  Currently, I am looking for a set of paintings, one of King Roland, one of his brother Archibald, and one of the angel statue in the courtyard of Castle Ironfist.  This set is of great value, and, as a collector, I'm willing to pay quite handsomely for it.  If you should gather the entire set of paintings bring them back to me and I'll be sure to compensate you well for your effort."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:662
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1566
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You don't have any of the paintings.  I'm looking for the set containing Roland, Archibald, and the statue."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:663
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1567
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Remember, I need the complete set of paintings-- they aren't worth much by themselves.  When you have the rest, bring them all to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:664
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1568
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wonderful!  This set has eluded me for years!  You more than deserve the reward I promised; here, hopefully this will be sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:665
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1569
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To be declared ArcoMage Champion, you must win a game of ArcoMage in every tavern on, in, and under the continent of Erathia.  There are 13 such taverns sponsoring ArcoMage events.  When you have accomplished this, return to me to claim the prize."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:666
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1570
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must claim a victory at ALL 13 taverns.  Until you do, you cannot be declared ArcoMage Champion."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:667
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1571
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!  You have become the ArcoMage Champion!  The prize is waiting in the chest right outside my house."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:668
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1572
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here is the %s you have lost.  Be more careful in the future."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:669
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1573
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You never had it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:670
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1574
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "People say the Dwarves live in the barren lands south of Harmondale, but that's not exactly true--They live UNDER them.  Look for their front gate in the center of the Barrow Downs where three bridges meet."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:671
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1575
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ever since the Warlocks of Nighon tunneled through Stone City from their island, travelers have been asking to pass through the city to get to Nighon.  The Dwarf King hates this, and would like to charge a hefty fee for people seeking to enter Stone City.  He has not started charging however, fearing political and possible violent repercussions with the Warlocks of Nighon."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:672
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1576
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Warlocks of Nighon live in Thunderfist Mountain--an extinct volcano on a large island a few miles from the mainland.  During the recent wars, the Warlocks tunneled through Stone City to transport their forces across the channel.  Those tunnels are still open and can be traversed."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:673
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1577
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "During the War, the Warlocks tunneled from Nighon through Stone City to get to the mainland and seize territory.  Even though they were pushed back to their island by Erathia, the tunnels remain."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:674
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1578
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dwarves live under the ground of the Barrow Downs--a barren collection of ancient gravesites built by their race centuries ago to honor fallen kings and heroes.  Not all of the barrows can be reached on the surface--many are magically connected to each other through a system of teleporters and traps that protect the graves from those who would rob them.  If you look closely at the walls you should see markings that might help you navigate."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:675
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1579
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We were making a fortune in the Red Dwarf Mines until the Medusas came!  We had to run before they turned everyone to stone.  Without our mining, we have almost no way to make a living.  Not the way for a proper Dwarf to live, I say!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:676
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1580
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bracada leased the land where we started the Red Dwarf Mine to us a few years ago.  That was until the Medusas came and took the mines from our people.  Only the Gods know what horrors go on in there now.  The mines were in the Northeast corner of Bracada."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:677
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1581
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When the Medusas took the Red Dwarf Mines from us, not everyone escaped.  There are still several statues in the mines.  They can be rescued if their statues haven't been broken yet, but you would have to fight through the Medusas to do it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:678
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1582
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you like our city?  It's not just a hole in the ground--it's a home in the ground!  Dwarves have been working this mountain for centuries!  There isn't much mining left here, though, and what there is happens to be in unstable and unsafe tunnels.  Be careful if you go to the lower levels."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:679
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1583
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Respectfully, my lords, I must say that no one expects you to last long because no other lords of Harmondale have lasted long.  The fighting and politics between Erathia and Avlee will claim you sooner or later.  Probably sooner."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:680
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1584
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Rebellions here in Harmondale are rare, but we've had a couple of big ones!  Most of the time lords here don't last long enough to rebel against, but there've been some wicked ones!  Not that I think you're wicked, my lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:681
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1585
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's good to see someone in Harmondale again, my lords.  The castle's been standing empty since the War, except for the goblins.  But they don't count, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:682
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1586
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What with all the wars that Avlee gets itself into all the time, and all the high taxes, I've moved to Harmondale to stay.  Harmondale sees a lot of violence, but at least they don't conscript.  You know, there's been so many wars in Avlee that one of the kings had a tunnel dug from his castle to the caves in the North just in case the castle was taken AGAIN."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:683
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1587
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A ways outside of Harmondale there's a cave system that's always been the home of bandits, monsters, and other ne'er-do-wells.  They're called the White Cliff Caves.  If you're ever robbed, or are looking for some evil doers to punish, all you got to do is go up there.  You'll find a fight for sure!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:684
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1588
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Did you notice that covered bridge on the way from Harmondale to Steadwick?  It's called Fort Riverstride, and it protects us from surprise Elvish attacks coming through Harmondale.  There's so many traps and tricks inside there, they say it will never fall without the help of treachery.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:685
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1589
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There's an artifact that Avlee and Erathia have been fighting over for decades.  Both claim it was made by their people, and have lost the thing to raids against one another many times.  It isn't even magical--just a trophy.  Fifteen years ago, the trophy was lost during a raid, and no one knows where it went.  Recently, rumors have been flying, and the hunt's been on to figure out where it went.  If they find it--watch out!  Blood will be spilt. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:686
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1590
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Because of all the tension in the air, Erathia and Avlee hired an arbiter to help them work out their differences.  He's staying in the \"House of Stars\" on the eastern edge of Harmondale territory.  Maybe he has some advice for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:687
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1591
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you ever feel like you need advice on what next to do, or you've lost something important, go visit the Arbiter in the House of Stars near the Eastern edge of Harmondale territory.  He often knows where lost items went, or has advice on what you need to do.  I'm sure you'll find him helpful."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:688
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1592
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The death of Judge Grey, Arbiter of Harmondale, has put the War on hold.  It's like the whole world is holding its breath, waiting for you to make a choice.  Better be careful who you choose--this sounds like a big one, my Lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:689
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1593
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The proving grounds, called the Walls of Mist,  is the place where all the wizards in Celeste have to go before they learn the High Art.  I hear it is much more of a moral test than a physical one.  You aren't allowed to kill any of the monsters in the maze."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:690
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1594
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The city of Celeste has been home to the Light for centuries.  It was established by King Magnus II  in 499 as the centerpiece to the Kingdom of Bracada, and as a beacon of hope to the rest of the world.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:691
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1595
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What you see on the surface in Deyja is only a small part of the true Kingdom of Death.  There is an underground city they call the Pit.  It can be reached from the surface only by way of the Hall of the Pit in Northern Deyja.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:692
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1596
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Celeste is the magical city built by the Wizards of Bracada centuries ago, and anchored half in the mountains, and half in mist high above Bracada.  You must use one of their teleporters to get there--you can find it near the center of Bracada."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:693
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1597
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There was another murder, recently, that's been all the talk around town.  Another body--young woman, so I hear--was found near the sewers.  Drained of blood, for the love of Light!  It's those thieves living' in the sewers I tell you!  Rats, they are.  Someone should go down there and put them out of business!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:694
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1598
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "During the War, the Warlocks had dealings with some strange creatures called the \"Kreegan\" in the mountains south of Avlee.  It's impossible to get there from the mainland, but the Warlocks dug a tunnel under the sea from their island that leads to the Kreegan's home."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:695
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1599
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We…overplayed our hand during the War, and failed to win any territory on the mainland.  Our \"allies\", the Kreegan, turned out to be very untrustworthy.  People from Enroth call them devils--now we know why.  At just the moment when we needed them most, they turned and ran, leaving us to face the wrath of the armies of Erathia and Avlee.  Next time, we won't be so trusting."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:696
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1600
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There's been quite a bit of activity in Deyja, people are saying.  It seems that Archibald Ironfist, the leader of Deyja (and former King of Enroth) has left the Pit for an island off the Eastern shore of Avlee.  A lot of Necromancers followed him there--seems there's some sort of split going on."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:697
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1601
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Rumors have been trickling out of Nighon that King Roland of Enroth may still be alive.  Some Warlocks have said that they personally saw him when they met with the foul Kreegan.  The rumors also say that the Kreegan are keeping him in a cage and mistreating him horribly."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:698
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1602
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A Soul Jar is what a Necromancer needs to complete the Ritual and become a Lich--an immortal undead monster that retains its mind and memories from life.  It's pretty obvious that this is not a desirable condition for most people, which is why the market for these artifacts isn't very good.  Nonetheless, Necromancers will do almost anything to get more--their profession's very existence depends on them."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:699
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1603
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "People have been disappearing recently.  Not just one or two, but several every day!  They go to bed at night, and the next day they aren't seen and their houses are empty!  I certainly wish someone would find out what it happening!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:700
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1604
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So much for the mighty defenses.  Word is the Necromancers, led by Archibald Ironfist, teleported straight into Clanker's Laboratory and took over.  I'm told that treachery from within had something to do with it, though."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:701
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1605
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Although the Warlocks are technically servants of the Dark, they usually aren't violent.  They will defend themselves if attacked, of course, but they won't start a fight unless you start it first.  They're quite reasonable, as a matter of fact, and they take their business seriously.  I've found dealing with them to be quite pleasant."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:702
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1606
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The underground complex Clanker has created is surprisingly well defended.  The front door will keep out all magical attacks, and the island makes it difficult for any sort of large force to land on the island.  So far, Clanker has kept to himself, and no one has seriously tried his defenses, but his best protection comes from a series of teleport blockers inside the complex.  No magical invasion force can teleport past the front door until those blockers are brought down first."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:703
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1607
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We made landfall on the western shore of Northern Avlee.  Walk into the sea from the farthest point west on the beach, and look around underwater.  The ship is unmistakable."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:704
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1608
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Lords of Harmondale!  Heroes, I say!  My cousin was one of the ones you rescued!  We are in your debt!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:705
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1609
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for delivering our people from the medusas!  The Dwarves of Stone City will not forget you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:706
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1610
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We owe you much for your daring rescue of our people.  Rebuilding your castle was the least we could do for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:707
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1611
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day, my lords.  I must say the people are changing their minds about your chances of survival.  Everyone is saying how wonderful it is to have stable rulers in the Castle!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:708
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1612
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's good to see the Castle rebuilt and those loathsome goblin bandits evicted.  Things are looking better around here since you took over!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:709
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1613
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard Fort Riverstride was taken with the aid of treachery!  What a shame that those wretches were able to wring concessions from the Queen in exchange for the return of what was already ours!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:710
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1614
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looks like the trophy fell into the hands of Erathia.  I hear there was quite a fight over it! "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:711
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1615
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looks like the trophy fell into the hands of Avlee.  I hear there was quite a fight over it! "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:712
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1616
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looks like the trophy fell into the hands of the Arbiter.  I hear there was quite a fight over it! "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:713
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1617
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The death of Judge Grey was a blow to all of us.  I hope his replacement does his legacy justice."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:714
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1618
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It looks like the consequences of your choice are just beginning, my lords.  I hope you chose wisely."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:715
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1619
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So it was a vampire that was killing all those people!  I hear you're the ones to get rid of it, too!  Thanks!  Everyone feels much safer now."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:716
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1620
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "They say you are being credited with rescuing King Roland!  That's quite a feather in your cap, my lords!  QUITE a feather!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:717
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1621
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looking for Expert instruction in one of your Skills?  Expert teachers for most Skills can be found in Harmondale, Erathia and the Tularean Forest. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:718
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1622
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here's your weapon; if you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more weapons."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:719
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:536
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:536
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1623
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You need ore for me to create weapons.  The better the ore, the better the weapon I can make."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:720
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1624
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here's your armor; if you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more armor."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:721
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:538
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:538
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1625
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You need ore for me to create armor.  The better the ore, the better the armor I can make."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:722
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1626
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here is your item; if you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more items."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:723
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:540
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:540
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1627
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You need ore for me to create items.  The better the ore, the better the items I can make."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:724
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1628
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The signal rocket on the west side of the island should be set of to warn ships off from approaching to close to that side of the island.  The reefs off the west coast have proven deadly in the past."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:725
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1629
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Beware the marshes of the southern tip of the island.  The dragon flies that pester our town spawn there!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:726
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1630
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fallen or dead trees can sometimes be the hiding place of some treasure or trinket.  However, it can also be home to insects or worse!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:727
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1631
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The teleporters of central Bracada can get you to numerous locations in the desert.  Just check the pillar in front of the teleporter for the location it will take you to.  Be careful however, some of the teleporters haven't been working correctly and will not show the destination!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:728
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1632
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Lords!  Lord Archibald sent engineers and artisans to upgrade Castle Harmondale!  Now we have an upstairs and downstairs!  Lord Archibald also left gifts in chests in these new areas.  The artisans are setting up shop in the entry hall and will have many wonderful items for sale!  Oh, yes, the workers discovered an older area to the castle--a torture chamber and dungeon!  We are very lucky!  I never thought Harmondale could afford such luxuries, my lords!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:729
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1633
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Lords!  Gavin Magnus sent engineers and artisans to upgrade Castle Harmondale!  Now we have an upstairs and downstairs!  Gavin Magnus also left gifts in chests in these new areas.  The artisans are setting up shop in the entry hall and will have many wonderful items for sale!  The workers, however, discovered an older area to the castle--a torture chamber and dungeon.  It isn't a pretty sight, I'm afraid."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:730
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1634
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Lords ::bows:: Now that you have cleared Castle Harmondale of the goblins and vermin, you should concentrate on removing the goblins from the area surrounding Harmondale.  To the east of here is the center of the disputed region.  Many great battles have been waged there between the forces of King Eldrich of the Elves and Queen Catherine of Erathia.  The goblins have taken the ruined fort in this area an use it to attack any travelers attempting to reach Harmondale!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:731
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1635
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Lords, remember Castle Harmondale is YOURS.  Feel free to relax while you're here.  Your sleep will never be disturbed by attacking monsters, nor will anything you decide to store in the castle's chests ever be stolen or removed.  You are home."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:732
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1636
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you seek aid from Erathia, light the beacon fires near the roads to the Barrow Downs, Erathia, and the Tularean Forest.  The Erathian forces near here will see the fires and rush to your aid!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:733
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1637
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Lords. Castle Harmondale stands ready."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:734
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1638
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pedestals can be found through out the land that can lend you temporary protection from certain types of magic. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:735
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1639
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"::You receive a telepathic message:: My…Lords.  My name is Archibald Ironfist.  You've probably heard of me--it is I who, up until recently, was the ruler of the Pit.  With my retirement, I find myself no longer concerned with the affairs of state.  I know that we were adversaries, but I am forced to ask for your help.  In return, I think I can help you.\n"
"\n"
"With the aid of equipment I have found in my new laboratory, I have discovered that my brother Roland, husband to Queen Catherine of Erathia, remains imprisoned by the devils in their foul, ah, dwelling.  I overheard that you're on your way to do battle with them (this equipment really is wonderful), and I want to make sure it goes well.  My brother has stolen the key to their leader's chambers, and has hidden it in the beastly cage they're keeping him in.  \n"
"\n"
"Please rescue him!  Not even I can bear to think of my brother in those conditions!  To help you along, I offer this weapon.  It was...found by my loyal servant sergeant Piridak, amongst my advisor's personal belongings.  I hope it helps."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:736
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:203
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:318
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1640
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"::You receive a telepathic message:: My friends.  I know you are working with my old advisors, but I must ask for your help one more time.\n"
"\n"
"With the aid of equipment I have found in my new laboratory, I have discovered that my brother Roland, husband to Queen Catherine of Erathia, remains imprisoned by the devils in their foul, ah, dwelling.  I overheard that you're on your way to do battle with them (this equipment really is wonderful), and I want to make sure it goes well.  My brother has stolen the key to their leader's chambers, and has hidden it in the beastly cage they're keeping him in.  \n"
"\n"
"Please rescue him!  Not even I can bear to think of my brother in those conditions!  To help you along, I offer this weapon.  It was...found by my loyal servant sergeant Piridak, amongst my advisor's personal belongings.  I hope it helps."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:737
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1641
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our friend Tolberti has a job for you now.  Go to him, and he will instruct you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:738
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1642
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our friend Robert the Wise has a job for you now.  Go to him, and he will instruct you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:739
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1643
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This 1000 gold will go a long way to keeping zombies off the roads.  Thank you for your contribution."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:740
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1644
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That's a shame.  What a coincidence, I think I see some zombies on the roads.  Perhaps next time you'll be more inclined to contribute."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:741
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1645
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  Here is a crate of Arrowheads.  Pip Hillier in Erathia pays the best prices for these. Be sure to see him!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:742
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1646
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ahh, a shipment of Tularean Wood from my friend Robert Belknap.  I hope everything is well with him. Here's your payment."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:743
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1647
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here's your crate of Griffin Feathers.  Robert Belknap in the Tularean Forest pays the best prices for these feathers.  Be sure to give him my regards when you see him."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:744
