#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:8
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A large dragon obviously makes his residence in these caves.  The dead bodies near his home might have been adventurers seeking the dragon's treasure."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:9
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The enormous size and lavish decoration of Lord Markham's Manor provide a striking contrast to the humble peasant homes and huts nearby."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:10
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "From the looks of the trash and decaying garbage on the ground outside, many generations of bandits have used this cave to hide from the law."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:11
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Once a stately mansion, this old house has long been abandoned by the original owners.  The current residents don't seem to keep the place up very well."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:6
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:7
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:230
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The entrance to this barrow is pleasing to the eye, yet at the same time forbidding.  The air is very quiet near the entrance."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:15
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The door is unlocked and unguarded from the outside.  The iron on the doorknob is rusting, and you can see a small hornet's nest in the corner above the door."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:16
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A nasty odor wafts from the entrance of this cave, propelled by an unseen subterranean breeze.  It smells like decaying meat mixed with brimstone and…peppermint?  Whatever.  Looks dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:17
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The unassuming home of someone unimportant…or, at least someone who wishes to appear that way."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:18
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This tomb must be the resting place of an eccentric recluse.  The tomb doesn't appear to have been disturbed in quite some time."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:174
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:87
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:94
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The front door to your new home stands before you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:88
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The grand entrance to Castle Gryphonheart stands before you.  A pair of tame griffins can frequently be seen circling above the castle."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:178
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:89
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Castle Navan is the traditional seat of Elvish power.  Centuries of plant growth around the castle contribute to its sylvan character."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:180
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:90
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Who knows why the Necromancers felt the need to build a castle deep within the bowels of the earth?  Castle Gloaming is ugly, sinister, and very, very secure."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:182
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:91
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Floating above most clouds gives Castle Lambent more sunlight per year than any other location.  The elegant architecture takes full advantage of the weather."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:192
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:92
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The dripping of water and a strange, unidentifiable squeaking are the only noises that seem to come from the entrance to this cave."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:193
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:93
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A large dragon obviously makes his residence in these caves.  Perhaps this is where those missing adventurers are..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:195
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:95
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "These caves are the traditional hideout of goblins and bandits.  Whatever lives there now doesn't make the place smell too good…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:96
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Foul water pours from a large drain pipe coming from the Erathian Sewer.  It is said the Thieves' Guild can be found in here."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:197
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:97
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This mighty fort does a superb job guarding the East Bridge from invaders.  It doesn't look like visitors are welcome inside the fort."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:98
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Fresh human or elvish footprints lead into this cave, and weeds and brush have been cleared from the entrance recently."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:199
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:99
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Faint sounds of distant explosions and mad laughter can be heard from beyond the door.  There is a sharp, acidic smell in the air."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:200
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:100
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A frightening spectacle of shadowy claws and twisted demonic figures beckons you inside.  You can hear a woman singing in the distance, but can't quite make out the words."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:201
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:101
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The last of a series of watchtowers that once guarded the border of Deyja, Watchtower 6 is battle scarred, but still standing tall."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:202
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:102
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The sharp, electric smell of magic fills the air outside the School--the result of hundreds of years of magical experiments and juvenile pranks happening in the same building."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:203
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:103
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Though recently abandoned by the Dwarves, you can still easily see the craft and care they put into this mine."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:204
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:104
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The proving grounds of the Wizards, the Walls of Mist floats on the clouds like a mirage of the sky.  It is an entirely magical construct."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:205
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:105
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Temple of the Light is one of the most beautiful and serene places in the world.  Any follower of the Light can feel their troubles slipping away as they walk in these hallowed halls."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:206
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:106
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Traitors and prisoners of war are frequently thrown in this horrible pit as object lessons in cruelty.  All Necromancers must also enter the pit and escape before they can complete their apprenticeships."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:207
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:107
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Temple of the Dark is still in use by the forces of evil.  Sacrifices are held monthly, and foul rites are performed routinely on the front steps."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:208
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:108
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The sound of unholy chanting and the screams and moans of the undead can be heard quite clearly from the entrance.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:209
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:109
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Overgrown and weather beaten, the Grand Temple of the Sun has seen better days.  It appears someone is still taking care of the place."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:210
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:110
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Warlocks of Nighon call this extinct volcano their home.  A network of natural and carved tunnels spread away from the mountain, permitting travel throughout Nighon and across the sea."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:211
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:111
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A huge, magical maze stretches before you as far as the eye can see.  Looking at it for long dazzles the eyes and confuses the mind."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:212
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:112
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Stone City is one of the great bastions of the Dwarven race in the world.  The front gate looks very secure."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:213
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:113
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Words cannot convey the horror.  One of the pipes must be an entrance…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:214
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:114
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Mercenary Guild is home to every swordsman who fails at banditry.  Visitors are unwelcome."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:215
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:115
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "These caverns have been the hideout of pirates and ne'er-do-wells for centuries."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:216
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:116
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A trail of ominous brown stains leads downstairs and into darkness…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:217
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:117
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A mighty fortress housing the fantastic and murderous Titans.  No one has ever entered and returned to tell the tale."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:218
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:118
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Once the proud center of a false religion, the Temple has fallen into disrepair.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:219
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:119
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "It doesn't look like much, but getting in isn't easy.  Careful not to stray from the path."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:220
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:120
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This incredible starship is but a small sample of the wonders of the Ancients."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:221 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:8
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A thunderous howl pierces your ears, provoking a feeling of dread. Whatever produced that sound is drawing near, with each step rocking the earth beneath your feet."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:222 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:7
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "As you go deeper into this vast network of tunnels, your instinct tells you that many dangerous creatures dwell within. You vow to remain vigilant."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/TRANS.TXT.py:223
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This tunnel leads to Stone City."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am Lord Markham, the benefactor providing the castle that is the prize of the this contest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Nice to see you again, how are you doing on the hunt?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, my name is Thomas.  I am the judge of the contest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you collected everything on the list yet?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:119
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to Emerald Island, my name is Margaret and I'll be your docent for your stay here."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:119
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What would you like to know?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:120
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, my name is Ailyssa.  I'm the Bard in charge of overseeing the entertainment on Emerald Island for the duration of the Scavenger Hunt."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:120
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, how are you doing?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:121
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hi there!  I'm Sally.  I don't usually see people this far from town, are you lost?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:121
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Still out here?  Town's back a ways to the south."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:122
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pssst…  Come here, I have an offer for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:122
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you've returned, no doubt to listen to my proposal."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:123
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello there, stranger <wink>.  Fine weather we're having, no?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:123
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Did you need something, stranger?  <whisper> Get away from me, are you trying to get caught on purpose?!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:124
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello there, friend.  May I have a word with you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:124
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again… friend."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:125
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't believe we have anything to talk about."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:126
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail and well met.  I'm Brent Filiant, a contestant in Lord Markham's scavenger hunt."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:126
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings again, friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:127
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, I'm Carolyn.  I handle the guild memberships for the Fire and Air Guilds here on the island."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:128
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm Roger and I sell guild memberships for the Body and Spirit Guilds on Emerald Island."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:129
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ahoy matey!  I be William Darvees, captain of this vessel."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:129
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Aye, good to see you again, mates!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:15
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:130
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, my name is Donna, I live here with my daughter Sally."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:15
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:147
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:130
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:262
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:131
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hi, I'm Grant.  Tor allows me to live in the back of his shop as long as I stay his apprentice."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:131
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hi again, did you need something?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:132
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, I'm Mia.  Do you need something?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:132
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes?  What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:18
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:133
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  You do not have authorization to proceed.  We request that you refrain from disturbing the students while they work."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:134
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to Emerald Island.  I will be your guide during your stay here.  From time to time I will appear to tell you about something you're about to see to help you understand your New World.  If you tire of my messages (I won't be offended if you do), just click on my portrait to talk to me then click on 'Tour Off' to silence me.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:135
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The shop you are near is the Blacksmith shop.  The blacksmith only sells weapons, but this one sells many different kinds of weapons, and some of them have magical properties.  You can also sell weapons here, but you won't get a good deal until you have a higher merchant skill.  To enter, just click on the front door."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:136
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The door to the west leads to the local Tavern.  The tavern is a safe place to sleep at night, and to buy food so you can sleep outdoors.  You can often meet interesting people in taverns, or catch the local gossip if you're looking for something to do.  To enter the tavern, just click on the front door."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:137
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This shop is the armor shop.  The armorer only sells helms, shields, and armor, but will buy nearly anything you can wear, if you don't want to make a separate stop at the magic shop.  Remember that a character needs skill in leather, chain or plate armor to be able to wear that kind of armor, or shield skill to use a shield."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:138
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This building is Carolyn Weather's private residence.  Carolyn makes a living by brokering magic guild memberships to aspiring wizards and other spell casters.  She will be happy to sell membership in the local Air and Fire guilds for a small fee.  You don't have to buy membership in a guild if you don't want to, but remember that you must be a guild member to buy spells and learn skills at a magic guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:139
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This building is another private residence.  Roger, the owner of the house, sells membership in the Spirit and Body magic guilds here.  The price is low, but you must pay if you intend to take advantage of the guild services, including spell purchases and skill teaching.  By the way, if you're getting tired of my messages, you can stop them by clicking on my portrait to talk to me then clicking on the 'Tour Off' topic."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:140
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This door leads to the training center of Emerald Island.  If you have enough experience points (gained from killing monsters and completing quests) you can come here to increase your characters' levels.  When you gain a level, you'll also get some skill points to spend on improving your skills.  You can only spend skill points on skills that your character knows--to learn new skills, try visiting the businesses around town and see if they offer lessons in anything you're interested in."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:141
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This tent is where the town's healer is located.  You can pay for any healing your characters may need here--even raise them from the dead.  You can tell if your characters are injured by looking at the green bar to the left of their portrait--the lower it is, the more injured they are.  Note that it isn't necessary to get healed at the healer--any ordinary damage and all spell points will be healed merely for resting overnight.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:27
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:142
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This well has a magical benefit--it bestows a powerful fire resistance spell on the drinker.  To have a character drink from the well, just select the character you want to have drink, then click on the well. There are many wells like this one in the game--you can look in your autonotes book under the \"Fountains\" tab for a list of all wells you've tried drinking from during the course of the game.The effects of this particular well last until you rest, but remember that different wells may have completely different effects."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:143
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are standing in front of the house in which Lord Markham has set up his temporary headquarters on Emerald Island. Lord Markham is the benefactor behind the scavenger hunt you are no doubt eager to win.  The contest judge is also inside, and he is the one you need to talk to in order to turn in hunt items you have found."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:144
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Spirit Guild can be found through the door to the east.  You must have a membership to use the services of the Guild, which include spell purchase and skill teaching.  To become a Spirit Guild member, you must first visit Roger in his house a little way southeast of here and purchase a membership.  Also remember, a character who wishes to learn a Spirit spell must have the Spirit magic skill!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:145
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Air Guild is on the other side of this door.  You must have a membership to use the services of the Guild, which include spell purchase and skill teaching.  To become an Air Guild member, you must first visit Carolyn in her house a little way southeast of here and purchase a membership.  Also remember, a character who wishes to learn an Air spell must have the Air magic skill!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:146
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This building is where you will find the town Alchemist.  The alchemist sells potions and potions ingredients, and is also a place where your characters may learn the Alchemy skill.  You must have alchemy skill to make even the most basic of potions, and you can do that by opening your character's inventory, picking up a potion ingredient, and right clicking it on an empty potion bottle.  You can use a similar procedure to mix two potions together.  Alchemists know that certain mixtures produce certain results, but it's a trade secret.  You'll have to figure it out for yourself.  Be warned that some mixtures are explosive!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:147
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This door leads to the Body Guild.  You must have a membership to use the services of the Guild, which include spell purchase and skill teaching.  To become a Body Guild member, you must first visit Roger in his house a little way southeast of here and purchase a membership.  Also remember, a character who wishes to learn a Body spell must have the Body magic skill!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:33
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:148
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found the Magic shop.  The magic shop is every true adventurer's favorite store.  Here you can buy and sell all magic items except for magic weapons and armor.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:149
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This building is where you may find the Fire Guild.  You must have a membership to use the services of the Guild, which include spell purchase and skill teaching.  To become a Fire Guild member, you must first visit Carolyn in her house a little way southeast of here and purchase a membership.  Also remember, a character who wishes to learn a Fire spell must have the Fire magic skill!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:150
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Be careful!  You are about to enter an area of the island that is infested with Dragonflies.  They are quite dangerous!  Lord Markham is NOT responsible if you are injured or even killed venturing into this part of the island.  You have been warned!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:151
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Um…It isn't wise to enter this cave.  A terrible dragon lives within, and few who enter leave alive.  If you really want to enter, just click on the back wall of the cave…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:152
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This is the entrance to the old Temple of the Moon.  It is infested with small vermin that can give a nasty bite, but it's not too dangerous.  It's possible there are items for the scavenger hunt within, so you should consider searching here at some point.  To enter, just click on the back wall of this cave."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I’m Bill Lasker, and I am the Master Thief.  [Bill makes a sweeping gesture with one arm, taking in the whole of the sewers.] I am undisputed ruler of all I survey, and I hear of everything that happens in my mighty kingdom.  I am at your service."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back.  Is your visit for business, or conversation?  I’m happy to supply either."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I’m Bill Lasker, and I am the Master Thief.  I rule this underground kingdom, and am responsible for the welfare of the thieves who live down here.  You have been killing my subjects.  I would strike against you, but I fear your allies would destroy me.  So I will deal with you, but my prices will be higher.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[spits] Hello, Thief killer.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:155
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings Rogues, how may I be of service?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings.  I am Seknit Undershadow, Master Assassin for the Enforcement Arm of the Necromancer’s Guild.  I am pleased to meet you.  Would you like a cup of tea?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, welcome my friends.  How are you doing today?  You really should try my tea this time."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:157
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, welcome my friends.  I hope you are doing well.  How about a spot of tea today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:158
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, fellow Assassins.  My tea and company are always yours."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail.  I am Sir Charles Quixote.  I am the humble champion of the people, and I am at thy service."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well met, my friends.  How goes the struggle against the forces of evil?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:160
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why do we dally?  Even now that monster could be laying waste to the countryside!  Tally Ho!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:161
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why do we delay rescuing Alice?  Who knows what plans the fiend has for this innocent girl?  Let us replace talk with action and rescue the poor girl at once!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:162
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Salutations Heroes!  I am certain thou hast much to accomplish before we dally about."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello?  You don't look like William's normal people."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I just want to go home."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello?  I don't think I've seen you before."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now what do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day.  William Setag, Villain Extraordinare, at your service.  Good to make your acquaintance."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A pleasure to see you again.  How may I assist you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:166
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Villains!  Welcome!  Too rarely do my villainous friends pay me visits."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello.  I am Bartholomew Hume, Master of this monastery.  Is there something I can help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, do you need anything?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fellow Masters!  It is good to see you, how may I do you service?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings again, Masters.  How can Bartholomew aid you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:54
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:169
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, my pupils.  I see you have found the proper tomb."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am Stephan Sand, Master of the…aggressive side of the disciplined life.  Once I was a monk, now I am something greater."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again.  Tell me what it is you desire."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you've achieved the exhalted status of Ninja, I have nothing further to give you.  I hope my teachings take you far."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you've achieved the exaulted status of Ninja, I have nothing further to give you.  I hope my teachings take you far."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:57
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you doing?  [Lawrence bows deeply) I am Master Mark, champion bowman.  I've won the Annual Avlee Tourney for the past 4 years!  But enough of me, how about yourselves?  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:57
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We meet again.  Need something?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:58
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:173
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome my friends!  That's a fine weapon you have there, but don't think for a moment you'll best me in this year's Tourney--I'm still the Master!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:59
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome.  [Mr. Snick barely speaks above a whisper.  There is a small, white scar at the base of his throat] Are you here to be trained?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:59
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have a reason... [Snick wheezes] for troubling me, I hope?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:60
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:175
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Students…[Mr. Snick rasps the word, then smiles] no longer.  I am proud to have helped you on your way.  Use your new weapon…[wheeze] wisely."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:61
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well met!  [Leda draws her blade and chops smartly at the wind] Are you here to fight, or here to learn?  Either way [her flourish ends in a knight's salute] I'm happy to oblige!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:61
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, and well met!  [Leda grins and shakes her head] I love saying that!  So.  What can I do for you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:62
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:177
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, champions!  Your courage and skill has all the tongues in the Kingdom wagging!  I am very proud of you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:63
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So!  You wish to learn to fight?  Well, you've found the right man.  For those of you who are Knights, anyway.  If you're not a knight, you still benefit from my teachings, but not as much."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:63
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Back for more teaching, kid?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:64
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:179
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Frederick rises hastily to his feet] None shall pass! [he blinks and rubs his eyes] Oh.  It's you.  Sorry, I thought you were someone else.  How goes the villainy?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Lysander doffs his hat and bows deeply] Salutations!  I am Lysander Sweet, and I am in charge of promoting Hunters to Rangers.  I have a task in mind if I think you're up to it.  It should prove quite educational!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Lords of Harmondale return!  I am honored.  What is your pleasure, my lords?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:66
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:181
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your good works have served the forest well.  And, I can see, the experience has served you well in turn.  May you continue to reap the rewards of your good deeds, my friends!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:67
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmmm. Make it quick!  You look like time wasters to me.  There's nothing worse.  You know, when I was a boy, my elders didn't tolerate no one lolligaggin around.  No slackers, neither.  [Ebednezer squints and leans closer to you] You're not one of them, are you?  Slackers? 'Cause I don't talk to slackers."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:67
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Time!  Everyone wastin' my time! [Ebednezer mutters something incoherent under his breath for awhile] You're still here?  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bounty Hunters.  [Ebednezer smiles slowly and evilly]  Now THERE'S a job!  Yes sir.  Get things done righteo quick, I'll venture. Heh."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bounty Hunters.  [Ebednezer smiles slowly and evilly]  Now THERE'S a job!  Yes sir.  Get things done righteo quick, I'll say. Heh."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The little king bows] Welcome to my realm, mortals!  Few attain the door, and for that, I commend thee.  But now that you stand at the threshold of Faerie, know that few return that dare to enter."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mortals!  You have found a way in, but can you remember the way out?  [the king laughs] Twisty the way, and treacherous the path!  Stay, instead, and feast with us!  The centuries pass like lazy Sunday afternoons!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:70
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:185
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, travellers. [the tree speaks VERY slowly] How.  Are.  You.  Today?   The trees are quite disturbed.  Angry.  The Heart of the Wood has been stolen by Walkers.  The Walkers will pay in blood until the Heart is returned."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:70
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:185
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you the same Walkers I just talked to?  You all look alike to me.  But the talking is good just same.  Do you have time?  Let.  Me.  Name.  My.  Ancestors.  [The tree sighs happily, and begins]  Leaf-point.  Who.  Spawned. Spotted Bark.  Who.  Spawned.  Three Branches.  Who spawned...[Blah, blah blah]"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The trees speak of Walkers who want to return our Heart.  I hope they do.  Walkers take so much."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:72
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:187
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ohhhhh…It's the Walkers from the South.  I remember you!  You returned the Heart.  The trees are very happy, and promise not to kill any more walkers.  Come and talk to me any time."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:73
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:188
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[High Priest Devine smiles and inclines her head] Sunlight Reveal, my lords.  How may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sunlight Reveal, my fellow Priests.  I am so proud to have you as members of our faith!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sunlight Reveal, my fellow Priests.  I am always delighted to see you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:75
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[High Priest Falk bows and clasps his hands together] Shadow Conceal, Lords.  How may I be of service?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shadow Conceal, Brethren.  Congratulations on your promotion to Priests of the Dark."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shadow Conceal, Brethren.  My time is always yours."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thomas Grey, at your service!  [The Wizard bows quickly and spreads his palms, smiling] "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Thomas Grey offers a peculiar half smile and folds his arms] I am still at your service, my lords!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My fellow Archmages.  Rare is the individual who can achieve this status.  Congratulations!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am honored to be graced with your presence, my lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:79
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:194
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[The Lich stares at you awhile before speaking] Who dares disturb me?  Earthly Lords?  Hmmph.  Your status matters not, once death's door has been passed."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:79
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why do you insist on bothering me?  [The Lich's eyes flare a hellish red for a moment] "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Death…[The Lich's voice is hoarse and quavery] isn't so bad when you've been through it once or twice.  Life was always more painful to me.  Are you pleased with your new status?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:81
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:196
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pleasant weather we're having, isn't it?  We are blessed to live in this climate, and have such mild Gods to appease.  Have you offered recently?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:81
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fortune be your friend, lords.  Do you seek my advice today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was pleased to offer the Ceremony of Ascension to you after your brave efforts to lay the dead to rest.  The world breathes easier from your help."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:83
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:198
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Foreign Lords!  How interesting!  My familiar said she could smell the earth of the lands across the sea on you.  My name is Tor Anwyn, leader of the Warlocks of Nighon, though not King of Nighon.  That title belongs to another.  Pleased to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:83
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A delight and a pleasure, lords.  Have you come for business or conversation?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations on your promotions to Warlock!  Few can pass the test and find themselves an appropriate familiar.  I'm pleased you were successful."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:85
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:200
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am yours to command, master."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the new lords! Please excuse the condition of the castle--it's been awhile since anyone has taken proper care of it.  I would have greeted you indoors, but for the Goblins.  A small tribe of them has moved inside.  I've asked them to leave, but they won't listen to me.  They were quite rude, as a matter of fact.  Perhaps you could...talk to them?  I'll be in the On the House Tavern here in Harmondale should you manage to 'convince' them to leave."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There's still goblins in the castle, my lords.  I hope you don't mind if I wait here while you convince them to leave.  One way or the other."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:87
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:202
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You rang, my lords?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:88
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So.  Lords of Harmondale, eh?  I am King Hothfarr IX, Lord of Stone City.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:88
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Back again?  Don't have much time for [heh!] Contestants.  State your case and move on.  My court is busy."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:89
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:204
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome, Harmondale!  Stone city is at your disposal."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Everybody run!  The Stonesnakes are upon… uh… what?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for rescuing me.  I am at your service."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ahhhhh!  Help!  They're coming  fo… me?  What happened?  Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for rescuing me.  I owe you my life."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Lady Ellen curtsies gracefully]  I am Ellen Rockway.  I speak for Erathia on matters of state.  I will be staying here in your court for the duration of your reign."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, Lords?  What would you like to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings.  I am Alain Hani, Ambassador from Avlee.  I speak for my country, and my word is Avlee's bond.  I will always be available for any business you wish to conduct."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Avlee is listening, my Lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:94
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lord Markham tells me you are the new lords of Harmondale.  Welcome to the peerage.  Now, why do you request an audience of me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:94
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:209
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am very busy.  This had better not be a social visit."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, Harmondale.  Before we conduct business, I would like to say I recently noticed you returned the wrong prisoner from Avlee.  Such a remarkable likeness!  I should execute you, but the war is over, and that would be bad form.  Just remember that your treachery has been...noted."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:96
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, Harmondale has new lords.  Again.  Well, [King Parson looks at his scribe] we better write their names down lest history blinks and misses them, eh?  Haw haw ha!  [Ahem] Yes.  Well, you had a reason for visiting me, right?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:96
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:211
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Harmondale again, hmmm?  Make it quick--my patience is already wearing thin."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You again?  You know, I was just asking my generals why the attack on Fort Riverstride was such a disaster when someone on my staff noticed the traps on the map YOU gave us were in the wrong places!  [the King chuckles, smiling] Imagine my generals' relief when we all realized that it wasn't incompetence that killed 74 elves, but treachery! Hahahahaha! [King Parson slaps his knee, then abruptly stops laughing and stares at you.]\n"
"\n"
"I would execute the lot of you, but the war is over. In the interests of harmony, you can live.  For now."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:98
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My lords, I have an urgent message from the Erathian Ambassador for you.  I am told it has details of an important event that is happening RIGHT NOW, and that you should read it immediately.  Here is the letter."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:99
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you doing, my lords?  I am Judge Grey.  I have the unusual job of arbitrating disputes between warring nations.  The position has it's rewards, but you'll never hear the people you're helping thank you.  I always know I'm doing the right thing when both sides are angry with me at once."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:99
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back, my lords.  Erathia and Avlee are at each other's throats again.  Feeling the heat yet?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ah, greetings!  My lords, I am Ambassador Wright from Bracada.  You know, the wizards on Erathia's southern border.  You've become very important persons!  Since Judge Grey died in your lands, you must choose another Arbiter to help settle the dispute between Erathia and Avlee.  \n"
"\n"
"I formally invite you to visit Bracada and meet Judge Fairweather, who we strongly recommend for the post.  I don't mean to be pushy, but I'm sure you understand your choice will affect future relations between our two governments..."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My lords, it is always a pleasure to see you.  I must once again urge you to consider our uh, I mean Judge Fairweather for the important post of Arbiter.  Take your time making the decision, but do be quick about it, eh?\n"
"\n"
"Remember, all you have to do is visit Judge Fairweather in Bracada and choose him for the job; then take him to the Arbiter's house here in Harmondale.  I am sure he will put a swift end to this nasty war."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:101
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A pleasure to meet you, my lords.  My name is Ambassador Scale, and I represent Deyja, the land of the Necromancers northwest of Erathia.  Now, I know what you're thinking--Necromancy!  Yuck!  Isn't that death magic?  Well, it IS, but we merely pursue knowledge for it's own sake; rather noble if you ask me.  We're not so bad.  You should speak with some of the fellows--they really know how to party.  [The Ambassador forces a smile] Ha ha ha!\n"
"\n"
"I invite you to visit Deyja.  When Judge Grey died, you became the ones who must choose his successor.  We have someone in mind who will encourage our enemies to...um...bring this terrible war to an end.  Yes.  I urge you to choose Judge Sleen.  \n"
"\n"
"It would mean so much to us, and we could do so much for you!  Think about it, but don't think too long!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:101
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My lords.  [Ambassador Scale wrings his hands and smiles in a most unsettling fashion]  You are still trying to make a decision, I see.  You must understand your choice is VERY important to us.  \n"
"\n"
"Perhaps you need directions?  Judge Sleen is in Deyja, which is the country northwest of Erathia.  You must do is visit him and tell him you're choosing him for the job; then take him to the Arbiter's house here in Harmondale.  He will take care of everything from there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:102
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The new lords of Harmondale, I presume.  I am Judge Sleen.  Let me be frank--my sympathies lie with Deyja and the Necromancers.  We want you to choose me for the job of Arbiter for the war between Erathia and Avlee.  Since both of those countries are the enemies of Deyja, I will be a fair judge.  However, choosing to be the ally of Deyja means CHOOSING WHAT OTHERS CALL \"DARKNESS\".\n"
"\n"
"This darkness business is pure rot.  Necromancy is nothing but the study death and what happens with the spirit after death.  Sure, the results can be a little grisly, but so is making sausage and the practice of law.  And nobody would say those jobs don't have their value.\n"
"\n"
"Choose me and be our ally.  Because if you cannot prove your friendship through this simple act, what else can you be but our enemy?  Remember, though, that once you choose me, you cannot later change your mind.  Your choice is permanent."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:102
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Still considering your choice, I see.  Let me remind you of what's at stake:  [The Ambassador holds up a finger]\n"
"\n"
"The length of the war--The longer it lasts, the better off we'll all be.  Erathia and Avlee will be weaker, and unable to interfere in our affairs.\n"
"\n"
"You will be allying with us.  There are things we can teach you...\n"
"\n"
"Most importantly, YOU WILL CHOOSE THE PATH OF DARKNESS.  This choice cannot be withdrawn."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:103
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:218
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for choosing me.  You will not regret your choice, I assure you.  The only thing that remains is for you to return to Harmondale with me, and bring me to the Judge Grey's old house.  I'll take it from there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:103
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:218
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We need to go to Judge Grey's old house in Harmondale.  Only then can I start my new job and begin to \"sort out this mess\".  [Heh!]"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:104
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have made the right choice, my lords.  The leader of Deyja, Archibald Ironfist, would like to speak with you.  From the Deyja Moors, enter the Hall of the Pit and make your way to the Pit.  Archibald awaits you in Castle Gloaming in the Pit.  Try not to keep him waiting."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:104
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am happy to see you again, my lords.  Deyja is very pleased with the way things have turned out.  Is there anything I can do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:105
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hello.  I've been expecting you.  I am Judge Fairweather.  I think it's important you understand that I DO work for Bracada, but I am neutral on the Erathia - Avlee war.  Obviously, we want you to hire me as the Arbiter over this conflict, and I will be a fair judge.  We need you to understand, however, that choosing me as the Arbiter will be CHOOSING THE PATH OF LIGHT.\n"
"\n"
"It is the right choice.  I will put an end to this destructive war as quickly as possible, and minimize deaths.  All you have to do is make a decision.\n"
"\n"
"Please choose the path of light, and reject evil.  Be our ally.  Just remember that whatever choice you make will be a permanent one."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:105
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No decision yet?  Why do you waver in the face of what is clearly the moral choice?  Think about it:\n"
"\n"
"Choosing me puts an end to the war quickly.  Many people will have you to thank for saving their lives.\n"
"\n"
"You will be allying with Bracada, and rejecting Deyja.  All the Light has to offer will be yours to learn.\n"
"\n"
"Most importantly, you will be CHOOSING THE PATH OF LIGHT.  This choice is permanent, and cannot be withdrawn."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:106
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank the heavens for guiding you right!  This is the best decision you have ever made, even if you don't believe it now.  The only thing left to do is for you to return to Harmondale with me, and bring me to Judge Grey's old house.  I'll see that matters are handled correctly."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:106
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We need to go to Judge Grey's old house in Harmondale.  Only then can I start my new job and put this horrible war to an end."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:107
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have made the wise choice, my lords.  Gavin Magnus, leader of the Wizards, would like to speak with you.  Go to the Bracada Desert-- the teleporter to Celeste will function now, and use it to enter Celeste.  Gavin awaits you in Castle Lambent.  Time is precious; don't waste it dallying around."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:107
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am happy to see you again, my lords.  Bracada is very pleased with the way things have turned out.  Is there anything I can do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:108
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"New Lords from Harmondale, I see.  Well, I am pleased to meet you at last.  I am sure the relationship between our two governments will be a long and mutually beneficial one.  You've made the right choice in allying with us.  There is much we need to talk about, but my advisors first insist that you walk the Wizards' Path before our relationship can progress.\n"
"\n"
"I know this test seems silly, but I assure its purpose is not.  You can take the test whenever you feel ready.  And if you fail today, you can always come back and try it another day."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:108
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Always good to see you, my friends.  Do you feel up to completing my little test?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:109
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:224
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back, my friends.  My advisors are anxious to speak with you.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:110
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am very lucky to have friends such as you.  We've come far, and only have a little further to go.  My most unusual advisors have great plans…plans that require the aid of you, my steadfast allies.  I'm confident you're up to it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:111
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"[Resurectra smiles, and curtseys] Lords.  I am Resurectra, chief advisor to King Magnus.  We are pleased you chose Judge Fairweather as the arbiter in the Erathia-Avlee conflict.  It's a sign of your good intentions.  However, if we are to have further dealings, you must first complete the King's test.  We do not have time for the the uncommitted or the faint of heart.\n"
"\n"
"After you are done with his test, return to me, and we will talk.  Rest assured you will find your alliance with us profitable."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:111
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, Lords.  You haven't completed the King's test yet.  I will not deal with you until you have finished his test.  Return to me when you are done."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:112
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am glad you passed the King's test.  It shows you are dedicated to the Path of Light.  Now we should get down to business.  My fellow advisors and I have some work for you if you're willing.  You will, of course, be rewarded.  And always remember, that whatever we ask of you, we are always moving toward a noble goal, one you will be proud to have been a part of."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:112
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:113
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:227
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Always a pleasure to see you, Lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:113
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Once again, thanks for completing the key for us.  We are in your debt for that act alone.  I'm sure we will be even more in your debt in the near future."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:114
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dark ones!  You have no idea what dreams you've discarded in favor of petty power.  Begone from here, and trouble us no more."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:114
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Sigh] Why have you returned?  I want nothing to do with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:115
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:230
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you have completed the Test, I too, have a request of you.  Unlike my friends, mine has little to do with advancing toward the Goal, but it is important nonetheless."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:115
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:116
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:230
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's good to see you again, lords.  I hope all is well with you and your realm."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:116
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I just want to say again that you've done a good thing.  Not only have we kept our promise to Queen Catherine, but we have rid the world of another monster.  Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:117
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What do you want, evil ones?  My axe itches for a chance at your throats."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:117
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have nothing to say to you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:118
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm pleased to hear you passed the test.  We must attack our enemies before they get too strong.  I have a plan I think will do lasting damage to their noxious brotherhood.  It's dangerous but bold, and cowards such as they will never expect it."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:118
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:119
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:233
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, welcome back my lords.  I hope all is well."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:119
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Glad you're here.  You'll be happy to know we've ordered a golem to bury the empty soul jars somewhere and forget where it put them.  They'll never be seen again."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:120
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, good, a visit from our enemies.  That always makes me so happy!  Come back anytime, so our guards can have another try at your lives, knaves!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:120
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our guards missed you again?  I'll have to talk to them about that."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:121
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Like my friends, I have a task for you as well, but now is not the time.  Finish their work first, then I will tell you about my mission."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:121
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm happy you're still alive and working for the Light.  Come and see me when you've finished my friend's tasks."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:122
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've finished their missions.  Good.  Our conflict with the Necromancers is rapidly coming to a conclusion.  I have a dangerous, but critical mission for you.  The future of your…er, our world depends on your success."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:122
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm glad you're back, friends.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:123
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Pleased to make your acquaintance.  My name is Kastore, chief advisor to Lord Ironfist.  [Kastore makes a sweeping gesture toward the other advisors] My associates and I agree that you've shown excellent taste so far over your choice of Judge Sleen in the Erathia affair.  I think future relations between Deyja and Harmondale will be quite rosy and profitable for all involved.\n"
"\n"
"However, I never trust someone I just met.  Before we can do business, you'll have to prove that you're...our kind of people.  Lord Ironfist has a test he likes to put new Necromancer recruits through.  If you can pass it, return to me and we'll talk more."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:123
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Although there are many things we could do for one another, you must first pass Lord Ironfist's test.  [Kastore snorts derisively] Because if you can't even pass THAT sorry test, what good are you to me, let alone yourselves?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:124
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you passed the test!  Good!  Now we can get down to business.  You'll find that working for us…[Kastore shakes his head, and starts over] No.  You'll find that working with us will advance our mutual goals and interests very quickly.  We have big plans--plans big enough to include aggressive people like yourselves.  As time passes, we will reveal our biggest plans to you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:124
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:125
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:239
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Kastore smiles] Welcome back, allies.  I trust you are well?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:125
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would like to take this moment to thank you, again, for all the work you have done for us.  The time fast approaches that our greatest plans will come to fruition, and we will all be elevated to the highest status!  Stick by us awhile longer, and your rewards will be greater that you have ever dreamed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:126
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lords of Harmondale, is it? [Kastore spits on the ground] What are you doing here?  Better return home and watch your border!  Something dark may cross it during the night…"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:126
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What now?!? Wasn't it hard enough to get here the first time?  Do you think we have anything at all to say to each other?  Begone!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:127
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello!  I am Maximus.  Good to have you on our side.  I'm glad you survived the Test.  I'm against wasting good talent on that test, but my associates insist.  [sigh]  What can you do?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:127
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:128
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:242
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Glad to have you back, allies."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:128
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I really can't thank you enough for bringing those jars back to us.  The Necromancers have been clamoring for their delivery for months!  This will improve morale around here 100%!  Once again, thanks!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:129
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:244
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have nothing to say to you, cowards!  One day, you and your entire town will be working in the mines for us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:130
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I knew you would pass that Test!  It really isn't that hard, if you are properly determined.  You just have to harden your heart and do what must be done.  The mission I have in mind for you will require that same resolve.  After you passed that test, I'm sure you're up to it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:130
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:131
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:245
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome, allies.  Always good to have you back."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:131
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent work at Clanker's Laboratory!  I know I already congratulated you on a job well done, but I just can't get over how well executed that entire plan was!  The boys in the lab tell me they've already got most of old Clanker's body back together again, and they've animated the reassembled corpse.  They've got him on Soul Jar research, but he's not quite as clever as he used to be, I'm told.  Oh well, at least we don't need to fear him turning on us, eh?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:132
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Honestly, didn't you people get the hint when all our minions were attacking you?  We don't want you down here!  And it doesn't do you any good blowing up our zombies--we just reanimate them!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:133
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I, too, have a task for you in mind, but it will have to wait until you are done with my associates' missions.  Return to me once you have finished their tasks."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:133
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Glad you're still on our side!  Come and see me when you're done with my associates' missions."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:134
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Now that you've finished my associate's tasks, I am ready to give you a much more dangerous, but very critical mission.  Our plans hinge on your success.  I know I can count on you.\n"
"\n"
"Oh, I almost forgot to mention!  Archibald is no longer in charge.  He left in a huff after we disagreed with how we should proceed with our plans.  He's moved into Clanker's laboratory now, and taken some of the less...motivated necromancers with him.  No loss there.  Kastore is King of the Pit, now."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:134
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome, friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:135
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"[Archibald smiles and rubs his hands together slowly] Our new allies from Harmondale!  Good to meet you in person at last.  I want to say right now that you chose the right side.  Anyone who has ever dealt with me knows I am a fair man to work for, and I reward loyalty well.  Stand by me, and you will go farther than you ever dreamed! \n"
"\n"
"While I am grateful that you chose us, and have complete confidence in your abilities and loyalties, my advisors do not.  That's ok, because they're here to question my judgement.  They believe that you don't have the stomach to work for us, and have devised a little test of your...determination.  I know it's annoying, but until you pass the test, they refuse to have anything to do with you.  I'm sure you understand."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:135
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How goes your preparations for the test?  You can take it anytime you want…just walk on down to the Breeding Pit and jump in.  [Archibald smiles, his face half hidden in shadow] It's always open."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:136
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hello, my friends…you are still my friends, aren't you?  My \"advisors\", my \"lieutenants\" [Archibald spits out the words], have the Pit, and their dreams of conquest.  I have come to realize they did not need me, nor did they want to study our art.  \n"
"\n"
"They want a world where there are no Kings, no loyalty, and no honor.  Just them and their slaves.  Well, they can have it!  After the soul jars were stolen, my lieutenants just shrugged, as though it was wagon wheels, or chickens that went missing, not the keys to immortality!  We were so close to devising a way to keep the body from decay after the Ritual was performed!  Now this--a setback that will cost decades.\n"
"\n"
"So, we have moved here--thanks to you--to continue our studies.  For what it's worth, I have renounced my claim to the throne of Enroth.  I don't think anyone believes me, but that shouldn't matter.  This island is quite secure, and we have fixed the breech that let you infiltrate it in the first place. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:136
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good to see you again, my friends.  You are welcome to visit anytime."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:137
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Find what you're looking for?  Don't worry--I'm not too angry that you invaded.  Most of my minions will regenerate, one way or the other.  There's not even much treasure left.\n"
"\n"
"[Sigh] Well, if you're here to fight us in the name of the Light, don't bother.  I've given up the conquest business.  My former allies [Archibald spits on the ground] have abandoned our great achievements in the arts of Necromancy, and now seek merely to conquer the world.  I have little doubt they will succeed.  It won't go well for you and your masters if they do.\n"
"\n"
"[Archibald looks at you more closely, now] Then again, perhaps they won't.  You have the smell of fate about you, as though you are destined for great things.  Perhaps you will stop them.  But smart money still bets against you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:137
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Back for more target practice?  You know, if you wait long enough, my people will regenerate.  Bigger challenge then."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:138
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back, allies.  My advisors are eager to speak with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:139
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:254
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excuse me, but visitors are not allowed here in Fort Riverstride.  I'm afraid I have to ask you to leave.  Any attempt to go further into the fort will be treated as hostile action, and will be dealt with as such."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:140
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This Watchtower preserves the borders of Deyja.  Visitors are not allowed in here, so you will have to leave.  If you attempt to enter further into the tower, you will be killed without hesitation."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:141
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:256
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  You have no business past this point.  Only those who have proved their purity may enter the holy sanctum. "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:142
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:257
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What have we here?  Did you honestly think you could tread safely amongst the power of the shadows?  It would not be safe for you, and you are not allowed past this point."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:143
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:258
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  You do not have authorization to proceed this way.  If you are looking for Queen Catherine's throne room, it is in the center of the castle behind the main staircase."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:144
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:259
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  Visitors aren't permitted in this section of the castle.  If you are looking for King Parson's throne room, take the lift down and follow the left corridor."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:145
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:260
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  Access to these areas is denied on orders from Gavin Magnus himself.  If you are looking for his throne room, go north from the entrance as far as you can, then go west as far as you can, and his throne room is to the north."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:146
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  You don't have permission to proceed through this area.  If you are looking for the throne room, you must go north from the entrance to the main room.  Then follow the small west passage to the waiting ship.  Use the ship's rudder to maneuver downstream and then exit the ship and proceed in the doorway."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:147
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:262
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings!  My name is Eric Swarrel-- I run the information desk here in the School of Sorcery."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:148
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:263
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for rescuing me!  Please take me back to Erathia as soon as you can."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:148
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:263
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are we almost back to Erathia?  I have information for Queen Catherine that cannot wait."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:149
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:264
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent decision to assist King Parson.  Just get me to Queen Catherine, and I'll handle the rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:150
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:265
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt!  Lord Markham doesn't want visitors wandering around his house.  If you came to speak with him, he's in his chamber directly north from the entrance."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:151
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:266
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My lords, I have been dispatched by the ambassadors from Erathia and Avlee to inform you of Judge Grey's untimely death.  We believe it was a heart attack, and there is no reason to suspect foul play.  \n"
"\n"
"However, they wish to speak to you at once, and urge you to return to your castle.  They have declared a truce until a successor can be found for Judge Grey."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:152
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:267
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, the new lords of Harmondale!  Just the persons I needed to see! "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:153
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:268
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for returning the Lantern of Light.  Ceremonies can continue normally at the temple!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:154
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:269
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the Lords of Harmondale. Perhaps you can be of assistance to me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:155
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:270
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My thanks for returning Haldar's remains!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:156
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:271
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lords of Harmondale, I need your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:157
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:272
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for returning my signet ring and restoring my business!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:158
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:273
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, you must be the Lords of Harmondale.  I am a collector of the finest historical items, perhaps you can deliver something to me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:159
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:274
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for returning the Parson's Quill sent by Lord Markham.  You help has made my collection complete!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:160
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:275
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings!  You're the new Lords of Harmondale, if I'm not mistaken.  Do you have a moment to assist me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:160
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:275
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again, Lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:161
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:276
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you so much for returning the Faerie Pipes to me!  I would have never been able to brave the Hall under the Hill myself."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:162
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:277
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My…'lords,' I have a message for you from Niles Stantley, an associate of Mr. Malwick, whom I'm sure you've already met.  I'd advise you to read this message and act on it with all due speed… Mr. Stantley does so admire punctuality."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:162
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:277
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I bring you news from Harmondale.  It seems members of the Mercenary Guild have found it quite the easy pickings, and have begun looting the city and the castle there."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:163
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:278
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, my friends.  I've come to collect on the deal you made with my associate, Mr. Malwick.  I trust you remember him from Emerald Isle?  "
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:163
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:278
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again.  I hope, for your sake, you're complying with my request."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:164
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:279
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, my lords.  Do you have a moment to assist an old dwarf in need?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:164
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:279
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Please assist us; Stone City would be in your debt."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:165
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:280
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for helping us by getting rid of those nasty Troglodytes!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:166
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:281
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day, my lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:167
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:282
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work on those griffins, my lords.  It is always a pleasure to see you."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:168
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:283
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have nothing to say to you.  Go away."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:169
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:284
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your lack of punctuality has cost yourselves and your town grievously.  I think you may find your bank account somewhat… pinched.  Consider this an important lesson learned.  Good day."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:170
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:285
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Growf!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:171
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:286
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, my lords.  May I have a moment of your time?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:171
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:286
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good to see you again, my lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:172
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:287
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well met, lords.  Do you have a moment to share?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:172
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:287
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A pleasure to see you again, lords."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:173
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:288
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Thanks for getting me out of that cage.  I thought I had managed to escape when I was able to steal a key from the guard, but it didn't open my cage!  Whatever it's used for, I'm sure you'll find it more useful than I will. \n"
"\n"
"I need to get back to my kingdom right away; who knows what sort of horrible things have happened while I've been away.  Excuse me for my abruptness, but I want to breathe fresh air again.  You've done both Erathia and Enroth a great service, and I'm in your debt."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:173
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:288
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How wonderful to see you again.  Thanks for helping me escape the Kreegan.  If you should find yourselves in Enroth, come by and visit Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:174
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:289
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "May I have a moment of your time?"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:175
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:290
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent work; my associates are quite pleased."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:291
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, lords.  Welcome to my humble home."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:291
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings again, lords.  May your stay here be a pleasant one."
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:177
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:292
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for your assistance in completing my collection.  You have my gratitude forever!"
msgstr ""

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/npcgreet.txt.py:178
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:293
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day!  Would you like to hear about the ArcoMage Championship?"
