#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:15
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back to the Guildhouse of the Merchants of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We have identified those we believe would join an alliance to stand against the crisis. These are: the Minotaurs of Ravage Roaming, the Clerics of the Temple of the Sun in Murmurwoods, the Dragons of Garrote Gorge, the Necromancers' Guild in Shadowspire, and Charles Quixote's Dragon hunting camp in Garrote Gorge.\n"
"\n"
"Now none of us believe that you can get all of them to work together, but with us and the Trolls already with the alliance, it should suffice if three of the five join us.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps you should begin by speaking with Sahil Ittalle who lives at the north end of the town. He is our guild's historian and the best person to brief you on our potential allies' various dispositions."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am Overdune, I hunt meat for the village of Rust. Or I did so before the lake of fire came to destroy our homes."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are back. How goes it with you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:18
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Leave me be. I morn the death of Vilebite, my son."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Th-thank you for giving my son Vilebite his rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Come in…you are always welcome here."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is only because you are under Bastian Loudrin's protection that I have allowed you this audience. Know you stand before Deftclaw Redreaver, Ultimate Flightleader of the Dragons of Jadame. I am not to be tarried with. Speak your business!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You disturb me again? This had best be important."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:21
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:34
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:83
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:101
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:83
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sir Charles Quixote at your service. Welcome to my camp headquarters. From here I oversee this hunting expedition.\n"
"\n"
"Are you here to trade? Most of what my goods are committed to orders already. I do, however, have some baby dragons for sale. And I suppose I could part with some of the lower grade adult hides."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You just caught me. I'm almost ready to leave for Ravenshore, but how may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was a long journey, but here I am. Good to see you again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail the alliance! How goes it with you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "And so I have made haste to Ravenshore. Already I grow weary of life among the prey animals. You had best be quick about the business of this alliance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, what is it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:27
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It has been a long time since I have traveled. I forget how beautiful parts of this land can be. I look forward to resolving the current crisis--the very least reason being that I can then take a long deserved sabbatical."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is good to see you again, friends. Thanks to you, things go well at Balthazar Lair. Already my herd has made great progress towards restoring our homes and shops. Perhaps you have visited the restored city?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Things go well for us in our war against the Temple of the Sun. Before I left, I saw the Shadowspire border made secure. Daily our troops force theirs back to their main temple in Murmurwoods.\n"
"\n"
"Again, on behalf of the Necromancers' Guild, I thank you. Now, let us get on with the business at hand."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, guild friends."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. I am Masul, Herdmaster of Balthazar Lair. On behalf of my herd, I thank you for saving us. I was sure that we were destined to perish. Now it seems we will survive. I look forward to rebuilding our lair."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How may I serve the saviors of my herd?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wha…who is it? Who is it! You may think my injuries make me easy prey raiders! But know my axe is sharp, and…and…hey…\n"
"\n"
"You're not the raiders! Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:31
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:81
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:95
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:96
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:112
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:81
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:96
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hail to you. I am Sandro. Thant and I are the high guildmasters of the Necromancers' Guild. With our fortunes diminished in Erathia and Enroth, it could be argued that we speak for the guild worldwide.\n"
"\n"
"We have heard that you are envoys from Bastian Loudrin. What is his need of us?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What is it? Be quick! We are very busy."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:33
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hah! The only advantage that the Sun Temple had against us is no more. With the Nightshade Brazier back in our possession, we no longer need worry about the daytime defense of Shadowspire. We can march our undead to their very doors. We will destroy their temple and wipe them from the face of Jadame! \n"
"\n"
"Now that the tide of battle has turned in our favor, we of the Necromancers' Guild can more generously consider the request made by our friend, Bastian Loudrin. Thant can take over here while I am away sitting on your alliance council."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who are you? I don't recognize you, but I'm sure that whatever your business, it will add to my troubles."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, Sandro has asked you to strike a blow against the Sun Temple! Though I hate the guild. I would be willing to help you. Half a serving of revenge is better than none."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, do we move against the Sun Temple? Shall we get for Sandro his Nightshade Brazier?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you are sent by his high holiness…Oskar Tyre thinks to activate his agent. Though I would wish him no good, I will do as he asks. Yes, I have knowledge of the guild's Skeleton Transformer and believe I can destroy it. Very well, let us do this thing against the Necromancers' Guild. I will at least be able to strike against one of my enemies!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you now ready to destroy the guild's Skeleton Transformer? I will join you and we can be about the task!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hah! So both Sandro and Oskar Tyre seek to use me against the other. I have thought of the possibility of this occurring. I believe that if I were to strike against one, it would become impossible for me to strike the other.\n"
"\n"
"So I guess we have a choice--help the guild or the temple. Which? I don't know, as my hatred for both is equal. I suppose I'll have to do with a half measure of revenge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, have you decided to steal the Nightshade Brazier from the Temple, or to destroy the guild's Skeleton Transformer? Either way…I will join you. But let us do it. I would slack my thirst for revenge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you are sent by Bastian Loudrin? Well, then. What would he have us hear?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Light upon you. What need you of our temple?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hail, heroes of Jadame! I'm glad you’ve returned. I want to make it clear that the merchant guild has made this guildhouse permanently open to you. \n"
"\n"
"Now that the crisis is over, the other council members have returned home. Though they are gone, good will prevails between us. The beginning of a new era of peace? We will see. Certainly it is a time of prosperity! Our caravans are already back in operation."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, Heroes of Jadame!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah well, very good to see you. Quite a lot of trouble is behind us, no? What brings the \"Heroes of Jadame\" to my camp?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:40
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Together we have done a great deed. I look forward to telling my heir the tale. How can I help you, heroes?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome. My cave is open to you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Light has shined upon us indeed. Our temple is always open to the \"Heroes of Jadame.\" How may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, friends?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How good of you to grace us with your presence. Heroes of Jadame. Saviors of Balthazar Lair. Both fitting titles for you who have done so much for me herd and for all of Jadame!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, Saviors of Balthazar Lair!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail! In the name of the guild, I welcome you. Know that we consider you our friends, Heroes of Jadame. What would you have of us today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, heroes."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you're looking for my master, Xanthor, he is not here. Can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmph. So you are the heroes of the alliance. Not much to look at, I must say. Still, I suppose you have survived much to see this day. I only hope you are up to the task I think fate has for you. If not, we are all surely doomed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:46
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:113
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:113
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are back? Have you need of advice? Or are you finding the task at hand too difficult?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There. It is built. Take this Conflux Key. As I have explained, it will allow you to use the crystal in the town square as a gateway--much as you've used the elemental gateways to reach the elemental planes. The crystal gateway will take you to the place between the planes.\n"
"\n"
"On this \"Plane Between Planes\" you must find the source of the cataclysm. What it is, I don't know, but whatever it is, it is there. Go now! The fate of the land, I'm afraid, lies on your shoulders. Be worthy of the task!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must go through the crystal gateway! It leads to the plane between planes. The cause of the cataclysm lies through it--seek out the source!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have conducted yourselves greatly. I must say I had my doubts about your abilities, but no longer. You are truly worthy of the praise that all lavish upon you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How can I help you, friends?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I sense some small presence in this chamber. Greater than gnats, but so much less than myself. Where is it….\n"
"\n"
"Ah, there it is. What have we here? Some of the beings of Jadame? Yes. Destroy them? Surely within my rights…but, no. It has been a slow millennia. Perhaps they will provide some diversion.\n"
"\n"
"Speak then, lower ones! What would you have of Escaton the Destroyer of Worlds?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ah the gnatlings are returned. I must consider why I allow them their continued existence. But this I will do some other time.\n"
"\n"
"Speak then, while you still may, puny ones."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings.  You seek instruction?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good day.  You seek to gain knowledge?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who is there? Am I finally to be released?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you here to free me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Help me! I have been able to live thus far, but for how much longer can I?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you now release me from my torment?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, mortals…good. You are not of my tormentors. Release me from this place! I will not harm you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Release me from this cell, mortals!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:54
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Free me quickly! I have survived so far, but it is only a matter of time before I am extinguished!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:54
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My fires dampen. Release me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. I am Sahil Ittalle, the historian of the Alvarian Merchant Guild. How can I help you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes? Can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you must be the alliance council's heroes. Well met. Catherine and I are here to help. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:56
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:86
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:57
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was a harrowing journey to reach your shores, I assure you! But the events of the cataclysm force all to extreme duties. I'm sure you understand. But down to issues. How can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:58
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings! I am Asael Fromago, the world's preeminent connoisseur of fine cheeses. Oh, some might say that Elkanah Juusto of Edenbrook holds the title, but he is a dilettante--a mere dabbler!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:58
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings! How may Asael Fromago, master of cheeses, serve you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:59
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:98
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:59
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:98
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, adventurer!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:60
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yeah? What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:61
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:62
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes? What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:63
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. How may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:64
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who are you? Clearly you are not of this realm. And how have you survived? I am amazed you have not been destroyed by the madness that has taken over my fellow earth dwellers!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:64
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good to see you again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. Though I have not yet succumbed to the madness, be aware! I feel its tug on my mind. I don't know how long I can hold out."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again. You are still safe in my presence. The madness has not overtaken me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:66
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The madness pulls at me, but still I maintain my sanity. If you have business with me, speak quickly. Even now I feel a compulsion to attack you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:66
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am still in my own mind, but for how long I don't know. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:67
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fear not, plane-travelers. For reasons I do not understand, the madness that affects my brethren does not affect me. How can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Madness reigns these watery realms, but it does not rule me. Somehow I am not affected. How can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:68
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:70
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "T-the madness p-pulls at my very soul. Each day is a st-struggle to maintain sanity. I w-will h-help you while I c-can, but be prepared to fl-flee!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I s-still maintain my-myself. W-what is it y-you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:70
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to my sanctuary. I have proofed this chamber against the maddening magic which affects my fellow citizens. You are safe as long as you stay here. How may I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't know what has befallen us, but it is awful! All my friends and family are affected by violent madness. Somehow I am not affected. But how can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:72
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, I understand you're out for adventure. I'd be glad to join you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:72
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back! Have you decided to take me with you in your travels?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:73
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is so boring around here! I mean, why did I spend all that time training if I'm not going to use my skills? Say, perhaps you could take me with you. Clearly you're headed someplace exciting!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:73
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, have you come back to take me on your adventure?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know the elder Dragons would never approve, but I don't care! I want adventure, and you're the best chance I'll see. Can I go with you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, can I come with you now? Can I?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:75
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Would you believe the Necromancers' Guild cast me out? I, Karanya Memoria? Fah! They were just jealous of my great potential. Not that this has stopped me from seeking dark knowledge--I do so now by my own path.\n"
"\n"
"Say, perhaps we could join forces!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:75
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, travelers! Ah, how I envy your lives of adventure. You know, I too know the call of the open road. I myself once sought new experiences--strange lands, strange people, and whatnot. Sadly, those days are over for me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good to see you again!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, and well met! I am Jasp Thelbourne--an Elf of daring deeds. This is no idle boast. You may have heard of the Idol of Seven Skunks? It was I who recovered it from the Temple of Eep for the Alvarian Merchant Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, again. How can Jasp Thelbourne, renowned adventurer do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I grow weary of the endless demands placed on my by my so-called \"master,\" the accursed Thant. He would have me stay here in Shadowspire as a guard. A \"guard,\" feh! I am meant for greater things. An adventure like yours is what I seek. Will you have me in your fellowship?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I'm still here, but I make preparations to leave as soon as an opportunity presents itself. Have you reconsidered? Will you take me now?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:79
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. I am Nathaniel Roberts. Without false modesty, I can say I am a mighty master of dark magic. It is your good fortune I have grown bored of Shadowspire and seek a company of adventurers such as yourselves to ally myself with. If you are agreeable, I will allow you to accompany me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:79
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, you have reconsidered my offer. Will you now agree to become my followers?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:80
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, a party of \"adventurers\"…hmmm. I suppose most dragons would just attack them outright, but then again I, Flamdring, have never been \"most dragons,\" no. Join them? Yes, perhaps I will. Perhaps I will."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:80
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah the adventurers return. Again the question arises: To join them or no? Yes, perhaps so…"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:81
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:81
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you? I am Hevatia Deverbero, a member in full standing of the Necromancers' Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:82
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, and may the Light shine on you. What can a humble priest of the Sun do for you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:82
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again. May the Light shine on you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:83
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:83
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes? Well, don't stand there tongue tied! I'm a busy man!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:84
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, and good hunting to you. I am Sethrc Thistlebone, a warrior of this village, such as it is."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:84
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, and good hunting!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:85
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:85
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. Welcome to my home. I am Rionel, axe warrior of Balthazar Lair."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:85
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:85
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to my home."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:86
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greeting! I am Adric Stellare, a former lieutenant of the Alvar Guard. I grew tired of the regimented lifestyle. Now I seek adventure."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:87
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:87
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am Infaustus, elder vampire and adventurer. I will talk with you if you are brief. I am busy making preparations to leave. I go to seek my fortune across the lands of Jadame."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:88
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:88
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Very impressive performance. Reaching me was not easy. Perhaps you are the adventurers I seek. You see, I wish to explore the world, and these days, even a Dragon would be smart not to travel alone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:89
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:89
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail, adventurers! I am Tempus, hunt leader and a knight of some renown in my native Erathia. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:89
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:89
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:90
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings! I am the mighty Thorne Understone. I know we have not met before--I never forget a face--but perhaps you recognize my name from ballads. You know, several have been written about me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:90
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again. What can the mighty Thorne do for you? Maybe I could sign my name on your shield as a keepsake. A lot of my fans seem to like that sort of thing."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:91
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail! I am Ulbrecht, a hero of the Vori campaigns. Be welcome in my home."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:91
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is good to see you again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:92
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wake after a sleep of thirty-four years, and already I have company! I see you have traveled far. Perhaps you can tell me what has transpired while I slumbered."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:92
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:95
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:93
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am Duroth the Eternal. By besting the guards you have earned the right of speaking to me. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:93
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What brings you again to Duroth the Eternal?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:94
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:94
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings! I am Weldrick Falconeye, Dragon training specialist. What can I do for you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:94
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:94
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello again…need any Dragons trained?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:96
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:96
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sethrik Fist at your service. Fine coffins made to order."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:97
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The call of madness it burns…burns! My mind…ahrgg! Wait! A moment of clarity…quickly! State your business! I can hold out for but a moment."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:97
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What…is…it…you…w-want?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:99
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:99
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ahoy, matey!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What do you want? My research requires great concentration--a concentration you are breaking with you're intrusion!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You again? What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:102
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you the new recruits? Of course you are! Why else would you be seeking me out? I'm ex-Captain Terrence, here to help you on your way to becoming proper Regnan sailors."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:102
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the new recruits again! What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:103
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:103
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How are you? What can a simple fisherwoman do for you today?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:104
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:104
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello?  Ah, someone else who seeks a way off this accursed island!  My name is Simon Templar!  I found my way into this temple as I was told it was the way out!  Let's travel together!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:105
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:105
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, do you seek guidance from the Light?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:106
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:106
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Nooo!  What…where am I? You rescued me?  My thanks!!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:107
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:107
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome!  I can make many wondrous things from the various ores that are indigenous to Jadame."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:108
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:108
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt! These areas are off limits to guests! Guild members only!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:109
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:109
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You may not enter here, puny ones! Stand back or become our prey!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:110
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:110
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt! Only members of our knightly brotherhood may pass this point. Others who attempt to pass will face our wrath!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:111
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:111
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Stop! You may not enter the storeroom!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:112
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hail! I'm Jeric Whistlebone. Welcome to my camp. We're on a hunting safari. You're welcome to look around, but don't interfere with our operation. This is no place for amateur fumbling about!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:114
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings. I am the Oracle of Jadame. The mysteries of the Hidden World are open to me. Through long years of training, I have gained a small measure of control over time and space. I can reach my hand through the void and bring things to me--both items and knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:114
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, and may the Balance always tilt in your favor."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:115
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:115
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halt! Only guild members and their guests can pass this point. Further, any guild members with you must be at least, conscious. You have old Leland with you, but he's in no condition to oversee you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npcgreet.txt.py:116
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCGreet.txt.py:116
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Help me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My fellow Journeyman, we face grave times.  Hopefully our Master will find a way for us to leave this troubled region and return safely to Alvar.  I would not wish to end my life here, even though it is the place of my birth."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dadeross led us here to trade with the Lizardman Clan of Onefang for their tobersk fruit.  He has gone to talk with Brekish Onefang, the village leader.  Perhaps you should look for him?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Regnan Pirates are a threat to the economy and free travel in Jadame.  Very few boats ply the sea, for fear of being sunk…or worse!  When in Ravenshore, I did hear rumors of a small band of smugglers who have been working beneath the notice of the pirates.  I wonder how they do that!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is as I have read in the prophecy of the Unmaking! \"...and a Mountain of Fire shall rise from the sea, like a wound drawn by the quick stroke of a dagger…\".\n"
"\n"
"You must find a way off of these islands, if not for the caravan, at least for yourself!  Someone must take news of what has happened here to the Merchant Council in Alvar!  They must know of the cataclysm and of the Regnan raid!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The pirates from the dread Island of Regna are using the cataclysm and the confusion created by it to aid them in overrunning the islands.  If they conquer Dagger Wound, they can use it as an outpost for direct raids on Ravenshore!  The Merchant Council in Alvar must be notified!  You must find a way to the boats and tell them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It will take several boats to ferry the entire caravan back to Ravenshore, or many trips by one boat.  This cannot be done until the waters around the Dagger Wound Islands are free from Regnan Pirates.  It is best that you return to Alvar and tell the Council of the Regnan attack.  They will send help to rescue us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In the middle of the night the ground shook!  Flaming rocks dropped from the sky!  Many of my people were hurt or killed!  Great damage was done to the village.  The bridges that allowed travel between the smaller islands and the main island were destroyed.  We found ourselves stuck on the main island, unable to reach those on the smaller islands who may be injured.  Many family members and friends are missing.  We cannot reach the islands with the boat docks, and thus we are unable to send to Ravenshore for help. I do not even know if any boats survived!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In time long past, my people used the Portals of Stone to travel quickly from island to island, but we have lost the knowledge of their operation. Only the pair connecting the village to the southwestern fields still functions. Now that the bridges are gone, we're trapped on the island!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A Cleric, by the name of Fredrick Talimere, has been living with us for the last few years.  He has been studying the Portals of Stone and the outer ruins of the Abandoned Temple.  Maybe he has the knowledge to get the Portals working again!  Find him and see if he will help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ah yes…\"the portals.\" I have been studying them and the lost culture that built them for years.\n"
"\n"
"They were built by the civilization that had its day long before the Lizardmen came to inhabit these islands. They were a means of instantaneous travel between the islands. Sadly, the power stones needed to operate them are in short supply."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The first night of the mountain of fire, I went to the beach to see if I could see anything of its eruption.  I cannot be certain, but as the volcano continued to erupt, I thought I saw Earth Elementals roaming the lava encrusted base of the mountain."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So Clanleader Onefang gave you that power stone he was holding onto! It will power the portal on the southwestern tip of the island. To use it, hold an image of the stone in your mind as you step onto the portal."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The ruins of a temple built by the lost civilization lies on the island just northwest of the main island. I have not explored it however, for dangerous reptiles have made it their lair. I do suspect that the temple leads to an underwater tunnel which surfaces near the boat docks on the northwest island.\n"
"\n"
"With the bridges out, that tunnel may be the only way to reach the docks and a boat to safety!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:15
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My brother, Isthric the Tongue, went to check on the tobersk plants on one of the lesser islands.  He has not returned!  I am afraid that he is one of those stranded by the cataclysm. He may even be hurt!  If you were to fix the Portals of Stone, he would surely be able to return, and we could get help to those who need it!  Find him for me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:16
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Granda used to tell us of the times past, when the Portals of Stone were the main travel route between the islands.  She told us that the keys to the Portals disappeared during one of the first raids committed by the Regnan Pirates.  If the Portals of Stone were working my brother Isthric could return back to the main island!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That rude man?  He's more concerned with that Abandoned Temple than he is with the life that goes on around him!  My Granda warned him that the Temple is a place of great Evil.  He never listened.  Now Granda isn't with us anymore and we have no one but Brekish Onefang to remind us of the past."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:18
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We have offended the Ancients!  Why else would they call up the Mountain of Fire!  The Prophecies tell of a time when the oceans would boil!  This is the beginning of the end!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are many Prophecies that tell of the destruction of Jadame and the entire world!   Most tell of a time when the world will be consumed by that which created it.  Perhaps the Ancients have decided to wipe us all out!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is one Prophecy, the Prophecy of the Snake, that I have been unable to find a copy of.  I think it may be most revealing about the future of Jadame.\n"
"\n"
"Fredrick Talimere, the Cleric, has told me of the snake ruins, and of the Abandoned Temple.  He is in agreement with me, that there may be a copy of this prophecy, somewhere in the temple.  Could you find it for me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You must find a way off of these islands. Someone must take news of what has happened here to our masters, the Merchants of Alvar!  They must know of the cataclysm and of the Regnan raid! \n"
"\n"
"I've written a letter to the Merchants of Alvar representative in Ravenshore, Elgar Fellmoon. In it I explain our situation here. If anyone can advise us on what to do here, it is Fellmoon. Take this to him now."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must bring my letter to Elgar Fellmoon in Ravenshore!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Take this crystal to Fredrick Talimere. I know that it has something to do with the portals of stone. Perhaps he can tell you how it functions."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bring the portal crystal to Fredrick Talimere. He will know what it does."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Merchant Council had sent our greatest warrior, Cauri Blackthorne, to consult with the Sun Temple priests about the disasters that have struck all of Jadame.\n"
"\n"
"Cauri left for the Temple of the Sun in Murmurwoods shortly after rumors of the cataclysms were heard here in Alvar.  She was to return after consulting the priests.  We are very concerned that she has not returned.\n"
"\n"
"As for your promotion, only Cauri can accurately test your skills and assess your worthiness for promotion.  If you find her, provide her with any assistance she may need and return here with news of her status and location."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found Cauri?  We really need to know what happened to her!  Without her, we are all diminished!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:27
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Thank you for your assistance with the Basilisk Curse.  Usually I am prepared to handle the vile lizards, but this time there were just too many of them.\n"
"\n"
"The Temple of the Sun asked me to check on a few pilgrims that were looking for the Druid Circle of Stone in this area.  When I found the first statue, I realized what had happened to the pilgrims.  \n"
"\n"
"I myself did not know of the increase in the number of Basilisks in this area.  They seem to be agitated by something.  I was going to investigate the Druid Circle of Stone when the Basilisks attacked me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"::Cauri looks over the Dark Elf(s) in your party::\n"
"\n"
"To rescue me, you must have researched my path, and investigated the places I had been.  This demonstrates the intelligence needed to succeed in dealing with the world and business.\n"
"\n"
"To get to where I was attacked, you must have the skills needed to fight the Basilisks and other threats, demonstrating your prowess as a warrior.  Skill in battle is needed when proper negotiations break down.\n"
"\n"
"To ask me for promotion demonstrates desire, and without desire success will always escape your grasp.\n"
"\n"
"You have all of the traits necessary to hold the title of Patriarch.  I will notify to Council upon my return.  It would be my pleasure to travel with you again.  You can find me in the Inn in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I need to investigate the Circle of Stone further for the Temple of the Sun.  Hopefully not all of the pilgrims met the fate of these. Hopefully there are survivors!\n"
"\n"
"Something has agitated the creatures in this area, and I think the source can be found in the Circle."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You know…I have a power stone that will activate the portal to the abandoned temple. And you have one that will allow us to reach the island where that portal is!\n"
"\n"
"If we joined forces, we could reach the temple with ease. What say you?\n"
"\n"
"Fredrick Talimere offers to join your party."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Cauri returned and informed us of this assistance you provided her.  She also notified us of your promotion.  Congratulations, may your profits bring you much joy!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Cauri Blackthorne was here well over a week ago, maybe longer.  She had asked us many questions about the elemental incursions.  We provided her with what information we had here.  She said she would return to Alvar with the information.  Before she left, we asked her if she could do a favor for us.  We asked her if she could check on a group of pilgrims that were traveling to the old Druid Circle of Stone to the northeast of here.  She assured us that she would check in on them on her way back to Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:33
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You come to me claiming to have a message from one of my caravan masters. Well, where is it then? If it was so important, perhaps you should have been better about not losing it along the way!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What is this? A letter from caravan master, Dadeross? Let's see…hmmm…\n"
"\n"
"Well, it seems that serious events are afoot. It is a pity--what has happened on Dagger Wound. Serious action may need to be taken, but I require more information…\n"
"\n"
"…and I think I know how to get it! Perhaps you would be interested in helping me? I will compensate you, of course. And, here. Take this as payment for delivering Dadeross' letter."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The local smugglers have the fastest boats in Ravenshore. If these were available to my agents, they could make quick scouting missions up and down the coast so we could see the extent of the cataclysm mentioned in Dadeross' letter.\n"
"\n"
"Here. Bring this letter to the smuggler leader, Arion Hunter. I'm sure it will \"persuade\" him to lend his services. You'll find his hideout westward up the coast.\n"
"\n"
"Oh, I almost forgot. The smugglers--they're wererats--and you know how they can be. Hunter can be reasoned with, but don't be surprised if his crew is less than civil."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Listen. We need those boats! Deliver my letter to Arion Hunter. Did you forget? His lair is to the west, up the coast!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Very good, and here is the payment we agreed upon. Hunter's boats will be useful to us through the crisis.\n"
"\n"
"Yes, \"crisis,\" I say! Since your initial visit, several other caravans have missed their scheduled stops. There are also the rumors. Twice I've heard of the appearance of a burning lake of fire rising out of the desert.\n"
"\n"
"Volcanoes! Lakes of fire! I fear the mysterious crystal has something to do with it. In any event, the guildmasters in Alvar must be informed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"As you may be aware, our guild headquarters is located in the city of Alvar. If you've never been there, the easiest way to reach it is to follow the river up through the canyon to the north.\n"
"\n"
"Go to the guild house and find Bastian Loudrin. Tell him about the crystal, and the rumors. Lourdrin will know what to do."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must reach Bastian Loudrin in Alvar. Go! He must be informed of recent events!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This is the home of Cauri Blackthorne, greatest Dark Elf warrior.  She is currently out, working for the Merchant Council of Alvar.  Perhaps you should consult them as to her whereabouts."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You did all that to my guards just to deliver a letter! Let me see that…\n"
"\n"
"…hmmm…Fellmoon wants my boats? Never! I…what!…he threatens my Irabelle…I…I…sigh…\n"
"\n"
"V-very well. You can tell Fellmoon he can have my boats. I guess there's no refusing the Merchants of Alvar what they want."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My cargoes are not the kind that want inspecting by harbor officials so my boats have to be, and are, the fastest on the coast of Jadame. They can even outrun a Regnan galley! From here they run west to Ravage Roaming and east to Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ancient Troll legends tell of a time when we did not live here in this desolate region.  They tell of a place that was quiet and tranquil.  We were driven from this place by the Curse of the Stone.  So for many hundred years we have dwelt here upon the Sand of Iron.  Now it seems we will be forced from this place as well.  The growing sea of fire has destroyed most of my village.  Many friends and family have perished.  This may indeed be the end of my Clan.\n"
"\n"
"There is a saying amongst my people, \"a thing lives only as long as it is remembered.\"  As long as I remember our homeland, then it will always be there for us to return too.  It just needs to be found."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Perhaps if you could locate our previous homeland, and check to see if the Curse of the Stone still exists.  If it does perhaps there is a way to remove it.  Any Troll in your party who completes this task would be promoted to War Troll of our Clan. Many honors are bestowed with this title, and you would be forever known to us as a legendary hero.\n"
"\n"
"One of our warriors, Dartin Dunewalker, set out to find this place.  He left thinking he would find clues among the stone fields of Ravage Roaming.  Perhaps you can find him there and work together--or at the least, find clues that will lead you to our goal."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Alliance must be completed, and a unified course of action decided upon.  Return to Alvar and consult the Merchant Council."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You have found our Ancient Home?  Its located in the western area of the Murmurwoods?  This is wonderful news.  Perhaps there is still time to move my people.  Unfortunately the Elemental threat must be dealt with first, or no people will be safe! \n"
"\n"
"All Trolls among you have been promoted to War Troll, and their names will be forever remembered in our songs.  I will teach the rest of you what skills I can, perhaps it will be enough to help you save all of Jadame."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You were sent to find the Ancient Troll Home?  Your assistance is welcomed!  I am at a loss; the clues I followed to this region have lead to a dead end.  No one here knows about the Curse of the Stone mentioned in our legends.  The Ogre Mage, Zog was less than helpful.  I was lucky to escape his fortress with my life. \n"
"\n"
"Although, he may have provided assistance with out meaning too!  When I mentioned the Curse of the Stone, he said if I bothered him further, he would be sure to cage me with his pet Basilisk!  Basilisks roam the Murmurwoods!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks again for your assistance with the Basilisk curse!  Hurry back to Alvar!  We must do what we can to save Jadame."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for finding our Ancient Home, once the treat to Jadame has been handled we can begin to move there!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found the Ancient Home for our Clan?  Without its location, my people will surely perish!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Disaster in Dagger Wound, too? This is indeed disturbing. If one were to believe all the rumors, one would think that all of Jadame is in upheaval and chaos.\n"
"\n"
"I wish I knew more. I rely on our caravan masters for news, but all who were supposed to arrive here this month have not. What I do hear, troubles me. Hurricanes, floods, and now a volcano! The worst I've heard is that a sea of fire has appeared in the Ironsand Desert--and this from many sources.\n"
"\n"
"I wonder if this crystal in Ravenshore has something to do with it. Its appearance at the onset of the calamity seems to be more than a coincidence."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All of this upheaval is seriously impacting our guild's business. I need more information, but I'm being buried in gossip and rumor.\n"
"\n"
"Many tell me of this sea of fire in the Ironsand Desert. I've heard the tale enough that I almost believe it. Confirmation or denial of the lake's existence would be of great help to me.\n"
"\n"
"If you would serve me, go to the Ironsand Desert and seek this lake. If it is indeed there, find me someone who saw it appear. Bring him back here so I can hear his story myself."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:53
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I must know more about what is going on in the Ironsand Desert. I can't use more rumors. I have enough of those already.\n"
"\n"
"I need you to actually go there. The desert is several days travel to the east."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:54
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Well, so it is true. Imagine…a lake of fire. But where is my eyewitness? I need to speak with someone who saw its formation. This is important…for reasons I'm unwilling to discuss with you now.\n"
"\n"
"Find me someone who saw the birth of the lake of fire! Try searching the Troll village, Rust."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:55
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You must form an alliance to stand against our threatened oblivion! Seek support from the Necromancers' Guild, Temple of the Sun, Minotaurs of Ravage Roaming, Dragons of Garrote Gorge, and the Dragon hunting party of Charles Quixote in Garrote Gorge. I'm sure that you will find it impossible to get all of them to agree to work together, but still, you must make your best effort.\n"
"\n"
"If we are to survive in this time of prophecy, my sages tell me that at least three of the groups I mentioned must agree to work together. Go and do this thing. If you value this world and your lives, go!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:56
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You have done what I feared was impossible. Though these times are fraught with uncertainties, that you have united key factions of Jadame goes a long way towards securing our continued existence.\n"
"\n"
"Well, I have done what I can. I leave the defense of the land to the alliance council. I hope they find the accommodations I have provided them in Ravenshore to be adequate--the guild house there is not our most luxurious. Still, I though it would be best if the council was located near the crystal.\n"
"\n"
"I wish them, and you, good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:57
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Yes, I was here when the lake of fire first appeared. A strange gateway appeared on the desert plain outside the village. The fire you see spilled forth from it. The fire spread like water poured on the ground.\n"
"\n"
"A wave of flames rushed over the edge of the village. Most of my people were lost instantly. What remains of this village is as you see it.\n"
"\n"
"I was in the hills overlooking the village when this all happened. I saw it all, but I can hardly believe it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:58
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I would come with you, If it were not for my father. So deep is his mourning for my brother, Vilebite, that he cannot care for himself.\n"
"\n"
"My father believes that Vilebite's soul cannot rest until his remains are at rest in the village tomb. Unfortunately, Gogs infested the tomb when the lake of fire appeared.\n"
"\n"
"Here! Take my brother's ashes. I'm sure my father's grief will lessen if they are placed in the tomb. Do this for me and I will travel with you to Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:59
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will go with you only after my brother's ashes are safely in the village tomb."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:60
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have done my family a great service. With his ashes safe in the holy sanctuary of the village tomb, Vilebite can lie in peace. My father, too is greatly improved. We have talked and I believe that he can now take care of himself while I accompany you to Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:61
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Vilebite was a good son. I will miss him. But at least I can take comfort knowing that he is at peace. Thank you for your kind and heroic deed."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:62
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My father believed that the Necromancers of Shadowspire were attempting to create an undead Dragon.  This would be a truly horrid beast. He believed is was his personal duty to stop them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:63
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My father Blazen, left here years ago to slay the Skeletal Dragons in the Shadowspire Region. Unfortunately, he has never returned.  He took with him, Ebonest, the greatest Dragon slaying spear ever forged. Charles Quixote has never forgiven my father for taking Ebonest with him.  Unfortunately we have no idea what befell my father.  Because my father was Charles’ second in command and responsible for the loss of Ebonest, Charles is unwilling to promote me to Champion, regardless of the merit of my skills. Perhaps if you find Ebonest, Charles with promote your knights and myself to Champions!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:64
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was captured in the center of the Mad Necromancer’s lab.  There I was tortured and many curses were placed upon me.   Ebonest must have been taken from me when I fell, and perhaps is still in the central chamber.  If you were to recover it and return it to Quixote, at least my family name will be cleared, and my daughter can continue her life without my failure haunting her."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:65
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Perhaps the Clerics of the Sun have a way to cure me, for they would be the only ones who would know how to counter the dark magics that afflict me. There is a friend of mine in Ravenshore named Dervish Chevron. He left the Temple of the Sun years ago to pursue his own research into the mysteries of Jadame.  Perhaps he would know of a cure, or even have it in his possession.  If he cannot help, promise you will return here and kill me so I may at last be at rest!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:66
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Zanthora moved here from the Shadowspire to continue experiments she began at the Necromancers' Guild.  She desired to create the ultimate horror, the Skeletal Dragon.  Her fellow Necromancers feared the end result. If the created Dragons where ever to escape Zanthora’s control, there would be no stopping them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:67
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Blazen Stormlance was my lieutenant and my friend.  I never understood his personal quest--this need to find these rumored Skeletal Dragons.  He took my greatest tool with him.  With Ebonest in my hand, I would have the Dragon problem well in hand.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:68
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Clerics of the Sun imbued this spear with their blessings, making it the strongest spear forged.  Its power is said to be able to slay any Dragon with one blow.  If this were so, I could end my conflict quickly, cleanly and efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:69
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Gem of Restoration may cure the knight, Blazen Stormlance, of what you say has befallen him.  There is no love lost between the Temple of the Sun and the Guild of Necromancers; any opponent of theirs is definitely a friend of ours.  Restore Stormlance to life so that he may rejoin Charles Quixote.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:70
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found my father?  Or the spear Ebonest?  We must get it back to Charles Quixote!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:71
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You found Blazen Stormlance?  What about MY spear Ebonest?  You have that as well?\n"
"\n"
"FANTASTIC!\n"
"\n"
"I thank you for this and find myself in your debt!  I will promote all knights in your party to Champion and teach what skills I can to the rest of your party. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:72
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What is this?  You ally with my mortal enemies and then seek to do me a favor?\n"
"\n"
"I wonder what the Dragons think of this. But so be it.  I am in your debt for returning Ebonest to me.  I will promote any Knights in your party to Champion, however they will never be accepted in my service.  The rest I will teach what I can. \n"
"\n"
"I do not wish to see you again!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:73
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"\"An alliance to unite Jadame,\" you say. If it wasn't Lordrin who was proposing it, I would normally have slain you for my supper.\n"
"\n"
"While intriguing, I cannot consider the idea now. We are under daily attack by the accursed knights of Charles Quixote. If he were not a problem, I could do as Lordrin asks.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps you could help me with Quixote?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:74
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Last month one of Quixote's raiding parties invaded our caves. They slew many and took with them the egg containing my unborn heir. While those foul slayers hold the egg, we cannot attack their encampment.\n"
"\n"
"If you were to return the egg to me, I could destroy Quixote. Do this for me and I will join your alliance."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:75
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you want me to join your alliance, you will have to help me against Charles Quixote. Bring me the Dragon egg he stole from me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:76
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To attain the status of Great Wyrm, a Dragon must prove that he can handle himself against a great number of foes.  He must face down the vermin that Charles Quixote would send against us.  To the southwest of here, Quixote has established an encampment of his puny “Dragon Slayers.”  This camp is lead by Jeric Whistlebone, the second in command of Quixote’s army.  Destroy this camp!  Kill all of those who serve Quixote in that region and return to me.  Return to me with the sword of  Whistlebone the Slayer.  In doing this, you will prove to me your worthiness.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:77
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You think I would promote a Dragon that serves those who have allied themselves with our Mortal enemy, Charles Quixote.  What arrogance!  What outrageousness!  You will have to prove yourselves to me! And in the proving you will deal a serious blow to your allies!  To the southwest of here, Quixote has established an encampment of his puny “Dragon Slayers.”  This camp is lead by Jeric Whistlebone, the second in command of Quixote’s army.  Destroy this camp!  Kill all of those who serve Quixote in that region and return to me.  Return to me with the sword of  Whistlebone the Slayer."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:78
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you slain the “Dragon Slayers?\"  Where is the sword of Whistlebone the Slayer?!?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:79
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you slain the “Dragon Slayers?\"  Or have you decided not to redeem yourselves in my eyes?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:80
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You return to me with the sword of the Slayer, Whistlebone!  You are indeed worthy of my notice!  The Dragons in your group are promoted to Great Wyrm!  I will teach the others of your group what skills I can as a reward for their assistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:81
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:81
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You return to me with the sword of the Slayer, Whistlebone!  Is there no end to the treachery that you will commit? Is there no one that you owe allegiance to?  I will promote those Dragons who travel with you to Great Wyrm, however they will never fly underneath me!  There rest of your traitorous group will be instructed in those skills which can be taught to them!  Go now!  Never show your face here again, unless you want it eaten!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:82
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:82
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have killed the Dragon Slayers, but where is the Sword of Whistlebone?  Return to me when you have it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:83
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:83
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hmmm…things must be serious if trader Loudrin is involving himself in matters other than his own fortunes...and I must say that there is a taint of doom in the air.\n"
"\n"
"If only for continued good business between my operation and his, I would normally entertain this notion of Loudrin's. Unfortunately, matters here are tying up all of my resources. I have none to spare for support of this alliance you speak of.\n"
"\n"
"Say, perhaps we can help each other? If you were to take care of a little matter for me, I could consider honoring your request."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:84
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:84
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One of my customers, an Ogre that goes by the charming moniker of \"Zog the Jackal,\" has seriously betrayed my trust. I gave him an item of great value on promise of future payment. This rather large payment never arrived. I sent a messenger to demand return of the item--a Dragon's egg of great potential. This messenger was slain!\n"
"\n"
"Needless to say, this matter concerns me greatly. I have allotted both money and men for the purpose of revenge. If, however, you were to recover the egg for me from Zog's fortress in Ravage Roaming, I would be glad to pledge service to your alliance."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:85
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:85
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you recovered the Dragon egg from Zog's Ravage Roaming fortress? Oh, never mind. I can see from your abashed expression that you have not.\n"
"\n"
"I stand firm on our deal. Bring me that egg, or I'll have nothing to do with your alliance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:86
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:86
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found Blazen Stormlance? But where is Ebonest?  Return to me when you have the spear and you will be promoted!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:87
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:87
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That cursed knight, Charles Quixote is assembling his best Dragon Slayers at an encampment to the southwest of here.  He must be planning another assault upon the Dragon Caves!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:88
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:88
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You would like my herd to join into an alliance? How could I refuse you? Not only have you saved us from certain death, we have suffered directly from the cataclysm the alliance is being created to fight!\n"
"\n"
"You have my pledge. With the greatest haste I myself will travel to Ravenshore to take a seat on the alliance council."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:89
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:89
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was the worst of horrors! I was on guard in the main labyrinth just north of here when the waters came. A great wave as high as my head flooded through the passages. I managed to reach this high chamber. I waited for others, but there were none. I fear that many of the herd are dead or trapped inside the lair."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:90
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:90
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Balthazar Lair has many levels. There are other chambers as high as this one., so there may be others who have survived.\n"
"\n"
"I have thought long on this. Though many of the tunnels are flooded, it may be possible to drain them using the doors and air vents as valves. In fact, the whole lair could be drained through the lower level escape tunnel. Help my herd! You would have our eternal gratitude."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:91
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:91
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I just feel it. There are still survivors of my herd trapped in the lair. If you can figure out how to drain the water from flooded passages, you may be able to reach them. Help them, I beg of you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:92
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:92
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Balthazar, the greatest leader in the history of our herd, led our warriors in a mighty battle against the Dark Dwarf vermin that erupt from the earth and spread like a plague. It was not a battle that went well for us. Though Balthazar and some warriors escaped, many were lost along with Balthazar's Axe--his regalia of office, and a powerful artifact as well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:93
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:93
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Only Masul, our herd leader, can deem an individual worthy of the title of Minotaur Lord.  One way to prove your worth, would be to recover his father’s axe, the Axe of Balthazar from the bowels of the Mines of the Dark Dwarfs.  Set your feet upon the path of this quest, and great is you future!  But we must be sure that the axe you find is indeed the Axe of Balthazar.  Take the Axe to Dadeross, a Minotaur in the service of the Merchants of Alvar, on the island of Dagger Wound.  He will be able to verify the truth of what you find."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:94
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:94
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "These little vermin work with or for the Elements of the Earth.  No one can tell which.  They burrow up from the earth in search of wealth, food, and slaves.  Nothing is left behind where these scavengers have been."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:95
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:95
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found the Axe of Balthazar!  Have you presented it to Dadeross?  Without his authentication, we can not proceed with the Rite’s of Purity!  Find him and return to us once you have presented him with the axe!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:96
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:96
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found the Axe of Balthazar!  Have you presented it to Dadeross? Ah, you have authentication from Dadeross!  The Rite’s of Purity will begin immediately! You proven yourselves worthy, and our now members of our herd!  The Minotaurs who travel with you are promoted to Minotaur Lord.  The others in your group will be taught what skills we have that maybe useful to them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:97
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:97
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was my pleasure to serve under Lord Balthazar, he was the finest herd leader in my tribe’s history.  Unfortunately, my services were pledged to the Merchants of Alvar, or I may have been in the battle where Balthazar fell.  Perhaps my ability and my axe could have saved my lord.  We’ll never know now."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:98
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:98
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Of course I would know Balthazar's Axe if I saw it!  Do you have it with you? This IS the axe!  You must take this back to Tessalar, so the Rite’s of Purity may be performed upon the axe, so it be made ready for the son of Balthazar, Masul.  Take this letter with you, it carries my personal seal, and statement that this is indeed the Axe of Balthazar!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:99
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:99
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where is Balthazar's Axe?  You waste my time!  Find the axe, find Dadeross and return to me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:100
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for returning the Axe of Balthazar to us!  When we complete the Rites of Purity, we will present the axe to Masul. It will then be known as the Axe of Masul and surely Masul will be a wise and just herd leader."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:101
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Of course I would know Balthazar's Axe if I saw it!  Do you have it with you?  If you find it, return to me so that I may certify that it is indeed the axe of my late lord, Balthazar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:102
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found Balthazar's Axe and I have authenticated it!  Hurry back to Tessalar so that the Rites of Purity may begin!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:103
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:103
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you returned Balthazar's Axe with my certificate to Tessalar!  The Rites of Purity have begun.  Soon Lord Masul will wield his father's axe as his own!  Greatness will return to my herd!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:104
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:104
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Of the many Prophecies of Jadame, the only ones that I have not be studied are the Prophecies of the Sun.  This temple was established by Tesius Dawnglow, who traveled here from Erathia many years ago to find these Prophecies.  Unfortunately, they were not found.  It is our hope that these Prophecies hold the solution to the events that are destroying Jadame."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:105
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:105
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know that the Prophecies can be found in the Lair of the Feathered Serpent.  However, I have no idea what that means, thus the clue is no help to me. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:106
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:106
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek promotion for the clerics of our faith who travel with you.?  I can promote you, but I do not place much trust or faith in strangers these days.  If you were to do something for me, such as finding the lost Prophecies of the Sun, and returning them to me, then I would be agreeable to promoting you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:107
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:107
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found this Lair of the Feathered Serpent and the Prophecies of the Sun?  Do not waste my time!  The world is ending and you waste time with useless conversation!  Return to me when you have found the Prophecies and have taken them to the Temple of the Sun."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:108
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:108
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found the lost Prophecies of the Sun?  May the Light forever shine upon you and may the Prophet guide your steps.  With these we may be able to find the answer to what has befallen Jadame! "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:109
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:109
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You return. True to your word, you have located the Prophecies of the Sun and taken them to my brothers in the Temple of the Sun.  you are truly worthy, and with the Sun’s blessing I will promote the clerics who travel with you.  After, I will teach the rest of your group what skills I can as their reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:110
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:110
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Korbu was the most powerful of the Vampire race.  Over one hundred years ago, he sought something that our kind cannot accept.  Absolution.  Somehow, Korbu began to experience guilt over the need to feed.  Or perhaps over the act of feeding itself.  He could no longer bear the thought of killing in order to survive.  Many of our elders argued with him.  He decided to find a place where he could ponder his existence.  Thus the Crypt of Korbu was constructed with slave labor in the Ravage Roaming region.   Korbu has not been heard from since he left.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:111
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:111
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In this time of chaos, we need the minds of all our elders.  Return to us with Korbu, or his remains, if he has perished.  If he has indeed perished, you must return his Sarcophagus with him.  We will attempt to reanimate him so that we may consult his wisdom."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:112
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You return to us with the remains of Korbu, but where is his Sarcophagus? We cannot complete the act of reanimation without it!  Return to us when you have both the remains and the Sarcophagus!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:113
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:113
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You return to us with the Sarcophagus of Korbu, but where are his remains? We cannot complete the act of reanimation without them!  Return to us when you have both the Sarcophagus and his remains!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:114
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you seek to achieve the ultimate in the darker arts.  The necromancer’s among you seek to turn themselves into Liches, the most potent of necromancers.  Very well, I can perform this transformation for you, but you must do something for me...and get something for yourselves.  I require the Lost Book of Khel.  It contains secrets of necromancy that had been hidden since Khel’s tower sank beneath the waves.  The Lizardmen of Dagger Wound celebrated when the sea took Khel and his knowledge from us.  With the volcanic upheaval in that region, I believe the Tower of Khel can be found.  Retrieve the book from the library and bring it to me!  Now, for yourselves, you will need a Lich Jar for every necromancer that wishes to become a Lich.  Zanthora, the Mad Necromancer keeps a large supply of these jars, perhaps she will sell you one!  If not you must take them from her!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:115
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:115
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have the Lost Book of Khel, however you lack the Lich Jars needed to complete the transformation!  Return here when you have one for each necromancer in your party!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:116
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:116
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You do not have the Lost Book of Khel!  I cannot help you, if you do not help me!  Return here with the Book and a Lich Jar for each necromancer in your party that wishes to become a Lich!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:117
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You have brought everything needed to perform the transformation!  So be it!  All necromancer’s in your party will be transformed into Liches!  May the dark energies flow through them for all eternity!  The rest of you will gain what knowledge I can teach them as reward for their assistance!  Lets begin!\n"
"\n"
"After we have completed, good friend Lathean can handle any future promotions for your party."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:118
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have brought us the Sarcophagus of Korbu and his sacred remains.  We will attempt to reanimate Korbu and seek his wisdom in these troubled times!  The vampires among you will be transformed into Nosferatu, and the others will be taught what skills we can teach them as reward for your service."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:119
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:119
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lair of the Feathered Serpent?  That could possibly refer to the poisonous couatl, but they have not been seen for centuries."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:120
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:120
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Prophecies of the Sun have never been found.  They may not event exist. The Prophecies were written by our greatest prophet.  If they are found it is our hope they will be returned to us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:121
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:121
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for finding the Prophecies of the Sun.  May the Sun always light you way and provide you with protection!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:122
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:122
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You returned Korbu to us, and we will always be in your debt!  Now leave me, so that I may consult the elders!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:123
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:123
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must be a member of this guild to study here."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:137
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:137
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Games are played with the house Arcomage deck. We will supply the opponent.  Victory conditions vary per inn. Build your tower, destroy your opponent's tower, or collect enough resources before your opponent does. \n"
"\n"
"Large yellow numbers in column are the generators. This is how many new units of a particular resource you will receive on your next turn. Small black numbers in column are the resources. This is how many units you have available to spend on your current turn.\n"
"\n"
"Cards: Each have their own cost to play, indicated in a small circle in the lower right corner of the card. The cost will be deducted from your resources according to the color of the card.  Left click on a card plays the card. Right click on a card to discard without playing.\n"
"\n"
"Red represents your Quarry Generator which produces your Brick resources, blue represents your Magic Generator which produces Gem resources, green represents your Zoo generator which produces Beast resources. \n"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:138
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:138
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 15, Wall of 5.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 30, one of the resources to 100, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:139
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:140
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:139
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:140
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 20 and a Wall of 5.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 50, one of the resources to 150, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:141
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:142
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:141
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:142
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 25 and a Wall of 10.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 75, one of the resources to 200, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:143
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:144
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:143
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:144
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 30 and a Wall of 15.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 100, one of the resources to 300, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:145
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:145
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 20 and a Wall of 10.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 150, one of the resources to 400, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:146
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:146
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 20 and a Wall of 10.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 200, one of the resources to 500, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:147
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:147
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 20 and a Wall of 50.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 100, one of the resources to 300, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:148
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:149
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:148
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:149
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 10 and a Wall of 20.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 125, one of the resources to 350, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:150
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:150
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Arcomage games here start with each player having a Tower of 50 and a Wall of 50.  The object is to get to either a Tower of 100, one of the resources to 300, or to destroy your opponent's Tower."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:151
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:151
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Lost Book of Khel will advance my skills in the dark arts beyond that of even Sandro!  I am forever in your debt!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:152
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:152
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We need to consult Korbu!  You have agreed to bring us his remains and his Sarcophagus!  Do not bother us until you have these items!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:153
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Korbu?  He was the greatest of our kind, and yet he always seemed troubled.  There are some of us that remember the times before he left. He always seemed disturbed to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:154
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Korbu left us after making the \"Arrangement\" with the necromancers here in Shadowspire.  We aid them in any research they are working on, and assist with the defense of their guild.  In return we are allowed to feed on the local population without hindrance."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:155
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:155
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Guild of Necromancers is very stingy when it comes to parting with Lich Jars.  You may be better off seeking out Zanthora, and obtaining one from her."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:156
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "the Lost Book of Khel is rumored to hold the secrets to the ultimate powers of the dark art of necromancy.  It may be good that no one knows where it is!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:157
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:157
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Bastian Loudrin has been a great friend to the guild. Sadly, I must refuse his request at this time. Even as we speak, my guild is embroiled in a battle for its very survival. For you see, the Temple of the Sun has declared a holy war on us. Most of our members are away in the fields either leading armies or raising zombies to serve in them.\n"
"\n"
"I wish I could say otherwise, but the accursed temple holds the upper hand. If only the balance would tilt in our favor."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:158
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:158
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If we had the Nightshade Brazier back in our possession, Shadowspire's defense would not be an issue. We could bring this war to the doors of the Sun Temple. We would annihilate them!\n"
"\n"
"Knowing its importance, the clerics keep the brazier in a secure chamber deep within their temple. Dyson Leland believes he can gain access to that chamber. Bring him to the temple, recover the brazier and return it to me. You want me in your alliance? Well, do this for me, and I will be in your debt.\n"
"\n"
"If you have any questions about the Nightshade Brazier ask Thant. It was he who created the thing."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:159
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will not join you until the security of the guild is secure. Bring me the Nightshade Brazier from the Temple of the Sun in Murmurwoods. We will talk again of alliance after that is done."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:160
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:160
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Early on our conflict, the Sun Temple attempted to infiltrate our ranks with a spy. Such foolishness--thinking they could so easily deceive a host of dark magicians!\n"
"\n"
"It was child's play to unmask their agent--one \"Dyson Leland.\" Since then we have turned him against his former masters, or so it would seem. Frankly, I don't entirely trust in his loyalty. Still, he has proven useful. As long as he does, we will continue to let him live."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:161
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:161
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"How can anyone's quest for power bring him to participate in the horrors of the Dark Path? And yet, here is a whole house of them! Oh, they will call themselves \"seekers of knowledge,\" but these magicians of death are abomination! Loathsome corruption incarnate!\n"
"\n"
"Only through my own fear can the foul Necromancers' Guild call itself \"my master.\""
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:162
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:162
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When I was young, all I wanted to do was to join the Order of Light--to be a selfless servant of the good. As soon as I was of age, I entered the Temple of the Sun with a heart filled with the fire of purity.\n"
"\n"
"What a fool I was. If there is goodness in the world, I have not seen it. There is certainly none in the halls of the Sun Temple! Hiding behind the righteousness of sanctity, Order members perform the worst crimes of greed and self-indulgence. If it were not so horrid, it would pass for something like irony."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:163
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A few months ago, I was called to a private audience with the Sun Temple head priest, Oskar Tyre. He sent me out on a mission of infiltration against the Necromancers' Guild. \"Become as they are,\" he said. \"Gain their trust. While you bide your time waiting to deliver a killing blow, feed us their secrets.\"\n"
"\n"
"A too simple plan from too simple a leader! Oh, I did as he said, bathing myself in evil so I might seem evil. But it was as if the guild could see into my heart. I was unmasked as a spy. Under threat of death, I now follow their orders. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:164
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join with you? An interesting idea. But what can you offer me? After all I have been through I find myself consumed with a thirst for revenge. I would go with you, but am unwilling to spend my efforts lightly. Give me an opportunity to hurt one of my enemies--the cursed Temple of the Sun or the abominable Necromancers' Guild--and I will travel with you gladly."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:165
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that the Nightshade Brazier covers Shadowspire in its fortifying darkness. Thant goes to lead his minions."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:166
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:166
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Certainly the elemental unrest concerns us greatly. Why one need travel only a short distance north from our temple to see a great maelstrom of unnatural duration and fury. But sadly we have other matters pressing.\n"
"\n"
"The sick horror that is the Necromancers' Guild must be blighted from this land! We wage holy war on the evil in Shadowspire. Our entire spirit and power goes into the campaign we wage against Sandro and his minions. Until that is done we cannot entertain participation in your alliance."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:167
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Then again, we could spare some resources for your alliance if the war would turn in our favor. Perhaps you could be our agent of fortune?\n"
"\n"
"Inside the Necromancers' Guild is a device known as the \"Skeleton Transformer.\" It converts living creatures into the skeletons which the dark mages use for the bulk of their reinforcements. If it were destroyed, we would quickly have the upper hand.\n"
"\n"
"We have an agent, Dyson Leland, placed in their guild. Find him and help him to wreck their skeleton making device. Do this and I will consider your request more favorably."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:168
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You come here again with talk of alliance? I have told you what you must do. Go to the Necromancers' Guild in Shadowspire, find Dyson Leland and help him to destroy their Skeleton Transformer!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:169
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:169
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Excellent work! With the Skeleton Transformer destroyed, I am more than confident that the light of righteousness will cleanse Shadowspire of evil. The Necromancers' Guild is as good as no more.\n"
"\n"
"As I agreed, you may now consider the Temple of the Sun an ally against the elemental cataclysm. I myself will sit on your alliance council in Ravenshore. I will make my departure arrangements with all due haste."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:170
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take the prophecy so lightly that you shirk the role it has cast for you? These are dire times calling for dire actions from all. Go forth across the land and forge the unity represented by the alliance. Go, unless you favor the oblivion that threatens us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:171
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Using Arion Hunter's boats we have managed to gather some information. I sent one to Ravage Roaming and another to the Dagger Wound Islands. It is reported that strange portal gateways have appeared in both regions. The gateway in the islands stands on the slopes of the large volcano that rose from the sea southeast of the main island. The Ravage Roaming portal is in the middle of the large lake. It is said that the water which formed the lake flooded out of the gateway."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:172
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Within hours of our first meeting, a most fortuitous development occurred. We were contacted by a great sage, Xanthor, of the Ironfist courts of Enroth!\n"
"\n"
"Using his great magic, he projected his image into this very chamber. He and Roland and Catherine Ironfist were at sea off our shores when the cataclysm occurred. They survived the resulting storms and now would like to land in Ravenshore to aid the alliance. Unfortunately, they are blocked by the Regnan pirate fleet. We must help them to land. Xanthor claims much knowledge of what has happened here. We need his council!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:173
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:173
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our sources believe the main Regnan fleet is in a hidden port somewhere on Regna Island. If you could sink the fleet in dock you could greatly cripple their ability to patrol the seas off our shore. Unfortunately, we don't have a fleet of our own strong enough to make a landing on Regna.\n"
"\n"
"Brekish Onefang has gotten message to us that the Regnans have built an outpost on an atoll off the main Dagger Wound Island. He believes this outpost is resupplied by mysterious means. His scouts never see ships land there, but they are always well stocked. Perhaps you should go there and solve the mystery. Perhaps the answer will convey you to Regna?\n"
"\n"
"Regardless of the means, the Regnan fleet must be sunk if the Ironfists are to land in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:174
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Your good work sinking the Regnan fleet has already had the desired results. Just yesterday morning, Catherine and Roland Ironfist arrived along with their sage, Xanthor. With them in the alliance, we are made stronger--immeasurably so.\n"
"\n"
"I will admit that the time of this crisis has contained some of my darkest moments. Thanks to your efforts I believe that the worst of this is over. I have hopes that we will indeed survive this."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:175
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:175
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must sink that Regnan fleet! It is imperative that the Ironfists be allowed to land safely. Their sage Xanthor has knowledge of the crisis that we cannot do without."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:176
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For all their claims of empire and their airs of civilization, the Regnans are the worst scum of Jadame. Why I cannot find myself the least bit surprised that they would take advantage of the crisis to expand their pirating operations. What concerns me most is their new outpost on Dagger Wound. I am sure they mean to use it as a base of attack on the continent. Why, it even puts them in striking distance of Ravenshore!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:177
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:177
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I have only met with him briefly, but I am convinced that Xanthor is remarkably knowledgeable about the workings of the elemental planes. Apparently he learned much from the Ironfists' elemental allies during their recent campaigns against the devils of Erathia.\n"
"\n"
"Even now he studies the strange crystal in the town square. You may find him there, or perhaps in the nearby residence we have provided him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:178
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We of the council have great faith in this Xanthor. He has told me that he is formulating a plan for dealing with the elemental crisis. If anyone can find a solution to our problems, it is he.\n"
"\n"
"If you would help us further, be of service to this great sage. Consult with him about the crystal and see what you might do for him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:179
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:179
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We look to Xanthor to formulate our next actions. Go to him and see how you can help."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:180
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That we have been joined by the royal court of Enroth has been nothing but good. I was worried they would be afflicted with the need for pomp which infects many other monarchs. I am gladdened to report that this is not the case with this king and queen. They disembarked and set directly to work on our problem. As key members of our alliance, you will find access to them easy. We have put them up in houses here in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:181
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:181
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "From what Xanthor has told us, I'm sure all of the elemental planes are dangerous. Still, I would advise you to take particular caution when exploring the Plane of Fire. Its denizens, according to reports from the Ironsand Desert, are being particularly belligerent."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:182
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All I know of the Plane Between Planes is what I learned from the Alvarian loremasters. Still, if the Destroyer's base is there, proceed with the greatest caution! It is said the plane is made of the stuff of chaos from which all the other planes are formed as if from clay. While chaos has a form, it is fluid. Whatever you see there will not be as it seems. And what is there may be subject to continuous change."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:183
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What the Alvar loremasters told me of the Plane Between Planes applies here. While I am sure the prisons of the elemental lords are prisons in every sense of the word, I am equally sure that they will not appear as one would expect."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:184
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Merchant Guild of Alvar owes you a great debt. As a small measure of repayment, we have decided to make this merchanthouse permanently available to you. Please take this gift from us as a token of our profound gratitude for your valorous deeds."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:185
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:185
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know being part of your alliance is important work. Still, I do miss the hunt! I keep imagining all the good fun my men are having while I'm here pushing around papers.\n"
"\n"
"Hurry up with this alliance business! I want to get this mess taken care of with dispatch! Without the thrill of the hunt, my life is missing its usual spark."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:186
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Judging from the tactics employed by the Regnan pirates, I suspect that Blackwell Cooper is involved. Cooper is an old…shall we say, \"associate,\" of mine. Why, if I were a gambling man, I'd bet gold that he is leading the Regnan expeditionary force on Dagger Wound."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:187
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:187
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know I hold the council's minority opinion on the subject, but really, I don't see why we have to involve some charlatan magician in this matter! Surely this crisis is solvable, like most things, with judicious application of a length of well-forged steel."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:188
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:188
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fah! If you ask me, this idea of Xanthor's is foolhardy! I say if we're facing attack by elemental armies, we should be raising an army to meet them. Frankly, all this talk of prophecy leaves me uneasy. This council is too much under the sway of the Ironfist's pet wizard. I say we take the fight to the elemental planes and introduce the invaders to the sharp edges of our blades!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:189
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I tell you, this Xanthor is sending you on a wild goose chase. \"Plane Between Planes,\" indeed! What hogwash! The worst of it is that we make no preparations for war in the event the crazy scheme fails, which I expect it will. This mad following of prophecy flies in the face of good military sense!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:190
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have had more of my share of doubts about this Xanthor, but it is the mark of a man how readily he admits his errors. It is clear to me now that he has given nothing but good and effective advise. If he tells you to rescue the elemental lords, then that is what you must do. Go! And good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:191
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Good to see you again, Heroes of Jadame. A good job there, saving the world, and all. You certainly have my thanks, and I'm sure, the thanks of many.\n"
"\n"
"I'm sure you've got plenty of other opportunities at this point, but let me know if you want a job hunting Dragons. Probably not much of a challenge for the likes of you, but the offer stands!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:192
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Small ones, hurry with your alliance preparations! My patience with this land lacking in caves and prey grows dangerously thin. Not only must I sleep in a barn, these people do not even raise cattle. I must live off of fish! Fah!\n"
"\n"
"If you value my good temper, be quick!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:193
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Reaching Regna Island is no small challenge. One of my scouts has reported to me that Regnan boats lie thick on the sea. He also said he saw that the Regnans have a craft that can travel beneath the water. It is said they supply their Dagger Wound outpost with the craft. Perhaps you can use it to reach Regna. The pirates will either miss your passage or take you for one of their own."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:194
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know this is not the time to think of revenge, but I would pass onto you something I learned about my enemy, Charles Quixote. The Minotaur king, Masul, mentioned that Quixote keeps a sword of great power with him in his keep. It is called, \"Snake.\" Perhaps your acquiring of it would help the alliance cause?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:195
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My Dragon patrols have located two of the elemental gateways. One lies on the side of a large volcano southeast of the largest Dagger Wound Islands. The other is located in the center of the large lake in Ravage Roaming. I know not where they lead, but you will have to cross a lot of water to reach either."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:196
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An Erathian Dragon visited my cave shortly before you arrived there. He reported to me that a new type of Dragon, one seemingly made of crystalline rock, has been seen in Erathia. I'm not sure why I tell you this. Perhaps the giant crystal in the town square reminds me of the story. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:197
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Interesting that the Destroyer himself sends you to undo his works. I guess I am not surprised. The workings of the greater Powers are mysterious at best."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:198
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have done this land and Dragonkind a great service. For this, we owe you. Know that we will tolerate your presence in our caves, further, we will not hunt you as prey."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:199
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Did you know that our temple in Murmurwoods is the first in this land of Jadame? It is our mission to bring the Light to all corners of the world--even here. We were surprised to see that our enemies, the Necromancers' Guild had preceded our arrival with their own. But no matter, they will soon be dealt with.\n"
"\n"
"Say, don't you think this merchant house would make a fine Sun Temple? I will bring it up with Fellmoon after the crisis is over."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:200
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:200
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you're off to Regna, you might want to look for the Mace of the Sun. When my brothers and I made the crossing from Erathia, we were attacked by the Regnan fleet. All but one of our ships escaped. Sadly, the lost ship was the one carrying the mission leader, Brother Howe. He had the weapon in his possession. I saw Brother Howe slain by the pirates, but perhaps they still have the mace."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:203
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You know…I have a power stone that will activate the portal to the abandoned temple. And you have one that will allow us to reach the island where that portal is!\n"
"\n"
"If we joined forces, we could reach the temple with ease. What say you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:204
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:204
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Looks like your party's all full up, so I can't travel with you now. But the offer still stands. If you need me, I'll be at the Adventurer's Inn."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:205
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Simon Templar, the knight, into your party?  If you would like Simon Templar to join you, click YES.  If you would like him to wait for you at the Adventurer's Inn, click NO."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:207
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Very well. You have done as I have asked of you. Now I will return the favor. I will travel with you to meet your merchant guildmaster, and perhaps beyond if you will have me. There is little for me here.\n"
"\n"
"Shall we be off?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:208
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It seems that you're party is too full for me to join. I will therefore travel alone to the Adventurer's Inn. Meet me there when you have room. Until then, farewell."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:209
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Would you like Arius the Minotaur to join you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:210
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will be happy to journey with you when your party is not so full. I will travel to the Adventurer's Inn. If you need me, I'll be there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:211
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you have Rohani Oscleton the Dark Elf join you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:212
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm glad you've decided to take me, but your party is too full. I guess I'll start my adventure by traveling to the Adventurer's Inn. See you there!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:213
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I am ready to travel. Shall we go?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:214
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmmm. It seems your party is full. I will travel to the Adventure's Inn. You will find me there ready to join you when you have room. Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:215
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Ithilgore the Dragon into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:216
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though your party is full, I will still join your cause. I will travel to the Adventurer's Inn. Meet me there if you want me to travel with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:217
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Karanya Memoria the Necromancer into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:218
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:218
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I cannot travel with you now; your party is too full. If you want me to journey with you, you will find me at the Adventurer's Inn."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:219
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you accept Maylander the Cleric as a follower?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:220
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm, I prefer to travel with a smaller party than you have. Tell you what…I'll travel to the Adventurer's Inn. If you want me I'll be there. 'Til then, farewell."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:221
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will always be in your debt for saving my father.  It would be an honor and a privilege if you allowed me to travel with you.'"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:222
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though I am honored that you would have me, I cannot join you for your party is full.  You can find me in the Adventurer's Inn if you ever wish my services."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:223
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Clan of Balthazar will always be in your debt for recovering the Axe of Balthazar and returning it to Masul.  Long may Masul lead us!  I would be honored if you would allow me to travel with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:224
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:224
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am honored that you would allow me to travel with you, however, I see that your group is full.  I will travel to the Adventurer's Inn.  You can find me there if you wish me to join you in your travels."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:225
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that my herd is safe, I will gladly join you. I'm sure Herdmaster Masul will not object to me helping the saviors of my people. Shall we?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:226
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can see that your party is too large to include me in its ranks. Still, my thirst for adventure has been whetted by your offer. I will travel to Ravenshore and seek my fortune there. Perhaps you will find me at the Adventurer's Inn there. I will look for you there!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:227
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Jasp Thelbourne the Dark Elf into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:228
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I'd be happy to go with you now, but your party is too full. But, I will make my services available to you. I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Seek me there if you would have me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:229
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Gethric Mercutura the Vampire into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:230
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:230
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, but your party is too full. But now, it is settled. It is a life of adventure I seek! I will travel to the Adventurer's Inn. If you will have me, I will be there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:231
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Flamdring the Dragon into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:232
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join them? Yes? But no, their numbers are too great. But adventure I still seek. Well then, to the Adventurer's Inn I must go, for there gather those who would seek their fortunes."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:233
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you travel with Hevatia Deverbero the Necromancer?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:234
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your party is too full for me to join. I will go to the Adventure's Inn. You can take me into your group there if you have the room."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:235
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Verish the Cleric into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:236
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know I would serve the Light well by joining you, but your party is too full. I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Meet me there if you have the room."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:237
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Nelix Uriel the Knight into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:238
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can't go with you. Your party is too full. But you know? Things here are wrapping up and I have little to do. I'll travel to the Adventurer's Inn and seek my fortune there. Maybe we'll meet up there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:239
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Sethrc Thistlebone the Troll into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:240
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm…you're party is too full, but still I wish to help you. I will go to the Adventure's Inn. If you need a strong clubber, you will find me there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:241
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you care to travel with Rionel the Minotaur?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:242
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can't go with you now. Your party is full. I will still make myself available to you. If you need me, I'll be at the Adventurer's Inn."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:243
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Adric Stellare the Dark Elf into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:244
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:244
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, I will gladly join you. Unfortunately, your party is too full. Tell you what. I'll go to the Adventurer's Inn. If you want to travel with me, you'll find me there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:245
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take the Vampire Infaustus into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:246
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would go with you, but your party is too full. I prefer to travel with fewer people. I go now to the Adventurer's Inn. There I will find my companions."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:247
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you ask Brimstone the Dragon to join you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:248
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, but your party is too full. Still, you are clearly the ones I seek. I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Join with me there when you have room."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:249
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many our the Shadowspire Guild thanks for recovering the Lost Book of Khel! Perhaps I can join you in your travels to provide my own personal assistance?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:250
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would like to join you in your travels to provide my own personal assistance but I see that your group is full.  You can find me in the Adventurer's Inn if you need me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:251
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was very noble of you to seek a cure for the knight, Blazen Stormlance.  I would like to join you in your quest! Will you have me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:252
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish I could join with you now, but your party is too full. I will wait for you in the Adventurer's Inn. Until then, good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:253
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Tempus the Knight into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:254
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:254
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I cannot travel go with you. Your party is much too large for my preferences. I like to work with a smaller, more mobile group. Tell you what. I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Join me there once you get rid of some of your dead weight."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:255
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will your travel with Thorne Understone the Troll?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:256
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:256
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great. Listen. I have some business I need to attend to before I can go with you. We'll meet at the Adventurer's Inn. I will join you there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:257
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:257
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Will you take Ulbrecht the Minotaur into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:258
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:258
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would go with you now, but your party is too full. I will make preparations then travel to the Adventurer's Inn. Meet me there when you have room for me. Until then, good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:259
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:259
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks again for your help!  May I join you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:260
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:260
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I would like to join you in your adventures but your group is already full!  I will await you in the Adventurer's Inn."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:261
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take Artorius Veritas the Vampire into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:262
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:262
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can't go with you, your party is too full. I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Join me there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:263
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:263
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you take the Dragon, Duroth the Eternal into your party?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:264
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:264
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will join you, but not now. I have to see to some matters which will take me some days to deal with. After I'm done I will go to the Adventurer's Inn. Meet me there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:265
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:265
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do you agree to travel with Nathaniel Roberts the Necromancer?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:266
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:266
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fah! You are more a mob than an adventuring party. I'm looking for a smaller group. I will seek them at the Adventurer's Inn. If you want to journey with me…well, perhaps you'll find me there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:267
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:267
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I will gladly join you. My desire for revenge has been a thirst long in need of slaking. You have provided me with the cup. Let us go and fill it!\n"
"\n"
"Dyson Leland offers to join your party. Do you accept?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:268
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:268
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Your group is too full for me to join, but here is my plan…I will make my escape from the guild and meet you at the Adventurer's Inn. It may take me some time to get there, as I must travel with caution.\n"
"\n"
"Meet me there when you can. My revenge has waited for over a year. It can wait a few more weeks. Wish me luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:269
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:269
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will be forever in your debt.  Not only did you rescue me from the lair of Zanthora, but you helped my daughter be promoted by Sir Charles Quixote.  I would like to join you in your travels!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:270
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:270
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Unfortunately, there is not enough room in your group for me to join you now.  I can be found in the Adventurer's Inn if you need me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:303
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:303
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To achieve Grand Mastery of the staff, you must deal with me! Before I can instruct you, you must have reached a Master Skill level of 10 with the staff, and pay my price of 8000 gold.  If you meet my qualifications, I will teach you to wield the staff dealing out addition damage equal to the level of your skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:307
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:307
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have a dagger and I bet I can kill you before you draw yours! Speed can kill and the dagger is the fastest weapon! With what I can teach you, you can carry another weapon in your off hand. Two are better than one. The Expert skills of the dagger can be yours if you have a dagger skill level of 4 and can pay my modest fee of 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:308
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:308
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ha!  The fastest survive! As a Master of the dagger I have and will survive! My teachings can greatly increase your chance of causing critical damage! If you have an Expert skill level of 7 and 5000 gold I can lead you to Mastery!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:309
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:309
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The quickest dagger--the one that is never seen--is the ultimate weapon.  You can rapidly attack your foe before he has a chance to strike you once.  With Grand Mastery of the dagger, this can be yours.  You must have a Master skill level of 10 and 8000 gold to receive my instruction."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:311
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:311
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mastery of the axe and skilled hands can split an opponent's head like a pudding. With my instruction you can have this ability! You blows will cause more damage than before, devastating your opponents! But first you must have an Expert skill level of 7 with the axe and pay my price of 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:312
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:312
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As a Grand Master of the axe, your opponents' armor will mean nothing.  The effectiveness of their armor will be cut in half as you slice it from their carcasses! I can teach you this skill, but you first must have a Master skill level of 10 with the axe and pay me 8000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:313
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:313
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Spear expertise makes you one with your weapon.  With this skill you will cause more damage to your foes.  I can raise you to an Expert level if your skill level is 4 and you have 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:314
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:314
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The spear is your weapon of choice? Would you like to learn to carry a shield or another weapon in your off hand to improve your combat ability?  This Master knowledge can be yours if you have an Expert skill level of 7 with the spear and 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:321
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:321
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A greater chance to subdue your foes means a smaller chance you will be hurt yourself.  Grand Mastery of the mace will increase your chances of stunning or even paralyzing your foes.  If you have a Master skill level of 10 and can pay me 8000 gold, I will instruct you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:322
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:322
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, now that things seem to be settled with our little war with the Temple of the Sun. Sandro has said that guild members may turn their attention to other matters. Since arriving in Jadame, I have seen little of it save for the lands of Shadowspire. Say...perhaps you could use my services!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:323
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:323
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish I could join with you. Sadly, our war with the Temple of the Sun takes up all of our time. The guild cannot spare me now."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:324
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:324
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes! I would love to join with you. Now that our holy war against the foul Necromancers' Guild seems to be going well, I find I have little to do around here. I will go with you if you will take me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:325
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:325
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The shield can be your friend.  It keeps those who wish you dead from striking at you.  With the Expert skill in shield I can teach you, you will eliminate the penalty to your weapon's recovery for carrying a shield.  This skill can be yours for 1000 gold and proof of a skill level of 4 with the shield."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:337
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:337
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With Expert Fire Magic you can learn all of the Expert spells for Fire.  Higher level spells may prove more potent and of greater assistance to your party.  Expert Fire Magic can be yours if you have a skill level of 4 in Fire Magic and can pay the price of 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:338
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:338
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With Master Fire Magic you can learn all of the Master spells for this element.  Higher level spells may prove more potent and of greater assistance to your party.  Master Fire Magic can be yours if you have an Expert skill level of 7 in Fire Magic and can pay the price of 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

