#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:363
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:363
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With Grand Master Dark Magic you can learn all of the Grand Master spells for this element.  Higher level spells may prove more potent and of greater assistance to your party.  Grand Master Dark Magic can be yours if you have a Master skill level of 10 in Dark Magic and can pay the price of 8000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:364
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:364
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Advancing your skills to the level of Expert with your natural Dark Elf Ability grants you the use of the Travelers' Boon spell. This spell combines the effects of the spells Wizard Eye, Torch Light and Feather Fall.  To achieve an Expert Skill level your normal Skill level must be 4 and you must pay me 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:365
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:365
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mastery of your natural Dark Elf ability would make you that much stronger!  With Mastery you gain the ability to Blind your opponents during battle.  To reach the Skill level of Master you must have and Expert Skill level of 7 and pay me 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:366
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:366
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek the skill of a Grand Master Dark Elf?  Not many gain this title.  Grand Mastery bestows the power of the spell Darkfire. This is a truly devastating magical attack!  You will need to prove you hold a Master skill level of 10 and pay a small fee of 8000 gold.  Once these requirements are met, Grand Mastery is yours!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:367
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:367
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Advancing your skills to the level of Expert with your natural Vampire Ability grants you the use of the Levitate spell.  To achieve an Expert skill level your normal skill level must be 4 and you must pay me 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:368
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:368
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mastery of your natural Vampire ability would make you that much stronger!  With Mastery you gain the ability to Charm your opponents during battle.  To reach the skill level of Master you must have an Expert skill level of 7 and pay me 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:369
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:369
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek the skill of a Grand Master Vampire?  Not many gain this title.  Grand Mastery bestows the power of Mistform, which makes you immune to all physical attacks!  Of course you will only be able to attack with spells in this form, but is well worth it!  You will need to prove a Master Skill level of 10 to me and pay a small fee of 8000 old.  Once these requirements are met, Grand Mastery is yours!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:370
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:370
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Advancing your skills to the level of Expert with your natural Dragon Ability grants you the use of the Flame Blast spell. This spell increases the power of your already might breath weapon.  To achieve an Expert skill level your normal skill level must be 4 and you must pay me 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:371
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:371
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mastery of your natural Dragon Ability would make you that much stronger!  With Mastery you gain the ability of Flight, allowing you to carry your entire party!  To reach the skill level of Master you must have an Expert Skill level of 7 and pay me 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:372
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:372
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek the skill of a Grand Master Dragon?  Not many gain this title.  Grand Mastery bestows the power of the Wing Buffet attack!  This attack pushes your opponents back, allowing you to unleash the full power of your Flame Blast!  You will need to prove a Master Skill level of 10 to me and pay a small fee of 8000 gold.  Once these requirements are met, Grand Mastery is yours!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:374
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:374
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wands, scrolls, rings and potions can be important items, and not knowing what they are is just foolishness.  With Mastery of the Identify Items skill you can attempt to identify weapons, armor, and other miscellaneous items.  For a small fee of 2500 gold and demonstration of an Expert Skill level of 7, I can teach you Mastery of the Identify Items skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:375
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:375
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Found and ancient item or relic and don’t know what it does or what its for?  Ignorance, in this case, is not bliss. In fact, it could very well kill. With Grand Mastery of the Identify Item skill you can attempt to identify anything you have found including artifacts and relics.  A Master skill level of 10 and 6000 gold is all that is required to learn this skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:376
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:376
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shop owners are a greedy lot.  Want to get better prices for what you buy and sell?  Then you better have the Merchant skill and fast. I can teach you the Expert level Merchant skill if you have a skill level of 4 and pay 2000 gold.  Expertise doubles your bonus towards prices."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:377
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:377
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shop owners are a greedy lot.  Want to get better prices for what you buy and sell?  Then you better have the Merchant skill and learn the ins and outs of trading. I can teach you Mastery of the Merchant skill if you have an Expert skill level of 7, a Personality of 50 and pay 5000 gold.  Mastery triples your bonus towards prices."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:378
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:378
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shop owners are a greedy lot.  Want to get better prices for what you buy and sell?  Then you better have the Merchant skill and learn the ins and outs of trading. I can teach you Grand Mastery of the Merchant skill if you have a Master skill level of 10 and pay 8000 gold.  Grand Mastery allows you to pay and receive the actual price for goods.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:379
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:379
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your equipment is only as good as the person who repairs it.  If you can't fix it, you could find yourself stuck in the wilderness with no armor or weapons.  This could be extraordinarily bad. Expertise with the Repair Item skill allows you not only the chance of repairing weapons, but armor as well.  This skill can be yours if you have a skill level of 4 and pay 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:380
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:380
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your equipment is only as good as the person who repairs it.  If you can't fix it, you could find yourself stuck in the wilderness with no armor or weapons.  This could be extraordinarily bad. Mastery of the Repair Item skill allows you not only the chance of repairing weapons and armor, but any broken miscellaneous item as well.  This skill can be yours if you have an Expert skill level of 7 and pay 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:381
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:381
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your equipment is only as good as the person who repairs it.  If you can't fix it, you could find yourself stuck in the wilderness with no armor or weapons.  This could be extraordinarily bad. A Grand Master of the Repair Items kill can fix ANYTHING that is broken.  This skill can be yours if you have a Master skill level of 10 and pay 6000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:382
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:382
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you think you are adventurers, do you?  There's not enough meat on you to protect you from the slap of a Dark Dwarven child!  Body Building is the only way to go.  You will be stronger and tougher than before!  An Expert of Body Building is tougher than the normal hero.  I can teach you this if your skill level is 4, pay 500 gold and are ready to sweat!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:383
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:383
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you think you are adventurers, do you?  There's not enough meat on you to protect you from the slap of a baby Troll!  Body Building is the only way to go.  You will be stronger and tougher than before!  A Master of Body Building is much tougher than the average hero.  I can teach you this if your Expert skill level is 7, pay 2500 gold and have and Endurance of 50! No pain no gain!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:384
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:384
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you think you are adventurers, do you?  There's not enough meat on you to protect you from the slap of a baby Dragon!  Body Building is the only way to go.  You will be stronger and tougher than before!  A Grand Master of Body Building is the toughest hero you can find.  I can teach you this if your Master skill level is 9, pay 6000 gold and have and Endurance of 50! No pain no gain!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:385
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:385
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not enough spell points for casting those Expert spells?  Meditation is what you need.  With an Expert skill in Meditation you get a double bonus to your available spell points.  This could mean one more powerful spell when you most need it!  Expertise can be yours if your skill level is 4 and pay me 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:386
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:386
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not enough spell points for casting those Master spells?  Meditation is what you need.  With a Master skill in Meditation you get a triple bonus to your available spell points.  This could mean one more powerful spell when you most need it!  Mastery can be yours if your Expert skill level is 7 and pay me 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:387
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:387
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not enough spell points for casting those Grand Master spells?  Meditation is what you need.  With a Grand Master skill in Meditation you get a quadruple bonus to your available spell points.  This could mean one or more powerful spells when you most need them!  Grand Mastery can be yours if your Master skill level is 10 and pay me 6000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:388
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:388
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Things are sometime hidden in the dungeons and castles of this land.   You may have missed something without even knowing it was there.  Perception increases your chance of finding these hidden things. Expertise in the Perception skill doubles your chances.  For 500 gold and a skill level of 4 in Perception, I will teach you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:389
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:389
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Things are sometime hidden in the dungeons and castles of this land.   You may have missed something without even knowing it was there.  Perception increases your chance of finding these hidden things. Mastery of the Perception skill triples your chances.  For 2500 gold and an Expert skill level of 7 in Perception, I will teach you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:390
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:390
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Things are sometime hidden in the dungeons and castles of this land.  You may have missed something without even knowing it was there.  Perception increases your chance of finding these hidden things. Grand Mastery of the Perception skill quintuples your chances. For 6000 gold and a Master skill level of 10 in Perception, I will teach you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:391
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:391
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An Expert level in the Regeneration skill doubles the number of hit points that you recover over time.  Expert teaching of this skill requires a normal skill level of 4 and a fee of 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:392
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:392
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A Master skill level in the Regeneration skill triples the number of hit points that you recover over time.  Master teaching of this skill requires a Expert skill level of 7 and a fee of 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:393
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:393
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Mastery of the Regeneration skill quadruples the number of hit points that you recover over time.  Grand Master teaching of this skill requires a Master skill level of 10 and a fee of 8000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:394
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:394
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tired of chests blowing up in your face?  Sick of poison gas clouds, fireballs, and lightning bolts sending party members to the Great Beyond?  Expert Disarm Trap doubles your chance of disarming these traps before they go off.  I will teach you Expert Disarm Trap if you have a skill level of 4 and can pay 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:395
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:395
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tired of chests blowing up in your face?  Sick of poison gas clouds, fireballs, and lightning bolts sending party members to the Great Beyond?  Master Disarm Trap triples your chance of disarming these traps before they go off.  I will teach you Master Disarm Trap if you have an Expert skill level of 7 and can pay 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:396
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:396
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tired of chests blowing up in your face?  Sick of poison gas clouds, fireballs, and lightning bolts sending party members to the Great Beyond?  Grand Master Disarm Trap eliminates these pesky traps entirely before they go off.  I will teach you Grand Master Disarm Trap if you have a Master skill level of 10 and can pay 6000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:397
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:397
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish I could. Unfortunately, we make holy war with the foul Necromancers' Guild. All of the Sun Temple's resources, including myself, are dedicated to that cause."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:398
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:398
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Adventure with you? Yes I will. In fact, before he left, Charles Quixote suggested just that. \"Nelix,\" he said, \"if those alliance heroes come by, you ought to consider going with them.\" Apparently, he thinks highly of you. Well, his recommendation is enough for me. Shall we go?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:399
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:399
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Go with you? I think not. Why would I want to join up with a bunch of amateurs when I have all the action I can handle here? Don't make me laugh. What can you offer me that a life of Dragon hunting does not?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:400
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:400
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Go with you? I like the idea, but I must stay here. I am one of the last veteran warriors left here. I must stay to protect the village."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:401
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:401
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, that sounds good. Though the village could use me to protect it, I think the best I could do for it would be to go with you. My people will be destroyed if the cataclysm is not ended. If I can do something to stop it, I should."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:402
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:402
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join your group? I would be glad to. Not only have you done a great service for my herd, it has become clear to me that your actions will decide our very survival."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:403
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:403
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Knowing what you are up against in combat can mean the difference between life and death.  Being able to identify the monsters and opponents you are fighting can make this difference. I can teach you Expert Identify Monster if you already have a skill level of 4 and pay 500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:404
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:404
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "He who runs away today lives to run away another day.  This doesn't necessarily mean he is a coward, however.  He may just be very smart.  He may know how his opponent attacks and what spells he may use, if any.  I can teach you Master Identify Monster if you have achieved an Expert skill level of 7 and can pay 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:405
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:405
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you can probe your enemies defenses and know his weaknesses, you will always prevail.  With Grand Mastery of Identify Monster, you will know how your enemies attack and what their defenses are.  This knowledge will allow you to attack their weakest points. I can raise you to Grand Master of this skill if you have a Master skill level of 10 and pay 6000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:406
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:406
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Knowledge of a single weapon is great.  Having knowledge of all weapons is even better.  Expert Armsmaster skill increases you chance to hit with any melee weapon you can wield. I can make you an Expert Armsmaster if you have a skill level of 4 and pay 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:407
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:407
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Knowledge of a single melee weapon is great.  Having knowledge of all melee weapons is even better. Master Armsmaster increases the damage you do with any weapon you can wield. I can make you a Master Armsmaster if you have an Expert skill level of 7 and pay 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:408
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:408
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Knowledge of a single melee weapon is great.  Having knowledge of all melee weapons is even better.  Armsmaster skill decreases the recovery time of any melee weapon you are already skilled with and gives the chance for greater inflicted damage.  Grand Master expertise doubles both your chance to hit and damage bonuses for the skill. I can make you a Grand Master Armsmaster if you have a Master skill level of 10 and pay 8000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:409
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:409
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join you? I must decline the offer. Though you have done a great service for my herd, I am not yet sure of your leadership. I want to help fight the cataclysm, but I'm not sure your way is the right one."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:410
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:410
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't think your exploits have gone unnoticed! Clearly you are adventurers of the highest caliber. I would consider joining your team…that is, if you will have me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:411
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:411
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see you too are adventurers. But…well, can I be frank? Though I don't doubt your potential, clearly you are not the most experienced group I've seen. I'd be happy to join you if you were more…shall we say, \"seasoned?\""
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:414
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:414
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The black potion is the Alchemist's ultimate creation!  They can affect so many different things and are even wonderful to taste!  Grand Mastery of Alchemy can be yours if you have a Master skill level of 10 in Alchemy, possess one of each of the best reagents and pay 6000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:415
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:415
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Learning allows you to gain more experience from your travels and encounters. Expert Learning doubles the bonus to gained experience, leading you down the path of greater wisdom.  I will instruct you in Expert Learning if your skill level is 4 and you pay me 2000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:416
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:416
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Learning allows you to gain more experience from your travels and encounters. Master Learning triples the bonus to gained experience, leading you down the path of greater wisdom.  I will instruct you in Master Learning if you have an Expert skill level of 7, pay me 5000 gold and have and Intellect of 50."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:417
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:417
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Learning allows you to gain more experience from your travels and encounters. Grand Master Learning quintuples the bonus to gained experience, leading you down the path of greater wisdom.  I will instruct you in Grand Master Learning if you have a Master skill level of 10, pay me 8000 gold and have and Intellect of 50."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:418
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:418
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Puddle Thain, is a most promising student.  If you seek Expert instruction in the uses of the Staff, you can find him in the city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:419
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:419
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Celia Stone, Master of the Staff, dwells in Troll village of Rust in the Ironsand Desert.  She can instruct you to Mastery of the Staff is that is what you desire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:420
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:420
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Tristen Stillwater, instructs all students of the Staff.  Only he can help you in attaining Grand Mastery of this fine weapon.  Seek him out in the city of Twilight at the base of the Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:421
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:421
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Aerie Luodrin currently dwells in Ravenshore.  She is a most dedicated student of the uses of the Sword and can instruct you to and Expert skill level with the weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:422
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:422
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Unfortunately Jaycin Cardron, Master of the Sword, felt that his skills would be more, shall we say, \"profitable taught\" to the Dragon Hunter's of Garrote Gorge.  If you seek Master skill level with the Sword, you will have to go to him at the Garrote Gorge Dragon Hunter Camp."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:423
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:423
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Miyon Dragontracker, Grand Master of the Sword, has joined the knight, Charles Quixote in his quest to exterminate the Dragons of Garrote Gorge.  You can find Miyon at the Dragon Hunter's Fort."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:424
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:424
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Expert instructor of the Dagger, Lori Vespers, lives in the Dark Elf city of Alvar.  Seek her out there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:425
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:425
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Jobber can instruct students of the Dagger to Mastery.  He lives in the city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:426
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:426
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Karla Nirses, the Grand Master of the Dagger trains all Regnan Pirates in the uses of the Dagger.  She dwells with them on the Island of Regna as they pay her well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:427
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:427
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Herald Foestryke, one of Charles Quixote's finest knights, is the Expert teacher of the skills of the Axe.  He can be found at the Dragon Hunter's Camp in Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:428
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:428
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jasp Hunter is the Master instructor of the axe.  He can teach you the skills that will lead to Mastery of the axe.  His home is in the seaside city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:429
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:429
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Garic Senjac, is the Grand Master teacher of the ways of the Axe.  His home is in Balthazar Lair in the Ravage Roaming region."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:430
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:430
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Matric Townsaver defended the city of Ravenshore against many Regnan Pirate raids.  His skill and instruction of the uses of the spear allowed the townsfolk to push the Pirates back. He can instruct you to Expert skill level with the spear."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:431
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:431
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ashandra Withersmythe is the Master teacher of the Spear.  Her instruction of the ways of the Spear will lead you to Mastery of the weapon.  She lives in the merchant city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:432
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:432
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yarrow is the Grand Master of the Spear.  Her keen eye and stalking ability have aided her in attaining this level of skill.  She uses the Spear to stalk the poisonous couatl of the jungles of the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:433
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:433
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shivan Keeneye is an Expert shot with the Bow.  Her teachings can lead you to an Expert skill level with this ranged weapon.  She lives in the village of Blood Drop on the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:434
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:434
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Oberic Nosewort teaches students of the bow in his home in Ravenshore.  If you seek Mastery of this weapon you must seek him out there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:435
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:435
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Solis, Grand Master of the Bow, lives in the Dark Elf city of Alvar.  She can teach you Grand Mastery of the Bow."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:436
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:436
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lisha Sourbrow teaches Expert uses of the Mace from her home in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:437
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:437
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Robert Morningstar, teaches Mastery of the Mace to the knights in Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:438
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:438
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Brother Hearthsworn, the Grand Master of the Mace, retired to the peace of the Ironsand Desert, seeking tranquility among the dunes of that region.  His home is in the village of Rust."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:439
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:439
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Qillain Moore used to serve the knight, Charles Quixote, but disagreed with his crusade to slay all the Dragons in the Garrote Gorge area. Moore still teaches Expert uses of the Shield from his home in the city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:440
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:440
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sheldon Nightwood lives in the city of Twilight, beneath the Necromancers' Guild on the Shadowspire.  She can teach you Mastery of the Shield."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:441
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:441
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The knight, Peryn Reaverston, holds the title of Grand Master of the Shield.  He is currently in service to Charles Quixote and teaches knights in the proper uses of the shield.  Search him out in the Dragon Hunter's Camp in Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:442
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:442
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Lizardman Thadin is the Expert instructor of the use of Leather armor.  His instruction will give you an Expert skill level with this armor.  You can find him on the Island of Dagger Wound."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:443
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:443
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Shamus Hollyfield dwells in the Minotaur city, Balthazar Lair, which is located in the Ravage Roaming region.  He can teach you Mastery of Leather armor."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:444
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:444
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Medwari Elmsmire makes the finest Leather armor in the realm.  She also holds the title of Grand Master of Leather Armor and can instruct you at her home in the village of Rust in the Ironsand Desert."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:445
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:445
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobren Forgewright assisted the city of Ravenshore in the First Pirate War.  Her forge glowed for four weeks straight as she made chain armor for the defenders of Ravenshore.  She still teaches Expert use of the armor from her home in the seaside port of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:446
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:446
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Halian Eversmyle learned all the skills he could from the Grand Master of Chain armor and then fled to the city of Alvar where he teaches Mastery of this armor to the Merchants of Alvar.  He will instruct you to Mastery as well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:447
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:447
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Seline Burnkindle teaches ways of using chain armor to its greatest advantage.  She lives among the Pirates of Regna."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:448
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:448
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bone teaches the Expert skills of Plate armor from his hut on Dagger Wound Island."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:449
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:449
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Botham was one of the finest warriors in the First Pirate War.  Ravenshore owes him a debt of gratitude.  Botham and his fellow swordsman led the charge against the first wave of Regnans.  Their Plate armor deflected all but the most serious blows.  He still teaches Mastery of Plate armor from his home."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:450
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:450
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Seth Ironfist, Grand Master of Plate Armor, is the true force behind Charles Quixote's crusade against the Dragons of Garrote Gorge.  Without his instruction in the use of Plate armor, Quixote's knights would be mere fodder before the wrath Redreaver's Dragons."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:451
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:451
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Taren Temper, fled Erathia to make a new life for himself among those who know nothing of the Temper history.  He teaches Expert skills in Fire Magic from his home in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:452
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:452
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Solomon Steele, Master of Fire, lives in the tranquil city of Alvar.  He can teach you Mastery of Fire Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:453
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:453
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Burn, Grand Master of Fire dwells in the oppressive heat of the Plane of Fire.  Perhaps the Gate of Fire that has appeared in the Ironsand Desert will lead you to him.  He can instruct you in Grand Mastery of Fire Magic.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:454
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:454
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Reshie teaches the Expert skill of Air Magic from his home on the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:455
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:455
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hollis Stormeye, Master of Air, made her home in Balthazar Lair, home of the Minotaurs.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:456
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:456
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Cloud Nedlon sought to make a deal with the Lords of Air.  He left to find a way into the Plane of Air, where he thought he would learn all that remained unclear to him about the ways of Air Magic.  You will have to travel to the Plane of Air to see if he was successful."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:457
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:457
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ulbrecht Pederton single handedly stopped the Second Pirate War.  He charged down the beach to come to Ravenshore's defense as the pirates began to land.  He manipulated the sea itself and forced the Regnan fleet back into the ocean.  Unfortunately this effort cost him the ability to use magic altogether.  He still, however, teaches the knowledge of Expert Water Magic.  He lives in Ravenshore to this day."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:458
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:458
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gregory Mist, Master of Water, makes his home in the village of Rust in the Ironsand Desert.  He claims to have a plan to use his magic to change the hot desert into a verdant green plain.  If he has the time, he can teach you Mastery of Water Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:459
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:459
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Black Current was once a powerful mage in this region.  Her ambition for power outgrew her caution and she attempted to conquer the Plane of Water.  She summoned a gate to the plane and stepped through.  She was never heard from again.  She was the Grand Master of Water Magic.  If she still lives you may find her in the Plane of Water."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:460
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:460
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ostrin Grivic, Expert instructor of Earth Magic, lives in the village of Blood Drop on the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:461
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:461
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Earth Magic Master Dorothy Sablewood helped end the First Pirate War.  With the aid of an unknown Air Mage, she erected walls of clay to keep the Regnan Pirates from leaving their boats.  She now teaches her skills from her home in Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:462
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:462
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Griven passed into the Plane of Earth after teaching his final lesson to Dorothy Sablewood.  Perhaps he lives there to this day.  Who knows what transpires in an elemental plane?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:463
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:463
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Straton Hawthorne can raise you to Expert level in the arts of Spirit Magic. He makes his home in the port city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:464
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:464
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Bethold Kern, serves the knight Charles Quixote in his crusade against the Dragons of the Garrote Gorge region.  Search him out there at the Dragon Hunter's Camp.  If you are lucky, he will have time to instruct you in Mastery of Spirit Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:465
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:465
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lasiter Ravensight, is the Grand Master of Spirit Magic.  He lives in the Murmurwoods close to the Temple of the Sun, where he continues his studies in to the essence of Spirit.  He can raise your skill in Spirit Magic to Grand Mastery."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:466
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:466
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Shane Krewlen, student of Mind Magic, can instruct you in the Expert skills of this arcane magic.  Seek him out in the Dark Elf city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:467
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:467
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Barthine Lotts, Master of Mind Magic, dwells in the Minotaur city of Balthazar Lair in the Ravage Roaming region.  Through her instruction can gain Mastery of Mind Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:468
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:468
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gilad Dreamwright, Grand Master of Mind Magic, has joined many other Grand Masters of Magic in the Murmurwoods region.  Here they work with the Temple of the Sun to further their combined skills and knowledge.  Gilad can instruct you to Grand Master skill level in Mind Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:469
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:469
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Zevah Poised, Expert instructor of the arcane skills of Body Magic, lives with his people on the Islands of Dagger Wound in the Ifarine Sea."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:470
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:470
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tugor Arin, Master of Body Magic, practices his healing skills in the service of the knight Charles Quixote in the Garrote Gorge region.  His skills in Body Magic are put to good use healing the unfortunate young knights who are wounded in the crusade against the Dragons of Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:471
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:471
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Critias Snowtree, dwells in the peace of the Murmurwoods forest away from the trials and troubles of the world.  Only he can instruct you in the ways of Body Magic and raise you to Grand Mastery of this arcane skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:472
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:472
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Archibald Dawnsglow, Expert instructor of Light Magic, practices his arts in the city of Ravenshore on the Ifarine Sea.  His parents gave his name not knowing that it was the same name as the leader of the Erathian Necromancers' Guild.  Archibald desires to have his own name made in the Light, not in the darkness of his namesake."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:473
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:473
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Lunius Dawnbringer, dwells among the the Clerics of Murmurwoods.He can promote you to Master of Light Magic, if you can survive the dangers of the forest."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:474
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:474
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Aldrin Cleareye, Grand Master of the Light, makes his home on the island of Regna.  He hopes to bring an end to the Pirates evil ways.  He can instruct you to Grand Masterey, if you survive the Pirates."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:475
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:475
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Patwin Darkenmore, Expert teacher of the ways of Dark Magic, lives among the Dark Elves of Alvar.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:476
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:476
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dark Magic Master Carla Umberpool followed the travels of Sithicus Shadowrunner, Grand Master of the Dark, and makes her home with the Necromancers of Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:477
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:477
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sithicus Shadowrunner, Grand Master of the art of Dark Magic, and has established a home on the Island of Regna.  Here the pirate captains get her blessing on the ships before a raid.  She can instruct you in Grand Mastery of Dark Magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:478
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:478
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kyra Sparkmen, Expert teacher of the Identify Item skill, lives in the city of Alvar.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:479
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:479
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Eithian, Master instructor of the Identify Item skill, serves the Merchants of Alvar, and currently lives on the Dagger Wound Islands. Many travelers bring their prizes to Eithian for identification.  He may have to time to instruct you to Mastery of this skill if you travel to him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:480
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:480
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Elzbet Roggen, Grand Master of the Identify Item skill, lives in the Shadowspire city of Twilight.  She can teach you what is needed to achieve Grand Mastery."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:481
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:481
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fishner Thomb, retired from service with the Merchants of Alvar and returned to his home Island of Dagger Wound in the Ifarine Sea.  Seek him out there for his teachings in the Expert way of being a Merchant."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:482
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:482
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fenton Iverson, Master Merchant of Alvar, tests all who wish to advanced with the skills of a Merchant.  You will find Fenton in the merchant city of Alvar, where he can instruct you to Mastery of the Merchant skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:483
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:483
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Raven Quicktoungue, Grand Master Merchant of Alvar, dwells in the city of Ravenshore.  There, Raven can watch the interaction of numerous races as the trade with each other.  Only he can raise your knowledge to Grand Mastery of the merchant skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:484
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:484
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Evandar Lotts teaches the Expert skills of Repairing Items.  He dwells in the seaside city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:485
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:485
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Quick Jeni, is the Master of the Repair Item skill. She lives in the village around the Dargon Hunter's Fort in Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:486
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:486
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Quethrin Tonk, Grand Master of the Repair Item skill, dwells in the tranquil Murmurwoods.  His skills have proven invaluable to the Temple of the Sun."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:487
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:487
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Menasaur, the strongest Lizardmen on the Dagger Wound Islands, is the Expert instructor of the Body Building skill. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:488
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:488
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kenneth Otterton, holds the title of Crusader, and serves under the knight Charles Quixote in Garrote Gorge.  Rumor has it that he wrestled a Dragon to the ground single-handedly.  Of course, other knights had to assist in the kill.  Kenneth also holds the title, Master Instructor of Body Building."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:489
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:489
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Mikel Smithson, holds the title of Strongest in Jadame.  He is also the Grand Master of the Body Building skill.  Seek him out in the village of Rust in the Ironsand Desert if you wish to perfect the strength of your bodies."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:490
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:490
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Alton Putnam, is an Expert in the art of Meditation.  He can instruct you if you seek him out in the seaside city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:491
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:491
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gretchin Nevermore, instructs all Clerics of the Sun the Master arts of Meditation. He dwells in the Murmurwoods near the Temple of the Sun."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:492
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:492
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lenord Nightcrawler, Grand Master of Meditation, serves as one of the foremost members of the Necromancers' Guild of Shadowspire.  He instructs all necromancers in the art of Meditation from his home in the village of Twilight."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:493
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:493
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Silk Nightwalker, Expert teacher of the Perception skill, makes his home in the Dark Elf city of Alvar.  Instructing the Merchants of Alvar in the skills needed to detect that which is supposed to remain secret occupies most of his time, however him may take the time to instruct you if luck is with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:494
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:494
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Helga Steeleye, lives among the necromancers of Shadowspire in the village of Twilight.  The Necromancers' Guild is thankful for her Master level instructions in the skill of Perception."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:495
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:495
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Grand Master Balan Suretrail lives in the Minotaur city of Balthazar Lair.  To gain his instruction in the skill of Perception, you must seek him out in Ravage Roaming."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:496
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:496
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kethric Tarent, teaches the Expert knowledge of Regeneration from his home in the Ironsand Desert, in the village of Rust."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:497
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:497
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "William Sampson, Master of Regeneration, lives in the peace of the Murmurwoods.  He uses the libraries of the Temple of the Sun to further his knowledge of Trollish history."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:498
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:498
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ush the Many Tailed, Grand Master of Regeneration and legendary warrior, lives among his people on Dagger Wound Island.  Legends say he has lost his tail thirteen times in battle against the Regnan Pirates, and each time he has grown a new tail!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:499
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:499
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Chevon Wist, teaches the Expert knowledge of the Disarm Trap skill, which has proven useful to those who explore the ruined temples near his home on the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:500
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:500
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kelli Lightfingers, Master of Disarming Traps, has retired to her home in the merchant city of Alvar.  There she still teaches young merchants the skills of trapping and disarming chests.  If you are worthy she can raise your Disarm Trap skills to that of a Master."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:501
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:501
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Gareth Lifter, Grand Master of Disarming Traps, lives on the opulent island of Regna, where he teaches his fellow pirates in the best way to trap their chests of stolen booty."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:502
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:502
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes! Yes! An excellent idea. You are just the kind of companions I am seeking. I have heard of you and your adventures."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:503
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:503
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No. I am an elder vampire. To be clear, you're not worthy of me. I seek adventure, not to be your caretaker. I don't have the patience to teach you all the basics."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:504
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:504
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, you seem worthy of my company. Very well, I will go if you will have me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:505
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:505
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I think not. Now that I've had a chance to look at you, it is clear that you are not worthy of my company. I seek a group of greater renown."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:506
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:506
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I must say I find the idea appealing. Hmmm, yes! The taste of the open road is just what I need. I have been long at this business of dragon slaying, and I must say it grows stale. A man must keep himself interested. I will go with you if you like."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:508
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:508
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tessa Maker, Expert in Monster Identification, seeks to improve her skills by cataloging the different Dragons of Garrote Gorge.  She is currently in the service of the knight, Charles Quixote."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:509
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:509
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Matric Keenedge, Master of the skill of Identify Monster, is currently studying the creatures of the Murmurwoods.  If you seek Mastery of this skill you need to seek him out there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:510
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:510
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Blacken Stonecleaver, Grand Master of Monster Identification, has seen every creature on the continent of Jadame.  He can teach you his knowledge if you find his home in the city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:511
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:511
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Knight Norbert Slayer, instructs all of Charles Quixote's knights in the Expert forms of  Armsmastery.  If you travel to Garrote Gorge, you can attend one of his teachings."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:512
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:512
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lasatin the Scarred, Master of the Armsmaster skill, lives on the Islands of Dagger Wound."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:513
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:513
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jasper Steelcoif, Grand Master of the Armsmaster skill, is one of the leaders of the Regnan Pirate Council.  He instructs all pirates in the use of weapons.  If you are brave enough to travel to Regna--and survive his instruction--you too, will have Grand Mastery of this skill."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:514
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:514
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must be joking! I am a rightly famous knight. Why would I want to travel with such riff-raff as yourselves? Oh, it might be fun after a fashion, but I do have my reputation to think of."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:515
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:515
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes! That sounds great. From what I hear of your adventures you have a chance to know greatness. With my help, we could make that chance a certainty. Well, shall we? I'm always looking for a chance to add to my legend!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:516
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:516
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join you? Ho-ho. What an amusing idea. Why would the great Thorne Understone travel with the likes of you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:517
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:517
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tabitha Watershed, Expert Alchemist, teaches the skills of potions and poultices from her home in the merchant city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:518
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:518
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Kethry Treasurestone, Master Alchemist, lives in the Murmurwoods, studying plants and mushrooms that grow in that peaceful forest."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:519
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:519
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ich, Grand Master of Alchemy, has studied the art of brewing for decades.  He knows all there is to know about blending reagents into beneficial and harmful potions.  Seek out his home in the lush jungles of the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:520
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:520
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Petra Mithrit, Expert in the skill of Learning, dwells near the Temple of the Sun in the Murmurwoods."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:521
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:521
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Garret Mistspring, Master of Learning, instructs all students of necromancy in the art of Learning.  For this the Necromancers' Guild rewards him well.  His home is in the hamlet of Twilight at the base of the Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:522
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:522
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wanda Lightsworn, Grand Master of Learning, is in the hire of Charles Quixote, and instructs all of his knights in the skills of Learning.  It is the hope of Charles Quixote that this will give his forces and edge in battle against the Dragons of Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:523
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:523
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Flynn Shador, Expert Vampire, lives in the city of Twilight, serving as eyes and a safe house for any Vampires that travel to that region.  He can instruct you in the Expert abilities of a Vampire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:524
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:524
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Douglas Dirthmoore, Master Vampire, will teach any whose skills measure up to his standards.  Once he is done with you, you will have Mastered the abilities native to all Vampires.  His home is in the Shadowspire village of Twilight."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:525
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:525
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though no one knows for sure, Payge Arachnia, Grand Master Vampire, is rumored to be the first Vampire on the continent of Jadame. She knows all there is to be known about living as a Vampire and can teach you the Grand Master abilities she possesses.  Seek out her lair in Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:526
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:526
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fedwin Dervish, can instruct you in the Expert ways of the Dark Elf.  Once you have learned from him, you will have begun a great journey to becoming a leader of your people.  Search him out in the Dark Elf city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:527
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:527
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lanshee Caverhill, Master Merchant of Alvar currently lives in the seaside port of Ravenshore.  She knows all about Mastering the natural abilities all Dark Elves have."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:528
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:528
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ton Agraynel, Master Merchant of Alvar, can instruct you in the Grand Master skills of a Dark Elf.  You will have to prove yourself worthy of his instruction, but the benefits are well worth the effort."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:529
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:529
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ishton, Junior Flight Leader of the Dragons of Garrote Gorge, instructs all young Dragons to an Expert skill level with their racial Dragon abilities.  He dwells here, in the Dragon Caves of Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:530
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:530
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Master Dragon Erthint is the Flight Leader of all of the Dragons that serve under Deftclaw Redreaver, and can instruct a Dragon in Mastery of his natural Dragon abilities. Erthint lives in the Dragon Caves of Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:531
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:531
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Klain Scarwing, is second in strength only to Deftclaw Redreaver himself.  Klain holds the title of Grand Master Dragon and instructs all Dragons in the use of their natural abilities.  See him if you wish to attain Grand Master status.  He dwells here in the Dragon Caves of Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:532
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:532
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Cleric sent you back with the Gem of Restoration?  I am free of this place!  Search me out if you wish for me to ever travel with you!  It would be my pleasure to join you in your journeys!  I will wait for you at the Adventurer's Inn in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:533
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:533
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not slain all of the vermin.  I have reports here that tell of Dragons still in the region.  Return when you have slain them all!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:534
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:534
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not slain all of the Dragon hunters.  A Flight returned just moments ago and reported seeing them out on the plains.  Return when you have slain them all!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:535
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:535
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here's your weapon. If you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more weapons."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:537
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:537
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here's your armor. If you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more armor."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:539
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:539
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here is your item. If you find more ore, I'll be happy to make you more items."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:541
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:541
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To be declared Arcomage Champion, you must win a game of Arcomage in every tavern on, in, and under the continent of Jadame.  There are 11 such taverns sponsoring Arcomage events.  When you have accomplished this, return to me to claim the prize."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:542
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:542
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must claim a victory at ALL 11 taverns.  Until you do, you cannot be declared Arcomage Champion."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:543
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:543
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!  You have become the Arcomage Champion!  The prize is waiting in the chest right outside my house."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:544
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:544
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, \"adventure.\" Surely I have not had enough of it recently. Since our war with the Frost Giants, I have done little but train young warriors. Say, you wouldn't happen to want a traveling companion? Perhaps I could come with you. I have many skills you might find useful, and I swing a deadly axe!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:545
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:545
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, adventure is a fine thing. Why I have had several. In fact, let me tell you about the time I….Say, it just occurred to me you are suggesting I adventure with you! A nice offer, but well…how can I say this politely? You're just not seasoned enough. I'm afraid I would grow bored with the kinds of challenges you are ready to face."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:546
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:546
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you suggest I come along with you to see the land for myself. An excellent suggestion. I am certainly well rested enough! Very well, I am ready to travel if you will take me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:547
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:547
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though I may not look it after my long sleep, know that you speak with one of the greatest vampires alive today. Go with you? I think not. Your inexperience would make you more of a hindrance to me than anything. I would do better on my own."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:548
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:548
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join you! Ha! I admire your audacity. Yes…admire it a great deal. Very well. You have my respect. I will go with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:549
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:549
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Join you? What a fool's notion. I already travel with a certain number of fleas. I don't need any more parasites. Be gone!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:551
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:551
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am pleased with these Ironfists and their sage, Xanthor. Though we have never worked together directly, their work in Enroth and Erathia against the Necromancers' Guild and the devils have clearly marked them as servants of The Light. I have full faith in their plans for saving us from the crisis."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:552
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:552
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Sun Temple has had much time to study the gateway which appeared in Murmurwoods. I am positive it leads to the Plane of Air. On several occasions my brothers have seen air spirits around the gateway. Some of the braver have peered through it and have reported seeing a whirling realm of clouds."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:553
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:553
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As a Priest of the Light, I have my own ideas about the source of the crisis. I am positive that either the Temple of the Moon or the Necromancers' Guild is somehow involved. Great Light! What if they've banded together? What a horrid thought."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:554
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:554
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm not sure you can trust the words of this so called, \"Destroyer.\" Certainly he is not the Destroyer of scripture. And all this talk of Kreegans and men living on many worlds. It flies in the face of the Truth my temple has shepherded from the beginning of time!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:555
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:555
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is good to have you with us, Heroes of Jadame. Know that the Temple of the Sun also considers you servants of the Light. You are always welcome among us."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:556
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:556
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish my first visit to Ravenshore was made under better circumstances. This town has a lot to offer and I wish I had time to explore it more. On the bright side, this merchant house has a great library. Have you seen it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:557
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:557
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Regnans have built and outpost on one of the Dagger Wound Islands. We fear they may attack Ravenshore. If this happens, we will evacuate the city. We will return once the garrison has rid Ravenshore of pirates."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:558
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:558
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When I became herd leader, I never expected my reign would be so full of rich experience. Certainly I never thought I'd meet anyone like Queen Catherine! Did you know that until she abdicated her rule in Erathia, she was ruler of both it and Enroth?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:559
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:559
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As you know, the gateway leading to the Plane of Water appeared near Balthazar Lair in Ravage Roaming. It lies in the middle of the lake created by the great flood that poured forth from it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:560
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:560
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You may have difficulty finding supplies in the lands beyond the crystal. When I left Balthazar Lair, I brought with me a quantity of the iron rations carried by my armies on campaign. Here, take what I have. They are light and nourishing. I hope you find them useful."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:561
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:561
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why if the imprisonment of the elemental lords is what started this crisis, then surely releasing them is the way to end it! They are beings of almost unimaginable power. Once freed of the Destroyer's control, they would be able to set things right again. This must be what the prophecy speaks of!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:562
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:562
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It cannot be said enough. My herd as well as all the beings of Jadame are forever in your debt. Thanks to your good work here and in the planes, Balthazar Lair can once again know greatness. You and your comrades are welcome here any time you wish to visit. A blessing on you all!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:563
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:563
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can't help feeling that I could be doing better work elsewhere. I'm sure Thant can handle operation of the guild in my absence, but still, sitting here on my hands while we are at war with the Sun Temple tries my patience. You really must be quicker about your duties!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:564
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:564
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When one thinks of the Regnans, the phrase \"masters of magic\" doesn't normally come to mind. But I caution you, the Regnan pirates have held their island for many centuries. They have had much time to both acquire and study arcane knowledge. Some powerful magicians live there. If you must face them in combat, be prepared for anything."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:565
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:565
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is not true that we of the Necromancers' Guild do not respect mages of other schools. That they have chosen paths leading to lesser powers is of their own concerns. This Xanthor is formidable for a wizard not of the Dark Path. As much as is possible, I find his advise, passably worthy."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:566
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:566
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have learned that the Dark Dwarves of Alvar hold an item I have long coveted, but may be of particular use to you if you when you travel among the elemental planes. The Ring of Planes conveys upon its wearer powerful wards against damaging spells of earth, water, air, and fire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:567
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:567
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In my studies I have learned something of this Plane Between Planes. It is written that its denizens are not born in the normal fashion. I have heard that creatures can be found there which manifest the energies of the nightmare dreams of humankind. I have little more information, but I imagine such a creature would be both powerful and malevolent."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:568
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:568
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A basic fact of magic is that Fire opposes Water, and Air opposes Earth. Within these parings, the one element has weaknesses regarding its opposite element. I expect the Destroyer exploits this principle in the construction of his prisons."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:569
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:569
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know I speak for the guild when I say we owe you a debt of gratitude. I discharge this debt by granting you and your companions safe passage through all lands under our control. No guild member will kidnap you for arcane experimentation, nor will any member consider you feed for his servants, living or otherwise. This guild edict will be in effect for a period of one year from today.\n"
"\n"
"And of course, you have my personal, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:570
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:570
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The master is not here at present. He went to consult with Elgar Fellmoon at the council chamber. Perhaps you will find him there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:571
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:571
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The crystal placed by the Destroyer in the town square serves two functions. One, if we do nothing, it will destroy the world. Two, it acts as a gateway to another realm of existence--the Plane Between Planes--where the Destroyer most certainly has his base.\n"
"\n"
"The crystal calls forth the elemental forces into our world and draws them to it. When these forces meet here at the crystal, the world will be destroyed in cataclysm. If we are to prevent this someone will have to use the crystal as a gateway to reach the Destroyer and either convince him to end his assault, or eliminate him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:572
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:572
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Since the crystal is attuned to the elemental forces, it will only pass through those who are themselves so attuned. I believe it is possible to create a key that will simulate attunement for a small group such as yourselves. I can make the key, but require components of pure elemental forces to do so.\n"
"\n"
"Such components exist in only one form that I know of. On each of the four elemental planes, you will find gemstones called the \"elemental hearts.\" Bring these to me and I will build the key to open the crystal gateway."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:573
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:573
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To go through the crystal gateway and confront the Destroyer, you need the key I must build! To build this key, I need the elemental heart gemstones from the four elemental planes! Go and get these for me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:574
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:574
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am glad that you have had some measure of success in retrieving the elemental hearts, but what you have is not enough. I need one from each of the four elemental planes before I can build the key to the crystal gateway. Bring me the rest of the hearts so we can proceed."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:575
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:575
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Something about this crystal seems to put a compulsion on the denizens of the elemental planes. Why else would they make war on our plane? I have heard yours and other first hand reports. It seems almost as if these elementals are driven by a madness.\n"
"\n"
"And madness it is! For destroying Enroth would create a mighty planar unbalance which would certainly victimize their own planes. They might even conceivably be themselves destroyed in the cataclysm. At the very least, they risk changing the nature of their own planes. I cannot see how such change could possibly be for the better!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:576
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:576
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"That the elemental lords are imprisoned on the Plane Between Planes explains much. I had wondered why the denizens of the Earth, Air, Water, and Fire Planes have become so hostile. Usually, they are content to keep to their own place in the order. I suppose it was necessary for the Destroyer to take the lords from their homelands. Without the lords calming presence, it would be much easier for him to compel the elementals as he has.\n"
"\n"
"It is important for you to free the elemental lords. They can restore order to their planes and prevent the cataclysm!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:577
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:577
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Yes, I have heard the name, \"Escaton.\" He is variously called in the legends of many cultures. I know not his nature, but it is his purpose to destroy worlds.\n"
"\n"
"Yes, \"worlds,\" I say. More and more evidence points to the conclusion that Enroth is not the only place in this universe where there is life. Tales from before the Silence speak of many living among the stars. Yes, it sounds impossible to think that one could live on a light in the sky, but consider that these stars may be like our sun. If this is so, then why can't these suns shine on other places like Enroth? If this was the case, then there could be a \"destroyer of worlds.\" I believe that this is what we face."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:578
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:578
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No, I don't think I will be leaving when the Ironfists continue their journey back to Enroth. Perhaps I will join with them in some years, but for now, I find myself fascinated by these lands. Though it is destroyed, I would study the remains of the crystal gateway. Never in my knowledge has there been in this world an artifact of comparable power. Perhaps I will find some use for the crystal shards?\n"
"\n"
"No matter. Regardless, when the Ironfists go, they will go without me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:579
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:579
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Without false modesty I must say that the Nightshade Brazier is the greatest creation of my dark arts. When its fires are properly tended, the accursed sun is incapable of shining within its area of influence. The soothing shadow of night takes up permanent residence over a vast region. Within these boundaries, vampires and other night creatures know freedoms they would not otherwise know. We are free of the crypts with no worries of the destroying light of day!\n"
"\n"
"And now the Temple of the Sun has taken my prize. It must be retrieved!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:580
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:580
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I am Escaton the Destroyer also called \"Devil's Doom,\" \"The Spider in the Web Gate\" and \"Ruin.\" There are places where I am worshiped as a god. But to myself I think of myself only as a servant to my greater masters.\n"
"\n"
"Know too that I have brought the cataclysm to your world, which must be destroyed. It is a doom you have brought on yourselves by failing to eliminate the devil Kreegans from your realms. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:581
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:581
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My masters are those who created me. They gave me form and function. I have thus proven indestructible. I destroy worlds infested by Kreegans."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:582
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:582
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "On your world they speak of a Silence which has lasted for a thousand years and more. I am old beyond that and my masters are ancient to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:583
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:583
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are more worlds than yours--a myriad of them. These worlds were once held in a great web whose threads could be traversed like bridges over rivers. What you call the Silence was marked by the breaking of the web which was built by my masters."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:584
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:584
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"At one time my ancient masters were caretakers of more worlds than there are apples in a bushel. Before the Kreegans--before the Silence--they were worlds of wonder. My masters were kings and queens of a golden civilization. I was made, not because I was needed, but because I could be made--a protector of that which needed no protection...a symbol of might to a mighty people.\n"
"\n"
"But now, and for a millennium, the Kreegan blight has eaten away the splendor of the worlds. And so have my masters fallen. They are warlords and generals, and I am their greatest soldier."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:585
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:585
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your world will be destroyed by the elemental forces that created it. The crystal in Jadame's central city compels those who live on the elemental planes to open their worlds onto yours. When their worlds meet at the crystal, the reaction will unleash irrepressible destruction across the lands, sky and sea. All things living will live no longer."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:586
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:586
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The cataclysm was brought into being when I performed the ritual Convocation of Cataclysm which brought into being the crystal. It is a weapon of last resort created by my masters to defend themselves against the Kreegans.\n"
"\n"
"I do have other weapons. But when I became aware of the Kreegans infestation on your world, I deemed the use of ultimate force necessary. Your world has fallen so far--it seemed certain you would not be able to defend yourselves against my enemies. Though I underestimated your abilities, and the Kreegans were ultimately destroyed, I still feel that I was right to err on the side of caution."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:587
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:587
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My masters, afraid the Kreegans would learn ways to corrupt me, have made me incorruptible. I am unable to undo the Convocation of Cataclysm once it has been performed. This command of theirs is part of my very being. I am powerless but to obey."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:588
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:588
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Convocation of Cataclysm, as powerful as it is, cannot of itself destroy a world. Each of the elemental planes is ruled by a lord. These lords can fight the compulsion placed on their lesser subjects. For this reason, I have removed the lords from their realms. They are my \"guests\" for the time being.\n"
"\n"
"Once the cataclysm has run its course, I will return them so that they might rebuild your realm and theirs."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:589
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:589
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In the time since the Silence, your world has lost knowledge of the Kreegan's origin. That they resemble the devils of myth has been enough for you, and indeed, \"devils\" is what most call them. The truth is they came from the beyond. Before they attacked us, my masters had no knowledge of them.\n"
"\n"
"The Kreegans infest our worlds and spread if they can. It would seem in an endless universe that they could expand in another direction than ours. But they have not made this choice so we must defend ourselves from them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:590
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:590
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I am aware that the king and queen of Enroth have rid your world of Kreegans. Still, your world is to be destroyed. Once I am called, I must perform the Convocation. Once the Convocation is begun, it must continue.\n"
"\n"
"I was called while Kreegan still lived on your world. It matters not that they were dust by the time I arrived."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:591
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:591
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If it were not for the Kreegans and the state of war they impose, my masters could rebuild the Web of Worlds and lift what you call \"The Silence.\" My masters have attempted to rebuild the Web many times, but the Kreegans always destroy it. Now they have concluded that the Kreegans must be entirely eliminated or the golden civilization will never rise again. It is to fulfill this purpose that I have been created."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:592
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:592
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"As far as I'm able to feel such, I am amazed that your world was able to eliminate its Kreegan infestation. They are quite a bit more…advanced than you. The king and queen of Enroth must be strategists of the highest order. Too bad that they were not able to finish their task sooner.\n"
"\n"
"If I could regret, I would regret having to needlessly annihilate your world."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:593
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:593
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Yes, your world does need saving! The cataclysm, if not stopped, will destroy it utterly.\n"
"\n"
"A quandary for you: I, as bringer of the cataclysm know how it can be ended. Further, I acknowledge that since there are no longer Kreegans on your world it need not be destroyed. But, as servant to my masters, I am compelled to let the cataclysm continue by not divulging my knowledge to you.\n"
"\n"
"Still I will ask you some questions. Perhaps there is something for you in the answers?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:594
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:594
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though I must destroy your world, what I need do I have already done. Until the cataclysm has culminated, there is nothing to stop me from indulging you with my conversation. This cannot continue forever. Nothing does.\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes questions create more questions. Sometimes they provide answers. I wonder what my questions will provide you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:595
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:595
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My masters have made me a holder, and not a giver, of knowledge. Still perhaps you have given yourself knowledge through my questions? I have given you all the questions I will, so you must look at what you have. Perhaps you should question the answers.\n"
"\n"
"A \"prison\" implies a prisoner. Who? \"Inside?\" Inside of what? And \"egg.\" What kind of egg? A bird's egg? Perhaps something like an egg?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:596
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:596
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Where does one serve to pay,\n"
"  Is not free to leave,\n"
"  But is free when one leaves?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:597
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:597
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes. Your answer seems to fit the riddle nicely. Perhaps that is the correct answer."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:598
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:598
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That doesn't seem right at all."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:599
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:599
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jails, prisons and cells come in many forms. We hear of so called \"prisons of the mind.\" But I wonder. The riddle seems to speak of a physical prison. What think you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:600
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:600
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What is there when\n"
"  You enter a room,\n"
"  And cannot be outside,\n"
"  Though you leave the door open?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:601
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:601
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The vagaries of language are many. Still, your answer seems to apply well to the question."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:602
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:602
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I suppose that could work…no, on second thought, it seems entirely wrong."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:603
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:603
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Inside. Inside what? And what is inside? And while we're asking...why?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:604
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:604
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A moon colored box\n"
"  meant to be opened from the inside\n"
"  protects the sun colored\n"
"  treasure of life.\n"
"  What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:605
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:605
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What else indeed could the answer be? I'm sure if one were to apply some thought, one could think of something. Still in these matters, it is best to have confidence in one's clearest thought. I suppose your answer could be correct."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:606
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:606
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't see how that could be the answer. Really I can't."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:607
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:607
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "\"Egg,\" yes. or perhaps, \"eggs.\" Eggs are a source of life, a seed of sorts. They are also of an unusual shape not found in many places elsewhere. Perhaps placing the answer in context will give a clue or some direction."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:608
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:608
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I would judge that you've answered the riddles correctly. I suppose in asking them to you I have in some way helped you. As far as I and my nature are concerned, this is sufficient.\n"
"\n"
"As a reward for your performance, take this small bauble. I have more than one and therefore, more than I require. And see? I can give it to you because I don't know you have the knowledge to use it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:609
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:609
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for releasing me. I go now to restore order to my realm and to do what I can for yours. Know that Shalwend, Lord of Air, holds you in his favor. Farewell."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:610
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:610
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "\"The Destroyer\" is a fitting moniker for one who would imprison me in such a fashion. If it were not for you, I, Acwalander, Lord of Water, would have soon perished. My passing would have had an unbalancing effect across all the planes. Thank you. I go now to set things right."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:611
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:611
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am free! Now will he who was fool enough to jail me--this Destroyer--feel my wrath. That I, the Lord of Earth, am called \"Gralkor the Cruel\" is no mistake. The suffering I have felt will be his returned in multitudes!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:612
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:612
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Free at last. My torment is over, but what of my subjects? I know the Destroyer has them compelled to a terrible task. My presence will sooth them. I must go. I must…farewell…"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:613
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:613
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No! Someone must remain here to guard the lair against the barbarian raiders. Come back after you've helped my herd. I may consider joining you then."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:614
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:614
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are many predators who would take advantage of the lair in this vulnerable time. I've already driven off looters…and worse. One of Zog's patrols stopped by soon after the flood. I fought them off, but some escaped. I am sure they will be back in greater numbers."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:615
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:615
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have no more rations to give. If you need more, you'll have to find food elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:616
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:616
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What with the damage caused by giant waves, falling rocks and the pirate raid, I don't know if our village will ever be the same. I know you have done great things for us, but not everything can be fixed once broken. I'm not sure what we'll do. Perhaps we will rebuild, or maybe we'll leave. Time and circumstance will decide."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:617
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:617
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good work dealing with those pirates. Now that they're gone, maybe Chief Onefang and his people can rebuild their lives. It really is a travesty what has happened here."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:618
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:618
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sadly, the caravan was one of the first things the pirates looted in their raids. I have no idea what they're going to do with three-hundred cases of tobersk fruit! Naturally, I miss the fruit, but the worst of it is the damage they did to the carts. It looks like I'll be here for at least the next season overseeing their repair. I just hope the task is done before the next tobersk harvest so I can see some return out of this profitless venture."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:619
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:619
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are indeed earning your way to this months bounty but have not yet reached the number of kills needed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:620
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:620
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yellow Fever is a very crippling disease that pops up every few years.  Usually we arrange for medicine from the mainland, but now that the bridges are destroyed, no one can make it to the docks!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:621
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:621
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here, take these scrolls of Cure Disease.  Maybe we can at least prevent an epidemic!  The six huts on the outer islands are infected.  If the teleporters between the islands are repaired, you can take these scrolls to the huts.  Unfortunately you will have to find three more scrolls in your travels."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:622
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:622
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Yellow Fever epidemic is over!  Thank you for your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:623
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:623
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I hear that Yellow Fever is once again spreading through the people.  Usually the water supply here on the main island is the primary source of the disease.  We used to get an Anointed Herb Potion from the mainland when the disease popped up.  Without access to the dock however, we cannot get this needed cure.  If you find a way to the mainland, perhaps the smugglers of Ravenshore have the cure.  If you can procure the Anointed Potion, return to me with it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:624
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:624
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you!  I will go introduce this to the water supply!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:625
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:625
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Perhaps you can bring me the basic ingredients for a Potion of Pure speed?  With them I can make this incredible potion and finish my studies in alchemy!  I will reward you well for your assistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:626
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:626
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Guild of Bounty Hunters serves the public by paying qualified individuals a fee for eliminating the threat of certain creatures or bandits in the realm of Jadame.  To achieve the rank of Novice Bounty Hunter you will have to earn 10,000 gold worth of bounties."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:627
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:627
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The ingredients!  Thank you!  Take this as a reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:628
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:628
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I believe I may know how to stop the destructive force of the mountain of fire!  I have found an ancient spell that should give me the power to send the mountain of fire back into the sea! To complete the spell I need an ancient relic called the Idol of the Snake.  With this item of power I should be able to complete the spell."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:629
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:629
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you for returning with the Idol.  Upon further study I discovered that the entire spell was useless.  Still, this is not your fault and you deserve some reward for returning to me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:630
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:630
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The packs of Dire Wolves that roam this region are a threat to travelers and commerce.  The Merchants of Alvar have instructed me to hire competent people to hunt down these wolves and to \"thin the pack\" in their words.  You look like skilled adventurers!  I will reward you well if you can eliminate the entire pack and those in their lair."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:631
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:631
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I pay 250 gold for every intact Dire Wolf Pelt that you return to me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:632
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:632
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The pack has been wiped out? Excellent!  Of course I will need to find a new business for myself.  Thank you for your efforts.  Please take this reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:633
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:633
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Merchants of Alvar took my family into what they termed \"protective custody\" and use this as the means to secure my services. However as the caravan with my family was returning to Alvar, they were attacked by Ogres and bandits.  The Ogre Zog, took my family from them!  He took them to his fortress in the Alvar region.  Now, I am to spy on the Merchants of Alvar for him.  As long as I do so, my family lives.  If I stop, they die.  Can you rescue them for me?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:634
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:634
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I send periodic reports of the activities of the Merchants of Alvar to the Dread Pirate Stanley in the tavern, The Pirate's Rest on the Island of Regna. Now that the Merchants have \"bargained\" for my assistance, we must deliver a false set of reports to keep Stanley from being suspicious.  Take this report to him in Harecksburg on the island of Regna!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:635
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:635
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You delivered the report to Stanley?  This is will at least buy us sometime before he becomes suspicious of the activities here in Ravenshore and those of the Merchants in Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:636
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:636
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I hear that you are looking for an Anointed Herb potion to purify the water supply.  The Smugglers of Jadame deal with all kind of strange goods.  If anyone would know about or have this anointed herb potion, it would be them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:637
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:637
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dark Elves of Alvar pay well for leather made from Naga Hides. Once treated and tanned, the Naga Hides can last almost longer than a Dark Elf's lifetime! "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:638
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:638
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will pay you 500 gold for each Naga Hide you bring."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:639
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:639
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many decades ago, the legendary Priest of the Sun, Camien Thryce, led a crusade against the Necromancers' Guild in Shadowspire.  The Guild was able to defeat Thryce's forces with the aid of the Vampires that also dwell in the Shadowspire region.  Camien Thryce carried with him the clerical artifact called Eclipse with him into battle.  The shield was lost when Thryce was struck down by a Nosferatu in the final battle."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:640
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:640
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have recovered the shield, Eclipse?  The Temple is grateful for you help in recovering this potent artifact.  Please, continue to carry the shield with our blessing."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:641
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:641
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you rescued my family?  I cannot guarantee that I will continue to provide my services unless they are safe!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:644
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:644
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The forces of the Ogre Mage, Zog moved into this area right around the time that the bright flash traveled across the night sky.  They harass and even kill travelers who seek to reach the city of Alvar. It would be of great service to Alvar if you were to eliminate all of the Ogres that harass the roads to Alvar and the Ogres in the fortress near the city of Alvar.  Return to me when you have killed all of the ogres in this region, and I will reward you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:645
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:645
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not defeated all of the Ogres!  The roads will not be safe until they are destroyed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:646
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:646
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  Now that the Ogres are cleared from the roads and no longer inhabit the fortress, the roads to Ravenshore, Ironsand and Murmurwoods are safe again!  Please take this 5000 gold as reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:647
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:647
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A Potion of Pure Luck would be of great assistance to any merchant.  One could stumble upon any number of great deals if his Luck was at its highest!  Bring me the basic ingredients for a Potion of Pure Luck and I will reward you well!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:648
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:648
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings Novice Bounty Hunter! The Guild of Bounty Hunters serves the public by paying qualified individuals a fee for eliminating the threat of certain creatures or bandits in the realm of Jadame.  To achieve the rank of Journeyman Bounty Hunter you will have to earn a total bounty of 30,000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:649
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:649
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  With this I can brew another Potion of Pure Luck.  Take this potion as your reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:650
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:650
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wasp stingers!  From cold remedies to herbal teas, a little bit of ground wasp stinger goes a long way!  Don't trust those who sell that weak ground wyvern horn!  Only wasp stinger will do if you want the best!  I'll pay you for every stinger you bring me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:651
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:651
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I pay 500 gold for every wasp stinger you bring me!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:652
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:652
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Trolls have a natural fear of fire!  Many of us perished when the Gate of Fire opened and spilled out the lake of fire! Without appropriate protection, there was nothing we could do."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:653
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:653
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The survivors in this region need Potions of Fire Resistance!  With them we can survive until a place is found for us to move to!  Take these potions!  Unfortunately they are all I have!  Deliver them to the six southernmost houses that remain standing in the village of Rust!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:654
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:654
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not delivered Potions of Fire Resistance to all of the houses!  If the lake of fire grows in size everyone will perish!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:655
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:655
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have at least pushed our demise away for a time, but a new home needs to be found for us!  Thank you for delivering the Potions of Fire Resistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:656
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:656
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Endurance.  That ability which keeps a warrior on his feet, or lets him down gently as he slides into unconsciousness.  A Potion of Pure Endurance can boost a person's ability to take damage to a legendary strength!  Bring me the basic ingredients of a Potion of Pure Endurance and I will reward you well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:657
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:657
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings Journeyman Bounty Hunter! The Guild of Bounty Hunters serves the public by paying qualified individuals a fee for eliminating the threat of certain creatures or bandits in the realm of Jadame.  To achieve the rank of Master Bounty Hunter you will have to earn a total bounty of 70,000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:658
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:658
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have brought me the ingredients as asked!  I am indeed grateful.  Takes this potion as your reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:659
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:659
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dragonbane Flower has many medicinal uses.  It also has some uses that are less than medicinal.  From this flower we can distill a poison that is deadly to Dragons.  With it we should be able to make quick work of the Dragon vermin that infest this region.  Find this flower and return to me with it.  You will not be disappointed by my reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:660
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:663
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:660
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:663
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I asked for the Dragonbane Flower and you return empty handed.  Why waste my time?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:661
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:661
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, this is indeed the Dragonbane Flower.  Once we have distilled the poison, we will wipe the Dragon population out!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:662
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:662
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dragonbane Flower has many medicinal uses.  It also has some uses that are less than medicinal.  From this flower a poison is made that is deadly to dragons, but the poison's antidote is also found in its petals. Find this flower and return to me with it.  You will not be disappointed by my reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:664
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:664
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, this is indeed the Dragonbane Flower.  Once the petals are ingested we will be protected from the poison that the Dragon Hunter's would use against us.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:665
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:665
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek to gain the favor of Charles Quixote?  Help us in his crusade against the Dragons of Garrote Gorge. If all of the Dragons in the region and in the Dragon Cave are slain, Charles Quixote will be sure to hear of your name! Return to me when they are all dead!  I will reward you well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:666
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:666
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have slain the vermin!  Here is the reward that I promised!  I will also personally mention your assistance to Charles Quixote!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:667
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:667
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You seek the favor of Deftclaw Redreaver?  Don't we all?  If you were to kill all of the Dragon hunters in the Garrote Gorge wilderness, I would be certain to mention you to him.  I would also be in the position to offer you a generous reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:668
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:668
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The infernal dragon hunters of Charles Quixote are dead? Fantastic!  We can once again enjoy the peace of Garrote Gorge without fear.  Here is your promised reward!  I will go speak with Deftclaw Redreaver of your bravery this instant!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:669
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:669
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Drum of Victory needs to be recovered if we are to ever defeat the Dragons in this region.  If you were to recover the Drum I would reward you well!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:670
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:670
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Drum of Victory was brought here by Charles Quixote.  Its deafening sound drives terror into the heart of any Dragon who hears it.  Unfortunately is was lost in a battle against the Nagas when Charles Quixote was trying to establish his keep, here in Garrote Gorge."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:671
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:671
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have returned with the Drum of Victory!  Charles will be grateful for its return!  Here is your promised reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:672
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:672
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For years the Guild of Necromancers has searched for the Bone of Doom.  The powerful artifact would be of great use to them if recovered.  If you were to find this item and bring it to me, you will be rewarded beyond your wildest dreams."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:673
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:673
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In times almost forgotten a powerful Necromancer named Zacharia almost dominated all of Jadame.  His mastery of the dark arts of necromancy and the elemental magics were combined with an unnaturally strong afinity for Dark energy. His legions of undead helped him enslave all peoples, including the Dark Elves of Alvar.  A plan was made by the Temple of the Sun to defeat Zacharia.  Utilizing the combined might of all of the Clerics in the Temple they forged the sword named Solkrist.  The Patriarch of the Temple led the legions of the Sun against the forces of Zacharia.  The battle raged for years after which the forces of the Temple of the Sun found themselves at the base of the dreaded Shadowspire.  There the Patriarch battled Zarcharia in single combat. At the end of the battle both the Patriarch and Zacharia lay dead.  The Patriarch had cut the left arm from Zacharia's body just as the Necromancer's last spell stopped the Patriarch's heart.  The power of the sword Solkrist instantly slew the Necromancer.  Solkrist disappeared forever in the mayhem after the fight, as did the arm of Zacharia.  The bone from this arm was so instilled with such Dark Magic that it was called the Bone of Doom."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:674
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:674
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the Bone of Doom!  The legend of Zacharia will continue!  Here is your reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:675
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:675
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Some say that Iseldir's Puzzle Box is cursed and that use of it will make the owner go slowly mad.  This can't be true!  All of my studies have provided me with enough proof to determine that the box is the ultimate game in Jadame--not that ridiculous card game, Arcomage.  The last reported owner of Iseldir's Puzzle Box was Zanthora, who is also known as the Mad Necromancer of Shadowspire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:676
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:676
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I ask you to recover the Puzzle Box and you return with nothing.  So you reward is nothing.  Return with the box!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:677
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:677
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Puzzle Box is mine!  Hours of mindless enjoyment at my finger tips!  Here, take you reward for it is nothing compared to the box!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:678
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:678
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A Necromancer's greatest ability is his Intellect!  Without sufficient Intellect, a Necromancer can find himself without spell points when he needs them most! If you bring me the basic ingredients of a Potion of Pure Intellect, I will reward you with the potion that I create!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:679
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:679
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings Master Bounty Hunter! The Guild of Bounty Hunters thanks you for your services to all of Jadame. We are at your disposal!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:680
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:680
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have returned with the ingredients, holding up you end of the bargain.  Here is your Potion of Pure Intellect."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:681
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:681
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We seek to put to rest the soul of the Nosferatu called Korbu.  We have heard rumors that the vampires of Shadowspire seek to resurrect this ancient evil.  There is a Vial of Grave Dirt kept hidden in the Vampire Crypt in the region of Shadowspire that is instrumental in bringing Korbu back to life.  Find us this vial and return it to us.  We will always be in your debt and we will reward you well."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:682
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:682
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Korbu scattered vials of the dirt from his original grave to safe guard himself.  This way he could always gain access to the dirt and move his crypt if he needed to."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:683
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:683
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, once we perform the Rites of Purification upon this dirt, Korbu will rest eternally.  We are in your debt and here is your reward as promised!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:684
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:684
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Personality--the cleric's truest strength.  If you were to provide me with the basic ingredients of a Potion of Pure Personality, I would be more than happy to brew one for you!  Bring me the ingredients!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:685
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:685
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are missing all or some of the needed ingredients.  Return when you have them all."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:686
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:686
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you learned the recipe or are very lucky!  Here is your potion!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:687
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:687
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wyverns are one of the toughest creatures that roam the continent of Jadame.  The Ancient Wyvern can even slay the mightiest adventurer with one blow.  The horn of the Ancient Wyvern is said to have many medicinal any magical properties.  There are many people who pay well for ground wyvern horn."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:688
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:688
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will buy Wyvern horns from you for 1500 gold!  I grind these horns up and sell them throughout Jadame.  Someday I hope to be able to ship them over sea to Enroth and Erathia.  That of course depends on whether the Pirates of Regna are still a problem to shipping or not!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:689
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:689
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "1500 gold!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:690
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:690
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Accuracy can determine who lives and who dies in battle.  If you cannot hit your opponent you will surely perish!  If you bring me the ingredients of a Potion of Pure Accuracy, I will brew that potion for you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:691
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:691
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not found the treasure of the Dread Pirate Stanley!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:692
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:692
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, the right ingredients always do the trick! Here is your potion."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:693
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:693
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The legendary Pirate Stanley is rumored to have stolen hundreds and thousands of gold pieces from the Merchants of Alvar.  No one has ever found where he has hidden his treasure.  Some say it isn't even hidden on the Island of Regna."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:694
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:694
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Years and years ago, I remember hearing that Stanley journeyed to Ravage Roaming to speak with the Ogre Mage Zog about a curse that had fallen upon him.  Apparently his memory was fading, and he was certain that an evil mage was responsible."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:695
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:695
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "He who finds the treasure of the Dread Pirate Stanley will be a rich person!  Will that person be you?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:696
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:696
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobersk fruit is native only to the Dagger Wound Island region.  Here the mild winters and humid summers provide the perfect conditions for the Tobersk fruit to achieve the correct levels of sugar and juice.  The pulp masters in Ravenshore pay good money for the tobersk fruit."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:697
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:697
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobersk brandy is favorite drink of the Lizardmen of Dagger Wound Island.  Some call it an acquired taste.  How ever you look at it, it equals pure profit!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:698
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:698
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobersk fruit is processed in Ravenshore into tobersk pulp.  Its from this pulp that the master brewers in Alvar distill tobersk brandy."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:699
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:699
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here the mild winters and humid summers provide the perfect conditions for the tobersk fruit to achieve the correct levels of sugar and juice.  Here you can purchase tobersk fruit so our pulp masters can labor over the fruit, processing it into tobersk pulp."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:700
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:700
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobersk brandy is a favorite drink among the Lizardmen of Dagger Wound Island.  Some call it an acquired taste.  How ever you look at it, it equals pure profit!  Be gentle with the bottles as you travel back to the islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:701
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:701
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tobersk pulp is combined with the waters of the Alvar River and is distilled over time until the brew masters declare it ready for consumption. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:702
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:702
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Heartwood of Jadame is used by the vampires of the Shadowspire region in the construction of their coffins.  The Heartwood's durability provides the coffin's owner with many years of rest during the daylight hours."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:703
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:703
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dried sunfish is a delicacy enjoyed by the High Clerics of the Temple of the Sun.  They pay good money for deliveries of this flaky, somewhat salty fish."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:704
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:707
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:704
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:707
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Pirates of Regna like flamboyant jewelry!  Amulets that fail to take enchantments cast by the Necromancers of Shadowspire fill this need quite well.  The Pirates pay some of their \"hard earned\" bounty to get these amulets."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:705
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:705
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Heartwood of Jadame is used by the Vampires of the Shadowspire region in the construction of their coffins.  The Heartwood's durability provides the coffin's owner with many years of rest during the daylight hours."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:706
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:706
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dried Sunfish is a delicacy enjoyed by the High Clerics of the Temple of the Sun.  They pay good money for deliveries of this flaky, somewhat salty fish."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:708
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:708
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Purchase Silver Dust of the Sea made by the Necromancers of Shadowspire. It is used by the smugglers of Ravenshore to hide their boats.  It provides the boats with a limited form of invisibility."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:709
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:709
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ground Wyvern Horn is reported to be one of the most potent reagents used by the necromancers of Shadowspire.  Unlike the reagents used by alchemists, this reagent is only used by the highest ranking members of the Necromancers' Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:710
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:713
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:710
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:713
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "These Forged Credit Vouchers are used by agents of the Ogre Mage Zog to acquire gold from the Merchants of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:711
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:711
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Purchase Silver Dust of the Sea made by the necromancers of Shadowspire. It is used by the Smuggler's of Ravenshore to hide their boats.  It provides the boats with a limited form of invisibility."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:712
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:712
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ground Wyvern Horn is reported to be one of the most potent reagents used by the necromancers of Shadowspire.  Unlike the reagents used by alchemists, this reagents is only used by the highest members of the Necromancers' Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:742
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:742
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the cure, but others in the area are still sick!  Be sure to deliver the cure to them as well!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:743
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:743
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am very sick, without a Cure Disease scroll I will surely perish from Yellow Fever!."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:744
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:744
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the cure! Be sure to deliver scrolls to those who still suffer from the Yellow Fever."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:745
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:745
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The epidemic continues! The people on the outer islands will perish!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:746
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:746
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Without the Anointed Herb Potion we cannot remove the poison from our water supply!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:747
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:747
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where is the Idol?  Do not waste my time unless you have it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:748
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:748
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Black Potions are made of a complex blending of many of the three basic alchemical reagents. Red reagents include Widowsweep Berries, Wolf's Eye, and Phials of Gog Blood.  Some blue reagents are Phoenix Feather, Phima Root, Meteor Fragment and Will O' Wisps Heart.  And some yellow reagents are Datura, Dragon Turtle Fang, Poppy Pods and Thornbark."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:749
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:749
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have repaired the Portals of Stone?  That is tremendous news!  Quickly, find my brother, Isthric and tell him to return home!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:750
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:750
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You found Isthric and told him how to return home?  We are indeed in debt to you, Merchant of Alvar!  I will speak well of you to Clan Leader Brekish Onefang.  Please take these potions of Cure Wounds as a reward."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:751
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:751
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have found the Prophecies of the Snake!  Perhaps the details of our future can be found in its writings!  Please take this reward for your assistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:752
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:752
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My brother Rohtnax lives!  And you have repaired the Portals of Stone?  I must return home to him, so that we can plan our family's survival!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:753
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:753
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thank you again for making it possible for me to return to my family! The Clan Leader shall hear of your help!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:754
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:754
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have killed all of the dire wolves in the region!  Travelers are once again safe. However, I now find myself in need of a new business!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:755
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:755
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have no more pelts, return when you have more!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:756
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:756
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My family returned and told me of how you rescued them.  Tell the Merchants of Alvar, that they no longer need rely upon our \"bargain.\"  I will keep my word to them and to you, my boats will always be at your service!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:757
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:757
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You do not have any Naga Hides!  You waste my time!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:758
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:758
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where is Eclipse?  Return to me when you have found the shield!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:759
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:759
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I pay 500 gold for Ogre Ears.  The Merchant Guild of Alvar supports me in paying this bounty to anyone who can kill and ogre."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:760
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:760
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Return to me with Ogre ears if you wish to be paid!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:761
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:761
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I only pay for Wasp Stingers!  Nothing more, nothing less!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:762
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:762
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the potion, but others in the area are without protection!  Be sure to deliver a potion to them as well!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:763
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:763
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I an defenseless against the onslaught of the sea of fire!  I need a Potion of Fire Resistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:764
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:764
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the potion!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:765
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:765
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for providing Potions of Fire Resistance to the southernmost houses here in Rust.  Perhaps we can survive until a new home can be found for us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:766
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:766
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Return when you have more Wyvern Horns and I will pay you more!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:767
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:767
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Royal Wasp Jelly is a delicacy!  The upper caste of Merchants enjoys this tasty treat with almost every meal!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:768
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:768
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I pay 1000 gold for Royal Wasp Jelly!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:770
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:770
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Return when you have Wasp Jelly and then I will pay you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:771
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:771
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Scattered around the land are the Challenges.  If your ability is great enough, and you best the Challenge, you will be award skill points to do with as you wish!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:772
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:772
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Dragons of Garrote Gorge are susceptible to a poison that can be distilled from the rare dragonbane flower.  The flower also is the only means of an antidote for the Dragons."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:773
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:773
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With all of the Dragons in the wilderness defeated, we can move on the Dragon Cave and eliminate the Dragons once and for all!  Thanks again for your help in defeating them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:774
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:774
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With all of the Dragon hunters in the wilderness defeated, we can move on their camp and eliminate them once and for all!  Thanks again for your help in defeating them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:775
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:775
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Return when you have the Drum of Victory.  You waste your time and mine otherwise!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:776
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:776
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I ask for the Bone, and you return with nothing. Be gone!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:777
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:777
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I need not see you again until you have the Puzzle Box!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:778
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:778
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You're new aren't you?  Tell Arion Hunter that I expect more of his rabble than the likes of you!  Give me the reports and leave my sight!  You make me sick!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:779
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:779
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not gathered sufficient bounties to allow us to promote you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:780
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:780
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You currently hold the rank of Novice Bounty Hunter, but lack sufficient bounty to be promoted to Journeyman."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:781
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:781
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You currently hold the rank of Journeyman Bounty Hunter, but lack sufficient bounty to be promoted to Master."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:782
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:782
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You currently hold the rank of Master Bounty Hunter! This is the highest rank of our guild."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:783
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:783
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lying as they do on opposite ends of the Light to Dark spectrum, relationships between the Necromancers' Guild and the Temple of the Sun have never been the best, but now they battle openly. Oskar Tyre, head priest of the Temple says a holy vision drove him to declare war on the guild so as to rid Jadame of the taint of darkness.\n"
"\n"
"Both groups are relative newcomers to our continent. The guild has set up its foothold in Shadowspire, and the First (and only) Sun Temple of Jadame is in Murmurwoods."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:784
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:784
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Through your delivery of the Nightshade Brazier into their hands, the Necromancers' Guild has come out on top in their war with the Temple of the Sun. The artifact's magic creates a permanent shadow of darkness which surrounds the Shadowspire region. Under this cover, vampires defend the land both day and night. This has allowed the guild to field larger forces of skeletons, zombies and other undead against the temple's armies. Each report I receive puts the heart of the battle closer and closer to the Sun Temple's doorstep."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:785
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:785
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Because you have destroyed the Necromancers' Guild Skeleton Transformer, the Temple of the Sun has come out on top in their war with the guild. The skeletons created by the device made up the bulk of the guild's reinforcements. Without these, the necromancers' forces crumble before the temple's advance. Each report I receive puts the heart of the battle closer to the Necromancers' Guild doorstep."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:786
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:786
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The renown Dragon slayer, Charles Quixote of Erathia, has set up a hunting expedition in Garrote Gorge. This is no \"safari,\" in fact, it's the largest operation of this type I've heard of. The hunters have a permanent base from which they sell hides, eggs, baby dragons, and other items. Garrote Gorge has always had a large Dragon population, but I imagine they must be facing extinction--so efficient are Quixote's hunters."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:787
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:787
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It seems Charles Quixote's Dragon hunting operation in Garrote Gorge has almost completely wiped out Garrote Gorge's Dragon population. I'm sure once their done, those mountains will be safer to travel. Still, I wonder what Jadame will be like without Dragons."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:788
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:788
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "By recovering Deftclaw Redreaver's heir for him, you've allowed him to safely attack Charles Quixote's camp. Dragon hunters operate by isolating members of their prey. They just aren't prepared to face Dragons in number! Needless to say, the camp's production of Dragon goods has dwindled to a trickle. A pity. The guild used to turned a good profit off them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:789
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:789
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Minotaurs of Balthazar Lair in Ravage Roaming are a proud culture. Their recent defeat of the Vori Frost Giants has, if anything, made them even more fiercely independent--more sure of their ability to face any task alone. Still, I have told the guild that they would make great allies, both to face the current crisis and later as trade partners."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:790
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:790
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "By rescuing the Balthazar Lair Minotaurs, you have ingratiated them to yourselves and by extension, to our guild. Even through the crisis, trade relations with them have improved immeasurably. Once maters of the cataclysm are resolved, I'm sure we will see a tidy profit--a direct result from your good work."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:791
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:791
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who knows the fate of Jadame now.  Perhaps you will find a way to save us from destruction?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:792
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:792
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jadame owes you a great debt!  You have saved the entire world from total destruction!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:793
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:793
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With the bridges destroyed by the eruption of the mountain of fire, we cannot get to the boat dock!  We are cut off from the mainland!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:794
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:794
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have repaired the Portals of Stone?  We are all in your debt.  If only it was safe to travel through the Abandoned Temple!  Well, at least we can attempt to get to the boat dock through there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:795
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:795
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We used to have a nice series of bridges between the small islands of this region and one large bridge to the main land.  The volcano destroyed all of these.  Now we cannot travel anywhere except by boat, but we cannot even get to our boat dock!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:796
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:796
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Did you know I was their captive for over six years? At first, I thought they were devils from hell, but now I am not so sure. They looked like devils surely, but did not act as demons. No, I think they were but another type of monstrous race, like ogres or goblins. Regardless, devils or not, I am glad the world is rid of them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:797
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:797
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Catherine and I have had dealings with these \"lords\" of the elemental planes. I've never trusted them, and now it seems I am right. They were our recent allies against the Kreegans, but a few months later, we find ourselves at war with them here! In both cases I understand neither their reasons for helping or hindrance. They are fickle beings at best...\"treacherous\" is perhaps a better word for them."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:798
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:798
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I must say I'm looking forward to returning to my lands of Enroth. It has been so long since I've seen them, or my son, Prince Nicolai. He was just a lad when I saw him last and now he is nearly grown. Sir Humphrey was a good choice for regent, but the land has been too long without its king at the reins of state."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:799
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:799
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "After we defeated the Kreegans in Erathia, I abdicated my throne into the regenthood of one of my generals, Morgan Kendal. I have left in his capable hands the task of choosing Erathia's new ruler. I'm sure this seems to be much to give up, but I am first and foremost, the queen of Enroth. We were sailing for there when the cataclysm struck, drawing us here."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:800
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:800
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Kreegans? They are no more; I am sure of it. After we put down Lucifer Kreegan, my armies scoured Eofol searching for any signs of their continued existence. We found none. No, the Kreegan infestation of our world is eliminated."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:801
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:801
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I fought alongside elementals in our campaigns against the Kreegan. I found them stalwart and loyal. I know Roland disagrees, but I cannot call their hostility here a case of fickleness. No, I think something else drives them to attack us--magic perhaps? You should speak with our sage, Xanthor. He has been studying the Destroyer's crystal. I'm sure he's come up with some theory by now."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:802
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:802
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We used to travel freely between the islands using the bridges.  These bridges were destroyed when the mountain of fire erupted.  Many families are trapped on the outer islands.  We don’t even know if the people who live there are still alive."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:803
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:803
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With the Portals of Stone repaired, we can at least check on the outer islands and those who live there.  We are in your debt for fixing the Portals of Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:804
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:804
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The boat dock on the northernmost island is the only way to travel between Dagger Wound and the mainland.  With the bridges destroyed, we cannot get to the boat dock and those arriving from Ravenshore cannot get to the village of Blood Drop!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:805
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:805
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We can get to the boat docks?  But we have to go through the Abandoned Temple?  Well that's something.  At least we can get to the boats."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:811
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:806
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have traveled to these lands to catalog its array of available cheese. My task is nearly complete, but there are yet three cheeses I have yet to sample. These are Frelandeau, Eldenbrie and Dunduck. I would reward highly any who could locate these rare and reputedly tasty culinary gems for me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:812
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:807
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You say you will find me the cheeses I desire, but here you are returned, empty-handed! Do not waste my precious time! Bring me cheese--Frelandeau, Eldenbrie and Dunduck! Do not return until you have them!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:813
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:808
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Very good, you have found me some of the cheese I seek. But now I have my heart set on a full cheese tasting with all three cheeses eaten at once so I can savor them in comparison. Come back when you have then all. I will not take what you have now. I don't think I could resist sampling what you leave--and then the cheese tasting would be ruined!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:814
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:809
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Excellent! Give me the cheeses! I must consume them!\n"
"\n"
"Ah….munch munch….frelandeau, exquisite….mmmm, and eldenbrie, wondrously smoky…and hmmm, dunduck…well, that's not very nice, is it?\n"
"\n"
"You have made my Jadamean cheese cataloging safari a success! I can die a happy man! You have the humble thanks of a man of cheese. And here is your promised reward!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:815
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:810
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are no people more dedicated to cheesecraft than the august cheese masters of Vori. Otherwise known to be rather barbaric, the Vori Frost Giants are true emblems of the potential of civilized development--at least as far as cheese making is concerned. Did you know that they have forty-two different words for \"cheese.\""
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:816
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:811
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Even as a lad I knew I had a special relationship with cheese. Why, my first memory is of nibbling a bit of farmer's cheddar from my mother's hand! From that day I knew it would be my passion to eat cheese, to know all of the endless variety of its tasty wonderment, and to search the world for rare and exotic cheese-stuff. And so have I made my life...and destiny."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:817
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:812
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With the cheeses you have brought me, I have now eaten all of the world's known cheeses. Now none can say that I, Asael Fromago, am not history's most eminent connoisseur of cheese! None can compare to my glory! Ha-ha-ha…"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:818
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:813
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The night the stranger came through here was the same night that the crystal erupted in the center of town.  I only caught a glimpse of the stranger.  He didn’t appear the potent mage that he was.  I was not in the town square when he summoned the crystal, but I did see the flash of light that traveled across the sky.  It was truly a terrible night."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:819
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:814
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A wanderer came into town.  Several ruffians sought to relieve this traveler of whatever wealth he possibly possessed. The wanderer barely paid any of them much notice.  With a small flick of his wrist all fell before him.  Then he walked to the town square and summoned the giant crystal that you'll find there today."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:820
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:815
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There is an ancient saying among the Dark Elf people,  \"a thing lives only as long as the last person who remembers it.\"  The events the night the crystal burst forth into our lives will live for a very long time.  Many of us saw the events of that night.  The mage who summoned forth the crystal said not one word to anyone us.  When he looked upon us, it seemed that all there was in his heart and eyes was pity."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:821
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:816
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When the mage came into town I didn’t think much of it.  This is Ravenshore.  Everyone who travels the roads of Jadame comes through here at some time or another.  I guess I should have paid more attention to him.  Seems he caused quite a stir in the town square."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:822
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:817
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Pirates of Regna own the seas.  No one can stand against them!  Several years ago, some fishing boat captains thought that they could sail to Erathia to get help dealing with the pirates.  We never saw or heard from them again."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:823
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:818
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Regnans are the worst slime to ever set foot on the shore of Jadame. They keep the peoples of this continent from trading with Erathia and Enroth.  What choice do we have?  Even the Merchants of Alvar couldn’t muster a fleet to deal with the pirates.  Rumor says that there are smugglers around that have found ways around the pirate blockades."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:824
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:819
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Regnans call themselves the Empire of the Endless Ocean--trying to make more of themselves than there really is.  All they are is bullies and bandits.  Of course, don’t tell them that I said that!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:825
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:820
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Over the last few weeks there have been reports of bandits and Ogres robbing travelers on all of the major roads of Jadame. Times just seem to be getting worse.  Between the Regnan Pirates and these bandits it seems that no one is safe to travel by any means."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:826
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:821
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Several of the warriors got together to go take care of the ogres that were camping on the road to Ravenshore.  That’s when we first had word of the fortress they were constructing to the southwest of here.  Since the fortress was completed the roads to the south and west have not been safe."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:827
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:822
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Smuggler of Jadame may be a myth, but I think not.  The Merchants of Alvar seem to be able to send small amounts of goods away across the sea to Erathia and Enroth.  Yet they own no boats of their own.   This would seem to support the idea that there really are smugglers.  Now why they work for the merchants is beyond the likes of me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:828
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:823
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wererats!  They are the worst of scum!  The pick through our trash at night!  Always scurrying around in the dark!  Never seen when the sun is up.  Gives one the shivers it does!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:829
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:824
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Cyclopes that dwell to the southeast of here have always been a threat to the village of Rust!  But the village has always been able to push back any raid.  They aren't so tough in small numbers, but if they can catch you out in the desert unaware, you will not survive!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:830
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:825
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The sea of fire took us all by surprise.  It spread through the eastern half of the village like wildfire.  Luckily its growth seems to have slowed.  Still I don’t know how much longer any of us can last."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:831
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:826
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We need to find a new place to live!  There is no way any people could live under these conditions.  Even the Cyclopes will be forced to move.  There are legends that talk about the ancient homeland that we traveled here from.  The stories say that it was lush and green.  If we only had such a place to return to."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:832
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:827
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are traders in Alvar and Shadowspire that trade for the different types of ore that can be found all over Jadame.  They use the ore to create items that they are more than happy to trade for more ore!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:833
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:828
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You know, it is said the Vault of Time was here before Ravenshore; the town was built around it. It is supposed to contain the treasure of the old Emperor Thorn who ruled the lands around here hundreds of years ago. Many come here to try and open the vault, but none succeed."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:834
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:829
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As if Quixote was not enough of a problem to plague us, we must also contend with Ilsingore, Ilsingore and Old Loeb--renegades among our kind! They think they can rebuild our race by scattering across Jadame and starting their own tribes. Fools! All they do is weaken us by removing themselves from our numbers. Yaardrake has fled to the Ironsand Desert. I know not where the others have gone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:835
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:830
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "While Garrote Gorge has the highest concentration of dragons in Jadame, I hear there is hunting to be had elsewhere. For instance, there is rumored to be a great old dragon out in the Ironsand Desert. Another is supposed to be somewhere in the badlands of Ravage Roaming."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:836
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:831
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When Charles Quixote brought us over from Erathia, we sailed past Regna Island. Since this was our first sight of Jadamean land on the voyage, it was an omen of our hunting expedition's future success that I saw an ancient dragon winging its way towards the island. How I wish I could get a spear in that one! It was the biggest dragon I'd ever seen!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:837
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:832
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, I was here the day the Destroyer walked through Ravenshore! I was at the blacksmith's getting a knife sharpened. He walked right past us like he owned the town. A crowd was following him at a distance. One of them threw a rock, but it bounced off a magic shield surrounding him. He didn't even seem to notice. Later I heard an explosion from the town square. I ran out to look, but the Destroyer was gone and that crystal and scattered bodies were all that remained."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:838
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:833
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yeah, I saw the \"Destroyer\" and well named he is! I thought he was a rich merchant, and he looked like easy prey, so I…well, I tried to rob him. I ran ahead of him and lay in ambush in an alley, waiting for him to pass. When he walked by, I made a grab for him. My mistake! I didn't even touch him! As soon as I got near him, I was thrown back by his magic. In fact, I was thrown over a house into the next street!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:839
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:834
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Those cursed ratmen--those so-called \"Priests of Eep\"--are nothing but trouble. More like a pack of thieves than holy men, they are! I'll warn you, traveler. Keep an eye on your equipment when they're around. They'll steal anything that isn't nailed down."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:840
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:835
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, if you're looking for cheese, I daresay you will find it in the churches of Eep. You know mice like cheese. Well, this rule also applies to the ratmen of Eep. It is said that they keep a horde of the stuff in each of their temples."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:841
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:836
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "On top of all of our problems here, the lord of our plane, Gralkor the Cruel is missing. He is a being of great power and could no doubt fight the dark magic which assails this plane."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:842
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:837
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish I understood what has happened here. One day it was life as usual here…and this is normally a peaceful realm. Then suddenly everyone was howling with violent madness and was filled with a thirst to crush your land of Jadame. Even now my fellow Earth Plane denizens work single-mindedly to push the firmament of our realm into yours."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:843
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:838
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Perhaps the reason I am not affected by the madness is that I carry with me an amulet given to me by the lord of this plane, Shalwend. It is said in our legends that he and the other elemental lords made your world. No doubt if Shalwend was here he could stop the creeping madness, but he is missing! Where is our lord in our time of greatest need?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:844
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:839
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It was clearly magic which caused the madness that has taken my fellow Plane of Air dwellers. On the day it struck there was instant chaos. All who were affected dropped what they were doing and began to howl. It was a chorus of horror! Only a handful of us maintain our sanity. Now, day by day, our glorious realm falls further and further towards a state of hellish decline."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:845
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:840
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am not unschooled in the ways of magic. Clearly some spell of almost unimaginable power has affected those that live in this watery realm. My main curiosity is to know why this has occurred. Clearly no one would risk using such power if it was not to achieve some terrible end. All I know is that the Plane of Water makes war upon your realm. From here, I can discern no reason to it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:846
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:841
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "W-what has h-happened to my home w-waters? All are c-consumed by m-m-madness! And worse, our l-lord is m-missing! Where is our r-ruler, th-the mighty Acw-w-walander! W-without him w-we are d-doomed!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:847
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:842
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know to your eyes, this plane must seem a hell-scape. But I tell you, normally it is not so. Before the madness we lived here together in a state of peace and harmony. But then, one day the madness fell and our Lord Pyrannaste was nowhere to be found. Perhaps his absence caused the madness? It may be so, he has never before been gone from this realm in my memory."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:848
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:843
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though the madness affects almost all of those that live here, it has not robbed them of their cunning. As I am sure you are aware, they make war on your realm, but it is not with crazed abandon that they do so. Leaders have emerged among the affected, and these make shrewd military designs against you. Even now they mass near the gateway to Jadame in preparation for a massive assault."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:849
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:844
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Snapfinger family tomb is one of the lowest in our village's burial catacombs. Since we are such an honored family, our crypt is the largest. It isn't the easiest place to find--even I have become lost looking for it! When I do, I find it by keeping a hand on the right-side wall. I eventually get there."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:850
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:845
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you found the shield?  The recovery of Eclipse is very important to the Temple of the Sun!  You must help us find it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:851
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:846
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks again for recovering the shield Eclipse!  I hope it has proven helpful in your adventures."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:852
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:847
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You never had it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:853
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:848
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Here is your missing item."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:854
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:849
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Well, that matter's done. I will make arrangements to travel to Ravenshore so I myself may sit on your council. Frankly, I could use a bit of change. I will leave my second in command, Reginald Dorray, in charge.\n"
"\n"
"Again, good job."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:855
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:850
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm sorry. I'd like to adventure, yes, but you're just not at my level."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:856
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:851
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sure, why not? I'm ready to go--just have to grab my gear! I'll show the guild who is worthy and who isn't!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:857
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:852
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "No…no, that life is over for me. Besides, if I were to take up the mace again, it would be with other companions. I'm afraid--if I may speak bluntly--I just can't see myself traveling with a group as inexperienced as yours."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:858
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:853
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Say, that sounds grand! Yes, I will go with you, if you will have me."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:859
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:854
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I think not! Why would I travel with the likes of you? Perhaps you didn't catch my name, \"Jasp Thelbourne?\" Yes, that \"Thelbourne,\" rabble. No, whatever you're up to, I'm not interested."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:860
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:855
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, we'd make quite a team! We have all done such great deeds, how could not further greatness follow from our joining together? I'll go with you if you want."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:861
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:856
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Now that I need not fear my heir's destruction. I will visit my revenge on Quixote. His camp will face the assault of fire and claw. Those who have hunted us are now our prey animals.\n"
"\n"
"As for your alliance…you have done me a great service. I will honor my debt. As soon as I've set my enemies to flight or the beyond, I will join the alliance council in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:862
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:857
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I tell you, with all that's going on, it's like an honest merchant can't get business done! I mean, we've always had to deal with Ogre raiders, but now they've grown so bold as to have built a fort right here in Alvar! Now no caravans can take the west road to Murmurwoods. The worst of it is most of my trade with the Temple of the Sun there!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:863
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:858
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have done us all a great service by clearing out the Ogre's fort. Now our caravans can freely travel to Murmurwoods. I thank you…and my purse certainly thanks you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:864
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:859
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sure we have wasps in Alvar--and rather large ones, too--but we tolerate them for good reason. Many of our customers desire wasp products. Say…if you want to get in on the action, the trader, Veldon, is a broker for wasp parts. He lives here in town, and I hear he is currently trying to fill a large order for wasp stingers."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:865
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:860
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not many people know this, but it is possible to train a Dragon. It's sort of like breaking a horse, except that it requires more special equipment and a lot of magic. Those tame Dragons outside the fort are an example of my work. Right now they are loyal to us, but I will bond them to their ultimate customer, Fennis Greenwood, a minor lord back in Erathia. Well, I will do so as soon as he pays us, that is."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:866
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:861
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Zanthora is a strange character. Not to say that members of the Necromancers' Guild are not all strange, but she is truly mad. I hear that other guild members simply refuse to work with her--so terrible are her experiments. Still, they value her dark genius. To keep her around, they built her a lab of her own out on the marshy wastes outside of town."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:867
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:862
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For the most part, the Necromancers' Guild has the local vampires under control…mostly. But there's one place you don't want to go! Most of them sleep in a communal crypt north of the guild. Watch out if you go there. They're a bit, shall we say…\"territorial.\""
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:868
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:863
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Necromancers' Guild? Hey, I think they're great. You should have seen this place before they came--nothing going on at all! Sure, we got vampires, skeletons and other undead running around. Still, I gotta say, things are sure a lot more lively around here!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:869
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:864
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As you might imagine, business is great. Oh, sure, the guild necromancers turn most of my customers into skeletons and zombies, but vampires are repeat business! Want a piece of the action? There's a wood dealer in town, Mylander, who is always looking for good Murmurwood lumber. If you have any he'll pay a pretty penny for it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:870
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:865
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hunting has become pretty hazardous of late, but still we must do it if we are to eat! Yesterday I was out along the western shore of the fire lake and found a tunnel that seems to go under the lake. I didn't explore it though. It was infested with gogs and worse...like everything else around here these days."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:871
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:866
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Even we who live here get lost. If you would not lose your way, follow the floating waystones. Ahhh…the madness returns….It returns!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:872
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:867
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, I'm glad you're out saving the world. I mean, someone has to do it. Me, I'm for the easy life. As long as I got my boat and my pole, and the fish are biting, I don't see any reason to do much else. Good luck to you though!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:873
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:868
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That Stanley, now there's a Regnan with some spark! Why I hear he's the one that got us in good with that thar Zog the Jackal--some sort of Ogre or giant Troll or something, I think--a genuine barbarian king. Now we got us our ships on the seas and a bunch of club swinging devils on the land. I tell ya, the Great and Mighty Regnan Empire is headed for greatness, what with the likes of the Dread Pirate Stanley doing for us!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:874
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:869
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh sure, we Regnans have to put up with a bit of competition--I'm talking about smugglers, you know--but I understand the Dread Pirate Stanley is putting the clamp on that. Why I understand he kidnapped Arion Hunter's family just so he can pressure the wererat into staying off our turf. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:875
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:870
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yeah, I know the \"Dread\" Pirate Stanley is the hero of the moment around here, but I say, fah! Sure he's done a lot for Regna, but no man does anything that doesn't help himself. Why I hear old Stanley's been shaving off the top of every deal he's in--and that's a lot of deals! What I'd like to know is where he keeps his booty. Probably not on Regna, I reckon. It wouldn't be a fortnight before someone dug it up!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:876
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:871
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have come up with a scheme for finding hidden treasure. Before you barged in, I was hard at work formulating a spell for sensing gold hidden beneath the ground. If I am successful, I plan to have a Dragon carry me over the wastelands of Ravage Roaming where the Dread Pirate Stanley's treasure is rumored to be buried. My spell will find it and I will be a wealthy man."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:877
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:872
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You mean the one just north of here? Well, none of us have anything to do with it. It's haunted!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:878
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:873
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't know where they're at, but I know there's some of them ratmen around here somewhere. At night I hear all sorts of squeaking and scuffling outside. In the morning, pretty much everything that isn't under lock or bolted down is gone. If I knew where that Eep church was. I'd take some of my boys over for a little...talk."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:879
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:874
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I was out with one of the crews working along the new lake searching for things that were washed out of the lair. We think we found the source of the flood. There is a strange gateway out in the middle of the lake. We don't have any boats, so we didn't explore it, but even from the shore, it is clear to see that it leads to a watery realm."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:880
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:875
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, if you haven't been to the fortress, that's the first place you should go. As you are aware from your orientation, the so-called fortress on this island is just a front to fool our enemies. You'll need to make your way to the real fort on the crescent island. Just take the underground passage marked on your orientation map."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:881
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:876
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know they call us \"pirates\" on Jadame, but really, we're just running our empire. It is not our fault that our Jadamean subjects refuse to acknowledge our rule and do not pay their taxes. Since they do not pay, we're forced to collect tribute in the form of booty. Actually we prefer it this way--saves us the trouble of having to actually rule the continent."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:882
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:877
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We vampires cannot normally walk about in the daylight, but Thant the Necromancers' Guildmaster has created an artifact to deal with this. A vampire wearing one of his Nightshade Amulets can move about freely day or night. Sadly, there are few available. I myself do not have one so must stay indoors during the day."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:883
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:878
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Normally, we vampires need one of Thant's Nightshade Amulets to travel freely during the day, but since you've brought us the Nightshade Brazier, glorious night covers Shadowspire around the clock! Now those of us who don't have the amulets can walk about during the day...well, at least as long as we stay in the area."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:884
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:879
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though it isn't my style, I must say a lot of folks around here like to cover themselves with all sorts of jewelry. They say it's fashion, but I just find it gaudy. Anyway, if you have any to sell go find Pavel in town. He does a brisk trade in all sorts of tacky junk."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:885
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:880
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You looking for sunfish? Sorry, can't help you. Funny thing is, I had a whole catch of them just last week, but Pavel the merchant bought the whole lot. Maybe you can get them from him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:886
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:881
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Centuries ago the largest battle to date between the Guild of Necromancers and the Temple of the Sun was fought on this spot!  So much magical energy was released that the very ground was scorched and is black to this very day!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:887
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:882
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Very good…or at least, as good as can be expected. You managed to bring three partners into the alliance--the minimum number my advisors told me would be sufficient to fulfill the \"…Jadame, must stand together…\" part of the prophecy. A pity it could not be more, but events of the cataclysm are clearly coming to a head. It is time to move onward.\n"
"\n"
"You must travel to Ravenshore and meet with the alliance council gathered there. With them, decide what must be the next step we take in meeting the elemental crisis."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:888
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:883
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We have a small warehouse downstairs. You are free to use the chests there to store extra equipment. Put anything in there you don't want to wander off!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:889
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:884
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Thank you for releasing me. Know that Shalwend, Lord of Air, holds you in his favor. \n"
"\n"
"I go now to restore order to my realm and to join with my fellow lords to do what I can for yours. Be warned! Our actions will destabilize the crystal gateway. Leave now for your home, lest you be trapped here forever.  Inform Xanthor of what has happened here. Farewell"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:890
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:885
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"\"The Destroyer\" is a fitting moniker for one who would imprison me in such a fashion. If it were not for you, I, Acwalander, Lord of Water, would have soon perished. My passing would have had an unbalancing effect across all the planes. Thank you. I go now to gather with the other lords. Together we will set things right.\n"
"\n"
" Be warned! Our actions will destabilize the crystal gateway. Leave now for your home, lest you be trapped here forever. Inform Xanthor of what has happened here. Farewell."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:891
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:886
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I am free! Now will he who was fool enough to jail me--this Destroyer--feel my wrath. That I, the Lord of Earth, am called \"Gralkor the Cruel\" is no mistake. The suffering I have felt will be his returned in multitudes!\n"
"\n"
"I go now to gather with the other lords. Together we will set things right. Be warned! Our actions will destabilize the crystal gateway. Leave now for your home, lest you be trapped here forever. Inform Xanthor of what has happened here. Farewell"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:892
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:887
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Free at last. My torment is over, but what of my subjects? I know the Destroyer has them compelled to a terrible task. My presence will sooth them. I must go to restore order to my realm and yours.\n"
"\n"
"Before I return to the Plane of Fire, I will gather with the other lords. Together we will set things right. Be warned! Our actions will destabilize the crystal gateway. Leave now for your home, lest you be trapped here forever.  Inform Xanthor of what has happened here. Farewell"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:893
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:888
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Oh, what a mess you've made of things! When I asked you to find me a witness of events in the Ironsand Desert, I thought it would be obvious that you'd have to return him to me in good condition! I mean look at the poor Troll! Take him to the temple and get him fixed up.\n"
"\n"
"And please...try to remember you're working for the guild. We do have a reputation for conducting ourselves with at least passing competence."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:894
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:889
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You found Ebonest?  What of my father?  Where is he?  I thought you were going to return when you had found both my father and the spear."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:895
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:890
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You found my father and Ebonest?  I will be forever in your debt!  We should take the spear to Charles Quixote, and if he is agreeable, he will promote me and any knights in your party!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:896
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:891
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are employed by the Merchants of Alvar, yes? Well, I think you should speak with Dadeross, the leader of your caravan. My far seeing vision tells me he is on the Dagger Wound Islands."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:897
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:892
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmmm…I cannot look too far ahead--for the ether is thick today. All I see is that you must deliver the letter Dadeross gave you to the merchant, Elgar Fellmoon. Fellmoon lives in the city of Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:898
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:893
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see a vision of you in which you take a letter from Elgar Fellmoon in Ravenshore to Arion Hunter, the leader of the Ravenshore smugglers. After this, you return to Fellmoon. The end of the vision is a blur, so you must not have lived entirely through it. Still, it is your fate to do these things."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:899
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:894
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't need my vision to tell me what you must do next. Do as Fellmoon asked of you. Go seek Bastian Loudrin, the guildmaster of the Alvarian Merchant Guild. He is in the city of Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:900
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:895
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see an important connection has not been made between the present and your future. You must return to Bastian Loudrin and continue your conversations with him. He will send you on the next step down your road."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:901
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:896
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In my dreams last night, I saw you traveling to the Ironsand Desert to find a witness to the formation of a great lake of fire which formed there during the cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:902
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:897
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is clear to me that you must bring the Troll, Overdune, to the merchant guild in Alvar."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:903
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:898
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see far through space today, but not through time. A great disaster has befallen the Minotaurs of Balthazar Lair in Ravage Roaming. I feel that your destiny is linked with their fate. You must rescue them from their peril."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:904
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:899
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There is great turmoil in the Balance. It has taken me some time to know its source, but I know it now. It is caused by the war between the clerics of the Temple of the Sun located in Murmurwoods, and the Necromancers' Guild of Shadowspire. It is your destiny to undo the turmoil by choosing one of these two to ally with."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:905
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:900
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There is great turmoil in the Balance. It has taken me some time to know its source, but I know it now. There is conflict between the Dragons and Knights who fight in Garrote Gorge. It is your destiny to ally with one of the two at the expense of the other."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:906
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:901
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have done good work in forging the alliances you have. It is now time for you to seek the council of those allies you have brought together. Seek them out in their council chamber within the merchant guild in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:907
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:902
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see an important connection has not been made between the present and your future destiny. You must return to the council chamber in the Ravenshore merchant guild. The councilors will send you on the next step down your road."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:908
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:903
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must do as the alliance council has asked of you. Find a way to Regna Island and sink the Regnan port fleet."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:909
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:904
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In case you haven't heard, Ravenshore is under attack by the Regnan pirates. The town has been evacuated. You must eliminate the pirate threat before the alliance council will return to guide you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:910
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:905
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you've sunk the Regnan fleet. Go and seek the wisdom of your alliance council. They will give you the next task that will make your destiny."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:911
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:906
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You must speak to the Ironfists' court sage, Xanthor. He is housed in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:912
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:907
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I see an important link between the present and your future has not been forged. Seek out the sage, Xanthor who resides in Ravenshore. He will send you on your destiny's next task."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:913
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:908
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is clear that you must do as Xanthor has asked of you. Go to the four elemental planes and find in each, an elemental heartstone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:914
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:909
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Now that you have the four elemental heartstones, you must now bring them to Xanthor in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:915
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:910
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your destiny lies through the crystal gateway in Ravenshore. It will take you to the Plane Between Planes. There you will find the source of the elemental cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:916
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:911
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have talked to the Destroyer, but have failed to gather from him the key which will unlock your future. Return to him and continue your conversations."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:917
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:912
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your path is clear to my vision. You must seek out the four elemental lords and release them from their prisons. These prisons are in the Destroyer's realm--the Plane Between Planes."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:918
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:913
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Seek out Xanthor! Though he is but a piece in the game of Balance, the next move you make towards destiny it through a meeting with him."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:919
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:914
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Balance is restored. Now that your destiny is made, I can no longer guide you--my sight only pertains to what is connected to the fate of Balance. What you do now is up to you. Good luck to you, Heroes of Jadame!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:920
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:915
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You cannot be promoted until we know where Cauri Blackthorne is!  Locate her, and she will promote you.  After she is found and has retuned to the Merchant Guild, I will be glad to promote any Dark Elves in your party to Patriarch."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:921
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:916
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Cauri told me of how you helped her with the curse of the Basilisk.  She has instructed me to promote any Dark Elves that travel with you to Patriarch."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:922
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:917
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You cannot be promoted until the Ancient Troll Home has been found!  Return here when you have found it and talk with Volog."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:923
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:918
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Before Volog left, he instructed me to promote any Trolls that travel with you to War Troll.  The village of Rust will be forever thankful to you!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:924
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:919
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You cannot be promoted to Champion until you have proven yourself worthy!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:925
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:920
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for you help recovering the spear Ebonest!  I can promote any Knights that travel with you to Champion."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:926
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:921
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not proven yourself worthy!  Until you strike a blow against the Dragon Hunters, none of you will be promoted!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:927
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:922
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have proven yourself and I will promote any Dragons that travel with you to Great Wyrm."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:928
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:923
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You cannot be promoted to Priest of the Sun until you have recovered the Prophecies of the Sun!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:929
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:924
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are always welcome here!  Of course I will promote any Clerics that travel with you to Priest of the Sun!  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:930
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:925
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not recovered the Lost Book of Kehl!  There will be no promotions until you return with the book!  Speak with Vetrinus Taleshire."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:931
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:926
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, you return seeking promotion for others in your party?  I have not forgotten your help in recovering the Lost Book of Kehl!  All Necromancers in your party will be promoted to Lich.  Be sure each Necromancer has a Lich Jar in his possession."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:932
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:927
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not found Korbu and until you have I refuse to promote any of you!  Begone!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:933
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:928
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Any Vampires among you will be promoted to Nosferatu!  I remember those who helped in the recovery of the Remains of Korbu."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:934
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:929
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have not found the Axe of Balthazar!  You are not worthy of promotion!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:935
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:930
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Herd of Masul is in debt to you.  Any Minotaurs in your party are promoted to Minotaur Lord!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:936
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:931
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My father sent you to rescue me?  I am grateful.  I will return to my father and let him know of your assistance!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:937
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:932
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Where is the Vial of Grave Dirt?  Do not bother me until you have it!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:938
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:933
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I cannot yet travel with you!  I would sooner sign on with a merchant caravan, than travel with you.  Return to me when you have discovered more of the world, and your place in it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:939
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:934
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I remember you!  The Book of Kehl has proven invaluable, and it would be a privilege to travel with you."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:940
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:935
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When you have grown and learned more of the ways of the world, then it would be my pleasure to travel with you.  Until then I have studies to complete here."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:941
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:936
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Certainly!  Traveling with you would be an honor!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:942
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:937
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have done us a great service, adventurers. On behalf of my herd, I give you our humblest thanks. Know that the Minotaurs of Balthazar Lair hold you in the highest regard. You will always be welcome among us."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/npctext.txt.py:943
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:938
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Excellent!  Now that the Ogres are cleared from the roads and no longer inhabit the fortress, the roads to Ravenshore, Ironsand and Murmurwoods are safe again!  "
msgstr ""

