#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:3
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"A Black Potion of Pure Might is any adventurer's dream.  The addition to permanent might can turn ANYONE into a fighting machine.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of four of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:4
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"A Black Potion of Pure Accuracy is any archer's dream.  The addition to permanent accuracy can turn ANYONE into a fighting machine.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of four of any yellow reagent type, plus two of any red reagent type and one of the blue reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:5
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Pure Personality will add to a character's permanent personality. This will increase the total spell points based off Personality. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus four of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:6
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"A Black Potion of Pure Endurance is any adventurer's dream.  The addition to permanent endurance can turn ANYONE into a fighting machine, increasing their hit points far beyond normal.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus four of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:7
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Pure Intellect will add to a character's permanent intellect, increasing the total spell points based off of intellect. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and four of the yellow reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:8
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:8
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Pure Speed could be the answer for a party who just doesn't get the jump on the monsters.  The addition to permanent speed could be just what is needed to allow you to recover and act before the monsters do.  You can never be too quick. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of four of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:9
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Pure Luck could be the answer for a party who is disarm trap skill challenged.  The addition to permanent luck could be just what is needed to allow you to duck before a trap goes off.  You can never have too much luck. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus three of any blue reagent type and three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:10
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Slaying can turn any normal weapon into a weapon of dragon slaying.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any red reagent type, plus three of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:11
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Black Potion of Stone to Flesh allows you to remove the stoned condition on a character. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:18
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:18
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Flaming Potion turns any normal weapon into a weapon of Flame. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:19
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:19
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Freezing Potion turns any normal weapon into a weapon of Frost. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:20
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:20
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Noxious Potion turns any normal weapon into a weapon of Poison. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:21
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Shocking Potion turns any normal weapon into a weapon of Sparks. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:22
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Swift Potion turns any normal weapon into a weapon of Swiftness. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus three of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:23
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Cure Paralysis eliminates the Paralysis condition. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:24
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Divine Restoration eliminates all conditions except stoned, dead or eradicated. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:26
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Divine Power is a more powerful spell point restorative than is the Magic Potion. To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any blue reagent type and any three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:28
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:28
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Fire Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to fire inflicted damage.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:29
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:29
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Air Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to air inflicted damage.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:30
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:30
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Water Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to water inflicted damage.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus three of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:31
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:31
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Earth Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to earth inflicted damage.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of three of any red reagent type, plus one of any blue reagent type and two of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:32
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:32
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Mind Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to damage inflicted by Mind Magic.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of two of any red reagent type, plus three of any blue reagent type and one of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:33
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:33
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"The White Potion of Body Resistance temporarily raises your resistance to damage inflicted by Body Magic.  To mix this potion you need the correct combination of one of any red reagent type, plus two of any blue reagent type and three of the yellow reagents."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:34
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:34
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"I Dadeross, certify, that the individuals who bear this letter with my seal, do indeed carry with them the Axe of Balthazar. Treat these fine warriors as family and give them all possible honors.\n"
"\n"
"Dadeross,\n"
"Journeyman Merchant of Alvar\n"
"Axe Master of the Ravage Roaming Herd"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:35
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:35
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"My Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"I have decided to find the Sarcophagus of Korbu in the hopes that Korbu himself may be able to provide the answers I seek.  The trip will be long and dangerous, for the denizens of Ravenshore, and the Dragon Hunters of Garrote Gorge will not receive any of our kind with a warm welcome. I will seek out what shelter I can on my way to Ravage Roaming.  I leave these notes behind to document my journey. If I am not heard from again, perhaps you will find Korbu.\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:36
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:36
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"My Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"As I had feared, Ravenshore is not a friendly place to our kind.  I was chased from the city limits by a torch wielding crowd.  It was like something from one of the stories told to frighten us when we first undergo the hunger, meant to scare us away from populated areas.  The dire wolves of this area did not seem to mind my presence, perhaps they recognize a kindred spirit. Tomorrow I will try to make it to Garrote Gorge, hopefully I will find shelter there.\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:37
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:37
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"My Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"Garrote Gorge is a battlefield.  The Dragon slaying knights of Charles Quixote and the Flights of Deftclaw Redreaver battle daily, with no end to their conflict in site. This battle seems senseless.  At least we have reached an uneasy relationship with the Necromancers of Shadowspire upon which we feed. Perhaps Korbu was indeed mad, for at least we do not battle to feed. Or is it right that another race give up their lives to sustain us?  I wonder.  Tomorrow I leave for Ravage Roaming.  None of our kind has been to this region since Korbu left us.  I do not know what I will find. Answers? Korbu himself?\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:38
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:38
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"My Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"Here in the Crypt of Korbu I have found nothing but tragedy.  Korbu has perished.  Perhaps he no longer had the will to prey upon others to sustain himself.  Guardian Nagas have infested the crypt, and reaching Korbu was indeed difficult.  Instead of answers, I find myself confronted with only more questions.  Why would Korbu accept his own death, instead of taking the life of another for sustenance. The greatest of our kind is nothing but a pile of bones and dust.  I will bring these remains back to the elders, perhaps they will find the answers that I cannot.\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:39
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:39
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"My Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"I fed today upon the body of a young knight. For the first time since I experienced the hunger, I felt something as I drained this woman of her life. I have no way to describe this sensation, only that it was very unpleasant. My mind wanders, and I think more and more of the reasons why Korbu left us so long ago. We experience eternal life, but at the cost of the lives of others.  \n"
"\n"
"There was a terrible wind storm from the north today.  I saw trees caught in the storm high about the northern range of the Dragon's Teeth.  I have never seen such a storm.   I will continue back through Ravenshore and then onto home.\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:40
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:40
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"Brethren,\n"
"\n"
"I approached the outskirts of Ravenshore today.  As I did, a strange glow emanated from the center of the town.  I could feel dark magics in the air.  After considering my reception the last time through this area, I have decided to head north through Alvar, and then east to the Ironsand Desert. From there I will return home to Shadowspire.  As I fed again this night, I felt that same feeling of dread as when I fed on the young knight.  I still see the terror in her eyes. Perhaps Korbu was right?  Is it wrong that we take lives to live?\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen Venitius"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:41
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:41
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"I was burned today.  The cover here in Alvar is few and far between.  The sun has scarred my face and hands. If only I had thought to ask the elders for a Nightshade Amulet to protect me.  Then my journey surely would have been a swift one. \n"
"\n"
"I have not fed since Ravenshore as I do not wish to experience the sense of dread I picked up in Garrote Gorge. Perhaps I will feed upon the Trolls of Ironsand when I reach there. I know that the Cyclops in that region are non-hostile to our kind since we arranged for a Alvarian merchant caravan to be waylaid near their camp.  I will rest in their Larder and then return home.  \n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:42
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:42
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"I am through.  Korbu was right.  It is not right for us to take the lives of others to sustain ourselves.  The feeling I have been experiencing must be remorse.  This must be what Korbu felt as well.  I will not feed again.  I will lay down as Korbu did and perish here in the Cyclops Larder.  It is my hope that Korbu will be forgotten and that his remains will be left here. I will secret them away, as I believe that he would not wish to experience life again.  Ancient legends of our people speak of a curse that was placed upon us.  It is my belief that we are indeed cursed.  Once you have felt remorse the only desire you have is for forgiveness.  For me this is now only a dream.\n"
"\n"
"Ciatlen"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:43
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:43
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"Guildmaster Fellmoon,\n"
"\n"
"I am sending this to inform you of disturbing events on the Dagger Wound Islands. My caravan is trapped here, but that is the least of it. Soon after we arrived, a great volcano rose from the nearby sea. It pushed before it a great wave which washed away the bridges connecting the islands to one another and to the mainland. Day and night the island is pelted by burning rocks hurled from the volcano. On top of all, the Regnans have taken this as opportunity to raid. I tell you, it is chaos!\n"
"\n"
"Caravan Leader Dadeross"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:44
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:44
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"Dear Hunter,\n"
"\n"
"Recent matters require me to request your cooperation and assistance. Specifically, I would like you to gift my guild immediate use of your boats for an indefinite period of time. Oh, I imagine this will impact your business, so let me make, as a gift in return, assurances of the continuing safety of your lovely daughter, Irabelle. I understand she is a pupil at the Alvar Academy. It would be a pity if her studies were interrupted by misfortune, no? I'm sure we agree, so I thank you in advance for your generosity.\n"
"\n"
"Elgar Fellmoon"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:45
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:45
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"…and now we make ready to win what we have so long sought. The improbable wasp nest lies in the canyon just north of our campsite and the prize within will be ours. I'm sure we'll succeed where so many others have failed. Not to say they were not stout enough, but rather that they were ill-prepared.\n"
"\n"
"It meant several months of careful collecting, but we have with us the magic we will need to maneuver in the hive. All the gold we spent gathering the scrolls will be well worth the investment. Money will not be a problem once we..."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:46
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:46
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Located in what is currently the city of Ravenshore, the Vault of Time is a curious relic of the Amberly Dynasty, the monarchy which ruled the areas along the southern coast of Jadame during the period 342-621 R.E. The last Amberlian emperor, Thorn III (589-633 R.E.) knowing the empire was crumbling, sealed his regalia away in the specially constructed vault to safeguard them for a day when he or his kin could return the empire to its former glory.\n"
"\n"
"Now that the Amberlians have definitely passed into history, Thorn's vault has become the focus of many treasure hunters. The magics sealing the vault have proven potent against any attempt to penetrate it. To this day, Thorn's treasure remains locked away from the eyes of all."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:47
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:47
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"STONE PORTALS\n"
"\n"
"These strange devices appear as stone squares set in the ground, and have short pillars at each corner. It seems they were built by the temple builders as a means of transportation between the islands. Magic is clearly involved. They are powered by enchanted onyx stones. I found one myself near the temple, and I know Onefang has another. Each portal requires its own stone for power.\n"
"\n"
"ABANDONED TEMPLE\n"
"\n"
"I have uncovered an engraving which seems to suggest that the abandoned temple at the northwest island connects underwater to the island to the northeast. If this is so, the builders possessed very advanced construction techniques."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:48
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:48
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"Arion Hunter,\n"
"\n"
"We will be watching you to guarantee your compliance with Zog's requests.  Any deviation from his orders, and the Pack Master will lead the Dire Wolves into your hidden sanctuary and drive you out into the sea. \n"
"\n"
"Remember, your opinions are not requested, only your compliance.  Deliver the reports on the Merchants of Alvar to the Dread Pirate Stanley as ordered and your family will be returned to you.  Eventually.  \n"
"\n"
"Zog\n"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:49
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:49
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"ANSWER SECTION\n"
"\n"
"Riddles, page 56: 1) Fifteen Ducks!  2) The Troll's Grandmother  3) Prison\n"
"\n"
"Riddles, page 57: 1) Egg  2) The chicken was upside-down. 3) Wasp Jelly on a Cracker\n"
"\n"
"Riddles, page 58: 1) Ogre Feet 2) Inside 3) They made soup."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:50
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:50
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Plan: Use old siege door system to drain lair.\n"
"\n"
"Lever Order: A, B, C, E, G, D, J, C, E, F, D, I, C, Lowest\n"
"\n"
"Reset: A\n"
"\n"
"Tritons: Watch out!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:51
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:51
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Finally! After years of failure, we've had a successful test fire of the Cannonball of Dominion. Not only did the cannon not explode, the shot produced the expected, wide area of fury destruction. Now, the challenge is to develop a suitable ship mounting for the experimental cannon located outside the fortress. Once we've accomplished this, we will forever rule the seas! Our ships will be capable of sinking entire fleets with a single shot from just one of these new cannons!"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/scroll.txt.py:52
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Scroll.txt.py:52
msgctxt "scroll"
msgid ""
"\n"
"It is inevitable; the temple is lost to us. Never did we think that our own creations would turn against us. Nor did we think they could so handily bring about our annihilation. Only I and my assistant, Khsth'thck, are all that remain of the Relic Wardens. This note is for any of the Keepers of the True Vision who come to reclaim the temple.\n"
"\n"
"Khsth'thck and I have already secured the holy idol. Remember, it is the sixth plate, not the fourteenth! We lost Warden Rsh'Dhx when that mistake was made last. I only pray the defenses will hold until you arrive.\n"
"\n"
"Faithfully yours,\n"
"\n"
"Yvwch'vhs xhl'brck, High Nestmaster"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:2
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Might is the statistic that represents a character's overall strength, and his or her ability to put that strength where it counts.  Characters with a high Might statistic do more damage in combat."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:3
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Intellect represents a character's ability to reason and understand complex, abstract concepts. Maximum spell points for Necromancers and Dark Elves are based on Intellect."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:4
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Personality represents both a character's strength of will and personal charm.  Maximum spell points for Clerics, Vampires and Minotaurs are based on Personality."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:5
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Endurance is a measure of a character's physical toughness and durability. A high Endurance gives a character more hit points."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:6
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Accuracy represents a character's precision and hand-eye coordination.  A high Accuracy will allow a character to hit monsters more frequently in combat."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:7
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Speed is a measure of how quick a character is.  A high Speed statistic will increase a character's armor class and the rate with which the character recovers from attacks."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:9
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Hit Points indicate how much damage your character can sustain before falling unconscious or dying.  A character is unconscious at 0 Hit Points or less, and dies when Hit Points reach -10  All Hit Points are restored after 8 hours of uninterrupted rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:10
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Armor Class is a measure of how difficult it is for a monster to hit a character.  The higher the Armor Class, the better the chance of avoiding an attack."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:11
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Spell Points are needed to cast spells.  Every spell has a Spell Point cost that is deducted from this statistic when it's cast.  Spell Points are restored after 8 hours of uninterrupted rest."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:12
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Condition shows the worst \"effect\" your character is suffering, such as poisoned, diseased, or dead.  Many conditions seriously hurt your character's ability to fight or perform other actions, and should be cured as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:13
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "The Quick Spell is the spell that will be cast when you use the \"s\" key to cast a spell.  You can set the quick spell by opening your spell book (\"c\" key), clicking on the spell you want to set, then clicking on the set spell tab at the left-bottom corner of the spell book."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:17
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:17
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Attack Bonus is the sum of all factors (skills, spells, Accuracy, etc.) that influence your character's chance to hit monsters with an equipped weapon.  "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:21
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:21
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Fire Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from fire based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce fire damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:22
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:22
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Air Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from air based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce air damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:23
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:23
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Water Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from water based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce water damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:24
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:24
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Earth Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from earth based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce earth damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:25
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:25
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Mind Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from mind based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce mind damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:26
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:26
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Body Resistance represents your character's ability to minimize damage taken from body based attacks.  Though a high resistance can greatly reduce body damage, it does not make your character immune."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:27
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/stats.txt.py:27
msgctxt "stats"
msgid "Skill Points are awarded whenever your character trains for a new level.  You can spend Skill Points on your skills at any time."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:2
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:2
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Vampire crypts are normally well hidden. That the Shadowspire vampires operate so openly is proof of their power in the region."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:3
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:3
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A burial mound. Though obviously centuries old, the door's inlaid and gilded decorations are clean and untarnished. They must be preserved by magic."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:4
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:4
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "When he passed away, Lord Brinne was mourned throughout the land. His tomb is a holy place visited by pilgrims and other well-wishers."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:5
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:5
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "You find a passage leading downwards. Do you enter?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:6
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:6
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The volcano has apparently pulled this ancient building from the bottom of the sea. Who were it's mysterious builders?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:7
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:7
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Alvarian Dark Dwarves are recent arrivals to the area. In a short time, however, they've built an extensive system of mines."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:9
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:210
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This cave is legendary in Trollish lore, and is a holy place. Other creatures, however, might just see it as a lair to occupy and defend."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:10
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:212
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "As with all places holy to the followers of Eep, this temple smells of damp fur and cheese. A chorus of squeaks, like chanting issues from within."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:11
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:214
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "As with all places holy to the followers of Eep, this small temple smells faintly of fur and cheese."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:12
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:216
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A church holy to the followers of Eep. It smells faintly of damp fur and cheese."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:13
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:218
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A cave entrance. A slight breeze from within brings you the faint smell of brimstone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:14
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:220
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A cave entrance. The lair of some monstrous beast?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:15
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:222
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The entrance to this cave has been crudely widened by a creature with claws capable of ripping the hard dark stone."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:192
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:53
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "History holds that Lizardmen temples of this period were guarded by traps and not monsters. What then to make of the reptilian slithering receding into the darkness?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:193
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:56
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The smell of freshly lumbered wood gives indication of this fort's recent construction. The large stacks of supplies show that the Regnan pirates are planning a lengthy stay."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:194
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:58
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Even in the freeport of Ravenshore, some goods must avoid official eyes. Such usually pass through this secluded cove in the care of the wererat smugglers."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:195
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:60
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "By the number of wolf tracks marking the approach to this wolves' den, either the wolves are extremely active or hundreds of them live in these caves."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:196
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:61
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Dark Elven Merchants of Alvar run a mighty trade empire spanning the reach of Jadame. This is their local guildhouse in Ravenshore."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:197
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:62
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "From the conflux key come a keening pitch which resonates through the crystal. A hidden depth is revealed--a passage that draws you with inexplicable attraction."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:198
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:63
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The hive emits a hum which sets your teeth rattling in your jaw. The breeze you feel is not the wind, but the blowback of a thousand monstrous wings."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:199
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:64
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Ogre armies need carry no winches to their fort building sites. Their strength of arm and back is sufficient to raise the massive beams and posts."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:200
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:65
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Trolls of Rust have entombed their dead here for centuries--each generation digging deeper catacombs beneath those dug before."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:201
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:66
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "What use do the Cyclopes make of this sinister vault? Whatever they do, makes it smell like a butcher's shop."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:202
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:67
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "A tunnel of solidified lava snakes downward. Can it possible provide safe passage beneath the lake of fire?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:203
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:68
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Made ruin in some long forgotten war, parts of this castle are still whole. The dragon hunters have made good use of these."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:204
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:69
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "By nature, dragons are solitary beings. Occasionally, a few will nest together, but here in Garrote Gorge they have built a mighty society."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:205
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:70
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The stonework façade of this ancient temple has crumbled into the sand of time. Still, its majesty--and mystery--remain."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:206
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:71
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Though this temple is newly built it already possesses a timeless quality."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:207
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:72
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The dark rock of these stone monuments cannot be found nearby. The nearest source is the Shadowspire Mountains a hundred leagues away."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:208
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:73
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This air vent seems to be the only entrance into the flooded Minotaur city, Balthazar Lair."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:209
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:74
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Zog the Jackal's preference for building on high ground has provided an unexpected boon in the form of protection from the raging flood waters."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:210
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:75
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Regnans have never been known for their subtlety. This thick walled and cannon studded castle is the very definition of 'forbidding.'"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:211
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:76
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "From a distance, this moss covered and crumbling stronghold seems long abandoned. Fresh boot prints in the mud and the signal mirror tell a different story."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:212
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:77
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "This strange craft seems capable of traveling both on and under the water's surface. A series of cranks operated the wheel of blades which propel it."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:213
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:78
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Brooding over the village below, the Necromancers' Guild exudes an atmosphere of domineering evil."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:214
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:79
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Though renown for her beauty, Zanthora's madness drives her to live apart from the company of others. In this forbidding castle she conducts her dark experiments."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:215
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:80
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:81
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "All buildings in the Plane of Air float. So why does this cloud castle seem particularly incongruous? Perhaps because its great size?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:216
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:82
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Tribute Tomb"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:217
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:83
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Not a stick of wood or other combustibles are visible in the walls and towers of this mighty keep of stone and iron."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:218
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:84
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "If there were any doubts of the Fire Elementals' hostile intentions towards Jadame, they are allayed by the presence of this rallying camp. "
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:219
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:85
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The Destroyer reigns from a macabre palace. What kind of being would choose to live inside the skull of a 400 foot tall giant?"
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:220
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:86
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The magic power of earth whirls around this cocoon-like encasement of earth and rock. A cry of torment like a dying wind issues from within."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:221
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:57
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Though the view is obscured by shimmering waves of heated air, through the gateway you perceive a hellish landscape of endless bridgeways spanning an ocean of lava."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:222
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:59
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "The gateway leads to an earthen tunnel which extends a few paces then tees off left and right. You can't say where the passages lead."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:223
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:54
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "You see no solid ground in the airy realm through this gateway. In the hazy distance you can see oddly shaped buildings that seem to float in the sky."
msgstr ""

#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/trans.txt.py:224
#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/Trans.txt.py:55
msgctxt "trans"
msgid "Looking through the gateway is like peering through a window into an underwater canyon. Creatures of all sizes swim menacingly in the distance."
msgstr ""

