#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1739
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "In addition to my duties as overseer of unlicensed business, I am the High Priest of Enroth.  It is my job to promote clerics to priests, and if warranted, priests to priests of light.  Right now, the rolls are full of priests, and I am unable to promote new ones without creating new positions.  To do so would be highly irregular, but if someone were to perform an extraordinary service for the kingdom, the promotion would be acceptable.  <Rubbing his temples> Come to think of it, there is a service I need.  A temple in Free Haven was destroyed by fire a few months ago.  If you could get it rebuilt, I would have a reason to promote any clerics among you to priest status.  Since I really want this job done, I am even willing to promote non-priests to an honorary priest status, and I will pay you well for your service.  You’ll need to hire a stonecutter and a carpenter and show them the temple you want them to work on."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1742
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It seems a bit quick to promote anyone to high priests, given that the promotion to priest has been so recent.  Why, many wait their entire lives to receive such a promotion, only to be granted it posthumously.  However, an extraordinary service could possibly accelerate that promotion to, well, right now for instance?and I do have such a service in mind.  The heretical monks that live on the islands east of Free Haven have stolen our sacred chalice.  Retrieve it from the monks and put it in the temple you rebuilt.  Then return to me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1745
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are successful!  It looks like I will have to keep my promise and make more irregular, early promotions.  I do so with pleasure.  I hereby promote all priests to high priests, and all honorary priests to honorary high priests."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1746
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Though your rise to priest of light status was almost unseemly quick, I have never seen finer priests of light in all my years.  I am grateful for all you've done for myself and for Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1764
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Your training does not end with what you have learned as a wizard, one final step remains.  Master wizard status completes your mastery of elemental magic.  Building on your wizard training, master wizards have vast magical ability– the most efficient and skilled use of magic anywhere.  Earning this training requires a powerful artifact, owned by the powerful Arch Mage Drael-.. no, it was Frundir-… no, that’s not right either.  Actually, I can’t seem to remember what the artifact was or who owned it.  I'd remember it if I saw it, though.  I know it can be found in Corlagon’s Estate near the Mire of the Damned.  Search for it there and return it; I must have it to train you to become a master wizard."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1766
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great news!  I remember what you need to find!  The Crystal of Terrax!  Oh, you seem to have found it already.  Well, perfect!  I can train you to master wizards, then.  The first arch mage, Terrax, used this Crystal to master the elements.  Fire, earth, water, and air all formed together to make it, and from analyzing it he learned a great deal about elemental magic.  In addition, its effect on light led him to his discoveries of light and dark magic.  Since that time, the study of this crystal has guided every new master wizard.  Let me show you the secrets of the crystal. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1802
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "20 years ago, I won the annual archery competition held at Castle Ironfist, and I have held the championship ever since.  This gives me the right to promote archers to the title of warrior mage and master archer as I see fit.  I’ll grant the title of warrior mage to all the archers amongst you if you do me a little favor. I need the key to the old Dragon Towers set up near every major settlement in Enroth to shoot down flying creatures.  I think that they can be set to shoot down only monsters, instead of shooting anything flying through the air. Since this is something of a pet project, I will reward honorary warrior mage status to the rest of you.  The key is in my old keep near the southern entrance to my lands.  I had to leave it there when the ogres and their companions took it from me a few years ago.  Return with that key and be rewarded.  And I won’t be crying in my beer if you kill a lot of those monsters while you’re at it.  They took my keep!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1804
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Very good!  You got the key, and hopefully slew a large number of those loathsome beasts.  I hereby promote all archers to the status of warrior mage, and all non-archers to honorary warrior mage."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1805
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The reason I wanted the key was to open the Dragon Towers and make the adjustments to prevent them from shooting flyers indiscriminately.  There is a way to adjust the towers to shoot at only large objects, and I want all of them adjusted for the good of the Kingdom.  Magic is becoming more common, as are stories of young Sorcerers getting shot from the sky because they didn’t know the function of the towers.  You have the key.  If you adjust all of the towers to shoot at only large objects, I will promote all warrior mages amongst you to master archers and promote any honorary warrior mages to honorary master archers."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1808
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I knew my faith in you was well placed!  You have fixed a major problem in our kingdom, not to mention doing yourself a favor—It’s now safe to fly above towns.  It is my pleasure to promote all warrior mages to master archers, and all honorary warrior mages to honorary master archers.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1809
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome, master archers!  You may warm yourself by my hearth any time!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1894
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not to brag, but I'm the best staff fighter in the land.  I will teach any student who is already an expert with the staff and has a high degree of skill (Rank 7) for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1896
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am amongst the finest swordsmen in the land.  I will teach students who possess a high degree of skill (Rank 7) for 5000 gold. I won't waste my time with anyone else."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1898
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The dagger is a quick and subtle weapon that needs more brains than brawn to use.  If you're already skilled enough (Rank 7), I can train you to master rank for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1900
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So, you want to train your axe skill the dwarven way?  My tutorage will show you how to dramatically increase the damage you inflict with an axe. I require a high skill (Rank 7) and 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1902
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A little practice with the spear keeps you from making deadly mistakes in battle, but a lot more practice will help you get the best results from your spear.  I will teach you the secrets of the masters if you've already had a little practice (Rank 7).  My fee is 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1904
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Many years ago, I discovered a technique for firing twice as many arrows as the conventionally trained archer can in the same amount of time. My teaching costs 5000 gold, and you must already be highly skilled (Rank 7) in the bow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1906
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of the mace can strike enemies senseless with a single blow.  I've been practicing this technique for years and have it down to a science.  If you have the skill (Rank 7), I can teach you my technique for 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1910
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's easy to use a shield, but hard to use it right.  I can drastically improve your defense if you give me the chance.  Since I only offer extremely advanced training, you have to be an expert student (Rank 7) before I can help you.  All I ask is 3000 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1912
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My teaching will bring you up to master ranking in leather armor for 3000 gold.  My students must already be highly skilled (Rank 7) in the use of leather armor for my teaching to be worth anything to them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1914
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Chain armor is a weapon of war, there's no doubt of that, and I'm careful who I train in its use.  I require my students to be well practiced (Rank 7) before I'll train them.  My fee is 3000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1916
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "One who is a master in the use of plate mail wears it as easily as he wears his own clothes.  I'll only teach it to skilled people (Rank 7) for 3000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1918
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Long have I studied the mysteries of fire magic, and have finally come to master the skill.  I can teach the highly skilled (Rank 7) some of the things I've learned for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1920
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Air magic is the most subtle and quirky of the elemental magics you can study.  Because of the difficulty involved in learning this skill, I require a high proficiency (Rank 7).  My price is 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1922
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of water magic with the Lloyd's Beacon spell can travel about the kingdom as much as he pleases.  I teach the skill to the most advanced students (Rank 7) for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1924
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can teach experts in earth magic to become masters of earth magic.  You must be very highly skilled (Rank 7) before I can help you, and my fee is 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1926
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The most advanced spells of spirit magic permit the practitioner to raise the dead back to life. The choice of bringing a soul back from its final resting place is a weighty one indeed, and I will only train those with sufficient skill (Rank 7) for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1928
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I will train any experts of mind magic sufficiently skilled (Rank 7) to master level for 4000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1930
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The mysteries of the body can be yours all for the low, low price of 4000 gold.  Only highly skilled (Rank 7) experts can benefit from my teachings."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1931
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can show you some of the secrets of light magic if you already have a little skill (Rank 4) to start with.  My fee is 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1932
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A master of light magic is amongst the most powerful spell casters in the world.  I can improve nearly any expert to master status, but I do not do this lightly.  I require a high skill (Rank 7) and 5000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1933
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah!  A student of darkness, no doubt!  If you want schooling in dark magic, I can help you if you've already practiced a little (Rank 4).  My fee is 1000 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1934
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can bring experts of dark magic up to master, provided they meet my standards.  I only teach the genuinely dedicated– those of high skill (Rank 7).  I make no exceptions, and charge only 5000 gold in the interests of spreading darkness throughout the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1936
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You may already have found that while being an expert in identifying your treasure is good, it's not good enough.  I change  that.  I will teach experts to become masters for 2500 gold.  All you need is sufficient skill (Rank 7)."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1938
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Rare is the expert merchant, but rarer still is the master.  I can finish your merchant's education for 4000 gold, provided you have the skill (Rank 7) and the charm (Personality 50)."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1940
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I teach experts in repair skill to be masters in the repair skill.  You must have a high skill (Rank 7) and 2500 gold for my fee."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1942
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If ever I've seen such pathetic weaklings as you, for the life of me I cannot remember!  Starving rats have more meat on their bones!  For a fee of 2500 gold, I'll beat you mercilessly until you become master body builders!  You must, however, already have spent time working out (Rank 7) and be tough enough to take my punishment (Endurance 50) before I'll have anything to do with you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1944
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who disturbs my meditation, as the pebble disturbs the stillness of the pond?  Ahh, seekers of the True Path.  If you have already traveled the path of meditation for some time (rank 7) necessary for my teaching, I can lead you to master status for 2500 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1946
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The lucky person with a well trained eye can often stay out of harm's way when a trap goes off unexpectedly.  If you've already had a lot of practice (Rank 7), I'll make you a master of the perception skill.  My fee is but 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1950
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It's one thing to kill a rich and powerful monster, but it's something else entirely to get past the traps it puts on its treasure chests.  My disarm training is the best in the kingdom.  If you're already an expert and have the skill (Rank 7), I can train you to master rank for 2500 gold."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1952
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I am the teacher of teachers, the master of learning.  I can bring your understanding of the world around you to new heights.  I will only train those who have studied under my old students and have a thorough understanding of my precepts (Rank 7).  If you are smart enough (Intellect 50), I can bring you to master rank for 5000 gold.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:1987
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jacques Kohl is working with Lord Stromgard to develop experimental recipes.  If he has time, perhaps he can assist you as well in mastering the art of Alchemy."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2103 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Path of Light"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2104 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Path of Dark"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2105 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you sure, you want to change your path? Dark spells will be vanished from your spellbook and dark magic will be erased from your mind. (Yes/No)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2106 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Are you sure, you want to change your path? Light spells will be vanished from your spellbook and light magic will be erased from your mind. (Yes/No)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2107 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is never late to turn back to light, child. Choose light side."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2108 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Darkness wait and it's patience is eternal. Choose dark side."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2109 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2110 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Either you've already choosen your path, or you are not ready to do it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2150
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:2
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This will sound odd, but bear with me, heroes. The name’s Verdant, and I am a time traveler. Something rather dire has occurred and I need your help. Actually, the world needs your help. I am but a messenger… and the probable cause of all the trouble, but that’s really not what’s important here. \n"
"What is important is that there is this clandestine scholar consortium. It has no name for it should not be spoken of, and hence has no need for one. We are a group of mages who researched the intricacies of time travel for the purpose of documenting the history of our world. Pure, untainted, unbiased. Something humans entangled in their affairs and fettered by political agendas are obviously incapable of doing. As the saying goes, ‘Winners write history’. And hence, we’ve mastered the art of time travel to witness the history and document it objectively, straighten out the mangled facts, uncover the truth buried beneath convenient lies.\n"
"It’s been working out great, our archives grow with each excursion, but this time, a little something went… a little wrong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2151
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"See, personally, I always found it disappointing how all the chronicles detail the lives of kings, queens, and other politicians. How they say, ‘and Queen Whatever knighted her heroes’. I don’t want to read about that, I want to read about the heroes. I want to know about mires they’ve trudged through, about the miles they’ve traversed, about the riches they hauled, and the little folk they’ve saved. \n"
"So I’ve taken it upon myself to write a chronicle that has all of it and more. I’ve chosen three groups of heroes whose deeds saved countless lives, and I’ve attuned my magic to visit them all at the very beginnings of their journeys. I meant to get to know them, understand where they come from, see the world through their eyes, breathe in the scent of their sweat and blood. Yes, literally, don’t be squeamish, it won’t do you much good in your line of work..."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2152
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "...Anyway, something went wrong with the ritual, some malfunction or other and, uh, well. I seem to have erased a group of heroes from existence. Or, alternatively, I’ve booted them to another existence, century, or era. Fingers crossed for the booting. Then, well, I’ve tried to fix it and the same thing kind of sort of happened to the second hero group. Before you ask – yes, you’re the third. No, you’re not getting booted or existentially eradicated. *Verdant glances over to a book she’s holding* Probably. As long as the same can be said for all of your organs, we should be good."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2153
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What I need you to do is really rather simple in concept. Basically, I know you’re capable of saving the world, so I will need you to do it a few more times. Just three times total, don’t worry! With the other two groups of heroes currently or permanently indisposed, you’ve got to pick up the slack or things will get really messed up. I mean, really: the history will rewrite itself, and, given the scope of changes and the amount of lives affected, who knows. The history might just say ‘Enough is enough!’ and explode everything. A wild, yet educated, guess. So you see the problem.\n"
"Oh, you didn’t know you were heroes? Right, right, I tend to forget how stable-timed people operate and think. Of course. Well, yes, welcome to the hero-dom. You can try to escape your path, but in all honesty, it will be much easier to just get the world saving done.\n"
"Personally, I think I actually love this idea. It may sound cold, but I can’t help it, heroes are my weakness. And three time world-savers? I’m about to melt on the spot. Mrrrau! A silver lining, you may call it, yeah?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2154
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"To travel through time and fall onto the paths that were meant to be traversed by the other heroes, you will need to use a Dimension Doors scattered across most magic-filled lands. Don’t worry, it’s mostly safe. \n"
"There are one in Murmurwoods, Dragonsand and Evenmorn Island if I recall, maybe somewhere else too. Find one of these spots and if, how you call it? If you have mastered Town Portal spell, just use it. Share your surprise after. Also you could find Dimension Door scrolls amongst junk in some shops, it will work too.\n"
"You don’t need to hurry too much, it takes time a good while to restructure itself and acknowledge the changes in its fabric, but try to get it all done before you get old, aye?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2155
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one's lovely if you like colors. I mean, fiery red, sky blue, earthly brown, sea emerald. Haha. Yeah, well, the elements are everywhere here, quite in your face. They... overflowed, you could say. It's kind of a crisis really. Either way, you would take the role of caravan guards, but worry not - caravan's done riding, no boring trips. You can rob what's left, sell it to the adorable lizards inhabiting the isle, and then get on with more interesting heroics. Please do. Mmmm... heroics. Yesss. Oh, and they even have unicorns there! Sadly, you may need to kill them. They're a little bit on the vicious side. Rrrawr."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2156
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh this one is special. You get to be LORDS. Hear me? LORDS. That sounds so distinguished, don't you want to be LORDS? Ha. But to get that swell title, you must first win a scavenger hunt on a little isle. It's no biggie, there's hardly any competition. I mean it - don't think to wait it out and let someone else win to be free from that little prison. It's not going to happen. Win it and then you're home - ruling a small patch of land sitting right between two warring kingdoms who each want a piece of said land. Well, the whole of it, really. Fun. But hey, you get to call yourself LORDS. Who cares about the rest?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2157
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one's simple. You're a bunch of happy kids saved by a nice warlock fellow, spent your lives training, now all grown up and ready to roll. No need for a heavy roleplay, just don't be jerks. Go around, slap some goblins, squash a spider or two, poke a devil. Umm... I mean, an apprentice wizard, yes. No devils anywhere, forget the devils. I don't think I should be telling you things about your future. Well, their future. But also your future now. You know what I mean. From zero to hero, take your time, enjoy the views... once you find a vantage point free of death. Which is not going to be easy. This land is swarming with killey things. Seriously. I love it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2158
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Good news: the whole hero-extinction mess wasn’t just my fault. Bad news: the whole hero-extinction mess wasn’t just my fault. In other news: there’s a Runaway Chaos that’s causing trouble and it must be caught and contained! More literally than one might like.\n"
"I won’t get into the technical details, because the more I’d say, the less you’d understand – it’s perfectly normal, not a slight against your wits in the slightest. But in the simplest terms, imagine there’s something we’ll call a Chaos Matter, it’s the force of Chaos in the universe. Entropy and all that. And from this matter, a bit… fell off, let’s say, and began causing unpredictable trouble. And though you may think – but that’s what chaos ought to be! Chaotic! Let me treat you with a slogan – In every Chaos there is Order, in every Order there is Chaos. \n"
"The Runaway Chaos is the aforementioned bit. It attached to my spells and made them backfire horribly, as you well know. You have to go to the Controlled Breach, capture the Runaway Chaos, and return it to the uh… Uneasy Origin Matter. Yes, I made that name up, but no sane person can memorize the one we use to describe it in the consortium without hearing it a hundred times over."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2159
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Controlled Breach is a place the consortium has created where it’s possible to see and interact with the Runaway Chaos, and through which the Uneasy Origin Matter can be reached. It’s an artificial realm-esque area where matters *Verdant snickers* can be safely handled without jeopardizing any real world places. \n"
"Ruins of Escaton's Crystal should be enough magic-filled to allow our old friend - town portal spell - teleport you there.\n"
"Once there, all you need to do is find the Runaway Chaos and return it to the Uneasy Origin Matter. What can you expect on the way? Aye, this even I cannot tell you. Since it’s a result of a time anomaly, we have obviously never seen it before. \n"
"What will happen to you after you go in and leave?\n"
"Well, um. Let’s not overthink things. I’m sure it’s going to be fun, though!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2160
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have to figure out the exact cause of this whole timeline kerfuffle. There might be some more anomalies that I’ve missed. You’ve helped me a bunch already, but would you mind terribly if I called on you again at some point? I mean, you’re face-deep in this mess as it is and it’s not like you’re getting out of it anytime *Verdant snickers* soon. Might as well keep helping me, right?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2161
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Nifty gizmo, isn’t it? This gem will let us speak wherever and whenever. But, eh, as always there’s a but. The thing is quite unstable and will need to recharge after each contact we make. To put it simply, it absorbs energy from the air around it. You can either give it a few days or jump into the time-travel door for an instant recharge. Ever wondered why you come out of those with your hair standing straight in all directions? Now you know. Energy. Tons of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2162 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG.txt.py:26 mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "(Charged connector stone will heal you up once per day.)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2163
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I’m glad you asked, this whole conundrum is making it rather difficult for me to sleep. I could pretend it’s the worry over the poor goobers I’ve punted out of our realm, existence, time, or whatnot that’s keeping me awake, but I’ve always been a big fan of truth telling. Lies are so much hassle to keep track of, aren’t they?\n"
"Basically, I don’t much care about the scrubs I’ve sent away, but I do care an awful lot about the heroes snoozing within them. And I want those heroes back, and I want to put them in another time of trouble to witness their glory and maybe save a life or two while we’re at it. Hence I’ve been hard at work locating the two missing groups. But to make it happen in a reasonable amount of time, I will need your help."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2164
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You could ask, what value does time hold to a time traveler? And hasn’t the other heroes’ suffering has already begun – or, in fact, ended centuries ago, should they have found themselves in another period? And to that I’ll tell you: stop over thinking things. Trying to make sense of it all will just give you a headache. A rookie mistake of anyone dealing with paradox-prone situations.\n"
"Look at it this way – we’re living in dangerous times. As all times are, really, so it’s not like we can hide elsewhen. *Verdant shrugs.* And so it’s not out of the realm of possibility that a dragon will eat me tomorrow, or the day after, and cut my work time short. It would be deeply troubling and unfortunate given that I’m also involved in other matters of great importance, but the point is – it could happen. I don’t know what awaits me in this timeline, provided I stay here, since I’ve never been here and now before… I think. Oh gods, now I’m doing it. Stop it, woman! *Verdant slaps her left ear as if she wanted the paradox musings to fall out of the right one.*\n"
"Anyway, what I need you to do is help me build a Telelocator. Doing that will increase the chance of my finishing the task before I become a dragon snack.”"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2165
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There’s two things to know here.\n"
"One: I cannot return the lost heroes to their own respective timelines as I’ve already attuned you to their paths. We’ll have to move them somewhen else or the universe could get really huffy and we would really not want that. If we plop them in some random, nicely troubled time and place they will start their own new paths, and all will be good.\n"
"\n"
"Two: to commence said plopping, we must first locate the poor goobers. That can be accomplished by building a device we call the Telelocator. That’s where you come in.\n"
"First things first, we need a Rod. Not just any rod, but a special rod of an infused metal. There’s a clan of Duergars dwelling near Alvar who dabble with this kind of ore. I’m sure they’ll have a rod somewhere around their complex, what half-competent blacksmith wouldn’t have one? I’d suggest to simply purchase it, but I’ve heard them Duergars are rather grumpy. And by grumpy I mean they would rather lodge an axe in your head than barter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2166
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How’s the Rod expedition going? No, I cannot use a wooden stick instead, stop asking or I’ll get one and use it for another purpose next time you do. Ass-whooping in the purpose, in case there was any doubt."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2167
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Brilliant. This is a wonderful rod. Have you run your hand over it? Try it! Bzzt. Bzzt! Fun, isn’t it? Next we’ll need a Guiding Gem."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2168
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire an Infused Metal Rod for Verdant to serve as a base of the Telelocator. She said Duergars of Alvar may own a few."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2169
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is no such thing as a Guiding Gem, obviously, we have to make one. I will need a large round crystal for this. LARGE. ROUND. And I mean, *SERIOUSLY ROUND*. None of that shady vendor garbage. If the stream gets skewed due to an uneven orb shape I might get a nosebleed of the century when I use the Telelocator. I’ve already sprayed the halls for the century two centuries back, and also for the one six from now, and I’m definitely not into repeating that experience.\n"
"So yes, round please. I’ve asked around and been told that the dwarves of the Stone City might have something like that stashed away. They sure love their crystals and when it comes to classy stone cutting they have no equals.\n"
"Is it possible you will have to steal it? Please, we are living in a world of wonders. Dragons, Unicorns, talking trees, might and magic. Of course it’s possible, what sort of a dumb question is that?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2170
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The dwarves are generally a very friendly folk. If they get mad at you, just bolt and give them a moment to cool off while firmly out of their sight. Or learn to be sneaky and don’t get caught in the first place. I’d advise the latter, but I won’t be surprised if you just go and slaughter everyone instead. You wouldn’t believe the things some world-saving heroes liked to do. *Verdant rolls her eyes, but a corner of her lips twitches in a way that makes you wonder if she doesn’t appreciate an occasional anti-hero spicing up her chronicles.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2171
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great, this is beautiful. So smooth… I could just sit and pet it for hours. Which I might well do until you return with the Wisp Wrappings, as there’s little progress to be made meanwhile."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2172
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire a Large Seriously Round Crystal for Verdant’s Telelocator. One could possibly be found in the Stone City located in Barrow Downs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2173
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Good, good, we almost have our thing pieced together. To attach the gem to the rod I need one more thing – Wisp Wrappings. It’s basically bandages, but infused with a strong spiritual essence. That can only happen if they touched the “flesh” of an undead and have spent some time being filled with a strong spiritual presence.\n"
"I know just the place to look for such a thing. Near the Castle Ironfist you will find a place that used to belong to a wizard named Corlagon. That hole is just swarming with all sorts of undead. If a piece of cloth ever fell off one of them, it will be perfect. Those ghosts there seem to be very… bed-sheety. So I wouldn’t be at all surprised if the entire area was littered with bits that tore off them while they flew around the corridors.\n"
"What? You don’t know what bed sheets are? You poor things! Grab yourself a ghost carcass in the Estate then and line your bed with it next time. You’ll thank me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2174
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don’t tell me not one of those ghosts has ever ran into a sharp nail sticking out of the wall or another?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2175
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lovely, that’s exactly what I needed. Mmm… and it smells delicious too. If you can look past the odor of death and rotting meat. Here try it, look for that subtle note in the background. Oh, come on! Why does no one ever want to share the simple pleasures with me? *Verdant pouts* Fine, business then. We need to enchant the rod and the gem now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2176
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire Wisp Wrappings for Verdant’s Telelocator. She suggested searching for some in the Corlagon’s Estate near Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2177
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:29
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Infusing the Guiding Gem might turn out to be an affair more expensive than dangerous. I’d love to reimburse you but, alas, I don’t have any currency valid in this here time period. In the place I’ve last visited with an intention to buy things they stopped trading in gold. *Verdant shows you a bunch of useless paper scraps* You could get a horse for this. Fun, no?\n"
"What I need right now are gems – a great variety of gems. Bring me one of %s. I need to powder them and experiment to find the right dust combination that will properly attune the Guiding Gem to the realms."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2178
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:30
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire %s for Verdant’s Telelocator. They can be found all over the world and bought from various merchants."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2179
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I really hope you like collecting things. Do not tell me otherwise, let me stay blissfully happy for you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2180
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:32
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, this is %s, I still need %s."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2181
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, aren’t these just gorgeous? It’s almost a shame to turn them to dust… I wonder if there could be another way---OKAY, FINE I’LL DO IT! No need for these death stares, what are you, gorgons? *Verdant mumbles something under her breath.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2182
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The rod can be enchanted with just a little bit of leg work. You will need to drop by the four Elemental Planes, but before you panic – don’t. What I need can be found near the very entrance of each of them.\n"
"All you need to do is go inside, boink the frame with a sword or whatever you have at hand, and pick up what falls off. These metal structures are surprisingly soft, it’s the rampaging elemental middle that’s holding it all together and actually shaping the thing. Who’d have guessed, huh? You may even just find some chippings lying around to save you the hassle. Seriously, an angry cat could probably bite one off.\n"
"Either way, bring me four of the chippings and I’ll melt them into the rod to give it the much needed power."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2183
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire Fire Portal Chipping, Water Portal Chipping, Earth Portal Chipping, and Air Portal Chipping for Verdant’s Telelocator. They can be found inside the Elemental Planes near the entrance portal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2184
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You can try to bite the frames if you want, too. If a cat can do it so can you. But remember – it must be the frame inside the realm. The outer ones are actually quite tough and would definitely chip your teeth instead. Don’t ask me why that’s so, I didn’t make them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2185
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:37
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've acquired %s Chipping!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2186
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Okay, give me these and let’s see how that works out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2187
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wonderful, gorgeous, beautiful. Now that we have this puppy in one piece and magical enough, on top of being attuned to the realms, we need to do one more thing before I activate it. Well, one-ish. We need to attune it to the heroic spirits, traits found in heroes, kindred souls of valiance, call it however you want. Long story short, I need you to hold it and let it become drunk with your awesomeness. The problematic part may be, you need to actually be awesome for the device to want to drink from you.\n"
"Luckily, it doesn’t need to feed on just one person. No, it won’t literally suck the thing out of you! Seriously? I’m being metaphorical. Why would I want to break you… *Verdant sighs and shakes her head.* Telelocator needs to feel Might, Endurance, Accuracy, Intellect, Personality, and Luck. If you feel strong at one of them, come forth, take it, and close your eyes. Tell it, in your mind, about your valor. If it deems you worthy and absorbs your essence – NOT by taking it away, I SWEAR – the Guiding Gem will glow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2188
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Harder! Try to squeeze it maybe?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2189
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up. Verdant whispers something under her breath with her eyes following every twitch of your muscles.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2190
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Maybe if you first do a few rounds up and down the stairs?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2191
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* I wish I could ‘attune’ myself to you too. I’m out of breath after a ten seconds run. Heck, I’m out of breath just talking about it. *Verdant pants.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2192
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Try squinting. More. More! Close your eyes! Aim with your mind alone! Eh. Still nothing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2193
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Can you hunt me a deer for dinner? I’ve been eating local shrooms for too many days already. Bleh."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2194
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Did it ask you a riddle or something? If so, do tell, I’m curious if I’d get it right."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2195
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Sweet. You know, we should meet for a round of Ugili Duli once. It’s a fascinating game, but nobody around seems to even get the rules. Much less pose a challenge!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2196
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Don’t worry, I personally think you’re very, very charming and… personable. Mrrr…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2197
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Then the gizmo and I are in agreement."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2198
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] How often do you step in poop? I find that’s a good measure of how badly the world hates you. Once you get to less than twice a day give it another go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2199
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* It’s our lucky day! The fortune smiles on us today! Hm. I had more cliches ready for this one, but they fled my mind. I guess you really *are* lucky."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2200
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Pass the test Might (70) to attune the Telelocator.\n"
"Pass the test Endurance (70) to attune the Telelocator.\n"
"Pass the test Accuracy (70) to attune the Telelocator.\n"
"Pass the test Intellect (70) to attune the Telelocator.\n"
"Pass the test Personality (70) to attune the Telelocator.\n"
"Pass the test Luck (70) to attune the Telelocator"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2201
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We’re almost there. I can nearly hear the desperate cries for help from our punted friends! Provided they still actually exist somewhere and haven’t been straight out erased from everywhere… let’s stick to nearly hearing their cries, aye?\n"
"Now this may be a toughie. To activate the Telelocator I will need a lot of power. Not a fancy power core kind of power, but still. Ten Philosopher Stones is what we’re looking for here. Once you bring them to me, we can finally use the thing! I’m getting excited."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2202
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "May I suggest an alchemy lab heist? Desperate times desperate measures and all that."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2203
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:55
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, %s more stones left."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2204
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Brilliant. No more talk. Let’s go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2205
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire 10 Philosopher Stones to activate the Telelocator."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2206
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"*Verdant performs quite a lengthy ritual to activate the Telelocator, and just when you begin to worry that it may not work after all this work, the device beams up and the sorceress opens her eyes wide. She’s looking straight at you, but her gaze is absent, as she’s not seeing you, but things from realms, or times, far away or long time away from here and now. Then, she speaks, strangely mechanically.”\n"
"Targets found. Realms: Attuned. Time: Attuned.\n"
"World: Ashan. Year: 1923\n"
"Targets’ Status: Incapacitated and confused. Targets’ predicted remaining lifespan: Eleven thousand and sixty six days.\n"
"Realms: Detached. Time: Detached.\n"
"*Verdant opens her eyes with a gasp.*\n"
"Aw, crap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2207
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Yes, we can do it. I don’t know how much you’ve heard, but I know exactly how to bring the lost heroes back into our world and place them in a more fair predicament. I will need some gruesome stuff for that. It’s all about sacrifice and suffering now, you know. Also, do make haste as always, but don’t worry about time too much. Telelocator has detached both timelines so as long as I’m alive and the universe doesn’t backflip, the heroes can be saved.\n"
"I will need you to bring me 5 Will’o’Wisp Hearts, 5 Wolf Eyes, 3 Phoenix Feathers, a vial of Troll Blood, a vial of Gog Blood, 2 Dragon’s Eyes, and a Focal Ring.\n"
"Then I will… Let’s not think or talk about it right now. Go, let’s save those Goobers so they can become the heroes we all know they can be!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2208
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That’s not enough murder. Get on it, aye? Trust me, I’m getting the short end of the stick here…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2209
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:61
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This is %s, fine. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2210
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:62
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Need %s more. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2211
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:63
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "And also, %s "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2212
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have to say, I was kind of sort of hoping you might not be back… Eech! Yes, I do have to mash it all together and drink it. In theory, so do you each time you drink this or that potion, but trust me, it’s a whole different story when you just straight out… mash it… no boiling… no magic. *Verdant closes her eyes and inhales sharply.* I feel sick and filthy already. Can you mix it for me at least? Leave the feather shafts out…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2213
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With *pleasure*?! What is that supposed to mean?! Some heroes you are! *She crosses her arms on her chest and kicks a pot your way. You mix the ingredients together and offer the sorceress the resulting goop. It is, indeed, a sight to behold… right before barfing.*\n"
"Here it goes. *It takes Verdant a good while to actually do as she must, but eventually she proves her dedication to the cause and downs the mixture.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2214
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Well, the ring seemed stuck in my throat for a moment, but I think it passed through. WHO made this recipe? *She glares at a book lying to the side then takes the device and begins to activate it again. The mechanical voice is back.*\n"
"Targets found. Realms: Attuned. Time: Attuned.\n"
"Targets: Attuned. Captured. Removed. Resummoned. Placed. Detached. \n"
"World: Enroth Year: 1176. Continent: Vori.\n"
"*The channeling is over and Verdant opens her eyes smiling at you.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2215
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All in all, that was pretty hero-efficient, I must say. One group for the prize of three and then two to spare for future or past catastrophes. Though with all of them placed in the same spot it might be a bit of a hero-oversaturation there. On the other hand, maybe they’ll fall in love and multiply eventually? If you ask me, I think the world needs all the heroes it can get. Yes, I *know* I can just check, don’t be such a buzz kill!\n"
"But great job, I mean it. Saving heroes, saving worlds, I might be falling in love with you myself. Just kidding, that’s a done deal. It was love at first sight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2216
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire 10 5 Will’o’Wisp Hearts, 5 Wolf Eyes, 3 Phoenix Feathers, a vial of troll Blood, a vial of Gog Blood, 2 Dragon’s Eyes, and a Focal Ring to bring back the lost heroes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2217
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Other heroes#Help the Goobers#Telelocator#Infused metal rod#Guiding gem#Wisp wrappings#Telelocator parts#Enchant the Gem#Enchant the Rod#Attune the Telelocator#Attune #Activate the Telelocator#Activate!#Save the Goobers!#Mix the potion#...#Dimensionally displaced goobers"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2219
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You see it about in field and town,\n"
"It cannot get up,\n"
"But will often fall down."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2220
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "rain"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2221
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The strongest chains will not bind it,\n"
"ditch and rampart will not slow it down.\n"
"A thousand soldiers cannot beat it,\n"
"it can knock down trees with a single push."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2222
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "wind"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2223
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"An untiring servant it is,\n"
"carrying loads across muddy earth.\n"
"But one thing that cannot be forced,\n"
"is a return to the place of its birth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2224
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "river"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2225
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With sharp edged wit,\n"
"And pointed poise,\n"
"It can settle disputes,\n"
"Without a noise."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2226
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "sword"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2227
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is too much for one.\n"
"Two it is meant for.\n"
"But it no longer exists,\n"
"When the two become more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2228
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:80
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "secret"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2229
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:81
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This old one runs forever,\n"
"But never moves at all.\n"
"He has not lungs, nor throat,\n"
"Still, a mighty roaring call."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2230
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:82
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "waterfall"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2231
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:83
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It can move over water,\n"
"But cannot fly.\n"
"It can move under water,\n"
"But stay quite dry."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2232
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:84
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "shadow"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2233
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:85
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It doesn't live with in a house,\n"
"Nor does it live without.\n"
"Most will use it when they come in,\n"
"And again when they go out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2234
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:86
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "door"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2235
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:87
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A shimmering field that reaches far.\n"
"Yet it has no tracks,\n"
"And is crossed without paths."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2236
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:88
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "ocean"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2237
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:89
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This engulfing thing,\n"
"is strange indeed.\n"
"The greater it grows,\n"
"the less you see."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2238
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:90
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "darkness"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2239
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:91
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When it comes in,\n"
"From sea to shore,\n"
"Twenty paces you'll see,\n"
"No less, no more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2240
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:92
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "fog"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2242
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:94
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "%s, friend! You are here, I'm so glad to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2243
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:95
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I thought I'm lost here, nice to see you again."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2244
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:96
#, python-format
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "At least one familiar face amongst this madness, %s!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2245
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:97
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Finally, friends!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2246
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:98
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who are you? Another horror of this place? If not, let's stay together."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2247
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:99
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, live being."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2248
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All the wizards around here have gone mad, but their golems are still functioning. The important part is, I don’t want to be here any longer than I absolutely have to."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2249
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Can you believe these swordsmen thought I was Prince Nicolai? Amazing. Anyway, at least it’s safe in here."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2250
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The area is swarming with fire elementals. I killed some, but they just keep on coming. Well, at least the fort is empty, so there’s that. Man, it’s so hot in here. Do you have any water? Anything liquid?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2251
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:103
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "These stinky hulks outside are about as friendly as they smell. I’ve snuck in here to wait for dawn to come, but it’s still dark outside and I’ve lost the track of time completely."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2252
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:104
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This place is a madhouse! The thing we’re looking for – the Runaway Chaos – it’s not a living being. Think of a ghost or a spirit of some sort."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2253
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:105
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This place… it sends shivers down my spine. It reminds me of Alvar, but we will find no elves here. The lights in the houses turn on and off, even though nobody is here. I think we should look for Runaway Chaos in one of the buildings."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2254
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:106
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Look, I found a diary of some poor sod. Or rather what remains of it. It seems someone got into the Breach long before us… if we can speak in terms of time around here at all. He wrote: “Everything in here is a reflection of things that happened, somewhere, somewhen. None of it is real, with the exception of the Personalities.” It looks like the poor fellow has failed to find a way out of here and began to lose his mind. The last pages are just filled with gibberish about some riddles."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2255
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:107
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My friends! I found it! The Runaway Chaos! Or maybe… maybe it found me? I don’t know, I don’t know, it all feels like a grand jest. It surrounded me with hellish creatures, monsters born of my nightmares. To scare me, perhaps, or just see what I would do. I fought to stay alive and it just laughed. As I say these words, I hear echoes of this screeching laughter piercing through my very skull. And when I finally fell to the ground, without a shred of power left to carry on, suddenly the nightmares… dissipated. Gone, every single one. But the wounds they left were real… and yet, when I looked down, there wasn’t a single cut. Only my torn clothes stood as proof that anything had happened at all.\n"
"And then the being spoke to me, in a voice so calm, my own shivers ceased. “I will ask you riddles five,” it said, “Answer them to feel alive. Make a wish if you succeed, maybe then you shall be freed.” I did not know the answers. But it let me be. I don’t know why. Maybe it felt pity. Or maybe it merely wanted to let me rest before it returns to torment me once again."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2256
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:108
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't waste my time!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2257
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:109
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Never heard of it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2258
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:110
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What is this? A new shop?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2259
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:111
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, I do love me some riddles. Tell me what this is:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2260
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I remember one from my childhood:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2261
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:113
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sometimes you can find riddles in random books. Delightfully unepexected. Like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2262
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one was mumbled in a tavern by a drooling drunk. His last words, actually:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2263
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:115
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm, yes, that will do. It was fun picking your brain, very enjoyable indeed. A good time begs a good reward. Make a wish and I shall make it come true."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2264
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:116
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't know anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2265
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Correct!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2266
#: mmmerge/nonprod/LocalizeTables.NPCText.txt.py:118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not quite, friend, not quite."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCText.txt.py:2699
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jars. Yessss. You have helped us greatly."
msgstr ""

